{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest","id":955241,"title":"Urchin Quest","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-21T15:38:16-07:00","id":955241,"title":"Urchin Quest","content":"You awaken to the sound of rumbling.<br /> <br /> It is raining. Hard. Little rivers are running black down the narrow alleys and streets of the Nightside ghetto down below you, and cold rain pours off the tiled roofs. The afternoon sky is grey and dark.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s the rumbling again. And a dull pain... It\u2019s not thunder then.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s your stomach.<br /> <br /> You haven\u2019t had anything to eat since you stole that bowl of swamp rice yesterday morning while Rat distracted the street vendor...just thinking about it makes your stomach ache with longing. Sometimes sleeping helps, but not today. You\u2019re too hungry to sleep, and you were dreaming about hot soup anyway.<br /> <br /> You are currently safe and dry, in your nest atop the warm brick roof of the Blackhand Company\u2019s great foundry. You\u2019re under an eave that pours all the water out past the pile of stolen laundry where you sleep, and you\u2019re close enough to one of the foundry\u2019s chimneys that its heat warms your bones and dries your tattered clothes. It\u2019s a little narrow, and you have to be careful not to actually touch the wall north of the corner for very long because it will burn your hands, and you have to be careful not to roll out onto the sloped roof and fall off in your sleep, and when the pouring rain isn\u2019t pounding the Nexus Snow down into the gutters the smoke means you have to hold a rag in your mouth to breathe through\u2026but this spot is yours. None of the other kids know about it, except Rat, who showed you the spot, and he\u2019s too big now to use it himself.<br /> <br /> \u2026the climb down is usually easy, but in the rain the bricks are probably going to be slippery. It might be dangerous. But you really, really need to eat.<br /> <br /> <b>Do You:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Stay here and try to get back to sleep:</b> You're starving, sure, but you're not stupid. You\u2019re not going to be able to get much food with a broken leg. You\u2019ll wait until the rain stops and climb down when it\u2019s safe. Sure, hunger hurts, but it\u2019s a dull pain. You can wait out the storm.<br /> <br /> <b>Go Find Rat:</b> He\u2019s big enough now that he\u2019s been able to join the Sluice gang. He might have some food, or have some job you can do to get some. Of course, the Canal Sluice is going to be even more dangerous in a big rainstorm like this than climbing down the roof\u2026and Rat's been weird since he started hanging with the Sluice gang. He keeps trying to act all tough. He might be super mean to you just to impress his new friends.<br /> <br /> <b>Visit Aunt Dwi:</b> She\u2019ll sometimes give you real food-a pork bun or a bowl of noodles. But if she\u2019s got a customer you\u2019ll have to wait, because if you interrupt her while she\u2019s with a client she\u2019ll thrash you\u2026and the last couple of times you went to her for food, she looked at you weird and said you were getting taller, weren't you, and insisted on giving you poppy juice\u2026which was fantastic! But you\u2019ve seen what happens to other kids who spent too much time drinking poppy juice with Aunt Dwi. They end up drinking poppy juice all the time, and working for her brothel, and because they're new they always end up getting the rough customers\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Go to the Nightside Street Market:</b> Traffic will be low because of the rain, which will make it harder to steal anything from any of the stalls\u2026but if nobody\u2019s buying, odds are good some of the food will start to spoil and get thrown away, so there might be some good scavenging.<br /> <br /> <b>Head over to the Imperium:</b> It\u2019s a long way to the Nexus District, and the Imperium is patrolled so you\u2019ll have to keep to alleys and rooftops to avoid getting picked up by their mercenaries...but fancy merchants and occasionally even visiting Dragonblooded trade there, and there are a couple of fancy restaurants that serve them, and the bins behind those restaurants often have good pickings. If you\u2019re gonna be going out in the rain to eat garbage, it might as well be really expensive garbage.<br /> <br /> <b>Go Fishing:</b> You have string and a couple of fishhooks. It\u2019s raining, and the streets are muddy. You should be able to get a few earthworms, and if you bait your hook right you might be able to catch some pigeons or maybe a raiton\u2026and if you don\u2019t catch anything, well, you can always eat the worms.<br /> <br /> <b>Go Begging:</b> It\u2019s raining, and foot traffic is low\u2026but if you beg close to one of the markets, you might be able to get enough coin for a hot meal. The downside is you\u2019ll have to deal with older beggars, some of whom are very territorial. Blind Jin sometimes gives you his spot in exchange for most of your take: he knows you\u2019re younger and cuter than he is. And it\u2019s easier to do puppy dog eyes at people when you still have your eyes.<br /> <br /> <b>Visit the Immaculate Temple: </b>It's a really really long way, almost all the way to the Cinnabar district. On a normal day you can get there by afternoon if you leave in the morning...but it's pouring rain and you'd have to pass along some really slick rooftops or go at street level through a couple of rough neighborhoods. The Immaculate monks give out rice to the poor, but they stop at sundown...you'd have to hurry, and even if you did you're not sure you'd make it in time to get any food...and then you'd have to find your way back in the dark.<br /> <br /> <b>Something Else:</b> Do you have any other ideas?<br /> <br /> <u><b>Inventory:</b></u><ul><li>Tattered Rags</li> <li>Fishhooks (3)</li> <li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Pile of Stolen Clothes (mostly rags)</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 08-21-2016, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:44:30-07:00","id":955251,"title":"","content":"Worms sound pretty good right about now.<b> Go Fishing.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:55:56-07:00","id":955258,"title":"","content":"<b>Visit the Immaculate Temple. </b>Let's enjoy the hospitality of Sextes Jylis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T19:50:58-07:00","id":955369,"title":"","content":"We want to go to the temple and get food and maybe listen to the Monks tell stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T20:45:02-07:00","id":955391,"title":"","content":"<b>Nightside Street Market. </b>Either pockets to pick or good scavenging. Seems like our best best on a day like this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T22:42:44-07:00","id":955440,"title":"","content":"While the other options are tempting, I vote going to the Immaculate Temple to get a handout. They're about the only group that doesn't expect anything in return, as mentioned they have such entertaining stories (the most entertaining diverge slightly from orthodoxy), and if you hurry, you might see them at Evening Meditation (boring as watching drying paint) and Martial Practice (More Kung Fu than you can shake a fishing rod at!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T09:48:08-07:00","id":955651,"title":"","content":"<b>Nightside Street Market</b>. It's a really long walk to the Immaculate Temple in the rain - and if we're late, we'll be soaked, cold and <i>even hungrier.</i> That sounds like a bad plan.<br /> <br /> Aunt Dwl isn't such a bad backup plan - maybe we could sneak some of the poppy juice away and trade it to one of the older kids for food. Maybe we could get away with that? It seems more dangerous than the merchants. who won't want to leave their tents to chase us off, which is why it's a <i>backup </i>plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9510,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","user":"BlueWinds","date":". 08-22-2016, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:27:16-07:00","id":955674,"title":"","content":"<b>Visit the Immaculate Temple. </b>It's the only sure bet for food. All the others are either dependent on luck or goodwill of others. If we had either of those we wouldn't have been an urchin to start with. <br /> <br /> Besides. Cool stories!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11676-exewon","name":"exewon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:46:35-07:00","id":955693,"title":"","content":"<b>Nightside Street Market</b>. Scavenge while staying out of the rain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11315-remulader","name":"Remulader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11315_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:55:44-07:00","id":955704,"title":"","content":"&gt;Visit Imperium.<br /> <br /> I am feeling audacious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:24:54-07:00","id":955731,"title":"","content":"<b>Visit the Temple</b> Sure food, and maybe we can learn a few bits of martial arts from watching. If cats can learn to open doors from just observing, we can do the same with fighting. Which would help us in the long run out on the streets too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12184-lazzerusthanatos","user":"LazzerusThanatos","date":". 08-22-2016, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12184-lazzerusthanatos","name":"LazzerusThanatos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12184_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T21:01:23-07:00","id":956133,"title":"","content":"You\u2019re tempted by the Nightside Market\u2026but in this rain, business is going to be slow and you\u2019ll stand out. There are a couple merchants there who might recognize you, you\u2019ve stolen from stalls before\u2026and it\u2019s a long way, but the Immaculate Monastery\u2019s a chance for a full bowl of rice instead of just a stolen apple or a piece of moldy bread.<br /> <br /> Carefully, you make your way to the edge of the roof. The tiles are slippery and wet, and the cold rain gets your hair in your eyes and numbs your fingers quickly now that you\u2019re out of your nest. You grab the rain gutter tightly in one hand for support and slowly lower yourself down until you\u2019re hanging over the city. There\u2019s a chipped brick your foot can go in\u2026there. You make sure your footing is steady, and slide your hand down the rain gutter. The lead pipe is cold, and slick, and slightly too wide for your hand, but it\u2019s at the corner of the building and you can use it for leverage to move back and forth as you pick your way down the brick wall. The Blackhand brothers built this foundry a long time ago, and there are plenty of spots where the bricks are chipped or worn away by weather. Some of them have birds\u2019 nests in them, but you\u2019ve already stolen all the eggs you can reach safely in good weather, much less this rain.<br /> <br /> Slide down\u2026grab this brick\u2026slide down\u2026left foot here, slide down\u2026it\u2019s slow going. You once saw Rat just grab the gutter and slide down it like a boat down a canal, but he came away with his hands bleeding at the bottom from the bolts fastening it to the building every couple of yards and anyway it\u2019s a lot more slippery now...<br /> <br /> <i>SHIT!</i><br /> <br /> Okay, it\u2019s alright, you caught yourself. A brick you usually stand on has apparently gotten looser now the weather is getting colder at night. Your grip on the pipe saved you from slipping. You clutch the drainpipe tightly while you probe with the big toe of your left foot for another foothold\u2026there. It\u2019s a stretch, but you can do it.<br /> <br /> Finally, after what seems like an hour, you reach the bottom. You jump off the wall from about two yards up, landing on your feet in a crouch. The balls of your feet sting from the impact with the rough wet cobblestone surrounding the foundry, but your fingers were starting to get really numb and your grip was getting clumsy. Better a fall you choose than one you don't.<br /> <br /> \u2026time to go to the Immaculate Temple. The question is...what route to take?<br /> <br /> <b>By Rooftoop:</b> You usually just go east by foot until you reach the canal, then follow it into the Nexus district and take to the rooftops from there. There are a bunch of rickety wooden causeways and rope bridges between the taller buildings in that part of town, and there are a lot of folks who use them to avoid street traffic below. After that climb, though\u2026not all the rooftop ways are going to be as well maintained as the Blackhand Foundry. A slip or a piece of loose masonry or rotted wood could injure or kill you. There\u2019s also a rumor that some merchant prince\u2019s pet Raptor Cat got loose and it\u2019s living in the rooftop maze of the Nexus district surviving on pigeons and the occasional kid. You know if you were a Raptor Cat you wouldn\u2019t want to be out in this weather\u2026but hey, maybe it\u2019s hungry too.<br /> <br /> <b>By Foot:</b> You could stay on ground level and follow the canal through the Nexus District instead of taking to the roofs. If you do, you\u2019ll be passing right through the Guild neighborhood-their headquarters are located there, and the guards they\u2019ve hired aren\u2019t particularly nice people. You\u2019ve heard stories of them grabbing kids and pressing them into service or forcing them to buy \u201criverboat tours\u201d and then selling them into slavery once they\u2019re out of city limits. After the Guild neighborhood, you\u2019ll have to pass through the territories of several different street gangs, any one of which has about even odds of ignoring you or roughing you up. Then through the Players\u2019 District, which is usually a fun place to visit but which will be kind of dull in the rain\u2026but there\u2019s more traffic there and you know a kid who got run over by a merchant prince\u2019s carriage in a hurry to call upon some actor or another.<br /> <br /> <b>By Boat: </b>There\u2019s also the canal\u2026if you can actually get a ride on one of the boats, you\u2019d only have to walk a few blocks! Of course, a ride on a canal boat costs money, which you don\u2019t have. So you\u2019d have to either talk one of the stingy boatmen into a free ride (which you might be able to if you're lucky, your father was a boatman before he died and a couple of them knew him) or, more likely, sneak aboard a boat and hope not to get caught. If you do get caught, you\u2019ll get thrown overboard, and with a big storm like this the currents are gonna be fast\u2026and, now you think about it, if you smuggle aboard you\u2019ll still have to jump ship and swim to shore once the canal gets you close to the Immaculate Temple\u2019s neighborhood, which could be real dangerous too\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>By Tunnel:</b> Or\u2026you could take a shortcut through the Undercity. It\u2019s pretty safe, except for Firewander mutants and the occasional ghost. And swarms of predatory rats.And folks too crazy to tolerate living in cramped quarters above ground. And some drug addicts. Still, it's not that bad- most anybody fast enough or strong enough to catch you is fast enough or strong enough to make a real living in the city above. But\u2026rainstorm. Some of the tunnels might be flooded out, which means either trying to find a new path and maybe getting lost in the underways or getting caught in a flash flood and drowning. Also, and you'd never admit this to Rat, but, well...it's <i>dark </i>down there!<br /> <br /> <b>By\u2026Hm.</b> Surely there\u2019s SOME safer way to get to the Immaculate Temple in bad weather\u2026<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T02:59:17-07:00","id":956230,"title":"","content":"Lets see how sharp our tongue is and try to talk our way into a boat ride.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T03:35:28-07:00","id":956242,"title":"","content":"We know a hundred ways around the city but none of them are safe for us. Let's go all &quot;Kim&quot; and offer to guide a poor lost pilgrim or itinerant traveller to the temple (for only a cursory fee, of course) and gain ourselves some safety in numbers!<br /> <br /> Let's look for someone who looks lost and pious, they shouldn't be hard to spot, all the locals are indoors today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T03:52:14-07:00","id":956247,"title":"","content":"<b>By Foot: </b>Sure there is the chance to be run over by a runaway carriage. or to be nabbed by guards and pressed into slavery.<br /> <br /> But by roof and we have the chance to fall to our deaths. Or be mauled by a raptor cat. By boat we again need to rely on goodwill or luck. Neither of which we have in ready supply. And by tunnel. Nobody likes drowning in the dark! At least a runaway carriage is easier to avoid then the rest of those options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11676-exewon","name":"exewon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T04:33:18-07:00","id":956260,"title":"","content":"<b>Other: </b>Carts and wagons from the foundry make deliveries or send out for supplies at all hours of the day. If you're quick and clever, you can hitch a ride on the undercarriage of one of these, hanging from the axles with your hands and feet. It's tiring, uncomfortable, and not exactly dry. But the carts do give you some cover and the drivers usually don't do any worse than yell at you if you're caught. You just need to find a vehicle headed the right way...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T06:15:34-07:00","id":956284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=956260#post956260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Other: </b>Carts and wagons from the foundry make deliveries or send out for supplies at all hours of the day. If you're quick and clever, you can hitch a ride on the undercarriage of one of these, hanging from the axles with your hands and feet. It's tiring, uncomfortable, and not exactly dry. But the carts do give you some cover and the drivers usually don't do any worse than yell at you if you're caught. You just need to find a vehicle headed the right way...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T08:10:58-07:00","id":956323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=956260#post956260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Other: </b>Carts and wagons from the foundry make deliveries or send out for supplies at all hours of the day. If you're quick and clever, you can hitch a ride on the undercarriage of one of these, hanging from the axles with your hands and feet. It's tiring, uncomfortable, and not exactly dry. But the carts do give you some cover and the drivers usually don't do any worse than yell at you if you're caught. You just need to find a vehicle headed the right way...</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's do this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T10:45:22-07:00","id":956414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=956260#post956260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Other: </b>Carts and wagons from the foundry make deliveries or send out for supplies at all hours of the day. If you're quick and clever, you can hitch a ride on the undercarriage of one of these, hanging from the axles with your hands and feet. It's tiring, uncomfortable, and not exactly dry. But the carts do give you some cover and the drivers usually don't do any worse than yell at you if you're caught. You just need to find a vehicle headed the right way...</div> </div> </div> </div>A fine idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11315-remulader","name":"Remulader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11315_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T12:45:21-07:00","id":956496,"title":"","content":"Go <b>by boat</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:10:45-07:00","id":957054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=956260#post956260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Other: </b>Carts and wagons from the foundry make deliveries or send out for supplies at all hours of the day. If you're quick and clever, you can hitch a ride on the undercarriage of one of these, hanging from the axles with your hands and feet. It's tiring, uncomfortable, and not exactly dry. But the carts do give you some cover and the drivers usually don't do any worse than yell at you if you're caught. You just need to find a vehicle headed the right way...</div> </div> </div> </div>5th-ing this idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12184-lazzerusthanatos","name":"LazzerusThanatos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12184_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:36:17-07:00","id":957074,"title":"","content":"I vote for the cart, seems the safest.<br /> <br /> If that isn't allowed, run across the roof tops, we probably know it better than the raptor cat; so quick thinking and the right choices could loose the little monster. But get a big stick - worse comes to worst, the raptor cat probably not chase us if it feels we'll put up too much of a fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T21:53:34-07:00","id":957400,"title":"","content":"Carts sound good to me. One with a big load might even have its tailboard lowered! But that's long odds against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T10:32:18-07:00","id":957697,"title":"","content":"Ah! That\u2019s right! The Blackhand Foundry sends carts of supplies out at all hours! They\u2019re a huge ironworks, they\u2019re always bringing in carts of iron to melt down and sending out wagons of forged goods to be or sold elsewhere. Usually most of these carts just take the goods to the canal and they\u2019re transported over water\u2026but these days, they\u2019re making a lot of axe and spearheads, and those need assembling before they\u2018re marketable. If you remember right, they send wagons over to the Cinnabar district to the hop where the handles get added. Getting under a wagon is easy, nobody cares if you hitch a ride so long as the horses are doing the work anyway! The hard part is they\u2019ll be going north a ways and then unhitching the horses and loading the wagon on a pulley cart. The Nighthammer-Cinnabar Line frowns on stowaways who don\u2019t pay for their fare. But it\u2019s raining hard, they won\u2019t want to be out inspecting cargo thoroughly\u2026it\u2019s worth a shot. You like the idea of not having to worry about gangs or slavers or raptor cats or drowning.<br /> <br /> You run down the muddy street, duck into an alley, clamber over a garbage pin, climb over a short fence, and arrive on the other side of the Blackhand Foundry. The road is much wider here, and stocky ponies are pulling dozens of wagons and carts. Large wagons are sitting around waiting to be loaded, and lots of men and women are scurrying about carrying crates or managing pulley systems to carry tons of new-forged metal on and off wagons coming up from the docks.<br /> <br /> For several minutes you watch, until you spot the right wagon-it\u2019s labelled \u201cSpears.\u201d That\u2019s the one! You can see it\u2019s mostly loaded. People are paying attention to it now. There\u2019s a sweet spot, though-once the loaders are done, they go and tell the driver (who is standing under a dry eave smoking and talking to all the other wagon drivers trying to stay out of the rain) who will then return to the cart. That gives you time to sneak in and cling to the bottom of the wagon. Which you do. One guy gives you a funny look, and you tell him Merchant Puramo sent you to see if his order is loaded yet and he gives you a look of contempt and tells you to tell Puramo loads are ready when they\u2019re ready and sending messengers to pester hardworking people just slows everything down. You nod, recite this back to him, and then wander off behind a wagon. Then you make sure nobody\u2019s looking and hide under the wagon.<br /> <br /> \u2026now the boring part. You have to wait several minutes before the driver comes back and the cart starts moving with a lurch. You cling tightly to the undercarriage, squinching your face with displeasure as you get spattered with mud and puddle-water.<br /> <br /> About half an hour later, your arms and legs are stiff and screaming from holding yourself under the cart. It\u2019s stopped and started several times due to the vagaries of traffic\u2026but now you can hear the high ringing hum of the pulley car\u2019s endlessly moving cable. The wagon stops, and the driver speaks with someone.<br /> <br /> \u201cLoad of spearheads from Blackhand Foundry.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGreat. Pull \u2018er up and unhitch the horses. We\u2019ll push the wagon up the ramp for you. You riding along?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNah. Should be a guy at the other end to pick \u2018em up. Don\u2019t envy him, we\u2019re running late. Hope he\u2019s got someplace dry to wait.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright. Cargo rate is-ah, there we go, thanks. Surprised they don\u2019t send you with. I know passenger fare\u2019s pricier, but the foundry\u2019s not worried about somebody intercepting the cargo?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou mean are we worried about somebody interfering with a large and regular trade between two established merchant houses?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026fair point. Alright, boys, we all ready? One, two, and PUSH!\u201d<br /> <br /> With another lurch, the wagon rolls backwards and up a brief slope before banging into something metal that echoes loudly. The impact rattles through your white-clenched fingers and down into the bones of your elbows. You see wet wooden boards below you: the floor of an industrial pulley-cart. A gate shuts, the world lurches slightly as the cart starts moving and the wagon rolls a little bit along the floor of the pulley cart\u2026and you\u2019re moving!<br /> <br /> You wait another minute to be sure, and drop to the floor of the pulley-cart, groaning quietly. Gingerly, you stretch out your arms and legs, trying to work out the knots from staying still and tense for so long. You roll out from under the wagon and into a crouch-carefully, you poke your head above the railing of the pulley-cart. There are several stops between here and your destination, and if caught at any of them it\u2019ll be bad. The pulley-cart operator is over at the front of the cart in a metal cage with some levers, and he\u2019s way too busy watching the line ahead of him to make sure the cart doesn\u2019t slam into him to notice you\u2026but when you\u2019re stopped, he might look around. Stowaways tend to get beaten pretty badly if they can\u2019t pay their fare, and sometimes they end up having to pay in teeth or fingers (which have a low market value, so it\u2019s usually a lot of them!) so you usually don\u2019t take the pulley car. It\u2019s nice! It\u2019s slow and steady. You lie back down on the floor, deciding it\u2019s safer to hide under the wagon than inside it-they\u2019re more likely to check it for contraband goods than they are to search under it.<br /> <br /> You relax and try not to think about how hungry you are for about an hour. Several times the driver stops the cart to avoid running to carts ahead of you on the line whose passengers have paid to get out along the line. Several times you stop at the big stations, and those times you cling once again to the bottom of the wagon to make sure nobody spots you. Mostly, though, you relax and enjoy the ride. Also, you grab a spearhead and tie it to your forearm with some of your twine so you can hide it inside your sleeve. You've seen Rat hide his knife like that, he says it's what the boys who are in the Sluice Gang do.<br /> <br /> Finally, the cart passes through a neighborhood you recognize-it\u2019s in the northern part of the Players\u2019 District. You hop the railing and roll.<br /> Ouch. The roads here are cobblestone, and that cart was moving faster than it felt like. Still\u2026nothing broken. Somebody in one of the pulley carts behind you yells, but by then you\u2019ve dashed down an alley and come out the other side.<br /> <br /> You melt into the fringes of the crowd, staying away from the wide roads where important people are driving carts and carriages. The Players\u2019 District is a lot of fun normally, with fire jugglers and sword eaters and speardancers and acrobats on stilts\u2026but today it\u2019s pouring rain, the crowds are thin, and only the performers who are a little bit desperate are out in the rain, along with stalls selling masks and makeup and other costumed finery. You consider snatching something gaudy to sell later, or maybe something warm to bring back to your nest\u2026but you decide against it. Bad idea to show up at the temple asking for food with stolen goods. You can always nab something on the way back home.<br /> <br /> Finally, after another hour of walking, you arrive at the Immaculate Temple. It\u2019s huge, with high walls and big wooden gates. The Immaculates are a little weird-unlike all the other temples, they refuse to put up statues of their gods, so the place seems\u2026empty, almost. Stern might be the word for it. The other temples all seem happy or somber or festive or dangerous, depending on what their god looks like out front. The Immaculate Temple just always seems really <i>serious</i> to you.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a line in front of the gate. Lots of beggars like you, standing in the rain waiting for rice. The line is moving pretty slowly. Every minute or so somebody comes back out the gate with a hearty rice ball in his hands. Most of them are stuffing their faces on the way out in the hopes nobody will decide to just mug them rather than waiting in line.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s late afternoon. They\u2019re probably not going to stop serving food for another hour or two\u2026but that is a long line. There\u2019s a chance you might not get your turn before they close the gates at dusk. What are you going to do?<br /> <br /> <b>The Right Thing:</b> Get in line and wait your turn for food patiently with the others, and offer your thanks to the Monks and short prayer to the Dragons like everybody else is doing.<br /> <br /> <b>The Smart Thing:</b> See if you can find someone you know in line and join them or, failing that, see if you can make new friends quickly-cutting in line is super rude, but you can spin it like they were holding a spot for you.<br /> <br /> <b>The Strong Thing:</b> You\u2019re here for food, not to get bored and then lectured. It looks like you could skip the line, skip the monks, and just steal a rice ball from someone leaving the monastery. You now have a blade, it'd be simple to mug somebody.<br /> <br /> <b>The Clever Thing:</b> At the rate that line is moving, they might close up before you get in and get your rice! But the monks don\u2019t just serve food, they also treat the sick and injured. So if you can just act really really sick, they\u2019ll probably take you inside and give you food! Maybe even some medicine you can pretend to eat and then sell once you\u2019re back out!<br /> <br /> <b>The Cruel Thing:</b> You need to get the line shorter to make sure you get your turn. All you have to do is spread the rumor they\u2019re also giving out rice on the Monastery\u2019s West Gate, and the line there is much shorter! Then once people start to leave, you get in line and don\u2019t have to worry about the rice running out.<br /> <br /> <b>The Brave Thing:</b> It\u2019s not fair of the monks to keep all that food inside and close the doors at dusk! There\u2019s a lot of people here! Why are we all waiting in line when we could storm the gates and take ALL the rice? You should try to start a riot!<br /> <br /> <b>The Wise Thing:</b> The Immaculate Monks always seem to have plenty of rice, and their temple is big and rich and gets lots of donations. It\u2019s not like you get to eat much meat anyway, and you have no idea why the older kids are all so interested in sex\u2026you should try to become an Immaculate Monk! Wait your turn patiently and ask the monk who is serving food about it when you get inside.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sneaky Thing:</b> The Immaculate Monks always seem to have plenty of rice, and their temple is big and rich and gets lots of donations. Skip the line, scout the place out, and come nightfall you can climb the wall and steal some food. And you can use your spearhead to chip some of those fancy gold inlays off their walls, maybe a gemstone or two off one of their altars...<br /> <br /> <b>The Wyld Thing:</b> You have a better idea!<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <u><b>Inventory:</b></u><ul><li>Tattered Rags</li> <li>Fishhooks (3)</li> <li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Pile of Stolen Clothes (mostly rags)</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Spearhead (Mechanically, it's a knife. If you can find a broomhandle and a couple nails, though, you'll have a real spear.)</li> </ul><br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <u><b>You Have Gained:</b></u><br /> <u><b>Attributes: (4/13 Allocated)</b></u><br /> Dexterity +1 (Climbing Down Slippery Wall), Strength +1 (Climbing Down Slippery Wall), Stamina +1 (Clinging unmoving to the undercarriage for an hour), Manipulation +1 (Dealing with suspicious Porter)<br /> <u><b>Abilities: (7/28 Allocated)</b></u><br /> Athletics +1 (Climbing Down Slippery Wall)<br /> Occult +1 (Choosing to get food at the Immaculate Temple rather than get food closer to home)<br /> Bureaucracy +1 (Knowing the comings and goings of goods at the Blackhand Foundry)<br /> Socialize +1 (Dealing with suspicious porter)<br /> Stealth +1 (Hiding Under the Wagon)<br /> Larceny +1 (Stealing a Spearhead)<br /> Craft (Weaving) +1 (Making Twine Armband for Spearhead)<br /> <u><b>Specialties: (0/4 Allocated)</b></u>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 08-25-2016, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T10:46:52-07:00","id":957704,"title":"","content":"Three meals a day! Let's become a monk! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ((Never mind the fasting... and the beatings*... for your own good of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ))<br /> <br /> (( *also known as Martial Arts Lessons))<br /> <br /> My second choice is the Smart thing, if the Wise thing isn't winning. Third choice is Clever thing if Wise/Smart Fails. <br /> <br /> In summary:<br /> <br /> 1. Wise<br /> 2. Smart<br /> 3. Clever","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 08-25-2016, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:58:48-07:00","id":957754,"title":"","content":"I doubt The Wise Thing would work out - if any desperate soul off the street could become a monk, most of them would. Also, I don't think we're going to invalidate the title of the quest 4 posts in... but I suppose it does no harm to ask.<br /> <br /> &gt;Start off with The Wise/Right Thing, but switch over to The Sneaky Thing the moment you see them start turning people away.<br /> <br /> (We are patient, but opportunistic!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 08-25-2016, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T12:10:16-07:00","id":957765,"title":"","content":"It should be noted that we are currently in Character Generation. Choices you make will spend your starting points to build your character. Once you've used Stealth to solve a problem three times, you'll be maxed out...and if you keep using Stealth to solve the problem, I'll be spending out of your Bonus Points to raise your Stealth score beyond three, for example.<br /> <br /> So you may wish to consider what sort of character you want to play in the future when you are considering how to deal with your present situation. These are formative experiences.<br /> <br /> Once you're fully statted up, this Quest will begin in <i>earnest</i>, but the Character Gen/Prologue section of the story is going to take a while. Also, once you're fully statted up, I'll be ROLLING to see whether you succeed at the actions you suggest instead of just running things by narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T12:23:27-07:00","id":957773,"title":"","content":"Do The Wise Thing, but if they close the gates before we can get a turn then try The Sneaky Thing.<br /> If we don't get inside in time it might just be a sign from the dragons that monkhood isn't for us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T13:18:46-07:00","id":957803,"title":"","content":"The Wise Thing! It would be a shame to bite the hand that fed us - being in the Sluice Gang when we grow up wouldn't be the worst thing in the world, but being a monk would be better. Food and clothing in return for a hard life? Well, we've already got the hard life, so it's a step up.<br /> <br /> If they turn us away, of course we can just thank them and be on our way (The Good Thing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T13:45:03-07:00","id":957824,"title":"","content":"All hail the dragons and boo to sex! <b>Wise thing</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11315-remulader","name":"Remulader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11315_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T15:45:48-07:00","id":957896,"title":"","content":"The wise way: People always say that being a monk is a harsh life. But they have beds and food. I don't. Joining up might not be the worst idea. Besides. I love their stories and what would be bad about learning more about the stories and the dragons and their chosen? We might even get a glimpse of the enlightened!<br /> <br /> Else: HTe good thing. Biting the hand that feeds you is a good way to get beaten like a bad dog. The monks are very good at beating people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11676-exewon","name":"exewon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T19:58:19-07:00","id":958013,"title":"","content":"Clever, Right, Wise, Sneaky (but only taking food; gold and gems are too likely to draw attention). Faking sick isn't too hard when you're relatively scrawny and already sore, and clearly a part of a class known for frequent illness. We're not out to hurt people here, after all. If the Clever Thing fails, the Right thing might work. If that fails, try the Wise thing - at the worst, they'll turn you down. If you're lucky, you might get a couple days' food and shelter during the testing for admission. And if they do turn you down, you can try to filch something, but that's pretty much a desperation move. Immaculate monks are very hard on thieves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T14:33:52-07:00","id":958424,"title":"","content":"You join the back of the line. You wait.<br /> <br /> Every now and then, the line shuffles forward.<br /> <br /> Your stomach growls. The people ahead of you in line chatter-it\u2019s a mother and her two children, both only about four or five years old. They keep whining about how slow the line is, and she keeps shushing them and telling them to be grateful it\u2019s raining, otherwise the line would be longer.<br /> <br /> Speaking of rain, you are cold. And wet. And the rain keeps pushing your hair down into your eyes so you have to wipe it away. You wish you had an umbrella or something. A couple of the people ahead of you in live have beat up old parasols to keep the rain off, and one guy has a heavy coat he\u2019s got draped over his head.<br /> <br /> You wait.<br /> <br /> The line shuffles forward, a little bit at a time. You consider again how easy it would be to just take your new knife and force someone to give you a rice ball after they leave\u2026but no. You\u2019ve had your food stolen before, you\u2019d feel guilty\u2026and perhaps more importantly, you\u2019re not sure you could get away with it. Now you\u2019ve been in line bored for a while, you notice that this area appears to have some guardians-there are a couple local mercenaries idling under awnings out of the rain, and a couple monks chatting with them. Probably not a good place to start something.<br /> <br /> The line shuffles forward. Your stomach growls. The interminable wait continues.<br /> <br /> Finally, after what seems like hours, you reach the gates of the monastery. The sun is low in the West and the shadows are growing longer. The sky is a strange dull yellow-orange color, as the brilliant sunset on the other side waddles its way through heavy rainclouds and thick Nexus smog. You enter the gates of the Immaculate Monastery.<br /> <br /> Inside, there is a large courtyard and a couple of tables. Large red-orange umbrellas shield huge pots of sticky swamp rice from the pouring rain, and two old bald men and a middle aged bald woman in Immaculate robes are handing out rice balls. There\u2019s still a lot of courtyard to cross, but you\u2019re inside the Gates! They\u2019re probably not going to kick you out now without feeding you!<br /> <br /> The line is still moving slowly, so you take in your surroundings. Past the tables are the buildings of the Immaculate Temple. There are still no statues, but the Temple is adorned with gleaming bronze and gold inlays that remind you of shimmering scales, and you can make out the bright colors of tapestries inside. There are several large trees surrounding the courtyard close to the walls that\u2019d make climbing in or out pretty easy. There are also some well-trimmed bushes that\u2019d be good for hiding. As you wait in line, you watch a young monk trimming them with a pair of clippers. There are about a dozen young men and women in the courtyard sitting cross-legged in the rain meditating in front of the temple. Their heads aren\u2019t shaved.<br /> <br /> You arrive at the table where the food is being handed out. All this time waiting in line you\u2019ve been thinking, and now you\u2019re in front of them you decide to ask. As you reach the middle aged bald woman you thank her for the food and offer a prayer to the Dragons\u2026and then ask her a question.<br /> <br /> \u201cPardon me, Ma\u2019am, but\u2026how do I become an Immaculate Monk like you?\u201d<br /> <br /> She gives you a big smile (ignoring the frustrated groans of the old woman behind you in line) and puts a rice ball in your hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not easy,\u201d she tells you. \u201cIt\u2019s a long and hard road, and most give up on it. What makes you want to become a monk?\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>What do you tell her?</b><br /> <br /> <b>Lie:</b> \u201cSextes Jylis and the monks is the only ones who ever really looked out for me. The Dragons are the only family I\u2019ve got.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Truth: </b>\u201cI already never get to eat any meat, and sex is dumb. And you folks seem to eat pretty well, and your temple is all rich and fancy.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Truth:</b> &quot;It seems like a better life than being a beggar.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Truth:</b> &quot;It seems like a better life than being a prostitute.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Truth:</b> &quot;It seems like a better life than being a thief.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Lie:</b> &quot;It seems like a better life than being a thief.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Lie:</b> \u201cI really want to help people, but I can\u2019t afford to do anything for anyone. Becoming a monk seems like a way to be able to help people. Like giving out rice!\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Truth:</b> \u201cI really like coming to weekly sermons and hearing stories about the Dragons, I love when they read out of the Immaculate Texts to us! I want to learn to read them for myself!\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Lie:</b> \u201cMy dad got killed when the river flooded last year. But I heard you Monks beat up the river god and stopped the flood and saved everyone!\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Truth:</b> \u201cMy dad got killed when the river flooded last year. But I heard you Monks beat up the river god! I wanna be able to beat up gods and control the weather!\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Lie:</b> \u201cAunt Dwi is real mean and beats me and makes me work at her brothel. But if I stay here at the Monastery, I\u2019ll be safe!\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Truth:</b> \u201cI..I don\u2019t think I\u2019m good enough to be anything else.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Truth:</b> \u201cMom died of the Black Lung three years ago, and I don\u2019t really have anywhere else to go.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Truth:</b> \u201cI want to learn martial arts! Wo-Pah!<br /> <br /> <b>Lie:</b> \u201cI need help with my meditation. Going without food and suffering is supposed to make your more enlightened, but it just makes me tired and hungry. I\u2019m never going to achieve enlightenment like this!\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Truth:</b> \u201cIf I\u2019m in training to become a monk I\u2019ll get food and a dry place to sleep and learn to read and write and treat the sick and do martial arts! Even if I change my mind in a couple years, I can use those skills to get a <i>real </i>job!\u201d<br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <u><b>Inventory:</b></u><ul><li>Tattered Rags</li> <li>Fishhooks (3)</li> <li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Pile of Stolen Clothes (mostly rags)</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Spearhead</li> <li>A Rice Ball</li> </ul><br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <u><b>You Have Gained:</b></u><br /> <u><b>Attributes: (6/13 Allocated)</b></u><br /> Stamina +1 (Waiting patiently in line while starving)<br /> Perception +1 (Casing the joint while waiting in line)<br /> <u><b>Abilities: (11/28 Allocated)</b></u><br /> Resistance +1 (Waiting patiently in line while starving)<br /> Integrity +1 (Choosing patience and wisdom)<br /> Larceny +1 (Casing the joint while waiting in line)<br /> Awareness +1 (Casing the joint while waiting in line)<br /> <u><b>Specialties: (0/4 Allocated)</b></u>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 08-26-2016, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T14:46:58-07:00","id":958432,"title":"","content":"(First you need to impress the monk and lies are always more impressive than the truth)<br /> <br /> \u201cI need help with my meditation. Going without food and suffering is supposed to make your more enlightened, but it just makes me tired and hungry. I\u2019m never going to achieve enlightenment like this!\u201d<br /> <br /> (and when that doesn't work, try honesty)<br /> <br /> &quot;It seems like a better life than being a thief.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u201cI already never get to eat any meat, and sex is dumb. And you folks seem to eat pretty well, and your temple is all rich and fancy.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Maybe too much honesty. When that doesn't work, try the truth)<br /> <br /> &quot;My dad got killed when the river flooded last year. Mom died of the Black Lung three years ago. I really like coming to weekly sermons and hearing stories about the Dragons, I love when they read out of the Immaculate Texts to us!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;and I don\u2019t really have anywhere else to go&quot;<br /> <br /> ((If this actually works, the Monks will be singing &quot;<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s-VRyQprlu8\" target=\"_blank\">Maria</a>&quot; in a few years.))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":".  Can't believe I forgot the stories! They are the best parts! 08-26-2016, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T15:00:39-07:00","id":958437,"title":"","content":"<b>Truth: </b>&quot;It seems like a better life than being a thief.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T15:06:27-07:00","id":958441,"title":"","content":"<b>Truth:</b> &quot;It seems like a better life than being a beggar.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Truth:</b> &quot;It seems like a better life than being a prostitute.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Truth:</b> &quot;It seems like a better life than being a thief.&quot;<br /> <br /> All three of these really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T18:51:56-07:00","id":958551,"title":"","content":"<b>Truth:</b> &quot;It seems like a better life than being a beggar.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Truth:</b> &quot;It seems like a better life than being a thief.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Truth:</b> &quot;It seems like a better life than being a prostitute.&quot;<br /> <br /> These three. Same as BadassOverlord, but switching the order slightly. Also, I just want to say that I'm really enjoying how you (Wise Old Guru) are in no rush to give us a gender. I presume we'll get one eventually, but for now it's not relevant, so it hasn't come up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9510,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","user":"BlueWinds","date":". 08-26-2016, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T19:10:18-07:00","id":958558,"title":"","content":"Lying to an Immaculate's pretty chancy. Better to play it straight\u2026 mostly. Some noble-sounding stuff, some practical stuff. \u201cMom died of the Black Lung three years ago, and I don\u2019t really have anywhere else to go. And, yeah, I want to learn martial arts and keep gods in line so they don't kill people like they killed my dad. And I like your stories, and enlightenment sounds really good, but I got no idea how to get there. Going without food and suffering is supposed to make you more enlightened, but it just makes me tired and hungry. I\u2019m never going to achieve enlightenment like this! And if I\u2019m in training to become a monk I\u2019ll get food and a dry place to sleep and learn to read and write and treat the sick and do martial arts! Even if I change my mind in a couple years, or I just can't cut it, I can use those skills to get a real job, instead of winding up a beggar or a thief or a whore. Or worse.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 08-27-2016, 12:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T20:42:15-07:00","id":958590,"title":"","content":"I like some combination of these two:<br /> <b>Truth:</b> \u201cI really like coming to weekly sermons and hearing stories about the Dragons, I love when they read out of the Immaculate Texts to us! I want to learn to read them for myself!\u201d<br /> <b>Truth:</b> \u201cIf I\u2019m in training to become a monk I\u2019ll get food and a dry place to sleep and learn to read and write and treat the sick and do martial arts! Even if I change my mind in a couple years, I can use those skills to get a <i>real </i>job!\u201d<br /> <br /> We know being a monk isn't an easy life, but an easy life was never on the table for us anyways. But these are the things we admire most about the immaculates, the things that excite us and make it seem like something worth being: wisdom, knowledge, strength, and a community that cares for it's members. And maybe, just maybe, with a little bit of our slowly budding wisdom we can manage to choke off that last bit before we imply that being a monk isn't a real job?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T21:24:51-07:00","id":958600,"title":"","content":"My version puts &quot;real job&quot; in contrast to &quot;thief, beggar or whore,&quot; so I'm not making &quot;monk&quot; sound like &quot;not a real job.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T20:24:41-07:00","id":959046,"title":"","content":"You take a deep breath.<br /> <br /> \u201cMom died of the Black Lung three years ago, and I don\u2019t really have anywhere else to go. And, yeah, I want to learn martial arts and keep gods in line so they don't kill people like they killed my dad. And I like your stories, and enlightenment sounds really good, but I got no idea how to get there. Going without food and suffering is supposed to make you more enlightened, but it just makes me tired and hungry. I\u2019m never going to achieve enlightenment like this! And if I\u2019m in training to become a monk I\u2019ll get food and a dry place to sleep and learn to read and write and treat the sick and do martial arts! Even if I change my mind in a couple years, or I just can't cut it, I can use those skills to get a real job, instead of winding up a beggar or a thief or a whore. Or worse!&quot;<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, shut it,\u201d the old woman behind you growls, shoving you so you splash down into the mud and grabbing a rice ball. \u201cSun\u2019s getting low and people back here\u2019s gotta eat! Get out of the way!\u201d There are grumbles of agreement from the people behind you in line.<br /> <br /> The middle aged monk you were speaking to chuckles and comes out from behind the table. A young bald man steps in from behind her to take her place handing out rice. She pulls you to your feet and walks you away from the line.<br /> <br /> \u201cWorking in solitude and striving to surpass your lot in life, you draw away from the perfection of the Elemental Dragons. Only by working together and accepting their present incarnations,\u201d and here she gestures at the people who were in line behind you, \u201ccan all beings mimic the Elemental Dragons and so approach their perfection. That is the wisdom of the Third Noble Insight.\u201d<br /> <br /> You nod your head in what you hope is an approximation of understanding. \u201cSee, that\u2019s what I\u2019m talking about! How am I ever going to get enlightened like you without somebody to teach me?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shakes her head. \u201cDon\u2019t worry about achieving enlightenment, child. It takes many lifetimes. Instead, strive to help others. You seek to better your station in life by becoming a monk-you seek food and shelter and knowledge and power. But the way of the Dragons is not about improving your lot in life, or even improving your birth in the next life. It is about learning to serve the rightful order of Creation, about helping others. Don\u2019t assume that you must be a monk or a whore. You can be many things, even without learning. A humble street-sweeper or painter or rat-catcher can find holiness in service to others.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026so\u2026I can\u2019t become a monk?\u201d<br /> <br /> She gives you a warm smile, puts her arm on your shoulder, and walks with you ask she speaks. \u201cI never said that. If you wish to devote yourself to the Order you will need to receive permission from the monks of the Procession of the Gray. You can see the men and women here in the courtyard meditating in the rain? Some of them have been meditating there for weeks. Only a handful will be chosen. They have forsworn all worldly possessions and will leave Nexus wearing only simple robes.\u201d<br /> <br /> She gestures to her own robe and sash. It doesn\u2019t seem all that simple to you. It\u2019s a nice hemp robe with a red linen sash.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey will travel by ship to the Blessed Isle to present themselves to the Paragon of Sextes Jylis. In her courtyard they will wait without food and without sleep until she notices them and invites them to join the Order. There are thousands waiting there, in rain or snow, and many are never chosen\u2026and the Imperial City is no friendly place to foreigners who have failed to impress the Paragon of Sexted Jylis with their virtue.\u201d<br /> <br /> She frowns for a moment, lost in thought, and her hand idly goes to a scar you hadn\u2019t noticed on her arm. She closes her eyes, and then looks down at you seriously.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou should not go. It is very rare for Sextes Jylis to accept anyone as young as yourself-children are not often wise enough to understand the commitment they are making. But if you return in a few years, after you have tasted wine and red meat and love, and you still wish to become a monk, then I will be happy to recommend you to the Procession of the Gray.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s your name, then?,\u201d you ask her. \u201c I\u2019ll want to know who to ask for if I come back.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m Banked Coals,\u201d she tells you. \u201cAnd now it is time for you to go home.\u201d<br /> <br /> You realize she has led you to the front gate. \u201cBut\u2026I don\u2019t have one!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am sorry,\u201d she says. \u201cBut if you have truly gotten by for three years on your own, you are strong enough to get by for a few more. The winters are always the hardest, and you\u2019ve managed at least two. I\u2019m afraid we need to save our spare beds for the very old and the very young, and the ill who cannot care for themselves, child.\u201d<br /> <br /> You frown. \u201cWell\u2026thanks for the rice ball, anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are welcome to it. And if you truly wish to learn, please keep coming to our weekly sermons. It is good for the soul to read the Texts together\u2026and if you do ever find yourself tempted towards unworthy behavior, consider the stories of Sextes Jylis. They were a great help to me in my youth.\u201d<br /> <br /> And then you are outside the monastery. You are about to say something else to Banked Coals-but you are interrupted by a great cry from the crowd on your right. The gates are closing, and many left outside weren\u2019t able to get in and get rice in time. The monks are apologizing and telling them there will be more food tomorrow\u2026but they are closing the gates nonetheless, and there are large burly monks with staves eyeing the crowd for troublemakers.<br /> <br /> Well.<br /> <br /> At least you got your rice ball.<br /> <br /> <b>What now?</b><br /> <br /> <b>Go Give The Rice Ball Away</b>: Banked Coals speech has moved you! You\u2019re hungry, sure, but there are little kids and old people in line who didn\u2019t get fed. You can give your rice to somebody who needs it more. You\u2019ve still got a rainy muddy night ahead and some fishhooks, you can catch fish or birds, and there\u2019s always Aunt Dwi to fall back on\u2026helping someone else is what Sextes Jylis would do!<br /> <br /> <b>Scarf Your Rice Ball Down Real Quick And Get The Hell Out of Here:</b> Before somebody less noble comes and takes it away from you!<br /> <br /> <b>Start Your Stakeout:</b> Becoming a monk and getting free lodging and food every day was a bust. But you got a good look at the inside of the Temple while Banked Coals was walking you through the courtyard, and those trees look pretty climbable. If you find a good vantage point to look down into the courtyard from and see where people are moving around, you should be able to figure out what areas are less well-guarded so you can rob the temple under cover of darkness.<br /> <br /> <b>Find Someplace to Sleep</b>: It is now dusk and you\u2019re a long way from your safe nest back in the Nighthammer District. You\u2019re not going to try and rob anybody, but you\u2019re not going to try and head back home until morning. There\u2019s raptor cats and worse out in Nexus after dark!<br /> <br /> <b>Head Home:</b> This isn\u2019t your neighborhood. Back in Nighthammer at least you know all the dangers and how to avoid them. The trip back to Blackhand Foundry isn\u2019t going to be easy\u2026but it\u2019s safer to keep moving and hopefully get home in a couple hours than stay in unfamiliar territory all night.<br /> <br /> <b>Get More Food:</b> Rice ball or no, you\u2019re still hungry! Dusk is when the fish bite, so you should gather some worms and head down to the canal. Maybe if you offer one of the boatmen half of anything you catch they\u2019ll give you a ride back to Nighthammer. A few of them were friends of your father, after all\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Something Else:</b> The night is young!<br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <u><b>Inventory:</b></u><ul><li>Tattered Rags</li> <li>Fishhooks (3)</li> <li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Pile of Stolen Clothes (mostly rags)</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Spearhead</li> <li>A Rice Ball</li> </ul><br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <u><b>You Have Gained:</b></u><br /> <u><b>Attributes: (7/13 Allocated)</b></u><br /> Charisma +1 (Choosing honesty over deception)<br /> <u><b>Abilities: (13/28 Allocated)</b></u><br /> Presence +1 (Making a good speech)<br /> Socialize +1 (Making a good first impression)<br /> <u><b>Specialties: (0/4 Allocated)</b></u>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 08-27-2016, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T20:50:42-07:00","id":959062,"title":"","content":"Finding a new squat, even for the night, could be tricky even with time to work on it during the day. At dusk? No chance. Not a safe squat, anyway. Better to head back to Nighthammer. Maybe on the way, there'll be fish to caught, if one of the boatmen will let you troll from his stern for a share. That'd make a better dinner than plain rice anyway. And the wall of the squat might even work for a sort of &quot;frypan.&quot; But what to do with the rice ball? Well, Sextes Jylis did preach compassion, and a boat ride meant a good shot at better food... and that girl with the toddler should still be playing with dolls. They could use some help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T20:53:28-07:00","id":959063,"title":"","content":"Eat the rice ball and Get more food. We can't help anyone if we starve to death. Bargain with our father's old freinds and get a ride to our regular sleeping spot.<br /> <br /> At we got some food in our belly, time to think about the Monks words and how we can help people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T21:16:32-07:00","id":959075,"title":"","content":"&gt;Give Rice Ball Away to the smallest child you see in line.<br /> <br /> Then Get More Food. Fish is better fare for a pre-teen anyway - we need the protein!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T22:09:34-07:00","id":959096,"title":"","content":"That lecture didn't make any sense.<br /> <br /> Go home, by boat if possible, and try to catch fish and/or worms along the way.<br /> <br /> I kinda feel bad for holding up the line... I can give most of my rice to somebody else. Or split it between two somebody elses. But I have to keep a little bit for myself in case I can't catch any fish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T05:54:41-07:00","id":959191,"title":"","content":"Welp, the Immaculate Philosophy is balderdash, so lets eat this riceball and begin the heist!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T06:02:16-07:00","id":959192,"title":"","content":"<b>Give The Rice Ball Away.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T09:16:33-07:00","id":959297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=959096#post959096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That lecture didn't make any sense.<br /> <br /> Go home, by boat if possible, and try to catch fish and/or worms along the way.<br /> <br /> I kinda feel bad for holding up the line... I can give most of my rice to somebody else. Or split it between two somebody elses. But I have to keep a little bit for myself in case I can't catch any fish.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Give half of the rice ball away, go home by boat, try and fish while going home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T16:15:02-07:00","id":959552,"title":"","content":"Meditating outside in the rain without eating obviously makes people soft in the head. Banked Coals seems nice enough, but her advice is pure crazy.<br /> <br /> Forget about being a monk. <b>Eat the rice ball</b> before anybody tries to take it from us, then let's go fishing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T08:26:32-07:00","id":967938,"title":"","content":"Is there any chance for this Quest to continue? I was enjoying it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T13:05:07-07:00","id":968094,"title":"","content":"It's gonna be slow (for the same reasons Boot is slow to update these days) and not particularly steady. But this quest will continue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:28:08-07:00","id":968181,"title":"","content":"Glad to hear that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:29:10-07:00","id":969932,"title":"","content":"Eat Rice Ball: 3<br /> Give Rice Away: 2<br /> Give Half Rice Ball Away: 2<br /> Heist: 1<br /> Boat Ride: 2<br /> Fishing: Yes<br /> <br /> You look at the rapidly cooling, increasingly damp rice ball in your hands. You look over at the line. Banked Coals\u2019 words about asking what Sextes Jylis would do echo in your head\u2026you take a step towards the line, which is now breaking into a wave of disappointed and angry people before the gates of the monastery.<br /> <br /> Then your stomach growls again, and you take a step back. You really, really want to eat this rice ball. You really, really want to do the right thing and give it away. You think about trying to do both-giving away half and keeping half\u2026but it\u2019s not a very big rice ball.<br /> <br /> You eat it. You feel guilty, and you feel angry for feeling guilty because it\u2019s easy for Banked Coals to talk about doing what Sextes Jylis would do when she\u2019s on the inside of the closed gates with plenty of rice to eat, but dammit, you still feel bad for not being able to feed anyone else. It makes you feel\u2026weak.<br /> <br /> No, <i>screw </i>this! You are going <i>home</i>, and you are going to get some food of your <i>own </i>on the way. You leave the crowd behind you, shouting as politely as they can at the monks inside the gates in the hopes of more food, and you head for the canal. As you get closer to the water, you can make out the sounds of the canal over the dull pounding of the gray rain. There\u2019s a low horn blast from one of the larger rafts, warning smaller craft of its location to prevent collisions in the fading light and heavy rain. The canal boatmen, without such luxuries, make do with covered lanterns and yelling.<br /> <br /> You stop a couple blocks short of the canal to see if you can catch some bait. The road here is cobbled stone, but by the side of the road there\u2019s some muddy dirt and grass growing along the edges of the buildings, where the eaves of the building are pouring waterfalls down onto the street. A little bit of searching quickly finds you six fat worms wriggling along the cobblestones to escape drowning. You shove them in your pocket and head for the canal, tying some twine to one of your fishhooks as you go.<br /> <br /> At the docks, it\u2019s not at all hard to find a ride: the storm has most sensible boatmen moored at the docks. There aren\u2019t too many people out today asking for open air canal rides on an evening like this, so many have called it a night and headed to some warm dry tavern to spend their earnings. There\u2019s a few still out, though: Nexus has plenty of commuters who live in one district and work in another, and pay a boatman to ferry them up and down the canals. Lots of these are workers in the Nighthammer district-the various foundries and ironworks pay well enough, and if your pay is good enough to afford anything else you don\u2019t generally decide to live with Nighthammer\u2019s late night clanging and choking black fogs.<br /> <br /> There, in the big black wide-rimmed hat with the white koi painted on it! That\u2019s Grinning Eel, and old friend of your father\u2019s. You never knew your father that well, but you have some faint memories of him dropping in from time to time with fish or coin to help Mother out. Once or twice Eel came with him. Grinning Eel is a grumpy old man\u2026but he\u2019s very fond of seafood.<br /> <br /> \u201cEel!\u201d You shout as you come down the docks. \u201cCan I get a ride to Nighthammer?\u201d<br /> <br /> He looks up, rain pouring off the rims of his hat, and squints. \u201cWell I\u2019ll be damned. How\u2019s it going, kid? Haven\u2019t seen you since I gave you that ride home after Calibration! Sure, I think I can make it over to Nighthammer for you. You\u2019ve gotten bigger. You got coin?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI have six worms and a fishing line, Eel. Figured I could catch you dinner and call it even.\u201d<br /> <br /> Eel frowns at you, his grey moustache twitching in distaste. \u201cAnd if you don\u2019t catch anything?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re not getting any paying fares here today anyway. If you give me a ride to Nighthammer, you might at least be able to catch some commuters on the way back who missed their regular boat.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah\u2026or I could get wrecked halfway there trying to go against the Nighthammer traffic in the dark. In the rain. For no pay.\u201d<br /> <br /> The old man seems like he wants to help you, but he\u2019s against giving out free rides on principle. What tack should you take here?<br /> ----<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re not going to get wrecked, Eel, you\u2019ve been doing this forever! You know that canal like the back of your hand. Give me a ride, it doesn\u2019t cost you anything and we might both get a free dinner out of it.\u201d (+Charisma, +Larceny, +Survival, Contacts: Nexus Boatmen)<br /> <br /> \u201cEel\u2026I don\u2019t like asking for help, but you and Father were friends, which means you\u2019re kind of the closest thing I\u2019ve got to family. If you don\u2019t give me a ride, I gotta take the rooftop roads by night in the rain, and even if I don\u2019t slip and fall I hear there\u2019s a raptor cat on the loose. Can\u2019t you help me out?\u201d (+Charisma, +Socialize, +Survival, Ally: Grinning Eel)<br /> <br /> \u201cGrinning Eel, I get that you\u2019ve got to make a living, but you\u2019re not doing that sitting here in the rain without a fare anyway. No money and a chance of fish is better than no money and no fish.\u201d (+Manipulation, +Bureaucracy, +Socialize)<br /> <br /> \u201cEel\u2026you\u2019re not getting any younger, and like you say wrecks happen in the canal all the time. Wouldn\u2019t you like to be able to tell the Dragons that you helped out a hungry kid just trying to get home on a rainy night? Maybe come back as something better in your next life?\u201d (+Manipulation, +Occult, +Socialize)<br /> <br /> \u201cYou and my Father were friends, old man. Dragons know he wasn\u2019t the most reliable guy, but he paid his debts, and so will I. If I don\u2019t catch anything tonight, I\u2019ll catch something tomorrow, or the next day, and it\u2019s yours.\u201d (+Manipulation, +Presence, +Bureaucracy)<br /> <br /> \u201cYou knew my Father, Eel. He was a deadbeat who gambled away all his money and died in debt. Mother always told me to be better than him, and I mean to do that. If I tell you I\u2019m going to give you a fish, then today or tomorrow or the next day, I\u2019m going to catch a fish and give it to you. I pay my debts.\u201d (+Charisma, +Integrity, +Presence)<br /> <br /> \u201cEel. It\u2019s evening. It\u2019s raining. That\u2019s when the fish bite! We\u2019re not gonna catch anything if we stay here yammering, but I bet on a day like today we can catch enough to sell what we can\u2019t eat at the market, if you really want coin so bad. Let\u2019s go!\u201d (+Charisma, +Survival, +Bureaucracy)<br /> <br /> \u201cEel\u2026you\u2019re right. I <i>have </i>gotten bigger since last time you saw me. I\u2019m big enough to work now, and you\u2019re getting older. You've got no customers right now, you're not busy. Give me a ride, show me how to steer and pole the boat, and if I\u2019m any good maybe in a few months you can relax in a dry tavern while I take the rainy nights. My Father was a boatman, it's a good trade, and you don't have any kids of your own to give the boat to when you retire, right?\u201d (+Manipulation, +Sail, +Bureaucracy, Ally: Grinning Eel)<br /> <br /> \u201cEel\u2026you\u2019re right. I <i>have </i>gotten bigger since last time you saw me. Now shut it and give me a <i>ride</i>, old man, or I <i>take </i>your boat and use <i>you </i>as fish bait.\u201d You pull out your knife and point it threateningly. (+Charisma, +Presence, +Melee)<br /> <br /> \u201cEel\u2026you\u2019re right. I <i>have </i>gotten bigger since last time you saw me. Perhaps if I can\u2019t catch any <i>fish </i>there\u2019s\u2026something <i>else </i>I can help you with?\u201d (+Appearance, +Socialize, +Performance)<br /> <br /> Something Else (+?)<br /> <br /> ************************************************** **************************************<br /> <u><b>Inventory:</b></u><ul><li>Tattered Rags</li> <li>Fishhooks (2)</li> <li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Improvised Fishing Line w/hook</li> <li>6 Large Earthworms</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Pile of Stolen Clothes (mostly rags)</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Steel spearhead (six-inch knife blade with a clumsy handle)</li> </ul><br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <u><b>You Have Gained:</b></u><br /> <u><b>Attributes: (7/13 Allocated)</b></u><br /> <br /> <u><b>Abilities: (15/28 Allocated)</b></u><br /> Survival 1 (Choosing to go fishing)<br /> Craft (Weaving) 2 (Tying a good knot on that improvised fishing line.)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Specialties: (0/4 Allocated)</b></u><br /> <br /> <u><b>Merits: (0/7 Allocated)</b></u>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 09-15-2016, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:52:11-07:00","id":969950,"title":"","content":"\u201cEel\u2026you\u2019re right. I <i>have </i>gotten bigger since last time you saw me. I\u2019m big enough to work now, and you\u2019re getting older. You've got no customers right now, you're not busy. Give me a ride, show me how to steer and pole the boat, and if I\u2019m any good maybe in a few months you can relax in a dry tavern while I take the rainy nights. My Father was a boatman, it's a good trade, and you don't have any kids of your own to give the boat to when you retire, right?\u201d (+Manipulation, +Sail, +Bureaucracy, Ally: Grinning Eel)<br /> <br /> Being Hungry sucks. Having a trade will help with keeping our belly full.<br /> <br /> (Is there a complete character sheet somewhere?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 09-15-2016, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:58:20-07:00","id":969958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=969950#post969950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cEel\u2026you\u2019re right. I <i>have </i>gotten bigger since last time you saw me. I\u2019m big enough to work now, and you\u2019re getting older. You've got no customers right now, you're not busy. Give me a ride, show me how to steer and pole the boat, and if I\u2019m any good maybe in a few months you can relax in a dry tavern while I take the rainy nights. My Father was a boatman, it's a good trade, and you don't have any kids of your own to give the boat to when you retire, right?\u201d (+Manipulation, +Sail, +Bureaucracy, Ally: Grinning Eel)<br /> <br /> Being Hungry sucks. Having a trade will help with keeping our belly full.<br /> <br /> (Is there a complete character sheet somewhere?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded, though again I doubt we can escape poverty that easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:59:06-07:00","id":969960,"title":"","content":"\u201cYou\u2019re not going to get wrecked, Eel, you\u2019ve been doing this forever! You know that canal like the back of your hand. Give me a ride, it doesn\u2019t cost you anything and we might both get a free dinner out of it. And with a teeny bit of luck, you'll find some other passengers on the way. You know there's alway people missing their regular boat.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:06:46-07:00","id":969966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=969958#post969958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seconded, though again I doubt we can escape poverty that easily.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We will still be living on the streets, but we may have a small source of income for food. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ((I imagine our nameless urchin is going to constantly try to improve his status. Which is against the immaculate values, but the Dragons never had to go without food has often as the urchin has. ))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:19:53-07:00","id":969975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=969932#post969932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cEel\u2026you\u2019re right. I <i>have </i>gotten bigger since last time you saw me. I\u2019m big enough to work now, and you\u2019re getting older. You've got no customers right now, you're not busy. Give me a ride, show me how to steer and pole the boat, and if I\u2019m any good maybe in a few months you can relax in a dry tavern while I take the rainy nights. My Father was a boatman, it's a good trade, and you don't have any kids of your own to give the boat to when you retire, right?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>first choice, though I question the existence of 'retirement' for poor folks in the 2nd Age<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=969932#post969932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cYou knew my Father, Eel. He was a deadbeat who gambled away all his money and died in debt. Mother always told me to be better than him, and I mean to do that. If I tell you I\u2019m going to give you a fish, then today or tomorrow or the next day, I\u2019m going to catch a fish and give it to you. I pay my debts.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>second choice<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=969932#post969932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cEel\u2026I don\u2019t like asking for help, but you and Father were friends, which means you\u2019re kind of the closest thing I\u2019ve got to family. If you don\u2019t give me a ride, I gotta take the rooftop roads by night in the rain, and even if I don\u2019t slip and fall I hear there\u2019s a raptor cat on the loose. Can\u2019t you help me out?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>third choice<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=969966#post969966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">((I imagine our nameless urchin is going to constantly try to improve his status. Which is against the immaculate values, but the Dragons never had to go without food has often as the urchin has. ))</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dragons' advice sounds like &quot;accept your lot of starving to death in the gutter&quot; and also &quot;you can't become a monk unless you stop wanting to be one.&quot; The first part is unacceptable and the second part is nonsense to a 10-year-old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-15-2016, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T11:13:04-07:00","id":970054,"title":"","content":"\u201cEel\u2026you\u2019re right. I <i>have </i>gotten bigger since last time you saw me. I\u2019m big enough to work now, and you\u2019re getting older. You've got no customers right now, you're not busy. Give me a ride, show me how to steer and pole the boat, and if I\u2019m any good maybe in a few months you can relax in a dry tavern while I take the rainy nights. My Father was a boatman, it's a good trade, and you don't have any kids of your own to give the boat to when you retire, right?\u201d (+Manipulation, +Sail, +Bureaucracy, Ally: Grinning Eel)<br /> <br /> Let'sget a job!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:10:54-07:00","id":970203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=969960#post969960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cYou\u2019re not going to get wrecked, Eel, you\u2019ve been doing this forever! You know that canal like the back of your hand. Give me a ride, it doesn\u2019t cost you anything and we might both get a free dinner out of it. And with a teeny bit of luck, you'll find some other passengers on the way. You know there's alway people missing their regular boat.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seconding this one here. We just want sleep, dryness and dinner right now. We've already been turned down by the monks - cold and hungry and in inner turmoil (&quot;what does all that stuff she said mean...&quot;) isn't the time for grubbing after an apprenticeship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9510,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","user":"BlueWinds","date":". 09-15-2016, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T15:13:13-07:00","id":970265,"title":"","content":"\u201cEel\u2026you\u2019re right. I <i>have </i>gotten bigger since last time you saw me. I\u2019m big enough to work now, and you\u2019re getting older. You've got no customers right now, you're not busy. Give me a ride, show me how to steer and pole the boat, and if I\u2019m any good maybe in a few months you can relax in a dry tavern while I take the rainy nights. My Father was a boatman, it's a good trade, and you don't have any kids of your own to give the boat to when you retire, right?\u201d (+Manipulation, +Sail, +Bureaucracy, Ally: Grinning Eel)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12278-broken25","name":"Broken25","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T16:13:22-07:00","id":970293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=969950#post969950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Is there a complete character sheet somewhere?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes...but it's just a PDF on my computer at present. Once you've spent your starting points, I'll make the charsheet public and we get get into the real meat of the adventure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:54:24-07:00","id":970483,"title":"","content":"Yay future boatman!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T07:08:59-07:00","id":970665,"title":"","content":"<b>\u201cYou knew my Father, Eel. He was a deadbeat who gambled away all his money and died in debt. Mother always told me to be better than him, and I mean to do that. If I tell you I\u2019m going to give you a fish, then today or tomorrow or the next day, I\u2019m going to catch a fish and give it to you. I pay my debts.\u201d</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T19:31:17-07:00","id":971674,"title":"","content":"Retirement Plan: 4<br /> Flattery Will Get You Home: 3<br /> HONOR! 1<br /> <br /> \u201cEel\u2026you\u2019re right. I have gotten bigger since last time you saw me. I\u2019m big enough to work now, and you\u2019re getting older. Give me a ride, show me how to steer and pole the boat, and if I\u2019m any good maybe you can retire and I take over in couple years.\u201d<br /> <br /> Eel raises an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cKid. It is raining. It is getting dark. The water is runnin\u2019 higher an\u2019 faster than I\u2019ve seen it in years. And this time of night there\u2019s gonna be heavy traffic. No way I\u2019m lettin\u2019 you steer my boat, you\u2019d get us both killed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut-\u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cShut it. Not happening. But fine, I\u2019ll give you a ride to Nighthammer. Catch me some fish. If you really wanna follow in your Daddy\u2019s footsteps, come talk to me sometime when the weather isn\u2019t shit and traffic isn\u2019t heavy and I\u2019ll see if you\u2019ve got the knack.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026thank you, Eel,\u201d you smile as you clamber into the boat.<br /> <br /> Once you\u2019re settled, Grinning Eel stands up and poles the boat away from the dock. You watch him carefully, studying his movements in the hopes you\u2019ll impress him when you take him up on that offer. It may not be as prestigious as being a monk\u2026but piloting a canal boat pays okay and seems a lot easier to break into, and nobody\u2019s making you sit in the rain studying and meditating. I mean\u2026you\u2019re still sitting in the rain and studying what Grinning Eel is doing, but at least you\u2019re going somewhere, not just staying in the same place.<br /> <br /> You reach into your pocket and pinch one of your worms to keep it from wriggling out of your wet hands as you place it on your hook. Grinning Eel lifts his lantern a bit to give you better light, then hangs it from a hook on the pole at the back of the boat. The flame gutters low and weak and sputters in the wet air, but the glass keeps it safe from the rain. You toss one end of your line into the water and loop the other end around your ankle. That way if you get a bite you can use both hands to haul it in.<br /> <br /> For a while, you wait for a fish. You spend the time watching Grinning Eel. He has a pole with a paddle on one end, and he stands at the back of the boat, peering into the gloom, cold rain pouring down the brims of his hat. Every now and then he cocks his head and adjust course a bit. You can\u2019t see more than a couple of boat lengths ahead through the rain, but Eel deftly adjust course a minute or so before each obstacle, guiding you around several mid-sized cargo rafts coming up the canal with oars. You get the impression he\u2019s doing it by ear. Closing your eyes and concentrating, you can start to make out the difference between the rhythmic slap-splash oars pulling some other boat up towards you against the current and the dull pounding of the rain. Eel doesn\u2019t steer much-the canal\u2019s current is steady and strong.<br /> <br /> You curl up against the cold rain and decide that you really need to get yourself a hat like Grinning Eel has got. It\u2019s interesting to study Eel for a while, but you soon get bored. Every now and then you\u2019ll shift to get more comfortable in the boat and the string tied to your ankle will tug gently and you\u2019ll start up, expecting a fish\u2026but nothing bites.<br /> <br /> After a time you reel in your line and find that the worm has fallen off it. You put another on the hook.<br /> <br /> \u201cTry tossin\u2019 the line over there,\u201d Eel grumbles. \u201cWhere the eaves of that building hang out over the water.\u201d<br /> <br /> You can\u2019t see any building through all the rain, but you nod and toss the hook in that direction.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlways bugs and shit falling off that roof into the water over there,\u201d Eel tells you. \u201cGood fishing spot.\u201d<br /> <br /> He\u2019s right! Not two minutes later you feel a tug at your ankle. You wait until you get a yank, then you jerk the line to set the hook. Eel puts his paddle in the water, and when the fish is tired out you haul it in hand over hand. It\u2019s not that big, but it\u2019s a fish! Eel holds the lantern out so you can see, and you smack its head hard with the flat of your \u2018knife\u2019 to stun it and then remove your hook.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood catch, kid. Just toss it in the bottom of the boat. Rain\u2019ll keep it fresh until we get there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWon\u2019t it bother your next fare if you\u2019ve got a fish flopping around under the seat?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFeh.\u201d Eel hangs the lantern back on its pole.<br /> <br /> You put another worm on the hook. \u201cThat one\u2019s your fare, Eel. Next one\u2019s mine.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFuck that. You catch another one, I get whichever is bigger, kid.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026fine.\u201d You grumble. You toss the hook back in the canal.<br /> <br /> There are several minutes of silence as you wait for another fish to bite. Then you hear splashing coming from up ahead.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright, be quiet, kid,\u201d Eel grumbles. Not like you haven\u2019t been quiet for five minutes anyway. \u201cNighthammer traffic\u2019s coming. I gotta pay attention.\u201d<br /> <br /> You nod. From downriver, you can hear boatmen calling to one another in the dark.<br /> <br /> \u201cOn your port!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAhoy the raft! \u2018Ey, I said AHOY THE RAFT!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat you over there, Tern?!\u201d<br /> <br /> Grinning Eel cups a hand to the side of his mouth and yells himself: \u201cOy! Comin\u2019 downriver along the north bank! Make way!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMela\u2019s tits!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShove over!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cEel, what\u2019re you doin\u2019 comin\u2019 downriver in the fuckin\u2019 rain at fuckin\u2019 sunset, man?!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGot a fare was runnin\u2019 late!\u201d Eel croaks back to the last caller, his grey mustache twitching. His voice sounds a bit raspy, probably he doesn\u2019t usually have to yell over the splashing of the driving rain on the surface of the water.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell I hope they\u2019re payin\u2019 extra, it\u2019s a shit night to be out!\u201d<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a gentle tug at your ankle. Another fish!<br /> <br /> \u201cMy rates is always reasonable, Whirling Eddie!\u201d Eel laughs.<br /> <br /> You wait\u2026another tug. Then the line pulls hard, and you yank back to set the hook\u2026caught a second fish! You\u2019re going to eat well tonight!<br /> <br /> \u201cSure, sure,\u201d Whirling Eddie laughs back. The lanterns of the Nighthammer boats are coming into view now, illuminating the rain in glowing circles around dozens of shadowy boat shapes. Each of them is likely packed with three or four passengers on their way home from working the day shift at the forges.<br /> <br /> \u201cEel! I got another one!\u201d You smile. \u201cFeels even bigger than the-woah!\u201d<br /> <br /> The twine yanks your ankle. Hard. Your boat swerves left\u2026towards all those lanterns and shadowy boat shapes.<br /> <br /> \u201cSHIT.\u201d Eel grits his teeth and slams his paddle into the water to correct your course. The twine tied around your ankle is taught, running up to the lip of the boat and then out into the rain at a hard straight angle. It\u2019s starting to dig into your ankle.<br /> <br /> <b>What do you do?<br /> <br /> Let the thing tire itself out and then reel it in! You\u2019ve obviously got a big one here, if it\u2019s got this much fight in it! That\u2019s dinner and breakfast and lunch tomorrow, or maybe a few coins at the fish market if you can land it!<br /> <br /> Try to reel it in now. If it\u2019s big enough to yank the boat off course, letting the fish tire itself out might mean getting dragged into a collision with the other boats, but you\u2019re not about to let this fish get away just because it might get you and Grinning Eel and five or six other people drowned!<br /> <br /> Take your new knife and cut the line. Food and money is nice, but it\u2019s not worth the risk of a collision.<br /> <br /> Take your new knife and cut the line. If it was YOUR fish it\u2019d be worth taking some risks, but you\u2019re not gonna risk your life when you already agreed the fish would go to Grinning Eel if it was bigger than the first one.<br /> <br /> Yell at the other boatmen to get the hell out your way! You and your fish are COMING THROUGH!<br /> <br /> *************************************</b><br /> <u><b>Inventory:</b></u><ul><li>Tattered Rags</li> <li>Fishhooks (2)</li> <li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Improvised Fishing Line w/hook</li> <li>3 Large Earthworms</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Pile of Stolen Clothes (mostly rags)</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Steel spearhead (six-inch knife blade with a clumsy handle)</li> </ul><br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <u><b>You Have Gained:</b></u><br /> <u><b>Attributes: (9/13 Allocated)</b></u><br /> +1 Manipulation (Persuading Eel to help you by appealing to his self-interest)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Abilities: (18/28 Allocated)</b></u><br /> +1 Sail (Studying Grinning Eel as he steered your boat, seriously considering following in Daddy's footsteps)<br /> +1 Bureaucracy (Negotiating a ride by offering to become a business partner)<br /> +1 Awareness (Learning the art of navigating by sound when visibility is bad)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Specialties: (0/4 Allocated)</b></u><br /> <br /> <u><b>Merits: (1/7 Allocated)</b></u><br /> <b>+Grinning Eel, 1 Pt Ally</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 07-01-2017, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T20:51:05-07:00","id":971729,"title":"","content":"Let it tire itself out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T21:04:02-07:00","id":971735,"title":"","content":"&gt;Try to reel it in. Use the weight of your body for leverage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T21:42:16-07:00","id":971756,"title":"","content":"I happen to know a bit about trolling, the proper term for what we're doing. There's no way that fish can keep up that fight for long if it's being pulled hard into the current; its gills won't be able to work properly. So pull it in! Give it to Eel without griping, and that's (hopefully) impress him with our honesty, and just landing it will show we've got the strength and grit to be at least worth considering as a successor. And it's not like we're getting the raw end of the deal; we've already landed one decent sized fish, so one way or another we both get a decent supper out of this. Besides, if we don't land it, that probably no supper at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T07:09:26-07:00","id":971912,"title":"","content":"Reel it in. This might be our white whale!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T08:30:03-07:00","id":971940,"title":"","content":"I like the yelling, while letting itself tire itself out. Sounds funny and just a bit entitled","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:42:08-07:00","id":972003,"title":"","content":"Reel it in and yell out a warning to the other boaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T14:14:57-07:00","id":972117,"title":"","content":"<b>Let the thing tire itself out and then reel it in.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T18:12:39-07:00","id":972250,"title":"","content":"&gt;Try to reel it in now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T08:40:12-07:00","id":975955,"title":"","content":"Let It Tire Itself Out: 2<br /> Reel it In: 4<br /> Out of my way!: 2<br /> <br /> No way you\u2019re letting this fish get away! Especially not in front of Grinning Eel, who you\u2019re trying to impress! You grab the taut twine and pull as hard as you can. The line stings your cold, rain-drenched fingers as you pull in about two arm lengths of line\u2026and as you pull, you pull the boat towards your fish, and towards the other boats.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat in the name of Heaven did you catch, kid?\u201d Eel grunts, paddling the boat hard in the opposite direction to the one you\u2019re pulling in.<br /> <br /> \u201cI dunno, but whatever it is, it\u2019s-\u201c you start to say, before a tremendous plume of water erupts from the canal ahead of you. In the dim lantern light, you can\u2019t make out the details, but the shape that bursts from the calm surface of the water is <i>immense</i>, dwarfing the little canal boat it has lifted up over the water in its vast jaws, and you can make out the gleam of teeth and yellow eyes in the light of the suddenly-swinging lanterns. The sounds of splintering wood and screams of panic come a split second later. The twine in your fingers cuts into your flesh as the slack you had pulled in runs back out of your hands, and then it almost lifts you bodily into the air by the ankle you\u2019ve tied it off to\u2026and then the monster up ahead dives, taking a whole canal boat with it, and the line pulls back down, and everyone is yelling, and Eel is cursing, and the boat is careening forward towards the other boats as the front side where you\u2019re sitting is pulled downwards\u2026<br /> <br /> It seems you have caught a river dragon. Think fast! Do you:<br /> <br /> <b>Cut the line, quick, before it drags you under! Then yell at Eel to make it to shore while it\u2019s distracted eating the people in that boat it just capsized!<br /> <br /> Cut the line, quick, before it tears off your whole leg! Then yell at Eel to row over and help rescue those people splashing around in the water before it comes back!<br /> <br /> Cut the line, quick, before it drags you straight into the rest of the boats and causes a massive pileup! Then yell to the other boats to get to shore, quick, before it comes back!<br /> <br /> Cut the line-that twine is going to snap anyway, no reason to let it cut your ankle any worse than it already has. Then, as calmly as you are able, <i>scream </i>at the top of your lungs: \u201cHELP! SOMEBODY PLEASE HELP! THIS RIVER DRAGON IS OBSTRUCTING OUR TRADE!\u201d<br /> <br /> Cut the line? Hah! This is how your legend begins! You are going to LAND that monster, and be FAMOUS, and be RICH, and make a RAINCOAT out of its SCALES! KEEP REELING IT IN!<br /> <br /> Or\u2026Something else?</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>*************************************</b><br /> <u><b>Resources You Have Available:</b></u><ul><li>Tattered Rags</li> <li>Fishhooks (2)</li> <li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Improvised Fishing Line with a damn River Dragon on the other end of it</li> <li>3 Large Earthworms</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Steel spearhead (six-inch knife blade with a clumsy handle)</li> <li>A fish</li> <li>An oil lantern</li> <li>Grinning Eel, expert boatman</li> <li>Some fifty feet of rope coiled in the bottom of the boat</li> </ul><br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <u><b>You Have Gained:</b></u><br /> <u><b>Attributes: (10/13 Allocated)*</b></u><br /> Strength +1 (Choosing brute force over patience)<br /> *Physical attributes now have 5 allocated, and therefore you are Phys-primary. Social attributes are at 3 and Mental 2, so secondary/tertiary categories are still undecided. You have to spend 1 point more on physical attributes. If you allocate both remaining points to Mental stats you'll be Mental secondary, otherwise you may devote 1 to Social and 1 to Mental to be Social secondary.<br /> <u><b>Abilities: (18/28 Allocated)</b></u><br /> Survival +1 (This totally would have worked if you'd just caught a fish)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Specialties: (0/4 Allocated)</b></u><br /> <br /> <u><b>Merits: (1/7 Allocated)</b></u>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 07-01-2017, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T09:34:09-07:00","id":975971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=975955#post975955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cHELP! SOMEBODY PLEASE HELP! THIS RIVER DRAGON IS OBSTRUCTING OUR TRADE!\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>((lol)) No... just, no. <b>I</b> would be blamed, and probably turned inside-out. Or Eel could get blamed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cut the line, quick, before it tears off your whole leg! Then yell at Eel to row over and help rescue those people splashing around in the water before it comes back!</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-25-2016, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T09:51:38-07:00","id":975982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=975955#post975955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cut the line-that twine is going to snap anyway, no reason to let it cut your ankle any worse than it already has. Then, as calmly as you are able, <i>scream </i>at the top of your lungs: \u201cHELP! SOMEBODY PLEASE HELP! THIS RIVER DRAGON IS OBSTRUCTING OUR TRADE!\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Too funny not to choose this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T10:06:55-07:00","id":975992,"title":"","content":"Cut the line, cut the line! The twine can't take that strain anyway! &quot;Eel! We gotta help the others!&quot; we yell to him, then louder, &quot;A RIVER DRAGON OBSTRUCTS TRADE IN THE CANAL TO NIGHTHAMMER FROM CINNABAR!&quot; hoping to catch the the attention of a relevant god, peacekeeper, or whoever. The authorities might not care about boatmen, but they do care about the smooth flow of trade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T13:00:07-07:00","id":976059,"title":"","content":"If we weren't a malnourished preteen, I'd say &quot;Grab the line, dive into the water, and try to stab out the dragons eyes with your knife.&quot; <br /> <br /> But we are a malnourished preteen, so let's cut the line and try to rescue who we can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T16:01:12-07:00","id":976135,"title":"","content":"<b>Cut the line, quick, before it drags you straight into the rest of the boats and causes a massive pileup! Then yell to the other boats to get to shore, quick, before it comes back!</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T01:19:20-07:00","id":976419,"title":"","content":"<b>Cut the line, quick, before it tears off your whole leg! Then yell at Eel to row over and help rescue those people splashing around in the water before it comes back!</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T04:55:02-07:00","id":976468,"title":"","content":"Reel it in! The story of how we (almost) caught a river dragon could keep us fed in a proper teahouse for weeks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/649-nightwinder","name":"Nightwinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T08:15:15-07:00","id":976527,"title":"","content":"Um... no. A river dragon is gigantic. These things are bigger than tyrant lizards, basically mosasaurs. They're big, strong, mean, and insanely dangerous. Fighting it up close is a great way to get killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T08:15:38-07:00","id":976529,"title":"","content":"<br /> <b>Cut the line, quick, before it tears off your whole leg! Then yell at Eel to row over and help rescue those people splashing around in the water before it comes back!</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T10:11:37-07:00","id":976596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=976527#post976527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um... no. A river dragon is gigantic. These things are bigger than tyrant lizards, basically mosasaurs. They're big, strong, mean, and insanely dangerous. Fighting it up close is a great way to get killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. <a href=\"http://static.panoramio.com/photos/large/53898884.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">This</a> is what we're up against (actually about the same size as a tyrant lizard). If we're lucky and it's a small one, more like <a href=\"http://blog.everythingdinosaur.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/pliosaurus_scale.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.<br /> <br /> I dunno why it took a worm as bait when its normal food is dolphins and giant sturgeon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-26-2016, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T10:29:27-07:00","id":976602,"title":"","content":"I don't think it did. I think it just happened to get the hook stuck in its mouth while swimming down the canal. That put it in a bad mood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T19:42:36-07:00","id":976891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=975955#post975955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cut the line? Hah! This is how your legend begins! You are going to LAND that monster, and be FAMOUS, and be RICH, and make a RAINCOAT out of its SCALES! KEEP REELING IT IN!</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the votes appear to be going for the sensible thing...but this is really the kind of person I want to read a story about <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T20:14:58-07:00","id":977558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wandering</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=976891#post976891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of the votes appear to be going for the sensible thing...but this is really the kind of person I want to read a story about <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This, it's gonna be epic!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T08:13:57-07:00","id":983927,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Cut the line-that twine is going to snap anyway, no reason to let it cut your ankle any worse than it already has. Then, as calmly as you are able, <i>scream </i>at the top of your lungs: \u201cHELP! SOMEBODY PLEASE HELP! THIS RIVER DRAGON IS OBSTRUCTING OUR TRADE!\u201d</span><br /> <br /> </span><br /> </i></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12278-broken25","name":"Broken25","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T10:33:04-07:00","id":984487,"title":"","content":"<b>Cut the Line, tell Eel to help victims: 5<br /> Cut the Line, then tell victims to get to safety: 1<br /> Pray to the Emissary for help: 3<br /> Sheer Hubris: 3</b><br /> <br /> With a quick slash, you cut the line connecting you to the River Dragon.<br /> <br /> \u201cEel!\u201d You shout, \u201cWe\u2019ve gotta help those people!\u201d<br /> <br /> Eel scowls. \u201cNo fucking way.\u201d<br /> <br /> He starts poling towards shore.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey\u2019re gonna get eaten, Eel!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can fit maybe six people in my boat, kid.\u201d Eel growls. \u201cAnd there\u2019s more than that in the water, and they\u2019re scared, panicking. They\u2019re like to capsize us trying to climb in if we go help them, and then we all get eaten.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe have to do something!\u201d You realize your hands are clenched in fists, and they\u2019re shaking. One of the fists is still clutching your knife.<br /> <br /> Eel bows his head. \u201cI was\u2026I knew your father. Gods know I wasn\u2019t the best of friends to him, but I\u2019m not gonna let his kid get eaten. Not on my boat.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou have to help them, you stupid old man! They\u2019re going to die!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cEverybody dies.\u201d Eel scowls, the swaying lantern casting deep, fast-moving shadows on his craggy face. \u201cBut we\u2019re not going to. Not today. Not while I\u2019m steering.\u201d<br /> <br /> There is a huge crunching sound, and more screams, and splashing. The river dragon has capsized another boat. It doesn\u2019t appear to be eating anyone yet, just destroying boats. Perhaps it\u2019s smart enough to try and get everybody in the water first, perhaps it\u2019s really stupid and thinks the boats are bigger food and is trying to eat them.<br /> <br /> \u201cEel\u2026if you rescue some people, they\u2019ll say you\u2019re a hero.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t wanna be a hero, kid. Tried that once, didn\u2019t like it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey\u2019ll pay you! You\u2019re saving their lives, they\u2019ll pay you so much money!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMoney\u2019s not worth getting eaten, kid. Not a good trade.\u201d<br /> <br /> You\u2019re halfway to shore now. The chorus of shouts and screams from the middle of the river is drawing onlookers from shore-even in this cold, heavy rain, a small crowd with broad hats or umbrellas has gathered to see what the fuss is about. Somebody shouts about a river boat crash.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s a River Dragon!\u201d You yell at them. \u201cSend help! It\u2019s smashing all the boats in the canal and eating everyone! It\u2019s\u2026it\u2019s obstructing trade up and down the canal!\u201d<br /> <br /> Eel slaps a hand over your mouth. \u201cAre you fucking crazy?!\u201d<br /> <br /> You push him away, and the boat rocks wildly.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou don\u2019t fuckin\u2019 try to call down the Emissary, kid!\u201d Eel snarls. \u201cDidn\u2019t your useless godforsaken parents teach you anything?!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell YOU\u2019RE not helping!\u201d You shout back.<br /> <br /> There is a flash of lightning. You are both silence by the sight of the river dragon, its vast bulk high out of the water surrounded by white spray, hanging over one of the river boats. For an instant, you can see every scale and every scar illuminated in stark monochrome detail. It is huge, and majestic, and terrible, and then it is dark again and there is a roar and a smashing of wood and more screaming. For several seconds, you and Eel stare into the darkness in awestruck silence, and there only the pounding of the rain and the sound of panicked thrashing\u2026and a hard, metallic, clicking sound.<br /> <br /> Click.<br /> Click.<br /> Click.<br /> <br /> The man standing on the boat with you has long white nails and he is holding a wooden staff, and he\u2019s clicking his nails against it. His demeanor is\u2026bored? Annoyed? It is hard to tell. The great locks of his white hair hang in a tangled mess, and his white robes are soaking wet. In the flickering light of the lantern, they are plastered to his skin, and you can make out hard, lean muscles and a tall lithe figure...and the faint outline of some kind of large tattoo on his arm and shoulder through the clinging fabric.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you,\u201d the figure says, turning to you. His silver mask is smooth and featureless, and rain drips down its surface. He presses a silver coin into your hand as you stare, open-mouthed.<br /> Then thunder rumbles, and the Emissary of Nexus soars out into the rain.<br /> <br /> Eel stares after it, his face haggard\u2026and then poles as hard and as fast as he can towards shore. He reaches a dock, and the waiting crowd helps pull you and the old man out of the boat in time to turn and watch as the water of the canal begins to boil.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2026what now?</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Emissary is boiling those people alive! You have to get a boat and go out there to help them!<br /> <br /> The Emissary is boiling the river dragon alive! You have to get a boat and go out there to harvest its teeth and eyes and other valuable components! And grab nets, we\u2019re about to have more fish than we could eat in a month!<br /> <br /> The Emissary is boiling the river\u2026but historically, that doesn\u2019t mean that\u2019s all the Emissary is doing. It could start raining knives or poison any minute, you have to get out of here!<br /> The Emissary is boiler the river\u2026you need to watch closely. How is he doing that?<br /> <br /> There\u2019s nothing you can do now the Emissary\u2019s here-the fish floating to the surface and the river dragon are going to get looted by other people, people with boats and nets. You need to grab your fish from the bottom of the boat and give it to Eel to pay him, and then head home to your warm dry nook and get out of this cold rain. And figure out what to do with a whole silver dinar.<br /> <br /> Something else?</b><br /> <br /> <u><b>Resources You Have Available:</b></u><ul><li>Tattered Rags</li> <li>Fishhooks (2)</li> <li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>3 Large Earthworms</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Steel spearhead (six-inch knife blade with a clumsy handle)</li> <li>A fish</li> <li>One silver Dinar!</li> </ul><br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <u><b>You Have Gained:</b></u><br /> <u><b>Attributes: (10/13 Allocated)*</b></u><br /> *Physical attributes now have 5 allocated, and therefore you are Phys-primary. Social attributes are at 3 and Mental 2, so secondary/tertiary categories are still undecided. You have to spend 1 point more on physical attributes. If you allocate both remaining points to Mental stats you'll be Mental secondary, otherwise you may devote 1 to Social and 1 to Mental to be Social secondary.<br /> <u><b>Abilities: (20/28 Allocated)</b></u><br /> Integrity +1 (You were willing to risk your own life to help others in accordance because it was the right thing to do, even if Eel wasn't)<br /> Occult +1 (You prayed to the Emissary, and the Emissary answered)<br /> <u><b>Specialties: (0/4 Allocated)</b></u><br /> <br /> <u><b>Merits: (1/7 Allocated)</b></u><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T11:22:35-07:00","id":984516,"title":"","content":"<b>[X] The Emissary is boiling the river dragon alive! You have to get a boat and go out there to harvest its teeth and eyes and other valuable components! And grab nets, we\u2019re about to have more fish than we could eat in a month!</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Money!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12278-broken25","name":"Broken25","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T11:33:11-07:00","id":984524,"title":"","content":"I say we learn at his side, there are worse anti-heroes to side kick for","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T11:54:53-07:00","id":984535,"title":"","content":"Realize that this mess is going to alienate Eel and he might not be our friend ever again. Pay him the fish now and apologize. Then... find a net or rope and try to throw it to pull people and fish out of the boiling water.<br /> <br /> ((We may be idiotic enough to pray to the Emissary, but surely we can't be dumb enough to actually jump into boiling water.))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T12:34:10-07:00","id":984551,"title":"","content":"....OK, this situation is officially FUBAR now. Neither misguided heroism nor naked greed will do us or anyone else any good, now. But still...<br /> <br /> &gt;Other - Pay Eel, then watch what happens. Run away if things get any more dangerous than they already are. DO NOT ENTER THE WATER.<br /> <br /> ...and let's never ask the Emissary for help ever again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T13:55:53-07:00","id":984588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=984535#post984535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Realize that this mess is going to alienate Eel and he might not be our friend ever again. Pay him the fish now and apologize. Then... find a net or rope and try to throw it to pull people and fish out of the boiling water.<br /> <br /> ((We may be idiotic enough to pray to the Emissary, but surely we can't be dumb enough to actually jump into boiling water.))</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=984551#post984551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&gt;Other - Pay Eel, then watch what happens. Run away if things get any more dangerous than they already are. DO NOT ENTER THE WATER.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of these. Pay eel, watch to make sure we're not about to die horribly, then look for fish or people near shore to eat or rescue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9510,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","user":"BlueWinds","date":". 10-09-2016, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T16:56:02-07:00","id":984653,"title":"","content":"Agreed. And the water might not actually be boiling, it might only be bubbling and churning. See what's going on, see if we can get some idea of what the Emissary is doing, and try to help whomever we can (and grab whatever we can, but that's secondary to helping people).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T23:00:12-07:00","id":984758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=984551#post984551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and let's never ask the Emissary for help ever again.</div> </div> </div> </div>AGREED<br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">10 characters</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T01:16:39-07:00","id":984782,"title":"","content":"Cowards. all of you! Where is your entrepeneur spirit?<br /> <br /> We aren't going to raise ourselves out of poverty if we let opportunities as good as this pass away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12278-broken25","name":"Broken25","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T07:29:39-07:00","id":984867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=984551#post984551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....OK, this situation is officially FUBAR now. Neither misguided heroism nor naked greed will do us or anyone else any good, now. But still...<br /> <br /> &gt;Other - Pay Eel, then watch what happens. Run away if things get any more dangerous than they already are. DO NOT ENTER THE WATER.<br /> <br /> ...and let's never ask the Emissary for help ever again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree to all these things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T13:32:52-07:00","id":996781,"title":"","content":"Try to Help People: 3<br /> Loot the Bodies: 4<br /> Attempt to get the Emissary of Nexus to be your Mentor?! 1<br /> Watch and Learn: 2<br /> <br /> <br /> As screaming starts from the middle of the river, the crowd watching from the shore decides it\u2019s probably time to be somewhere else. Anywhere else. The boats and boatmen whose vessels are still intact are skirting the middle of the river, giving the Emissary and the wreckage a wide berth. The people in the middle of the river scream and thrash\u2026but by the time you\u2019ve managed to get out of your boat and grab a big bundle of rope you could maybe throw to somebody\u2026the screaming has stopped.<br /> <br /> Bodies bob in the water, the pale of their clothes little more than daubs of color against the blackness of the water. Here and there you see a dead fish bobbing white through the heavy rain\u2026and the vast white bulk of the River Dragon\u2019s belly slowly surfaces along with great gouts of white steam rising up from the canal. The cold and heavy rain pounds the steam down to a few feet over the water. It would be pretty, if dozens of people weren\u2019t floating dead in the water.<br /> <br /> Eel is staring, muttering a quiet prayer. You look at him\u2026and back to the river. It looks like everybody is too scared to do anything\u2026but that\u2019s not going to last long.<br /> <br /> \u201cEel!\u201d<br /> <br /> The old man ignores you and stares out at the river.<br /> <br /> \u201cEel!\u201d This time you throw the bundle of rope at his head, and he clumsily ducks and catches it.<br /> <br /> \u201cWHAT?!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cEel. This is our chance. While everybody else is too scared!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you daft, child?\u201d Eel glowers at you. \u201cOur chance for WHAT, exactly? To get boiled like a couple of duck eggs?\u201d<br /> <br /> You sigh. \u201cEel. How much is a River Dragon tooth worth over at the Alchemists\u2019 market?\u201d<br /> <br /> Eel raises an eyebrow. \u201c\u2026I see your point. But I gave you your ride and I\u2019ve got the fish you promised me in the bottom of the boat. Why should I cut <i>you </i>in?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou need an extra pair of hands. And, um. Do you really want to be the first person to put your hands in that River Dragon\u2019s mouth? Maybe it\u2019s tougher than the Emissary thought.\u201d<br /> <br /> The old man stares at you. \u201cGods. You\u2019re your father\u2019s kid, alright\u2026fine. Get back in.\u201d<br /> <br /> Moments later, you are poling back out into the river. The bottom of the boat is hot against your bare feet, and the steam rising from the river is scalding. Normally you\u2019d be frightened\u2026but after a day trudging through freezing rain, it actually feels pretty nice!<br /> <br /> You near the River Dragon\u2019s corpse. The Emissary is floating nearby, standing on a roiling bank of steaming fog as though it were solid ground. It cocks its masked head, watching the two of you approach the monster. Eel tries hard not to look. You give the Emissary a nervous wave. It\u2026waves back, seeming faintly amused, then turns and sails away across the canal and out into the rain-swept darkness.<br /> <br /> Eel takes his pole and gingerly pokes the River Dragon in the head. When it continues to float upside-down, he gets a bit more confident and pokes it harder, in the eye. Nothing happens.<br /> \u201c\u2026I think it\u2019s dead,\u201d he tells you, poling closer.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood. Alright, I\u2019m gonna see if I can cut out some teeth.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGet its eyes too, if you can,\u201d Eel nods. \u201cDunno what they\u2019re worth, but alchemists always have pickled eyes floating in glass bottles.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cEyes.\u201d You nod.<br /> <br /> Eel brings the boat up right alongside the monster\u2019s head. Its huge snout is half the size of the canal boat, and twice as wide. This close, the River Dragon smells\u2026delicious. A little bit like hot turtle soup from the stand outside Aunt Dwi's brothel. You reach out and poke it with your knife. No reaction\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cHurry,\u201d Eel tells you. \u201cI can see folks on shore getting in their boats. We\u2019re about to have some company!\u201d<br /> <br /> You grab the River Dragon\u2019s huge snout and, straining, lift it so it leans on the boat, which tips dangerously.<br /> <br /> \u201cHo! Careful there, kid!\u201d<br /> <br /> Armed with your Nighthammer-forged spear blade, you lift the creature\u2019s front lip to reveal fangs the size of your forearm. You stab deep into its gums and begin sawing. It\u2019s\u2026slow, hard work. Once you\u2019ve gotten the base of the fang revealed, it\u2019s still hard to pry the tooth loose\u2026but you manage it. The long spearpoint is definitely better at stabbing and prying than at cutting.<br /> <br /> \u201cOne fang down,\u201d you tell Eel.<br /> <br /> \u201cGreat! We\u2019re lucky it\u2019s such a shitty night out. Looks like our competition\u2019s only two or three boats, kid!\u201d<br /> <br /> As you saw out fangs, Eel greets your fellow scavengers with a wave and a big grin, telling them there\u2019s plenty for everybody and asking if they want to grab the other side and help pole the big fucker to shore or if they just want to harvest out here to cut out the folks who don\u2019t have boats. It\u2019s agreed to do the butchering out in the middle of the canal, and men with hooks and large knives quickly set to work cutting the River Dragon and divvying up the pieces. One of the boats ignores the monster completely and starts rounding up the dead bodies to search them for silver teeth or jewelry, and maybe to sell any recognizable corpses back to their families for funerary rites.<br /> <br /> After an hour of finger-numbing sawing and hacking and yelling in the cold rain (for the canal cools rapidly), you\u2019re done.<br /> <br /> Eel finishes your ride home and drops you off in Nighthammer with a tough, rubbery, stinking spleen stuffed full of what he has deemed \u201cyour cut.\u201d Which pretty much means everything he was able to get hold of but didn\u2019t have any room for in the boat or in his net. He promises to give you some more lessons on being a boatman and lets you keep your fish, telling you he made plenty of profit off you tonight!<br /> <br /> Nobody\u2019s out in the rain to question you staggering down the street covered in blood and gore carrying a large and bloody \u201csack\u201d over your shoulder. You managed to get back to your nest, and with some difficulty you manage to get your loot up onto the roof with you and curl up under the eaves.<br /> <br /> Food, a fish to eat tomorrow, a whole silver dinar, and a bunch of stuff you can sell at the market for more coin! And on top of that, Eel really likes you and referred to you as his apprentice talking to a couple of the other boatmen. All in all, a pretty good day!<br /> <br /> It\u2019s pretty late now-the bell over at the Foundry just rang for eight o clock a few minutes ago. What now?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> -Sleep! You\u2019re safe and well fed and warm and dry, but you\u2019re exhausted. If you\u2019re going to haggle River Dragon teeth tomorrow, you should do it with a clear head and probably after you\u2019ve changed into clothes that aren\u2019t covered in blood and eaten your fish for breakfast.<br /> <br /> -Get Clean. You\u2019re covered in blood and bits of River Dragon organs. Strip down on the slippery roof tiles and stand in the freezing rain and scrub out your hair until most of it washes off, or else you\u2019re gonna be covered in flies if the rain lets up before tomorrow morning. Dry out under the warm eaves of the Blackhand Company\u2019s foundry before you put on dry rags, so you don\u2019t catch a flu during the night.<br /> <br /> -No time to rest-go sell your loot NOW, before anybody else gets to the Alchemist\u2019s market with River Dragon bits. If you\u2019re lucky and you can get somebody out of bed, you might be able to offer to connect an alchemist with Eel and the other boatmen, so he can have a monopoly on the goods tomorrow. That could be real profitable\u2026if he doesn\u2019t just have his guards rough you up and take your merchandise and go to haggle with the boatmen on his own.<br /> <br /> -You want to hit the market first, but nobody\u2019s going to haggle in good faith with a kid. You need some muscle that looks old enough to barter with. Perhaps you could cut Aunt Dwi in, she knows a few alchemists and healers who might be good buyers\u2026or perhaps you should get a hold of Rat. He\u2019s been a jerk lately, but he\u2019s got some connections with local drug dealers and might be able to get you in touch with an alchemist who won\u2019t ask too many questions.<br /> <br /> -Selling the stuff is dumb. You should put the meat over one of the foundry\u2019s smokestacks to make sure it\u2019ll keep-that\u2019s enough meat to eat for weeks! Maybe a month if you can get a pot of stew going...That patch of skin would make a great purse, or maybe armor plating to put under your shirt in case somebody stabs you, if you can boil off the fat under it and sew it up to some leather with some twine and get rid of the stink\u2026and you bet those River Dragon fangs would sell better if they were carved, like the carved mammoth tusks you\u2019ve seen at the stands for the merchants who trade up North. Worked goods sell for more than raw materials!<br /> <br /> -Selling the stuff is dumb. You've spent enough time around the monks and generally wandering the Temple District learning about spirits from their stories, to know that River Dragons are spiritually potent. Drinking its blood, prepared properly, could let you breathe underwater. Eating its tongue (which you have a sizeable chunk of in your bundle) could let you speak in the languages of birds. Those fangs could be carved and inlaid with powdered jade or molten moonsilver to make potent magical talismans! That's why the alchemists would pay for the ingredients! Why sell this stuff when, if you can hold onto it long enough to figure out how to USE it, you might be able to give yourself magic that could make you rich?<br /> <br /> -Something Else?<br /> <br /> <b><u>Resources You Have Available:</u></b><ul><li>Tattered Rags</li> <li>Fishhooks (2)</li> <li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>3 Large Earthworms</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Steel spearhead (six-inch knife blade with a clumsy handle)</li> <li>A medium sized fish</li> <li>One silver Dinar!</li> <li>Six River Dragon Fangs (two big ones the size of your forearm, four smaller ones a little longer than your hand)</li> <li>A four-by-four swatch of thick, scaly River Dragon hide</li> <li>A River Dragon Spleen? You think it\u2019s a spleen? Tied in a bundle</li> <li>A Spleenful of River Dragon Parts, including one eyeball</li> </ul><br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <b><u>You Have Gained:</u></b><br /> <b><u>Attributes: (12/13 Allocated)*</u></b><br /> Dexterity +1: You just spent an hour climbing all over a giant dead lizard and cutting it up with hands numbed from the cold using a tool not intended for that purpose without cutting off any of your own fingers.<br /> Intelligence +1: Instead of thinking in the moment and running away from danger, you quickly came up with a plan for long-term profit.<br /> <br /> <i><b>*You may spend no more points on Physical Attributes, which are primary for you. How you spend your last Attribute point will determine whether you are Social or Mental Secondary.</b></i><br /> <br /> <b><u>Abilities: (23/28 Allocated)</u></b><br /> Larceny +1: You spotted an opportunity for profit in spite of danger and went for it!<br /> Medicine +1: You can learn a lot about anatomy dissecting a giant corpse in the pouring rain!<br /> Melee +1: You can learn a lot about knifework by dissecting a giant corpse in the pouring rain!<br /> Athletics +1: You can learn a lot about climbing and balance by clambering around on a giant floating corpse trying not to fall off (the main thing you learned is that having a good stabbing implement to anchor yourself with really helps!). That climb to and from your nest on the roof doesn\u2019t seem so bad now at all!<br /> <br /> <b><u>Specialties: (0/4 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Merits: (1/7 Allocated)</u></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 11-01-2016, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T13:36:03-07:00","id":996782,"title":"","content":"Get clean* and head to bed. Get up early tomorrow to sell stuff.<br /> <br /> *Monks always say cleanliness is a virtue.<br /> <br /> ((Sorry, I always wanted to explore the Immaculate Religion from a mortal's point of view.))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 11-01-2016, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T14:24:55-07:00","id":996807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=996782#post996782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Get clean* and head to bed. Get up early tomorrow to sell stuff.<br /> <br /> *Monks always say cleanliness is a virtue.<br /> <br /> ((Sorry, I always wanted to explore the Immaculate Religion from a mortal's point of view.))</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Good hygiene is important, especially when you live in squalor! <br /> <br /> No sense going out to the market at this hour. Honest merchants close their doors after dark. <br /> <br /> No sense keeping the goods either - the value we'd get in selling them probably outweighs what we'd get in employing our amateur crafting or occultist skills. <br /> <br /> As a sidenote, how old do you have to be to start one of those bank accounts with the Guild? Is there a minimum balance? A whole dinar is a lot of money for us to hold onto - we should invest it in something rather than risk it getting stolen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T15:31:56-07:00","id":996843,"title":"","content":"&gt;<b>1 Get Clean.</b> Cleanliness is a virtue, and flies are gross.<br /> <br /> &gt;<b>2 Sleep.</b> zzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzz<br /> <br /> &gt;<b>3 Sell fangs to the alchemist. </b>Where are we going to get jade or moonsilver? Maybe we can buy it with that silver dinar... but that dinar could also buy a lot of food.<br /> <b>Also</b>, See what the alchemists will offer for the eyeball and spleen.<br /> <br /> &gt;<b>4 </b>You've spent enough time around the monks and generally wandering the Temple District learning about spirits from their stories, to know that River Dragons are spiritually potent. Drinking its blood, prepared properly, could let you breathe underwater. Eating its tongue (which you have a sizeable chunk of in your bundle) could let you speak in the languages of birds.<br /> That patch of skin would make a great purse, or maybe armor plating to put under your shirt in case somebody stabs you, if you can boil off the fat under it and sew it up to some leather with some twine and get rid of the stink<br /> <b>Also, </b>smoke whatever bits of meat are neither valuable enough to sell, nor magical enough to do special stuff with. That's a fair bit of meat. And don't boil off the fat, scrape it off and eat it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T17:07:13-07:00","id":996893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=996782#post996782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Get clean* and head to bed. Get up early tomorrow to sell stuff.<br /> <br /> *Monks always say cleanliness is a virtue.<br /> <br /> ((Sorry, I always wanted to explore the Immaculate Religion from a mortal's point of view.))</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Get clean, go to sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T19:27:43-07:00","id":996950,"title":"","content":"Get clean, set some of the meat to get smoked, and go to sleep. Sell the stuff tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T20:04:39-07:00","id":996963,"title":"","content":"Since most Exalted folks are used to Resources, thought I'd give you an idea of what a Dinar looks like.<br /> <br /> One Koku, which is the realm paper scrip equal to half a Bit of Jade, is equal to 0.96 Dinar. I'm gonna round it to A Koku equals a Dinar for the purposes of keeping it simple, since we only have one.<br /> <br /> That's one month at peasant wages working in the Realm, or three months of unskilled day-to-day grunt labor in Nexus. It's enough money for a family of four to eat meat for a weak (chicken or fish) or rice and cheap vegetables for six weeks. It's enough money to buy yourself a dozen goats or a couple of dairy cows, though not land for them to graze on, for that you'd need to pay a grazing fee. It is not enough to purchase a quality riding animal like a horse or a camel, nor is it enough to buy you a working animal like an ox or a mule. A Dinar is enough to buy yourself eight new sets of simple peasant or workman's clothing, or a single nice outfit you could wear to deal with the professional artisans in the city. It is not enough to afford any decent drugs or medicines, nor is it enough to afford a sword. It's enough to easily afford a small quantity of simple tools like chisels, hammers, awls, shovels, crow bars, knives, axes, or hatchets, or enough to afford inexpensive weapons like javelins, spears, tridents. It's enough to afford quite a bit of raw ingredients you could use to put your Craft: Weaving skill to use-needles and thread, or wicker, are cheap. It's enough to afford any Thrown weapon (knives, hatchets, needles, slings, lassos, nets, bolas...) but not enough to afford any Archery Weapons (bows, flamepieces) or any form of armor. It's not enough money for anything occult, or at least not anything with real power-for the donation of a Dinar you might be able to afford to have a priest at the Temple District inscribe your name on a prayer strip to hang in the temple for good fortune, but it's not enough for them to make a true offering on your behalf.<br /> <br /> It is enough to open a bank account with the Guild, who would be happy to store the money for you (and invest it and keep their returns on your Dinar). It is not enough for the Guild to issue you cheques drawn on your account, you'd need to visit the bank in person to withdraw cash if you wanted to use your money. The Guild requires a minimum of ten Dinars in an account before they begin to pay interest based on the Salt Rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 11-01-2016, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:22:21-07:00","id":997191,"title":"","content":"Clean up, get some sleep. Then go talk to Aunt Dwi, see if she can help you find someone to buy the fangs, and advice on which of the other bits should be sold, and which could be prepared for other uses, like water breathing, and which ones are just meat. Really work that these things are from a river dragon killed just last night, by the Emissary itself no less, and that you harvested the fangs yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T18:34:31-07:00","id":998003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=997191#post997191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clean up, get some sleep. Then go talk to Aunt Dwi, see if she can help you find someone to buy the fangs, and advice on which of the other bits should be sold, and which could be prepared for other uses, like water breathing, and which ones are just meat. Really work that these things are from a river dragon killed just last night, by the Emissary itself no less, and that you harvested the fangs yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds good, I hate missing a monopoly though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T20:51:36-08:00","id":1012363,"title":"","content":"<b>Sleep First: 0<br /> Practice Hygiene, THEN Sleep: 4<br /> Sell On Your Own: 2 (+1 Fangs Only)<br /> Cut Aunt Dwi In: 2<br /> Cut Rat In: 0<br /> Smoke Some Meat For Later: 2<br /> Do Some Crafting: 1<br /> Occult Plans: 1</b><br /> <br /> You\u2019re tired, and the roof tiles in the rain are slippery and dangerous\u2026but you\u2019ve seen what life is like for people who get sick on the streets of Nexus. It\u2019s not pretty. Like Aunt Dwi always says, \u201chygiene before profit.\u201d<br /> <br /> Carefully, you strip down and hang your clothes on the edge of the eave above you, hoping the pounding rain will wash some of the blood out of them. You stand naked and shivering on the roof, the flimsy layer of warmth your wet rags provided stripped away. You rub the blood off yourself as best you can, and you scrub your fingers through your scraggly black hair, getting it all wet and then clawing along its length in the hopes of removing anything that\u2019s gotten caught in it. Your hair is gonna be a mess tomorrow, you can tell. You consider tying it up with your twine and just chopping it off with your new knife\u2026but then, you remember Aunt Dwi also always says you have gorgeous hair and you feel conflicted. A bad haircut could mess up your chances if you\u2019re trying to do business tomorrow even worse than frizzy tangles\u2026<br /> <br /> You\u2019ll worry about it tomorrow. Now clean, and freezing, you carefully make your way back up to your little warm dry ledge, and take some choice bits of meat from within your bundle along with the fish you caught. You tie some twine around them, and gingerly make your way farther up the roof to hang them over the smokestack. Hopefully the constant flow of hot air and smoke will preserve the meat. At the very least, they\u2019ll keep bugs off it. You pick your way across the slippery roof tiles back to your nest, and wrap yourself in some dry rags next to the warm wall of the foundry. You don\u2019t even really hear the eternal clanging of the hammers and the rumbling of the forges below anymore, but you can feel them vibrate through you as you lie there, and the noise and the rhythm is comforting. Slowly, you drift off to sleep.<br /> <br /> <i>Your dreams are full of distant thunder and flashing teeth and huge scaled forms dancing through the rains high overhead. They terrify you, but instead of running you climb building after building to try and get closer to them. You run so hard you find yourself panting and coughing, struggling to breathe. You reach out towards them, to pull yourself up into the sky alongside them\u2026but you slip, and you are falling, and the world below hurtles up towards you and-</i><br /> <br /> You\u2019re falling! You wake suddenly, and put out your hands to catch yourself on the eave above. You had started to roll away from the flat section right under the eaves and out onto the sloped roof\u2026but you caught yourself in time. You\u2019re starting to see why Rat gave this spot over to you. You\u2019re a little bigger than you were when you first started sleeping here, and there wasn\u2019t much space to sleep on to start with. Heart still pounding, you stare up at the steel-gray skies and consider spending the Dinar the Emissary gave you to rent a place to live. A whole Dinar would probably be enough to get you one month\u2019s rent\u2026<br /> <br /> It\u2019s early morning, now, and the rain is gone. The streets below are full of thick, soupy white fog. From the rooftop, it\u2019s like looking out over a slowly frothing river with the tops of buildings sticking up from it like islands. It\u2019s beautiful\u2026but your eyes quickly sting and begin to water. Without the rain to pound it into the ground, the choking smog of the Nighthammer District tints the whole scene faintly yellow-brown, and right up here on the rooftop under the stacks spewing it into the sky\u2026well, you\u2019re getting almost as smoked as the meat you tied up last night. You tie a band of fabric around your nose and mouth, like you usually do, and consider your options.<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t really want to cut Rat or Aunt Dwi in on your cut of the River Dragon\u2026but you don\u2019t\u2019 really know how much your stuff is worth, either, and between that and being a kid you\u2019re likely to get either laughed out of the place or just cheated by whatever alchemist you go to. You decide that Dwi is your best bet-she already works with an alchemist who makes medicines for her brothel, and he wants to keep her as a client-but you also decide it would be smart to keep some of the haul for yourself. You decide to bring about half of your haul to sell with Dwi\u2026and once you know what it\u2019s actually worth, you can sell the other half on your own.<br /> <br /> Still hoping to beat anybody else who helped harvest the Dragon on your way down to the markets, you dress quickly, putting on a slightly-less-squalid set of rags from your heap. You grab one of the big fangs and two of the smaller ones you got from the River Dragon, and pull out the eyeball and bundle it up in cloth.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a quick climb down to street level, and then a short walk to Dwi\u2019s brothel. As usual for this early in the morning, everyone there is asleep-the brothel stays open late and its workers usually don\u2019t rise until the afternoon. You greet the drowsy doorman, who nods sleepily to you. He\u2019s at first reluctant to let you to bother Aunt Dwi\u2026but when you tell him you\u2019ve got a way for her to make some money he grudgingly lets you in. If there\u2019s one thing Aunt Dwi loves, it\u2019s ways to make money.<br /> <br /> She meets you in her office, after keeping you waiting only about five minutes. She has tapestries on the walls depicting scantily clad dancers, and a big desk. The chairs are big and oddly shaped, and they have blue cushions.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood morning,\u201d she says. Her face was painted last night, but this morning it\u2019s smudged and tired. \u201cOx tells me you have a proposition for me. I assume\u2026it has something to do with the armful of ivory you\u2019re carting about?\u201d<br /> <br /> You know Dwi reasonably well. She\u2019s heavily motivated by profit, but she\u2019s also easily flattered by compliments on her appearance. Dwi also sees herself as a protective motherly figure and likes it when people ask her for help or advice, and is fond of meddling in people\u2019s affairs. How do you want to go about this negotiation?<br /> <br /> (It's dialogue suggestions time!)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Resources You Have Available:</u></b><ul><li>Tattered Rags</li> <li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Steel spearhead (six-inch knife blade with a clumsy handle)</li> <li>One silver Dinar!</li> <li>Three River Dragon Fangs (one big ones, two smaller ones)</li> <li>One River Dragon Eyeball wrapped in cloth</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Resources Back at Your Nest:</u></b><ul><li>Fishhooks (2)</li> <li>A medium sized smoked fish</li> <li>Three River Dragon Fangs (one big one, four smaller ones)</li> <li>A four-by-four swatch of thick, scaly River Dragon hide</li> <li>A River Dragon Spleen? You think it\u2019s a spleen? Tied in a bundle</li> <li>A Spleenful of River Dragon Parts</li> </ul><br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <b><u>You Have Gained:</u></b><br /> <b><u>Attributes: (12/13 Allocated)*</u></b><br /> *You may spend no more points on Physical Attributes, which is primary for you. How you spend your last Attribute point will determine whether you are Social or Mental Secondary.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Abilities: (24/28 Allocated)</u></b><br /> Medicine +1: Hygiene Before Profit!<br /> <b><u>Specialties: (0/4 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Merits: (1/7 Allocated)</u></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T04:50:05-08:00","id":1012494,"title":"","content":"Put on your best &quot;I'm just a poor kid and I don't know anything&quot; humility act, laced with a smattering of compliments.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh Auntie, I don't know what to do! I... found... all these ingredients at the canal the other day. River dragon parts, fresh! But I don't know what they're worth, or who I'd sell them to. But I thought, 'I'll ask Auntie Dwi! She's so smart, and so charming, and men trip over themselves to serve her. She'll know what to do!' And now here I am. So... can you help me? Pleeeease?&quot;<br /> <br /> There's a chance that she'll try to trick you into giving the goods to her so she can sell them at a higher price. If she says the stuff is worthless, just give her a sad look and leave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 12-05-2016, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T14:37:57-08:00","id":1012784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1012494#post1012494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Put on your best &quot;I'm just a poor kid and I don't know anything&quot; humility act, laced with a smattering of compliments.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh Auntie, I don't know what to do! I... found... all these ingredients at the canal the other day. River dragon parts, fresh! But I don't know what they're worth, or who I'd sell them to. But I thought, 'I'll ask Auntie Dwi! She's so smart, and so charming, and men trip over themselves to serve her. She'll know what to do!' And now here I am. So... can you help me? Pleeeease?&quot;<br /> <br /> There's a chance that she'll try to trick you into giving the goods to her so she can sell them at a higher price. If she says the stuff is worthless, just give her a sad look and leave.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can do nothing to improve on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T16:48:34-08:00","id":1012868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1012494#post1012494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Put on your best &amp;quot;I'm just a poor kid and I don't know anything&amp;quot; humility act, laced with a smattering of compliments.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Oh Auntie, I don't know what to do! I... found... all these ingredients at the canal the other day. River dragon parts, fresh! But I don't know what they're worth, or who I'd sell them to. But I thought, 'I'll ask Auntie Dwi! She's so smart, and so charming, and men trip over themselves to serve her. She'll know what to do!' And now here I am. So... can you help me? Pleeeease?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> There's a chance that she'll try to trick you into giving the goods to her so she can sell them at a higher price. If she says the stuff is worthless, just give her a sad look and leave.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah this is pretty good. I would like to come across a little more mature but I couldn't say how to do that. Great job my friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T16:52:41-08:00","id":1018262,"title":"","content":"I hope this quest still exists cause it's a favorite of mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T14:12:01-08:00","id":1021684,"title":"","content":"<b>Base Flattery: All the votes.<br /> Something Else: None of the votes.</b><br /> <br /> You know Aunt Dwi likes to be a protective motherly figure, and you know she\u2019s fond of flattery. You decide to play this to the hilt.<br /> <br /> \u201cAunt Dwi, thank you for seeing me! There was a river dragon at the canal last night, and I was able to get away with some of it! I have a couple teeth and an eye\u2026I don\u2019t really know any alchemists, though, so I don\u2019t know what they\u2019re worth, or who to sell them to\u2026but I figured, \u2018I\u2019ll ask Aunt Dwi! She\u2019s smart, and I know she\u2019s charmed a couple different alchemists into tripping over each other for her business. She\u2019ll know what to do!\u2019 and so\u2026here I am. Can you help me, Aunt Dwi? Pleeease?\u201d<br /> <br /> Aunt Dwi looks you up and down, frowning slightly in thought\u2026then smiles.<br /> <br /> \u201cChild, you really need to come work for me. That pout of yours is coming along nicely. Not quite as cute as it used to be, but starting to get charming in other ways\u2026if only we could do something with that hair.\u201d<br /> <br /> She must see your concern in your face, because she laughs, leaning in to inspect one of the river dragon teeth. \u201cPerhaps not yet, then. It seems you\u2019re finding other ways to take care of yourself. Very resourceful, child. I should be able to help you sell your\u2026wares. Blue Root\u2019s apprentice is visiting this afternoon with some medicines for my staff. I\u2019ll have her arrange a meeting between her teacher and myself, and we can discuss your Dragon\u2019s fangs.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you, Aunt Dwi!\u201d You give her a big smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t thank me. I\u2019m taking a sixty percent cut.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThirty.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re not in a position to bargain. Talk to any alchemist wearing <i>that,</i> and they\u2019ll offer you table scraps instead of Dinars.\u201d Dwi smiles at you. \u201cBut I appreciate the effort. Fifty percent, then, and you agree to let me get you something nice to wear.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026Deal.\u201d More money and free clothes isn\u2019t something you\u2019re willing to turn down. And once you know what the goods are worth, nice clothes might help you sell the rest of your stash on your own.<br /> <br /> \u201cClever child. Now tell me, how in the name of Luvilla did you wind up with river dragon teeth?\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>What now?</b><br /> <br /> Tell her the whole story-including how you\u2019re apprenticing yourself to Grinning Eel and intend to become a canal courier rather than a prostitute. (Raise Integrity)<br /> <br /> Tell her the whole story\u2026minus your arrangement with Grinning Eel, and minus the part where you called down the Emissary and he gave you a coin. (Raise Socialize)<br /> <br /> Tell her a slightly dramatized version of the story designed to make you seem smarter and braver than you are. (Raise Performance)<br /> <br /> Change the subject to talk about these new clothes you\u2019re getting and the possibility of working for Aunt Dwi. What would that entail? (Raise Appearance. Raise Socialize. Gain Aunt Dwi as a one-dot ally. If you vote for this option, please also vote for a gender identity-the conversation will go differently depending on whether our Urchin is male, female, nonbinary, or one thing but passing for another.)<br /> <br /> Change the subject to ask about the medicine Blue Root\u2019s apprentice is bringing over today. You\u2019re not going to get sick just visiting, are you? (Raise Medicine)<br /> <br /> Change the subject to ask about the \u201cmedicine\u201d Blue Root\u2019s apprentice is bringing over today. You know Aunt Dwi deals in opium, and you know there\u2019s real money in that, but it\u2019s a dangerous business. Perhaps you can offer some assistance\u2026 (Spend Bonus Points to raise Larceny to 4)<br /> <br /> Change the subject to ask about family. Your mother used to work for Aunt Dwi, and Dwi was very fond of her. For all her many faults, Aunt Dwi is one of the few people who knew her, and can tell you stories about her. It\u2019s one of the reasons you keep coming back here. (Gain Aunt Dwi as a one-dot Contact)<br /> <br /> \u2026Something Else? (Gain Something Else!)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Resources You Have Available:</u></b><ul><li>Tattered Rags</li> <li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Steel spearhead (six-inch knife blade with a clumsy handle)</li> <li>One silver Dinar!</li> <li>Three River Dragon Fangs (one big ones, two smaller ones)</li> <li>One River Dragon Eyeball wrapped in cloth</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Resources Back at Your Nest:</u></b><ul><li>Fishhooks (2)</li> <li>A medium sized smoked fish</li> <li>Three River Dragon Fangs (one big one, four smaller ones)</li> <li>A four-by-four swatch of thick, scaly River Dragon hide</li> <li>A River Dragon Spleen? You think it\u2019s a spleen? Tied in a bundle</li> <li>A Spleenful of River Dragon Parts</li> </ul><br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <b><u>You Have Gained:</u></b><br /> <b><u>Attributes: (12/13 Allocated)*</u></b><br /> *You may spend no more points on Physical Attributes, which is primary for you. How you spend your last Attribute point will determine whether you are Social or Mental Secondary.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Abilities: (25/28 Allocated)</u></b><br /> Socialize +1 (Taking advantage of known Intimacies to get Aunt Dwi in the mood to help you rather than profit off you)<br /> <b><u>Specialties: (0/4 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Merits: (1/7 Allocated)</u></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 07-01-2017, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T04:40:14-08:00","id":1021935,"title":"","content":"I want to vote for Raise Integrity, but I also want to propose my idea for gender identity for our urchin. <br /> <br /> Sex at birth: female <br /> Gender identity : female <br /> Gender expression : male<br /> <br /> Being a girl on the streets is tough. Aunt Dwi screamed all the horrible things that could happen to you after your father died and you turned down her offer for a place to stay. You have never know aunt dwi to be the overly emotional type, so you took her warnings to heart. Your father always treated you half boy anyways, so you figured you could pass as one. <br /> <br /> And it worked. The only person who knows the truth is aunt Dwi on the account she pulled you into the world in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T05:06:23-08:00","id":1021945,"title":"","content":"Change the subject and ask about family.<br /> <br /> I second wonderandawe's proposal for sex/gender/expression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 12-25-2016, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T09:48:08-08:00","id":1022016,"title":"","content":"Tell her the whole story\u2026minus your arrangement with Dancing Eel, and minus the part where you called down the Emissary and he gave you a coin.<br /> <br /> A third vote for wonderandawe's sex/gender/expression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T16:33:07-08:00","id":1023023,"title":"","content":"Female passing as male but either the larceny or possible prostitution angle","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T20:02:57-08:00","id":1023086,"title":"","content":"Change the subject to talk about these new clothes you\u2019re getting and the possibility of working for Aunt Dwi. Fourthing wonderawe's idea. And also as about our mother if we can sneak thet in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T20:40:49-08:00","id":1029897,"title":"","content":"<b>Tell The Whole Story: 1<br /> Tell The Abridged Version: 1<br /> Talk About New Clothes/Working for Dwi: 2<br /> Talk About Drug Deals: 1<br /> Talk About Mom: 2<br /> Female Passing For Male: 5: It\u2019s Unanimous! We'll worry about sexual orientation at some later time.</b><br /> <br /> \u201cI got lucky.\u201d You shrug. \u201cListen, Aunt Dwi, I like the idea of new clothes, believe me, but\u2026well, I\u2019ve seen the stuff you have the girls around here wearing, and-\u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cYou disapprove of my fashion sense?\u201d Dwi has raised an eyebrow and appears to be trying not to chuckle.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not that, it\u2019s\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI understand, child. You\u2019ve obviously made a serious effort to avoid notice. It\u2019s smart not to seem too attractive when you\u2019re out on the street, there are all manner of unsavory characters out there.\u201d<br /> <br /> You nod. \u201cThank you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s why I\u2019m always telling you to come and work for me! You\u2019d be safer here, and you deserve to be able to be yourself instead of trying to hide under dirty rags. And believe me, hiding isn\u2019t going to get any easier, young lady! You have your father\u2019s eyes, but you look just like your mother did at your age, and if you\u2019re half the looker she was covering yourself in dung isn\u2019t going to stop people noticing you. You\u2019d be safer here at the Flaming Peacock. At least you\u2019d have someone to watch out for you.\u201d<br /> <br /> You lower your eyes. \u201cMother didn\u2019t want me to work here, Aunt Dwi.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course not.\u201d Dwi sighs. \u201cGods, child, our profession is rarely anyone\u2019s first career choice. But the pay is good and once you get decent at it the work is easy and often even pleasant. Green Lily\u2026 wanted better things for you than she had for herself, and what mother doesn\u2019t, but the fact is the only reason she lived to know you as well as she did was that working at the Peacock pays well enough to afford healers and herbs to treat the Black Lung\u2026well, so long as you don\u2019t spend it all on drugs and jewelry.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026I know that, Aunt Dwi.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know, child\u2026I don\u2019t mean to pressure you. There\u2019s too many boys and girls out there doing this job against their will already. I won\u2019t have it in my house. It\u2019s just...I worry for you. You\u2019re not much more than skin and bones, your hair is a mess, I\u2019m seriously concerned you may wind up sick or worse out there. I can\u2019t keep you here if you don\u2019t work, it wouldn\u2019t be fair to anyone else, and gods know everyone else has troubles they could use help with\u2026but know you have a place to come to, if you need it.\u201d<br /> <br /> You find yourself a little touched. It\u2019s nice to remember there\u2019s someone out there who actually cares about you\u2026even if you suspect it\u2019s mostly out of guilt and lingering fondness for your Mother.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you, Aunt Dwi. It\u2019s good to have a safe place to run to\u2026if I ever need to run someplace, I mean.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, you always have a safe place here at the Peacock. We all loved Lily\u2026some of us more than others, of course-and a lot of the girls remember taking care of you when you were just a little thing, in the back rooms while she worked. She brought in a lot of business, and she didn\u2019t keep it all to herself, and she was always there to back someone up if they were having a bad day or a bad client. Any daughter of Green Lily is a friend of ours.\u201d<br /> <br /> You find yourself legitimately tearing up just a little bit. It\u2019s not often you hear anything about Mother, and somebody else telling you about how nice she was\u2026it\u2019s bringing back a lot of happy memories you\u2019ve been not-thinking-about-because-being-sad-hurts. You remember the muffled sounds of the Burning Peacock, giggles and grunts and laughter through thin walls, and the little games the girls used to play with you to keep you from making noise and bothering any of the paying customers. You remember the smells of the place-sweat and wine and poppies and smoke. You remember the smells of dried herbs and the muttering of one of Aunt Dwi\u2019s alchemists, when Mother\u2019s cough was getting really bad\u2026you remember tears and shouting and screaming, too, though the reasons for them are mostly hazy now.<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026thank you,\u201d you tell Aunt Dwi again. You really mean it. Even if you wanted to take her up on her offer-and a big part of you kind of wants to, to have a place to belong-you can\u2019t stay here. Too many memories.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s no trouble, child. I can always use new help, and my regulars are always delighted to see new faces. Honestly, if you\u2019re really set on continuing to dress like a boy, that wouldn\u2019t necessarily be a problem, some of them might even pay a little extra for-\u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cAunt Dwi.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry. Sorry. So, I\u2019m guessing no gauzy silk numbers for you, then... That\u2019s most of what I have available, I\u2019m afraid, but I\u2019m always happy to take a couple of the girls shopping. If you don\u2019t want anyone to discover your gender\u2026well, the clothes make the man. What sort of new outfit would you like for me to arrange for you?\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>An Outfit For Business</b>-you want to be able to deal with legitimate merchants, and that means looking clean-cut and classy. Maybe with a nice robe that could cover a snug vest for when your figure starts to develop\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>An Outfit For Winter</b>-You got through the last couple winters by alternately huddling with a bunch of other urchins in an upper section of the Underways, taking Dwi up on her hospitality, and stealing lots of blankets from clotheslines ahead of time. But having a nice cold-weather outfit could possibly save your life this year.<br /> <br /> <b>A Boatman\u2019s Outfit</b>: It\u2019ll require telling Dwi you\u2019re following in your father\u2019s footsteps, and he\u2019s not exactly her favorite person. But having a nice looking outfit that can handle some water without damage or shrinkage could help a lot if you\u2019re serious about starting as Grinning Eel\u2019s apprentice.<br /> <br /> <b>A Craftsman\u2019s Outfit</b>: You\u2019re honestly a pretty good weaver, at this point-you can make your own clothes, though they won\u2019t be fancy. What you really need is a good leather apron with lots of pockets for needles and spools of thread and scissors and suchlike. With the money you get from this River Dragon Teeth deal, you can make any other outfits you need, with cloth and a bit of practice anyway\u2026and hey, being a seamstress? Doesn\u2019t usually require poling around on the canal in bad weather or sleeping with belligerent drunks.<br /> <br /> <b>A Thief\u2019s Outfit</b>: You want something with lots of pockets for various tools, alright\u2026and for hiding your loot. You\u2019re a solid pickpocket, but you\u2019re not great at sneaking, which has led to problems. Something inconspicuous in brown or green so it\u2019s easy to hide, something sturdy that can handle climbing or running, something that a little blood\u2019ll wash out of easy\u2026something with hidden pockets in the lining.<br /> <br /> <b>A Monk\u2019s Outfit</b>: Simple robes and meditating in the rain? Bring it on! Alternately\u2026well, if meditating in the rain doesn\u2019t do it for you after a while, the aspiring monks get to stay in the Monastery overnight, so it could be a good start to robbing the place.<br /> <br /> <b>A Dancer\u2019s Outfit</b>: Dwi actually kind of has a point. Maybe you should go for something you can wear if and when you decide to try using your Wiles instead of your wits. I mean, you haven\u2019t felt \u201cpretty\u201d since before Mother died. Even if you don\u2019t want to work for Dwi, it might be nice to own at least one girly feeling thing.<br /> <br /> <b>A Warrior\u2019s Outfit:</b> If you\u2019re going to be staying on the street, life is going to be dangerous\u2026and apparently more so as you get older and start taking after your Mother. You need protection. Something mobile\u2026but able to turn away a knife or soften the blow of a club. Something to let you deal with the Sluice Gang without worrying about getting beat up. Maybe a buff jacket or a robe with plates sewn in\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>\u2026something else? (Please note that if your vote also includes a picture of the outfit you want, it counts for two votes!)</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Resources You Have Available:</u></b><ul><li>Tattered Rags</li> <li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Steel spearhead (six-inch knife blade with a clumsy handle)</li> <li>One silver Dinar!</li> <li>Three River Dragon Fangs (one big ones, two smaller ones)</li> <li>One River Dragon Eyeball wrapped in cloth</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Resources Back at Your Nest:</u></b><ul><li>Fishhooks (2)</li> <li>A medium sized smoked fish</li> <li>Three River Dragon Fangs (one big one, four smaller ones)</li> <li>A four-by-four swatch of thick, scaly River Dragon hide</li> <li>A River Dragon Spleen? You think it\u2019s a spleen? Tied in a bundle</li> <li>A Spleenful of River Dragon Parts</li> </ul><br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <b><u>You Have Gained:</u></b><br /> <b><u>Attributes: (13/13 Allocated-No More Attributes Without Spending Bonus Points. You Are Phys-Primary, Social Secondary, Mental Tertiary)</u></b><br /> Appearance +1<br /> <b><u>Abilities: (27/28 Allocated)</u></b><br /> Socialize +1<br /> <b><u>Specialties: (0/4 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Merits: (3/7 Allocated)</u></b><br /> +Ally 1: Aunt Dwi, owner of the Flaming Peacock Brothel<br /> +Contacts 1: Nexus Prostitutes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 07-01-2017, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T04:29:16-08:00","id":1030000,"title":"","content":"I'm going back and forth between boatman and winter. I can't decide!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T04:44:57-08:00","id":1030002,"title":"","content":"I say, &quot;Business.&quot; With a little luck, we should be able to <i>buy </i>the clothes we need once we've gotten our amateur merchantry act together. Also, what she said earlier about merchants not taking us seriously kind of stung.<br /> <br /> My second choice would be &quot;Boatman.&quot; Businessware won't be good for that kind of work, if we follow up on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T08:16:08-08:00","id":1030064,"title":"","content":"I favour business attire. We're going to be, hopefully, dealing with merchants and other (in modern terms) white collar sorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T21:29:17-08:00","id":1030424,"title":"","content":"We've seen plenty of kids let a lucky windfall go to their head - they come into some money, blow it all on something assuming that their luck is turning, and be right back where they started a month ago.<br /> <br /> A vote for boatman. We have a promising apprenticeship lined up - let's leverage the good fortune we've had, and not reach beyond our grasp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T15:20:30-08:00","id":1031349,"title":"","content":"Business, I'm not savvy enough for pics but I think this link is correct. It also looks warm to me.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orig15.deviantart.net/9065/f/2015/148/d/9/late_medieval_merchant_v1_by_macx85-d8v2jf1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://orig15.deviantart.net/9065/f/...85-d8v2jf1.jpg</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11567,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","user":"Jairain","date":". 01-13-2017, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T19:07:58-08:00","id":1043806,"title":"","content":"<b>Boatmans\u2019 Outfit: 3<br /> Winter Outfit: 1<br /> Business: 4</b><br /> <br /> \u201cIf it\u2019s okay\u2026\u201d You look at your feet. \u201cI\u2019d like something I can talk to merchants in. Something so I\u2019ll get taken seriously. I might not\u2026someday you might not be around, Aunt Dwi, and I don\u2019t want to have to work through a middle man if I need to buy or sell something. Something I can wear that will make people take me seriously.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dwi nods. \u201cI see\u2026well, if you really want to get taken seriously you\u2019d need expensive clothes. People with real money or status wear it on them\u2026but I\u2019m guessing I could probably get you clothes that make you look reasonable professional\u2026like a courier or a guild clerk or a craftsmans\u2019 apprentice or something\u2026hm. Yes, I\u2019ll see what I can do.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you, Aunt Dwi.\u201d You give her a slight bow, and she smirks, amused by your attempts at politeness.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you, child.\u201d Dwi chuckles. \u201cYou\u2019ve given me an excuse to go shopping, and something interesting to do this afternoon. The Season of Water is always so foggy and cloudy and gray\u2026you\u2019ve added some color to my morning. And an excuse to chat for a while with Blue Root\u2019s apprentice. I swear, every time the young lady comes by with medicines she stares straight ahead like a horse with blinders and if she catches a glimpse of one of the girls out of the corner of her eye she turns beet red, it\u2019s adorable. One of these days I\u2019m going to persuade her to stick around and become a paying customer\u2026hm. Child, have you had any breakfast? Can I offer you something to eat?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u2026do you want to spend the morning with Aunt Dwi? Actually, it\u2019s still very early: the morning fog outside is heavy and the city is just starting to wake up. For some reason, you find yourself filled with a strange sense of\u2026weight. It\u2019s as though your decision about what to do this morning is going to profoundly alter the shape of your whole life\u2026you got lucky yesterday, but now you feel like the other shoe is about to drop.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>So what <i>are </i>you going to do this morning?</b></div> <br /> <br /> Aunt Dwi always ends up trying to serve poppy juice along with any food she gives you, and even though she acts nice you\u2019re afraid of becoming one of her pretty pet addicts. BUT YOU\u2019LL STAY FOR BREAKFAST, BECAUSE YOU\u2019VE LEARNED TO ABSOLUTELY NEVER TURN DOWN FREE FOOD! <b>(This option is dangerous! Gain Socialize Specialty: Asking for Favors. 3-vote Powerup: If you are able to resist the poppy juice with your current stats, Spend BP to raise Resistance and Spend 3 Merit points to take the Toxin Resistance Merit. Going down this road leads to a life of politics and intrigue. Cutthroat iceblooded murderous intrigue.)</b><br /> <br /> No, you need to get back to your rooftop to check up on your stash of smoking meats to make sure the birds haven\u2019t gotten at it\u2026and eat some of your own breakfast before your smoked fish goes bad. <b>(This option is dangerous! Gain Survival Specialty: Urban Environments. 3-vote Powerup: If you are able to deal with it with your current Survival, Spend BP to raise Survival and 3 Merit Points to gain a potent Familiar. Going down this road leads to a life of crime. Dashing acrobatic rooftop crime.)</b><br /> <br /> Stay here all day. You want to be here when Dwi talks to the alchemist\u2019s apprentice-the conversation might give you some idea of what parts of a River Dragon are valuable. You only brought the fangs and an eyeball, but you have some hide and some meat stashed back at your nest and if Dwi and the apprentice get to talking you can gather more information. <b>(Spend BP to raise Occult to 3 and Bureaucracy to 4. Going down this road leads to a life of magic. Messy, bloody, back-alley magic.)</b><br /> <br /> Go back to your nest\u2026and then to the market! Dwi\u2019s buyer won\u2019t be here until the afternoon, and by then the local market might be flooded with River Dragon teeth! Let Dwi negotiate for what you\u2019ve shown her\u2026but try to sell the rest on your own, early. <b>(This option is dangerous! Spend BP to raise Bureaucracy to 4. Gain Bureaucracy Specialty: Gauging Supply and Demand. 3-Vote Powerup: If you\u2019re able to pull it off with your current Bureaucracy and penalties for being a preteen in tattered rags, you\u2019ll get a chance to Spend 1 Merit Point for Resources 1. Going down this road leads to a life of trade. Predatory, avaricious, pernicious trade.)</b><br /> <br /> Let Dwi handle the business arrangements, and spend your morning tracking down a room to rent. The Emissary gave you enough silver to cover a small apartment for a month, and Dwi should hopefully be making you more money. With a roof over your head and a door between you and the world, you\u2019ll have a safe space from which to start building a life. You can probably even get a closet to hang your new business attire in to keep it looking good. <b>(Stop being homeless! 4-Vote Powerup: You will gain an opportunity to learn to read. This isn't going down a road. It's just getting a cart and packing it before you decide what road to go down.)</b><br /> <br /> You need to spend your morning heading over to the Guild District and opening a bank account. You have cash, and if this deal with the River Dragon bits goes well you\u2019ll soon have more\u2026but on the street you\u2019re one mugging away from losing all this work at any time. If you stash your coin with the Guild, it\u2019ll let you save up so the money will still be there when you need it. It\u2019s spring now, being on the street isnt\u2019 so bad\u2026but you should make sure you can still afford an apartment in nine months\u2019 time when winter is starting. <b>(This option is dangerous! Spend BP to raise Bureaucracy. 6-Vote Powerup: You will gain an opportunity to join the Guild. This road leads to a life of violence. Desperate, disciplined, inevitable violence.)</b><br /> <br /> You should spend your morning visiting Grinning Eel. You can follow up and make sure he still wants an apprentice\u2026and more importantly, you know he has a whole boatful of River Dragon parts. If you can tell him you\u2019ve found a solid buyer, you might be able to get a cut of his windfall as well as your own! <b>(This option is dangerous! Spend BP to raise Sail. 3-Vote Powerup: If you\u2019re able to pull it off, gain the chance to spend a Merit point for Resources 1. This road leads to a dock, and thence to a life on the river. The deep, fast, merciless river.)</b><br /> <br /> You should go to the temple and make a small offering to thank the gods and the Immaculate Dragons for your luck yesterday, and to pray for a good deal with Dwi\u2019s alchemist. The fact that you went looking for help from the Dragons yesterday and then a Dragon showed up to offer you unexpected wealth, and then that night you dreamed about Dragons...well, that\u2019s something to pay attention to. <b>(This option is dangerous! Spend BP to raise Integrity and Occult. 4 Vote Powerup: If you\u2019re able to handle it, you will gain an opportunity to spend 4 Merit points on the Thaumaturgist Merit. This road leads to a life of miracles and wonders. Twisted, unnatural, Wyld wonders.)</b><br /> <br /> \u2026something else? <b>(This option may be dangerous! Spend BP or Merit points as appropriate to the suggested course of action! If it is dangerous\u20264-Vote Powerup: Gain 3 EXP. This road may lead to the Scarlet Throne or the depths of Malfeas...but at least it's a road you chose yourself!)</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Resources You Have Available:</u></b><ul><li>Tattered Rags</li> <li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Steel spearhead (six-inch knife blade with a clumsy handle)</li> <li>One silver Dinar!</li> <li>Three River Dragon Fangs (one big ones, two smaller ones)</li> <li>One River Dragon Eyeball wrapped in cloth</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Resources Back at Your Nest:</u></b><ul><li>Fishhooks (2)</li> <li>A medium sized smoked fish</li> <li>Three River Dragon Fangs (one big one, four smaller ones)</li> <li>A four-by-four swatch of thick, scaly River Dragon hide</li> <li>A River Dragon Spleen? You think it\u2019s a spleen? Tied in a bundle</li> <li>A Spleenful of River Dragon Parts</li> </ul><br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <b><u>You Have Gained:</u></b><br /> <b><u>Attributes: (SPENT)-May be raised with BP.</u></b><br /> <b><u>Abilities: (SPENT)-May be raised with BP.</u></b><br /> Bureaucracy +1 (You will dress\u2026for business!)<br /> <b><u>Specialties: (0/4 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <b><u>Merits: (3/7 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <b><u>Bonus Points: (0/21 Spent)-From now on, every update, we spend at least 1 BP.</u></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 07-01-2017, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T19:56:35-08:00","id":1043826,"title":"","content":"...we are patient, but opportunistic. The last day gave us an incredible windfall - we need to find a way to either save or invest it, if we want to get off the streets for good. I say... invest!<br /> <br /> First choice: rent an apartment. With real clothes and a real place to sleep, we will be <i>much </i>better situated to build ourselves a career in whatever area we choose. Literacy would really help, in any event.<br /> <br /> Second choice: go to the temple and make an offering. Maybe we'd like to learn more about the Faith, and haven't totally given up on becoming a monk yet.<br /> <br /> Third choice: stay all day in a place that is warm and dry. Learn the ways of back-alley magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 02-04-2017, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T20:28:18-08:00","id":1043835,"title":"","content":"An apartment sounds nice, but we don't know if we have the funds to have it last more than one month anyway. Probably a good idea to wait until after we've sold some of our loot. So that will be my <b>3rd Choice</b>. But if we are to make a decent amount we need to know what is worth.<br /> <br /> So my <b>1st choice</b> is to stay here and meet the apprentice alchemist, (we could use some company that isn't competition), and learn a thing or two from her and Aunty Dwi.<br /> <br /> Of course if we are staying anyway, we should <b>HAVE BREAKFAST</b>. Never turn down free food and take it easy on the poppy juice. You need to pay attention when the apprentice arrives. 2nd choice","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T20:29:28-08:00","id":1043836,"title":"","content":"Apartment. Even a poor one is better than our current &quot;residence,&quot; especially in bad weather. Failing that, we managed an amazing feat yesterday, maybe listening in on Aunt Dwi's conversation with the alchemist's apprentice will give more insights we can capitalize on, or if that doesn't work out, a visit to the Temple might not go amiss...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T21:10:47-08:00","id":1043846,"title":"","content":"Apartment and life of trade!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T09:16:51-08:00","id":1044015,"title":"","content":"First choice - Stay for breakfast, and a life of intrigue!<br /> <br /> Second choice - Go and make an offering at the temple. Dreams of a dragon, wealth of a dragon, prayers of a dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T09:41:34-08:00","id":1044031,"title":"","content":"I can't decide between Dancing Eel and the River or the Temple and the Wyld. <br /> <br /> I guess we will find an apartment and figure it out from there.<br /> <br /> My choices:<br /> <br /> 1. Apartment<br /> 2. The Temple<br /> 3. Dancing Eel","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T12:48:10-08:00","id":1044677,"title":"","content":"Firts choice: get an apartment; second choice: stay here all day<br /> <br /> Great stuff as always btw","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T19:28:04-08:00","id":1044824,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to say how much I enjoy this story!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T03:26:41-08:00","id":1044975,"title":"","content":"We could stay for breakfast, head out to rent an apartment and be back in time for the meeting with Dwi &amp; the alchemist's apprentice","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T14:16:55-08:00","id":1051140,"title":"","content":"<b>Leases and Literacy: 7 (WINNER! 4-Vote Powerup Unlocked!)<br /> Breakfast and Intrigue: 3<br /> An Urchin\u2019s Intro to Alchemy: 4<br /> Wyld Times at the Immaculate Temple: 3<br /> Morning in the Market: 1<br /> Dancing with the Eels: 1</b><br /> <br /> It feels strange to turn down free food\u2026but right now, you and Dwi are doing business together, and you don\u2019t want to be in her debt any more than you already are. Besides\u2026staying here, staying warm and dry and enjoying the gentle euphoria of the poppy juice\u2026it\u2019s too tempting. You don\u2019t want to give yourself a chance to rethink your decision not to stay and work for Dwi over breakfast.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you, Aunt Dwi,\u201d you lie, \u201cBut I\u2019ve already eaten this morning. I think I should go, I\u2019ll get in your way if I\u2019m here. Can I leave this River Dragon eyeball and the teeth with you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course, dear.\u201d Dwi nods as you put the goods on her desk. \u201cAnd after I\u2019ve made our deal with the alchemist\u2026how can I find you? I do want to make sure you get your share.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll come back tomorrow morning,\u201d you promise, making your way to the door. \u201cAnd Aunt Dwi\u2026do you know any landlords with cheap rooms to rent?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHm. I know a few...you\u2019re looking to get your own apartment?\u201d You nod. Dwi raises an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cLiving space in Nexus isn\u2019t cheap, child. It\u2019s why so many of my girls choose to live in their rooms here, I give them a discount. Most people split the cost with several room mates\u2026what\u2019s your budget?\u201d<br /> <br /> You\u2019re a little paranoid about telling anyone you have money on you, especially so MUCH of it. Living on the street has taught you to be cagey about that sort of thing\u2026but you decide you can trust Dwi.<br /> <br /> \u201cI, uh, have one Dinar.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m impressed! And do you have any friends who could chip in to split the rent with you?\u201d<br /> <br /> You consider. The closest thing is Rat, and he\u2019s just as broke as you were yesterday. \u201c\u2026no.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHm.\u201d Dwi shrugs. \u201cA Dinar won\u2019t get you very far down here in Nighthammer proper unless you split rent with several other people, there\u2019s too many people who want to live close to the foundries and the dock markets\u2026but if you head north to Nightside, rent is pretty cheap\u2026actually, yes, head to the Blackwall neighborhood and talk to Gleaming Smile. He\u2019s one of my old regulars, and he manages some property there. Mention me and I\u2019m sure he\u2019ll give you a fair bargain. Make sure you get something on at least the second floor.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFloods?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAt least a couple times a year.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks, Aunt Dwi.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPlease, think nothing of it. But you know, for a Dinar, I could let you stay here for\u2026\u201d<br /> You shake your head. She stops.<br /> <div align=\"center\">*****</div> <br /> <br /> Stepping out onto the street, you stuff a wad of rough fabric into your mouth to wet it, then unfold it and tie it once more around your mouth and nose-the masks work better when they\u2019re damp. The Poor Man\u2019s Breath has gotten worse as the morning shift at the foundries has gotten to work, and the fog rolling through the streets is a dingy gray. By nightfall it\u2019ll be black.<br /> Nightside isn\u2019t a long trip, but you make sure to make it take a little longer-you avoid the parts of town where you know some of the bigger kids hang out, and you try to cut a line somewhere between the parts of the markets wealthy enough that you\u2019ll be out of place and the parts poor enough that you\u2019re likely to be jumped. After about an hour, you\u2019ve reached the Blackwall neighborhood.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s\u2026well, if you were out begging today it\u2019s not where you\u2019d be going. The tenement buildings are uneven here, and the roads are little more than muddy tracks. The alleys are tight even for Nexus-you could walk down them without difficulty, but an adult would need to move slowly, and in single file if he was in a group. Blackwall\u2019s name comes from the coloration of its buildings: they\u2019re all just clay bricks and mud and timber supports and straw\u2026and the plaster of the outer walls is discolored below a height of about eight feet from years of Black Snow and repeated flooding. It\u2019s crowded-you bump into plenty of people on your way in-and everyone is wearing masks. Through the hubbub of conversation in the shanty markets, you can hear the constant sound of coughing. Young men with tattoos and long knives tucked into their sashes lurk in doorways smoking and talking quietly to one another.<br /> <br /> Whether it\u2019s the black fog, the drugs, the floods, the violence, or the mold that lingers after the floods recede\u2026people born in Nightside don\u2019t usually make it past thirty, and old folks who move here don\u2019t usually make it more than a decade before the Black Lung takes them.<br /> <br /> But they <i>do </i>have <i>homes</i>! You can see windows open all up and down the squat tenement blocks here, with faces looking out of them. Some of them have flower pots with flowers. You see a few gleaming balls of red amidst the greenery on a rooftop-someone\u2019s tomatoes are coming in. The sky is full of clotheslines flapping in the breeze, and the clotheslines are full of clothes. You\u2019re not sure how you\u2019d feel about wandering this neighborhood after dark, at least before you got to know people\u2026but in the smog-tinged morning sunlight there are little kids chasing each other around in the street and old ladies selling squash and herbs. Even the fishy smell of the shallow canal one block over seems comforting. This neighborhood seems...nice. You\u2019d definitely want to learn all the <i>rules</i>: what alleys are safe and what aren\u2019t, who is friendly all the time and who is dangerous when drunk, and you wouldn\u2019t want to stay here forever\u2026but you think you could find yourself liking Nightside.<br /> <br /> Gleaming Smile isn\u2019t a hard man to find-asking about on the street quickly gets you directed to his \u201coffice.\u201d It\u2019s a run-down room on the first floor of a run-down building. The building is right next to the canal, and the stairs are caked with mold from the floods. A rat as long as your arm stares at you fearlessly from one of the steps, only scampering away as you walk past. When you arrive, you find that Gleaming Smile obviously lives in his office, though he\u2019s drawn a curtain across it to separate his desk and several cabinets of paperwork from his living area. His name fits: his smile is full of false teeth, mostly copper or brass.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo. Dwi sent you, eh?\u201d He smiles, and the light from his open window makes his teeth sparkle in the gloom. He must polish them. \u201cMust be pretty handy \u2018tween the sheets if <i>that </i>old witch is doin\u2019 you favors, eh, boy? Well, you\u2019re lucky. I <i>do </i>have a room to rent. Third floor, even! My current tenant is late on her rent, and not the first time neither. Haven\u2019t seen her in weeks, wouldn\u2019t surprise me if she got her damn self gutted in an alley someplace... Three quarters of a Dinar gets you a month. You pay up front, you stay the month. If I don\u2019t have next month\u2019s rent by the first day of next month, you\u2019re late, and I charge you one eighth-Dinar as a penalty. If I don\u2019t have my money by the sixth day of the month, I come into your apartment, take all your shit, and sell off your possessions to try and cover the rest of the month. And I kick you out on the street. Got it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026got it.\u201d You nod.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood. I take payment in Guild Scrip if you got it. You pay in coin, I give you a monthly discount of one-eighth Dinar, it saves me on exchange fees.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDeal. When can I move in?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFirst you gotta sign a leasing contract agreeing to to all that, <i>plus </i>covering any damages you make to the building. You punch a hole in a wall or something and <i>you </i>pay to fix it. You can\u2019t pay to fix it? Then you WORK to pay to fix it. You owe me on repairs and try to run away or weasel out of it\u2026well, I\u2019ve got a deal with the Iron League, and they track you down. This contract makes it so anyone helping you hide from them is <i>impeding trade</i>. Got me?\u201d<br /> <br /> Gleaming Smile has pulled out a contract and an inkwell from a drawer and placed them on his desk.<br /> <br /> You nod. \u201cI won\u2019t damage anything.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen sign here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI, um. I can\u2019t write.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCan you read, boy?\u201d<br /> <br /> You shake your head.<br /> <br /> \u201cShouldn\u2019t sign something if you can\u2019t read it.\u201d He glowers at you. \u201cIt\u2019s not safe.\u201d<br /> <br /> You give him your best disarming smile. \u201cAunt Dwi told me you drive a hard bargain but you\u2019re an honest man, Gleaming Smile. I trust her taste in men.\u201d<br /> <br /> He gets a chuckle out of that. \u201cShe\u2019s your <i>Aunt</i>, is she? Fair point, lad! Just\u2026put an X right here, and dip your thumb in the inkwell\u2026then wipe it on this cloth\u2026good. Now press your thumb by the X on that line\u2026good. It\u2019s just this once, though. Don\u2019t go signing shit you can\u2019t read! Or at <i>least </i>get somebody you trust as can read it for you!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you. I won\u2019t.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood. Right this way.\u201d<br /> <br /> You\u2019re given a brass key on a braided cord thong and advised to keep it around your neck at all times-replacing a lost key counts as damaging Gleaming Smile\u2019s property, he explains. You go up another flight of stairs and down a hall\u2026to your new apartment! You can\u2019t help being excited. Your heart beats a little faster as Gleaming Smile opens the door.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s\u2026furnished. There\u2019s a wooden table, and a chair, and a cupboard. There\u2019s a closet with hangers. There\u2019s a window-no glass, but bamboo shutters, and a little ledge with a flower pot and a dead plant on it. There\u2019s a chamber pot, and a washbasin, and even a little black iron cooking stove on legs and a wooden box next to it full of pressed charcoal! A bedroll has been rolled out onto the floor and takes up most of the room.<br /> <br /> The whole place stinks-the chamberpot hasn\u2019t been emptied. The hangers in the closet are festooned with adult-sized clothing. The cupboard is open, and appears to be filled with dirty dishes\u2026as is the washbasin. There\u2019s a huge scorch mark on the ceiling above the little iron stove where something cooking below set the ceiling paint alight. There are clothes all over the place, and every surface-the table, the chair, most of the floor and bedroll-is stacked high with crumpled scrolls and empty wine bottles\u2026and books. You\u2019ve never seen so many books!<br /> <br /> \u201cFucking <i>scholars</i>.\u201d Gleaming Smile growls. \u201cBlew all her money on drinks and books, I wager. Owes me two months' back rent, and how am I supposed to make up the loss? Not like I can sell empty bottles\u2026and I\u2019m betting the only other people who\u2019ll buy her fuckin' scrolls and books are other broke wannabe-<i>intellectuals</i>. I swear, if the whole damn University of Nexus went up in flames nobody\u2019s miss \u2018em.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt, um. Seems a bit messy,\u201d you point out.<br /> <br /> \u201cTrue. I can clean all this shit out before you actually move in\u2026or, if you\u2019re willing to save me the trouble and deal with the mess yourself, I can charge you a five eighths of a Dinar instead of three quarters for your first month.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCharge me <i>half </i>instead of five eighths and you have a deal.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s a quarter Dinar for a day\u2019s cleaning? No deal, kid.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFair enough.\u201d You point out. \u201cBut before you make your decision\u2026those wine bottles aren\u2019t all <i>empty</i>.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026the chamberpot was already full.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. OH.\u201d Gleaming Smile looks around. \u201cThat\u2019s\u2026okay, yeah. Fine. Your apartment, your mess. Half a Dinar for the first month\u2019s rent, after that it\u2019s back up to three quarters.\u201d<br /> \u201cDeal.\u201d<br /> <br /> You show him your Dinar, and Gleaming Smile heads back down to the office with you to make you some change. With your discount for paying in silver, you wind up getting your first month\u2019s stay for only three eighths of a Dinar!<br /> <br /> Gleaming Smile gets you a bucket and some soap and advises you to scrub the scorch marks off the ceiling. He also gets you a large woven-wicker basket to put trash in, and requests you dump it down the third floor\u2019s main chute instead of just throwing it all out the window onto the street-piles of trash in public walkways apparently hurt local property values and are an incredible nuisance. He goes on about the subject. At length.<br /> <br /> Finally, he departs, and you\u2019re left in your new home, surrounded by a huge mess. You are about to get to work cleaning the place out\u2026when the clothes hanging in the closet move.<br /> A slightly chubby woman in her early twenties with bags under her eyes and tangled hair pokes its way out from between two coats. She\u2019s wearing thick white foundation and smudged violet lipstick, and round glass lenses held to her ears by a bent wire frame. She looks sort of like an owl might, if it got hungover and somebody attacked it with the contents of Aunt Dwi's makeup kit.<br /> <br /> \u201cIs he gone?\u201d <div align=\"center\">*****</div> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b><u>What now?</u></b></div> <br /> <br /> <b>-Politely but firmly tell her to vacate the premises: this is your apartment now.<br /> <br /> -Tell her she\u2019s been evicted and this is your apartment now\u2026then offer to let her sublease if she can pay half the rent. If you\u2019re lucky and she has even a little money, you can stretch your Dinar into two months\u2019 rent.<br /> <br /> -Send her to Aunt Dwi: you can\u2019t really help this woman with her financial problems while you\u2019re dealing with your own, but Aunt Dwi is always looking for new faces\u2026<br /> <br /> -Show your knife, take whatever items of value she\u2019s got on her, and then hand her over to Gleaming Smile. He\u2019s probably going to want her to pay him back for the scorched ceiling\u2026and any other damages you find while cleaning the apartment.<br /> <br /> -Something Else?</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Resources You Have Available:</u></b><ul><li>Tattered Rags</li> <li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Steel spearhead (six-inch knife blade with a clumsy handle)</li> <li>2 Quarter-Dinars, 1 Eighth-Dinar</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Resources Back at Your Nest:</u></b><ul><li>Fishhooks (2)</li> <li>A medium sized smoked fish</li> <li>Three River Dragon Fangs (one big one, four smaller ones)</li> <li>A four-by-four swatch of thick, scaly River Dragon hide</li> <li>A River Dragon Spleen? You think it\u2019s a spleen? Tied in a bundle</li> <li>A Spleenful of River Dragon Parts</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>You Have Gained:</u></b><br /> <b><u>Attributes: (FINALIZED).</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Abilities: (FINALIZED)</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Specialties: (1/4 Allocated)</u></b><ul><li>Bureaucracy: \u201cHaggling.\u201d</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Merits: (3/7 Allocated)<br /> Bonus Points: (2/21 Spent)-From now on, every update, we spend at least 1 BP.</u></b><ul><li>2 BP Spent: Raised Bureaucracy to 4</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T14:43:08-08:00","id":1051152,"title":"","content":"<b>Tell her she\u2019s been evicted and this is your apartment now\u2026then offer to let her sublease if she can pay half the rent. If you\u2019re lucky and she has even a little money, you can stretch your Dinar into two months\u2019 rent.</b><br /> <br /> ...if she gives you the bed. She can have the floor and closet and keep all her things here taking up space, but the <i>bed. </i>You could have a <i>bed.</i> To sleep in. How awesome is that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T18:27:42-08:00","id":1051269,"title":"","content":"Offer her the sublease. If she doesn't have money, she can pay by giving reading lessons.<br /> <br /> In any case, she should help clean up. It's her mess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T19:16:34-08:00","id":1051299,"title":"","content":"Offer to let her stay, if she pays half the rent and teaches you how to read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T17:07:29-08:00","id":1051757,"title":"","content":"Sublet for half rent AND teaching us how to read. Quarter rent is she has more to offer that could help in the future, education or contacts or such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T20:41:27-08:00","id":1051836,"title":"","content":"...and if she's at all helpful, ask if any of these books contain pictures of river dragon anatomy, so we can know if that thing we grabbed was a spleen or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T15:57:20-08:00","id":1054494,"title":"","content":"She can sublet if she can pay her back rent and half the rent going forward, because Gleaming Smile won't let us sublet if she doesn't pay the back rent. And clean up this mess and let me have the bed.<br /> <br /> Teaching us to read and letting us read her books covers 2 months half-rent though.<br /> <br /> <br /> This afternoon, we should go back to watch Aunt Dwi bargain with the alchemist's apprentice. That will be really helpful for when we sell the other parts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 02-24-2017, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T16:56:14-08:00","id":1054510,"title":"","content":"We're pretty good at bargaining. She can sublet for half the rent, plus teaching us how to read. And we get the bed. If Gleaming Smile wants to collect back-rent from her, she's on her own.<br /> <br /> Still, this is someone with valuable skills and she's obviously in a bad way. Smells like opportunity!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T18:49:47-08:00","id":1054575,"title":"","content":"Smells like something at any rate. This chick didn't even clean the chamber pot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T19:55:30-08:00","id":1054605,"title":"","content":"She couldn't pay her rent before...why do we think she can pay us now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T20:03:05-08:00","id":1054608,"title":"","content":"Part of subletting would be finding out why, and whether half-rent is something she can manage.<br /> Part of getting her to pay off her back-rent is that the landlord will hopefully allow it, and then help evict her if she doesn't pay.<br /> <br /> The alternative is that she pays us nothing and we cover all the rent ourselves. So unless she makes us miserable and continues being a slob, or is drunk a lot, we have nothing to lose.<br /> <br /> Unless we can find a more trustworthy roommate. I doubt that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 02-24-2017, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T18:56:43-08:00","id":1055033,"title":"","content":"<b>Hello, Discounted Rent\u2026I Mean, New Roomie: Unanimous</b><br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, for now,\u201d you tell her. \u201cWho are you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am the Transcendent Princess of Umbral Infini-whoops.\u201d<br /> <br /> In attempting to dramatically exit her closet, she gets caught on a button knocking down a couple hangers with outfits on them and tripping to land on the bedroll. She lies on her back on the bedroll, staring up at the ceiling with an expression of abject despair.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo\u2026this is your mess, then?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe world is my mess,\u201d she moans.<br /> <br /> You look down at her, not entirely sure what to make of the situation. She really reminds you of some of Dwi\u2019s girls who have spent too much time in poppy dreams and too little time in the real world.<br /> <br /> \u201cListen, um\u2026Princess. This is-\u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cTranscendent Princess. Of the Umbral Infinitudes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026okay, that <i>cannot </i>be your real name.\u201d<br /> <br /> Again, she groans. \u201cYou sound just like my father. Cultures all over Creation have coming of age ceremonies where they choose their own names! One\u2019s name should speak of one\u2019s rank, or one\u2019s accomplishments, or one\u2019s aspirations! A name is a thing of power, and to let another choose that name for you is to give up a vital-\u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cLady. I am\u2026I am not calling you Trancing Princess of the Umbral\u2026Infinisims?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cInfinitudes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s an infinitude?\u201d<br /> <br /> She rolls onto her side and rests her head on her hand, looking up at you. \u201cIt\u2019s an uncountably vast number of something. Like if your armies are unending, you have an infinitude of soldiers.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo your name means you\u2019re a princess of unending\u2026what, exactly?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShadows!\u201d She rolls her eyes at you as thought you\u2019re an idiot. \u201cUmbral, it\u2019s an adjective modifying infinitudes. It means \u2018shadowy,\u2019 but it has connotations as well of ghostly or phantom phenomena, or a silent but ever-present companion similar in that respect to one's shadow.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo\u2026you picked a name for yourself that means\u2026\u2019I\u2019m royalty and command a vast army of ghosts?\u2019 then?\u201d<br /> <br /> She rolls her eyes. \u201cShadows. Ghostly is just a connotation.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo this vast army of\u2026shadows\u2026can they, um, do dishes?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGods, you sound <i>exactly </i>like my father! I don\u2019t <i>have </i>a shadow army <i>yet</i>, the name is <i>aspirational</i>! It represents my commitment to achieve my-\u201d<br /> <br /> You close your hand on the handle of your knife, briefly considering actual violence...and then release it, taking a deep breath.This woman is particularly annoying.<br /> <br /> \u201cListen. Princess.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf the-\u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cShut your mouth or I swear to the Dragons I will slit your throat and see how many months\u2019 rent I can get by selling your organs to a back-alley alchemist!\u201d<br /> <br /> She shuts her mouth, and stares up at you, obviously and abjectly terrified. You\u2019ve never actually experienced anyone being\u2026scared of you. It feels odd. But not actually <i>bad</i>\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cYou currently owe Gleaming Smile a bunch of money. Nod your head yes or shake it no.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nods her head. You can see tears welling in her eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you have enough money to pay him back, or a way to GET enough money to pay him back?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shakes her head no.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay. Is all this your mess?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nods her head yes.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd you have NO source of income.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shakes her head again.<br /> <br /> \u201cShit\u2026listen, what\u2019s your <i>real </i>name?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cW-White M-Moth.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay. Moth. What do you <i>do</i>? How <i>were </i>you paying your rent back <i>when </i>you were paying it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI, um. I\u2019m a student. At the University of Nexus. I\u2019m studying funerary traditions and warding rites under the Master of Nine Black Chains. He's from Sijan. I was\u2026I was living on the stipend Mother gave me to cover food and living expenses, but I used it up faster than I meant to.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026this <i>stipend</i>. Was it a one-time thing, or does your Mother give you money regularly?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe, um. She gives me money at the start of each Season.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s Resplendent Water now\u2026so you\u2019ll get more money at the start of Ascending Earth?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nods, sniffling a little.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow much money does your Mother usually give you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not really sure\u2026usually ten or twelve Dinar?\u201d<br /> <br /> You open your mouth in shock. Then you close it again.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2026you spent twelve Dinar\u2026since the start of last month?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nods glumly.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut. But you\u2026twelve\u2026\u201d You find yourself spluttering slightly. \u201cHow?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBooks, mostly. And, um. Wine. And clothes. And makeup? And supplies.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSupplies.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFor the Master of Nine Black Chains. We needed chalk, and incense, and lots and lots of candles, and molten lead, and herbs, and a white goat that had never seen-\u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cShut it.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nods.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay. Here\u2019s the deal. This is <i>my </i>apartment now, Moth. I just signed the lease, I\u2019m renting it out. And I do NOT want your <i>filth </i>all over <i>my </i>apartment. The way I can see it, I can either kick you out\u2026or I can let you stay and just not tell Gleaming Smile about it.\u201d<br /> <br /> White Moth\u2019s eyes widen with hope.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you agree to pay me for half the rent for your time living here. <i>And </i>if you agree to pay Gleaming Smile back for the back rent you owe him. As soon as you get the money from your Mother.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nods, smiling.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlso! If you\u2019re living in my apartment, you will clean up after yourself or I turn you over to Gleaming Smile and he will probably sell you to some whorehouse someplace to get his money back. You will clean your dishes, clean the chamberpots, clean your clothes\u2026and clean yourself, because I swear, lady, I cut up a giant lizard last night and walked past piles of garbage on my way here and we both smell better than you do right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> White Moth is no longer smiling.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlso\u2026you\u2019re going to teach me to read.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou...can\u2019t read?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot yet. But every day you\u2019re gonna teach me. That way if Gleaming Smile catches you <i>before </i>you pay me what you owe me\u2026at least I\u2019ve gotten <i>something </i>in exchange for letting you stay here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026very well, I can use it as a chance to review. It\u2019s a deal...but don't get any creepy ideas about sharing a bedroll or anything!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo objections. I can smell your bedroll from all the way over here. Now help me clean this place up. I\u2019m seriously worried about catching the plague.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, okay\u2026don\u2019t throw out all the empty wine bottles, though. I need a few for Master of Nine Black Chains, so we can make spirit-traps.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026spirit-traps?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTraps for evil spirits.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026okay, another rule. No bringing evil spirits into my apartment.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026deal. Um. Thanks. For letting me stay here, I mean.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t thank me. It\u2019s just cheaper to split rent, Moth.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf we're going to be living together, could you\u2026<i>not </i>call me Moth?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell I\u2019m <i>not </i>calling you <i>Tapdancing Princess of the Umbral Infinitudes</i>.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTranscendent! And why not?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBecause you\u2019re not actually a princess, for one? I can\u2019t believe you picked your own name and that was the best you could come up with.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah? What\u2019s <i>your </i>name, then?\u201d <div align=\"center\">******<br /> <br /> <b>Actually...what <i>is </i>your name?</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Resources You Have Available:</u></b><ul><li>Tattered Rags</li> <li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Steel spearhead (six-inch knife blade with a clumsy handle)</li> <li>2 Quarter-Dinars, 1 Eighth-Dinar</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Resources Back at Your Nest:</u></b><ul><li>Fishhooks (2)</li> <li>A medium sized smoked fish</li> <li>Three River Dragon Fangs (one big one, four smaller ones)</li> <li>A four-by-four swatch of thick, scaly River Dragon hide</li> <li>A River Dragon Spleen? You think it\u2019s a spleen? Tied in a bundle</li> <li>A Spleenful of River Dragon Parts</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>You Have Gained:</u></b><br /> <b><u>Attributes: (FINALIZED).</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Abilities: (28/28 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Specialties: (1/4 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Merits: (4/7 Allocated)</u></b><ul><li>Mentor 1: White Moth</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Bonus Points: (4/21 Spent)-From now on, every update, we spend at least 1 BP.</u></b><ul><li>2 BP Spent: Raise Presence to 3</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 02-25-2017, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T19:56:22-08:00","id":1055048,"title":"","content":"Tavi. Our name is Tavi.<br /> <br /> Also, the Master of Nine Black Chains sounds like a great person to stay away from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 02-26-2017, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T21:06:49-08:00","id":1055071,"title":"","content":"Our name is Ah Fang - meaning &quot;Little Beauty.&quot; Our mother could be a sap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T21:19:22-08:00","id":1055072,"title":"","content":"I totally forgot what our sex/gender is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T21:26:40-08:00","id":1055074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jairain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1055072#post1055072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I totally forgot what our sex/gender is.</div> </div> </div> </div>We went with &quot;Sex - female, gender identity - female, expression - male&quot;. On account of how being a girl on the streets alone sucks even worse than being a boy on the streets alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T22:02:04-08:00","id":1055086,"title":"","content":"Right right right, thanks much for reminding me. Our name is something cool, I can't think this evening. Ah Fang sounds kinda like swearing though...just saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T08:44:26-08:00","id":1055257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1055048#post1055048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tavi. Our name is Tavi.<br /> <br /> Also, the Master of Nine Black Chains sounds like a great person to stay away from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of these things. Let's stay away, and also be named Tavi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T11:22:43-08:00","id":1055320,"title":"","content":"Xualin or Lin for short.<br /> <br /> A name meaning &quot;Elegant gem&quot; or &quot;Outstanding fine jade&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, Transcendent Princess of the Umbral Infinitude would make a great future Abyssal. Though, I think whichever Neverborn who offers her an exaltation may regret it...<br /> <br /> <b>Neverborn: </b> White Moth, you have died. If you wish to live, pledge your service to me and cast your true name into the Void.<br /> <b>White Moth:</b> Sweet! I hated my name anyways. *Ditches name into the void.*<br /> <b>Neverborn: </b> Deathknight, I shall name you....<br /> <b>Nameless Deathknight: </b> Transcendent Princess of the Umbral Infinitude!<br /> <b>Neverborn:</b> I was thinking more Crimson Herald of Unending...<br /> <b>Nameless Deathknight: </b> No! I want to be called Transcendent Princess of the Umbral Infinitude!<br /> <b>Neverborn:</b> That name doesn't strike fear into the hearts of....<br /> <b>Nameless Deathknight:</b> I sold my soul to you. At least I get to pick out my own fucking name!<br /> <b>Neverborn: </b> Alright! I shall name you... Transcendent Princess of ... what was it again?<br /> <b>Transcendent Princess of the Umbral Infinitude:</b> of the Umbral Infinitude<br /> <b>Neverborn: </b> That. Whatever. Just take your exaltation and go. If you annoy the inhabitants of Creation as much as you annoy me, they will commit suicide before next Calibration.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-26-2017, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T14:37:03-08:00","id":1055792,"title":"","content":"I'm going with Tavi, because anything that sounds 'too girly' will give our gender away and all those bad things we talked about happening to other girls on the street are far more likely to happen to us if everytime we introduce ourself we give the game away.<br /> <br /> I am not opposed to that not being our real name though. I do like the other suggestions","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T19:18:32-07:00","id":1070437,"title":"","content":"<b>Tavi: 3<br /> Ah Fang: 1<br /> \u201cSomething Cool\u201d: 1<br /> Xualin: 1</b><br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m Tavi,\u201d you tell her.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s that mean?\u201d White Moth raises an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cMean? It means <i>me</i>.\u201d<br /> <br /> She groans as if in pain. \u201cLook, um, Tavi. If I\u2019m gonna be teaching you, you need to get that words are important. Words have power! A name is a word you give power over you, and the meaning of your name can affect your destiny or get used against you by your enemies! Do you know why you got named Tavi?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI guess my Mother thought it was a nice sounding name. Certainly better than the pile of words you threw together!\u201d<br /> <br /> White Moth frowns. \u201cPrincess-\u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, seriously. If people can\u2019t remember your name, or pronounce it, then what\u2019s the point of even having one?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s aspirational!\u201d Moth seems to be on the edge of tears. You decide not to press her any further, and to change the subject. To something actually useful.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure. Look\u2026right now, your name doesn\u2019t matter, what matters is that this apartment gets clean. Let\u2019s get started.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay.\u201d Moth sits up. \u201cBut I have to leave a little after noon, I have a meditation session scheduled with the Master of Nine Black Chains.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI think we can get the place cleaned up by then,\u201d you declare.<br /> <br /> And so you do! The big trash basket Gleaming Smile gave you comes in handy. Most of the clutter in the apartment goes right into the basket: bottles and inkstained rags and crumpled paper wrappers from the fried food stand down the street, which White Moth apparently frequents regularly. Moth keeps wanting to throw away other stuff too, valuable stuff: dirty dishes, dirty but perfectly serviceable clothes, empty glass bottles\u2026just talking to her is a little grating. She actually suggests throwing away a full-sized fur winter coat because it will \u201cbe out of fashion by next winter anyway.\u201d She gets grumpy when you force her to actually wash her dishes and her clothes.<br /> <br /> The two of you agree to a demarcation of space, and Moth gives up half her closet for your clothes. You let her keep the bedroll, you\u2019ll make a nest in the corner once you bring your pile of clothes over from your current nest. Maybe someday you'll even be able to afford a bedroll of your own. After a dozen or so trips from your new apartment down the hall to the waste chute to clear out piles of garbage...the place is starting to actually look nice! You take a cruel pleasure in teaching an increasingly whiny Moth how to scrub a floor, something she has obviously never done in her life.<br /> <br /> By the time you let White Moth leave for her meditation practice, you have a nice clean wooden floor and a clean chamberpot and some new clothes and a stove and a window of your very own\u2026and most importantly, a door you can put between you and the rest of Nexus. Closing the door after White Moth, you put your hands on your hips and survey your apartment with a sense of pride. You\u2019re a little tired from spending all morning cleaning, and you\u2019re more than a little hungry. It\u2019s early afternoon, so Aunt Dwi is probably meeting with her alchemical contact right about now\u2026what should you do next? <div align=\"center\">*****</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>-Take a nap.</b> Now that you think about it, you\u2019re <i>exhausted</i>! You\u2019ve been sleeping on a hard roof for weeks, and your dreams last night kept you from getting much actual rest. Even before last night hunger has frequently interrupted your sleep. Now you can sleep <i>under</i> a roof, which you\u2019re given to understand is much more comfortable. You deserve a rest after all this work!<br /> <br /> <b>-Go check up on Aunt Dw</b>i. See how the deal went. Unless you make more money you only have this apartment for a couple of months, you need to get out and start hustling to keep your good fortune going! Knowing what your merchandise is going to sell for is important, you need that information to make other decisions!<br /> <br /> <b>-Go get your stuff from your nest and bring it to your apartment.</b> Your clothes will keep longer if you get them out of the weather, and your River Dragon bits, which are hopefully a source of further income, are probably safer behind a locked door than just sitting on a roof where the birds might get at them.<br /> <br /> <b>-Go find something to eat! </b>You have a little money, a rare thing for you! You should get over to the market and load up on cheap durable staples like rice and dried mushrooms! If you can\u2019t find a buyer for your river dragon meat\u2026well, it\u2019s pretty well smoked, so it should keep for a while, and if Dragon tastes anything like lizard it\u2019ll be pretty good in one of your new soup pots, so you should get some bamboo and some spices for stew as well, if you have money left over...a pot of soup can last a good long while, if you keep it simmering.<br /> <br /> <b>-Go set up a bank account.</b> You\u2019re living with a deadbeat and possibly alcoholic roommate now. It's not clear whether she's at all trustworthy! Who knows who else she owes money to in addition to the landlord? You need a safe place to keep your money where she can\u2019t get at it. A bank account with one of the Guild Banks is a way to do just that.<br /> <br /> <b>-Go talk to Gleaming Smile.</b> Tell him about your arrangement with White Moth, and try to persuade him to ignore the back rent she owes him and let her stay with you above board-at least until she gets her allowance from her rich mother. If he lets her stick around until her mother gives her a pile of cash, he stands a better chance of getting his money back than if she leaves-and if her allowance never arrives, he knows exactly where to find her to get it back the hard way. Worst-case scenario, he doesn't agree and drags he away. It\u2019s not like Moth has earned a lot of your loyalty, here, and you don\u2019t want to risk losing your new home by angering your landlord if she gets caught on her way in or out over the next couple of months.<br /> <br /> <b>-Go spend some time with Grinning Eel.</b> Even if the River Dragon thing pans out, that\u2019s just a one-time infusion of money. Nightside is pretty close to a major canal. A stable career like working a canal boat would give you a reliable way to keep a roof over your head and food in your cupboards, and getting that apprenticeship with Grinning Eel started as soon as possible, before he forgets about his deal with you or changes his mind, is the only lead you actually currently have on steady work.<br /> <br /> <b>-Go do...something else?</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Resources You Have Available:</u></b><ul><li>Tattered Rags</li> <li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Steel spearhead (six-inch knife blade with a clumsy handle)</li> <li>2 Quarter-Dinars, 1 Eighth-Dinar</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Resources Back at Your Nest:</u></b><ul><li>Fishhooks (2)</li> <li>A medium sized smoked fish</li> <li>Three River Dragon Fangs (one big one, four smaller ones)</li> <li>A four-by-four swatch of thick, scaly River Dragon hide</li> <li>A River Dragon Spleen? You think it\u2019s a spleen? Tied in a bundle</li> <li>A Spleenful of River Dragon Parts</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Resources at your Nightside Apartment:</u></b><ul><li>A Small Library</li> <li>Dishes (One Cupboard Full)</li> <li>1 Box Pressed Charcoal</li> <li>Small Iron Cooking Stove</li> <li>Several Dozen Empty Wine Bottles</li> <li>A potted plant (Deceased)</li> <li>Some hand-me-down clothes White Moth gave to you rather than throw away</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Resources at your Nightside Apartment:</u></b><ul><li>A Small Library</li> <li>Dishes (One Cupboard Full)</li> <li>1 Box Pressed Charcoal</li> <li>Small Iron Cooking Stove</li> <li>Several Dozen Empty Wine Bottles</li> <li>A potted plant (Deceased)</li> <li>Some hand-me-down clothes White Moth gave to you rather than throw away</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>You Have Gained:</u></b><br /> <b><u>Attributes: (FINALIZED).</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Abilities: (28/28 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Specialties: (1/4 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Merits: (4/7 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Bonus Points: (6/21 Spent)-From now on, every update, we spend at least 1 BP.</u></b><ul><li>2 BP Spent: Willpower 4</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 07-01-2017, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T19:41:48-07:00","id":1070447,"title":"","content":"Put it in the bank, yo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T19:53:09-07:00","id":1070454,"title":"","content":"Bank and then check up on Aunt Dwi","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T19:58:51-07:00","id":1070455,"title":"","content":"Dwi then bank, might as well get all the monies before depositing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T22:27:52-07:00","id":1070490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jairain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1070455#post1070455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dwi then bank, might as well get all the monies before depositing</div> </div> </div> </div>seconded, please","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T05:29:07-07:00","id":1070579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jairain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1070455#post1070455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dwi then bank, might as well get all the monies before depositing</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 03-30-2017, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T07:34:48-07:00","id":1070630,"title":"","content":"Go to Aunt Dwi, even if we missed an opportunity to talk to/watch her talk to and alchemist, we still need to ask how it went. Then the bank, then get our stuff off the roof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T19:43:46-07:00","id":1075684,"title":"","content":"<b>Go to the Bank: 1<br /> Visit Dwi First: 4</b><br /> <br /> You decide to head back to the Flaming Peacock to talk to Aunt Dwi. If she\u2019s gonna be paying you, you might as well have all the money when you go to open up an account with one of the Guild banks. You leave your apartment with more than a little reluctance, but locking the door behind you feels really, really good. You have a place that\u2019s yours!<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a bit of a hike back to the Flaming Peacock-now that it\u2019s mid afternoon, traffic in the streets is much busier. You save yourself some time by cutting through a few alleys and taking some of the rooftop-ways, but still you find yourself panting a bit by the time you arrive at the brothel. You tell Ox at the front door that you\u2019re here to see Dwi and he nods and tells you you\u2019re expected-but to keep quiet and take the left-side stairs behind the beaded curtain right after you go inside. It\u2019s still early, but there are now paying customers in the building-local merchants springing for a quick bit of fun on their late lunch breaks, mostly, and a few sailors in town for a couple days while their ship gets loaded who have now woken after last night\u2019s debauchery.<br /> <br /> As you climb the stairs toward Dwi\u2019s office, the smells of the Flaming Peacock assail you with familiarity and with old memories. Incense and sweat and the cloying scent of opium pipes and sex and wine. It reminds you so much of Mother\u2026You knock politely, and Dwi calls you into her office. Her makeup has been reapplied, and she looks like a gleaming porcelain doll. Also, she\u2019s grinning from ear to ear.<br /> <br /> \u201cDid you know, Tavi, that one can grind a River Dragon tooth into a powder that you can mix with some other herbs to make a tea to increase strength and vitality? Apparently it\u2019s very useful if you own some gladiators and you want them to bulk up quickly and get very aggressive\u2026although apparently some folks just prefer to use it as an aphrodisiac.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, Aunt Dwi. I didn\u2019t know that.\u201d You smile. That sounds promising.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd did you know that you can pickle a River Dragon\u2019s eye in Malfean honey and drink it to gain the power to see invisible spirits for five days and five nights?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat actually sounds really neat. It\u2019s too bad we don\u2019t have any Malfean honey. So\u2026your alchemist is going to buy them, then?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes! Apparently a lot of the other people who helped butcher the thing with you last night had the same idea as you did, so we\u2019re not going to get too much for the teeth\u2026but the eye was a good pick, there\u2019s only one more of those out there so the increased supply won't mess with the demand. I\u2026ahem. I made <i>very </i>sure the apprentice offered us a fair price for it.\u201d Dwi looks as smug as a cat who has just eaten somebody's pet bird.<br /> <br /> \u201cI like the sound of that, Aunt Dwi.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll bet you do! It\u2019s a shame you didn\u2019t get your hands on its tongue or its liver! Apparently if you can smoke the tongue over a sacred brazier under the right constellations, you can eat it and gain the power to talk to birds. And if you bathe in a concoction that includes the bile from the liver, it makes your skin as hard as River Dragon scales so blades can\u2019t harm you. That one would sell really well.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026interesting.\u201d You manage to maintain your composure. Is it possible that the organ you have back at your nest is a liver rather than a spleen? You don\u2019t really know River Dragon anatomy all that well.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlchemy is fascinating.\u201d Dwi nods. \u201cAlthough in my experience, alchemists are more so. I haven\u2019t collected yet, but I\u2019m sure Blue Root will pay up. So here\u2019s your fifty percent. We can go shopping for your clothes once I actually get paid.\u201d<br /> <br /> Aunt Dwi hands you a cheque, written in her careful hand upon thick and ornately decorated Guild stock. You look at it. You\u2026can\u2019t actually read, so you\u2019re not sure what it says, but\u2026<br /> <br /> Dwi seems to recognize your problem. She smiles sweetly. \u201cYour share is 25 Dinar.\u201d<br /> <br /> Your eyes get big. That\u2019s\u2026that\u2019s more than a year of rent!<br /> <br /> \u201cMy advice, Tavi? Go set up a bank account with the Guild. That way you\u2019ll earn some interest on it. And don\u2019t spend it all in one place!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know that I could spend 25 Dinar all in one place if I wanted to, Aunt Dwi!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt seems like a lot of money now, child\u2026but you\u2019d be surprised how fast 25 Dinar can go, when you\u2019re buying food and clothes and real medicine. And especially when you need to buy coal and oil in the winter. Be frugal.\u201d<br /> <br /> You nod, stupefied.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis is a cheque drawn on my account with the Guild. It\u2019s made out to you by name. This way you don\u2019t have to carry all that coin on you. But don\u2019t lose it or get it stolen, child.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course not! I\u2019ll head over to the Guild district right away and put it in account!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood. I recommend you try the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants, their interest rates are good and they\u2019ve been around a long time so you know they\u2019re not going to invest all your money on a risky caravan route and go belly up. And you might want to put most of it into a sealed account without cheques so you get a better interest rate on it and you don\u2019t have the option to spend it without a penalty. That way you have to save it for when you really need it. Wish I'd set one of those up back when I was your age...\u201d<br /> <br /> You nod, and smile, and shake Dwi\u2019s hand, and you head down the stairs feeling lightheaded.<br /> <br /> Twenty five Dinar! That\u2019s food for months! That\u2019s enough to buy a small herd of goats, or a few milk cows! That\u2019s enough to buy a bow, or a really finely forged sword! That\u2019s enough for all the weaving supplies you could ask for! For that much money you could buy a cart and a permit and start your own business in one of the street markets selling baskets or carpets or something! Or you could buy a big coop and a bunch of chickens and start a rooftop farm and sell fresh eggs to all the market stalls, and pay Gleaming Smile to let you use the roof! That\u2019s enough money to hire some people to work <i>for </i>you for a few weeks!<br /> <br /> Wandering through the crowded street markets, you don\u2019t notice the smell of sweetrolls or frying meats, or the sound of sizzling noodles, all things that would normally fill you with irrepressible longing. You are so distracted by your thoughts of what you could do with all that money, in fact, that you turn into a shortcut alley on the way to the Guild district and run right into the Leopard Gang. You stop just short of physically bumping into their leader, Seven Leopard. He\u2019s holding a middle aged and balding man up against the wall of the alley by the front of his shirt, and holding a curved knife to the man\u2019s gut. The man is sweating profusely and rustling in his purse with one hand, a desperate expression on his face.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, kid.\u201d Seven Leopard looks lazily over at you, without letting go or easing up on his knife. \u201cHow\u2019s it goin\u2019? Don\u2019t see you much over on this side of the market.\u201d<br /> <br /> You bow deeply. Seven Leopard likes that sort of thing. He thinks of himself as a criminal with class.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am doing well, Seven Leopard. It\u2019s an honor to see you at work.\u201d<br /> <br /> Several of Lepoard\u2019s thugs smirk or chuckle. There are six of them. From time to time these guys shake down you or the other urchins who operate in the market-in exchange for being allowed to operate in \u201ctheir territory,\u201d they take a cut of whatever gains you make from pickpocketing or begging or stealing in the market. They don't usually do more than rough you up a bit-most of them were street kids themselves before they got big, and they tend to go easy during the winter. Rat tells you he's done some lookout work for them, and they treat you okay as long as you're working for them and Seven Leopard is around to keep order.<br /> <br /> \u201cJust keepin\u2019 the neighborhood safe.\u201d Seven Leopard smiles. \u201cYou see this bastard here? He\u2019s been selling Qat. Not the good stuff, though. Nasty shit. Got a friend of mine real sick. Guy stops eating, starts getting real bad stomach pains. Then he goes all nuts and starts tryin' to paint all the walls he can find, but he doesn\u2019t have any paint so he starts stealing peanut sauce from the market and getting it all over anything he can reach. Nearly bit my nose off when we tried to calm him down. Just doesn\u2019t seem <i>right </i>to do that sorta thing, not without givin\u2019 the neighborhood some sort of <i>compensation</i>, does it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot at all, Seven Leopard.\u201d You nod.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, it\u2019s just not the kind of business we want around here.\u201d Leopard pokes the point of his knife into the sweating merchant\u2019s gut. \u201cTell me, boy, what do you think we oughta <i>do </i>with garbage like this?\u201d<br /> <br /> The Leopard Gang is smirking and sniggering\u2026and apparently waiting for your answer.<br /> <br /> What should you say?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>-You should kill him. He doesn\u2019t matter much, but it\u2019ll send a warning to the other garbage like him.<br /> <br /> -You should take the profits he made from selling his Qat. No need to hurt him, since nobody really got <i>hurt</i>, but he shouldn\u2019t get any benefit out of selling inferior product in your market.<br /> <br /> -You should mark his face, so people know not to mess with the Leopard Gang. That\u2019s what that big curved knife is for, right? Leaving impressive scars?<br /> <br /> -You should get him to give you the name of his supplier. This guy\u2019s just the middleman-if you <i>really </i>wanna protect the neighborhood, Leopard, you need to track down his source, or you\u2019re just gonna get somebody else selling the same shit here tomorrow.<br /> <br /> -You should let the poor bastard go. If we rough up all the merchants selling inferior goods around here\u2026well, soon we won\u2019t have any merchants left. If you have good stuff, you sell it in the rich parts of town. If you scare away all the guys doing business in your neighborhood, Leopard, the money will dry up, and that's no good for anybody.<br /> <br /> -Throw him in the canal. What else would we do with garbage?<br /> <br /> -Make a public example of him. Take him out in the market and make him apologize to everyone for selling his tainted qat.<br /> <br /> -Look, Leopard, you already scared him shitless. Just let the poor bastard go home. He\u2019s just trying to make ends meet, just like the rest of us.<br /> <br /> -Don\u2019t say anything, just pull out your knife and stab the bald guy yourself. You know from experience the Leopard Gang is gonna shake <i>you </i>down next, and showing a bit of killer instinct will make them think twice-and hey, impressing them isn't a bad idea. You might need to hire some muscle a little ways down the road...<br /> <br /> -Don't say anything, just run. You know they'll shake you down next, but you can probably lose them in the crowded market, and they probably won't be eager to chase a street urchin who's likely to only have a pocketful of food or stolen coin when they have a bigger fish in hand already.<br /> <br /> -Something else?</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Resources You Have Available:</u></b><ul><li>Tattered Rags</li> <li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Steel spearhead (six-inch knife blade with a clumsy handle)</li> <li>2 Quarter-Dinars, 1 Eighth-Dinar</li> <li>A Cheque for 25 Dinars from Aunt Dwi!</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Resources Back at Your Nest:</u></b><ul><li>Fishhooks (2)</li> <li>A medium sized smoked fish</li> <li>Three River Dragon Fangs (one big one, four smaller ones)</li> <li>A four-by-four swatch of thick, scaly River Dragon hide</li> <li>A River Dragon Spleen? You think it\u2019s a spleen? Tied in a bundle</li> <li>A Spleenful of River Dragon Parts</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Resources at your Nightside Apartment:</u></b><ul><li>A Small Library</li> <li>Dishes (One Cupboard Full)</li> <li>1 Box Pressed Charcoal</li> <li>Small Iron Cooking Stove</li> <li>Several Dozen Empty Wine Bottles</li> <li>A potted plant (Deceased)</li> <li>Some hand-me-down clothes White Moth gave to you rather than throw away</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>You Have Gained:</u></b><br /> <b><u>Attributes: (FINALIZED).</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Abilities: (28/28 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Specialties: (2/4 Allocated)</u></b><ul><li>Larceny Specialty: Nexus Street Gangs +1</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Merits: (4/7 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <b><u>Bonus Points: (8/21 Spent)-From now on, every update, we spend at least 1 BP.</u></b><ul><li>Larceny 4 (2BP)</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 04-09-2017, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T20:29:38-07:00","id":1075697,"title":"","content":"Since we are all economic now, we should teach the Leopard's a lesson. Convince them to get the name of the supplier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T20:54:30-07:00","id":1075702,"title":"","content":"I agree, name of supplier. We could draw our knife and demand the info gaining some of the respect stabbing him might get us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T21:27:11-07:00","id":1075719,"title":"","content":"Tell them to get the name of the supplier... and run as soon as they all look away.<br /> <br /> We do <i>not </i>want to get mugged while carrying more money than we'd ever dreamed of possessing until now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T04:50:01-07:00","id":1075836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1075719#post1075719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell them to get the name of the supplier... and run as soon as they all look away.<br /> <br /> We do <i>not </i>want to get mugged while carrying more money than we'd ever dreamed of possessing until now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. Also, let's try to avoid selling bad Qat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T09:05:42-07:00","id":1075917,"title":"","content":"Supplier... and apology. And scat at the first opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T13:40:23-07:00","id":1076077,"title":"","content":"Yeah, get the name of the supplier...and make a quick exit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T20:50:56-07:00","id":1086040,"title":"","content":"<b>Get Name of Supplier: 6<br /> Apology: 1<br /> Show of Force: 1<br /> Run Away: 4</b><br /> <br /> <br /> You take a deep breath. This\u2026really wasn\u2019t something you wanted to have to deal with today. The Leopard Gang isn\u2019t as bad as some of the people you could run into in an alley in Nexus\u2026but they\u2019re not good people to run into in an alley either.<br /> <br /> \u201cLeopard, you should get him to give you the name of his supplier. This guy\u2019s just the middleman-if you <i>really </i>wanna protect the neighborhood, you need to track down his source.\u201d You frown, trying to create the impression that this is deep thought that you\u2019re really straining over, and not a basic and obvious conclusion they should have come to on their own. Nobody likes a smartass. \u201cOtherwise\u2026you\u2019re just gonna get somebody else selling the same shit here tomorrow. And I figure the source is the guy who\u2019s making the real money, so he\u2019s better to shake down, too, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> Seven Leopard blinks slowly\u2026then smiles.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, kid. You\u2019re not as dumb as you look!\u201d He turns back to the bald drug peddler and leans in. \u201cHow about you tell us who\u2019s selling you the stuff?\u201d<br /> <br /> Once everybody is focused on the interrogation\u2026you take the opportunity to slip back out of the alley and lose yourself in the crowded market again. You hope you haven\u2019t just started another turf war\u2026but mostly you\u2019re cursing yourself for letting haste to get to the bank cause you to forget your caution. Taking a shortcut through back alleys with tons of money on you? You\u2019re a Nexus native, not some farm girl tourist fresh off a boat! You shake your head ruefully as you take the slower, longer way toward the Guild District. You skirt the southern edge of Sijantown, switchback over the rooftops to avoid some neighborhood patrols in Lookshytown (you\u2019re not welcome there since you almost got caught pickpocketing a few months ago-the Lookshyan military folk stationed here are out of towners and easy targets, but they\u2019re not known for being friendly to thieves) and then cut south towards the Nexus district. You give River Park a wide berth, which costs you an hour or so, but nobody smart goes in there on their own.<br /> <div align=\"center\">****</div> <br /> <br /> After a longish trip, you arrive in the Nexus District, and make your way towards Yinhang Square. You need to ask directions a couple of times-it\u2019s not often you\u2019re traveling in this part of town-before you find the offices of the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants. The grizzled looking mercenary at the door wrinkles his nose and gives you an appraising look\u2026but lets you go in.<br /> <br /> The offices of the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants are filled with polished wood and decorated with elaborate carvings and gilt inlays. You can see through a door in the back that clerks are bustling about putting large scrolls into wooden drawers in the back room, but out front there is just an elderly gentleman in expensive silk robes sitting at a desk. He is wearing narrow spectacles and reading a ledger. As you arrive, he looks up.<br /> <br /> \u201cHello, young man,\u201d he says. \u201cIs there something I can\u2026help you with?\u201d He gives a questioning glance at the mercenary guarding the door, who simply shrugs.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, I hope.\u201d You bow. Old people like that sort of thing. \u201cI am looking to open an account, and my Aunt Dwi recommended your bank as particularly dependable.\u201d<br /> <br /> The old man raises an eyebrow. \u201cDwi, eh? Hrm. She understands we only give our clients credit for referring to us new clients of\u2026quality, yes?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was not aware you gave your clients credit for referring people at all.\u201d You shrug. \u201cI recently\u2026came into possession\u2026of some alchemical supplies, and she helped me with the negotiations to sell them. My cut is twenty five dinar. Is that \u2018quality\u2019 enough?\u201d<br /> <br /> The man closes his book and strokes his thin white beard, an expression of amusement spreading across his dour face. \u201cIndeed, child. Come, have a seat in my office, and we shall talk. FENG! Get out here and watch the desk!\u201d<br /> <br /> A harried-seeming clerk emerges from the back office and takes the man\u2019s place at the desk, as he stands and walks around to grip your hand in a cool and somewhat dry handshake.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am Fifteen-Fingers Liu, the senior accountant in this office of the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchant Company. It is a pleasure to meet you, young\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTavi.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYoung Tavi. Right this way.\u201d<br /> <br /> You are guided to a small office with silk tapestries on the walls depicting frogs in suits of armor doing battle with one another on an elaborately rendered landscape. Fifteen-Fingers Liu takes a seat behind another desk, and gestures for you to sit opposite him in a huge and, you quickly learn, ridiculously comfortable leather chair. On the desk, there is a miniature tree in a pot\u2026and an abacus with gleaming red beads.<br /> <br /> \u201cTavi. Do you have a cheque?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, sir.\u201d You show him the slip of paper Aunt Dwi gave you. He takes it and looks it over, then smiles.<br /> <br /> \u201cVery good. Do you have regular work, boy, or is this money a singular windfall?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell\u2026I\u2019m hoping to get more regular work. I\u2019m hoping to apprentice myself to a canal boatman.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAn honorable profession for a young man.\u201d Liu nods. \u201cWhere are you staying?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIn Nightside. It\u2019s well above street level,\u201d you add quickly, seeing him frown. \u201cI have a nice apartment. It\u2019s small, but it\u2019s a fair price.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat fair price, exactly?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s three quarters of a Dinar per month, in Guild Scrip\u2026but I get a discount, so it\u2019s only five pieces of eight if I pay in coin.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you know if your landlord takes cheques?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUm. He didn\u2019t say. But I don\u2019t think so.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not surprising.\u201d Liu sighs. \u201cBut we can certainly get you Guild-backed scrip or silver, if that\u2019s what you need. Other than your housing, do you have any other significant regular expenses?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026not\u2026really?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen I am going to recommend to you our most basic account\u2026and also a separate fund for the purpose of saving money. I think you should consider giving yourself a few dinars to live on and put the rest into one of our interest bearing accounts. That way you make a little money. The salt rate is unusually high these last few months, so it might be a good idea to put a hefty chunk of your funds into an account with a fixed rate and a reasonably long term.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026\u201d You\u2019re not really sure what to do, here. You\u2019re really good at haggling and barter and pricing, but you\u2019ve never really actually dealt with interest rates or bank accounts or anything like this, and you\u2019re feeling a bit out of your depth. \u201cYou\u2019re going to\u2026pay me\u2026to put my money into one of these accounts. Why? How do you make money off all this?\u201d<br /> <br /> The old man smiles. \u201cAh, the most important question in any business arrangement! You have a good head on your shoulders, Tavi. On these types of accounts, you agree not to take your money back for a fixed term-sometimes a year, sometimes five, sometimes ten. We agree to pay you based on how long you leave your money with us-the longer, the more we pay. We take your money and we invest it-we might loan it to people looking to start businesses and make money off the loans, we might buy a stake in a company we think is going to be profitable, we might simply combine it with lots of other clients\u2019 money and deposit it into a similar account at a larger bank that will offer us a better rate than we are offering you because we have more money. At the end of the term, we agree to pay you back a fixed amount, regardless of whether or not we\u2019ve made a profit.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd\u2026what happens if I need the money before the, um, term\u2026is over?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe give you back your money\u2026but you pay a penalty. Instead of making money, you\u2019ll lose a little bit, because you broke our arrangement.\u201d<br /> <br /> You frown in thought. \u201cSo the money is useless now, but at the end of the term I have more of it\u2026what happens if your bank goes out of business while you have it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s\u2026unlikely. The Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchant Company has been in business for one hundred and forty years. We have four offices here in Nexus, as well as offices in Calin, Great Forks, and Thorns. In the unlikely event that something disastrous were to happen to our branches here in Nexus, our remote offices would honor the company\u2019s commitments-we didn\u2019t last as long as we have by keeping all of our eggs in one basket. You might need to take the official records of your ownership of your accounts to another bank to act as a go-between on your behalf, but they would be able to recover your funds eventually.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026okay. I want to make sure I can afford to pay rent this winter, though.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen how do you feel about keeping ten dinars for yourself and locking up the remaining fifteen? That will get you most of the rest of the year. I can set you up with an account with a term of nine months, that way if you haven\u2019t found reliable income you will have access to your funds again before your rent money runs out.\u201d<br /> <br /> You nod. \u201cThat\u2026that sounds good.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cExcellent. These are our most common types of account, so I have copies of the paperwork all ready, just awaiting your signature.\u201d Liu pulls out a desk drawer and pulls out two large scrolls. \u201cBefore you sign anything, I want you to understand how your regular cheque account works. We will start out with your ten Dinars. You may visit me here and put more money in whenever you like, and you may also come here to withdraw money in Guild Scrip or in silver\u2026and in Realm Scrip, Cowries, or even Jade, if you\u2019re willing to pay a rather hefty fee to cover the cost of shipping. We will offer you cheques you can use to pay any merchant who will accept the credit of the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchant Company, which is most of them. Please be aware that if you give someone a cheque for more money than you have we will honor it\u2026but you will be borrowing money from us. If we are not paid back before the end of that day\u2019s business, we will charge you a sizeable fee. If we are not paid back after a week, we will close your account and send debt collectors after you. While pressing you into slavery is not legal within Nexus, chaining you a treadmill and forcing you to work off your debts grinding grain into meal at a ridiculously low hourly wage without breaks or much in the way of food\u2026is. Do you understand?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes.\u201d You smile. \u201cI\u2019ll make sure not to spend more money than I have.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cVery good.\u201d Fifteen-Fingers Liu grins. \u201cNow that we understand each other\u2026the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants pride ourselves on the quality of our service. If there is ever anything we can help with, if you ever need any financial advice, if you ever believe you have been treated unfairly in a business dealing\u2026we have resources available to help you, some free and some for a nominal fee. Please sign here\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> You pretend to look the documents he\u2019s handing you over carefully\u2026but you can\u2019t actually read. You figure Aunt Dwi wouldn\u2019t steer you too wrong, though\u2026so you sign.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd here\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> You sign again.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd here as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> Aaand you sign a third time.<br /> <br /> \u201cCongratulations! You now have two accounts with us.\u201d Liu takes your cheque from Dwi. \u201cI will deposit this for you. While I do, please take this.\u201d<br /> <br /> He hands you thick book bound in red leather. It has an ornately rendered flower embossed on the front.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe front few pages are a testament to your ownership of an account with us. The rest of the book is a complementary ledger that you can use to record your transactions and keep track of your expenses and your account balances. We recommend that you write down anything you purchase and make a record of how much you have in your account afterwards. That way you won\u2019t accidentally spend more money than you have. There is also a book of cheques in there you can use to make payments if you don\u2019t want to carry cash\u2026and there\u2019s a small seal you can ink and then press on your cheques. We won\u2019t accept a cheque as valid unless it has the unique seal we give you today, we\u2019ll assume it\u2019s been stolen from you and fraudulently filled out.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCan I get a new seal if this one gets stolen?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course! They\u2019re not free, though, so please take care with that one. Lots of people wear them on thongs around their necks. I personally usually keep mine here at our offices and stamp cheques in advance so I\u2019m not carting it about the market.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHm.\u201d You\u2019re not sure if leaving it back at the apartment with White Moth is the safest place for it. You open the ledger as Liu leaves the office and heads back to give your cheque from Dwi to one of the clerks in the back. It looks like several people have come in while you were speaking to him, and they\u2019re speaking to a clerk at the counter and handing him papers or getting papers in return. Probably withdrawing money as Guild Scrip\u2026<br /> <br /> Liu returns, and gives you a slip of parchment with a seal imprinted on it.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis is a receipt for you, a record of how much money you have deposited and how much you currently have in your accounts with us. If we ever cheat you, you can take this to the local Guild offices and request that they take punitive action\u2026not that that\u2019s going to happen. We didn\u2019t get to be as successful as we are by getting ourselves a bad reputation.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you, Fifteen-Fingers Liu,\u201d you say, standing and bowing slightly. \u201cYou have been very helpful.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are most welcome, Tavi.\u201d Liu chuckles. \u201cIs there anything else I can help you with?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUm. Can I get a little bit of Guild Scrip from my account? I want to have just a bit of cash on me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIndeed.\u201d He leads you to the counter and shows you how to ask the clerks for a withdrawal. You tuck the money into your shirtfront.<br /> <br /> \u201c I wish you luck, Tavi. And\u2026be careful with abruptly coming into the possession of expensive goods. It can be a good start to a career, to be sure\u2026but it\u2019s best to get regular work. I did some freelance\u2026finding\u2026of valuable items back when I was about your age. It can be a dangerous business.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you, sir.\u201d You bow again, and tuck your ledger into your shirt as Liu shows you out.<br /> <br /> By now, it is late afternoon. The sun will be setting in a bit over three hours\u2026and it\u2019s about an hour and forty minutes back to your home neighborhoods if you take the same route you took here. You could probably get home in half that time if you took some shortcuts through more dangerous sections of town\u2026but you\u2019re not eager to give that a try carrying your new account ledger and seal and cash.<br /> <br /> What should you do now? Ha, who are you kidding? You have most of your money safely stashed away, and you can hide the silver back home to pay rent next month\u2026but you have a Dinar worth of scrip! That\u2019s a whole month\u2019s wages for most people! And you\u2019re in the Guild District! There\u2019s no WAY you\u2019re not going to do some shopping on your way home. If you leave yourself a bit of cash for a canal boat home, it\u2019ll drop you off just a couple blocks from your Nightside apartment. That way you won\u2019t have to carry stuff a long way.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>No, the real question is\u2026you\u2019re going to budget yourself six of your sixteen bills of scrip for shopping. What are you going to buy?</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clothes</b>! Dwi might get you a fancy set, but you\u2019d like some plain utilitarian clothes as well. Stuff with belts and pockets. And perhaps a thong-necklace to hold a coinpurse around your neck. A durable new outfit will set you back about two of your sixteenth-Dinar bills, so you could afford a couple. And for a sixteenth-Dinar, you could afford a nice bag to carry your stuff in. If you're gonna get clothes...you should get them first, so other merchants will take you more seriously.<br /> <br /> <b>Livestock!</b> You don\u2019t have room for sheep or goats, and you\u2019re not sure you could afford to feed them\u2026but you can get one chicken for a sixteenth-Dinar, or three for two! Chickens can live on cheap grain or seeds, or table scraps in a pinch\u2026and they produce eggs! Eggs mean stable income. It\u2019d be a bit of a pain to set up a hutch for them in your new apartment, but it\u2019s well within your crafting expertise, and it\u2019d be free food for the winter\u2026and chickens are free meat, if times get tough. For a sixteenth Dinar you could also probably get some seeds to plant in your little flower pot. Perhaps something like cabbage or herbs that will grow and can be eaten a little at a time all year round...<br /> <br /> <b>Weaponry!</b> Your makeshift spearhead-knife is okay\u2026but for a sixteenth-Dinar you could buy a REAL knife. Something solid and durable, made of good Nexus steel and intended for mercenaries or Lookshyan soldiers. For just a little less you could get a stout walking staff\u2026and for three sixteenths you could get yourself a dependable hatchet\u2026you could afford something big like a mace or a trident, but you\u2019re pretty sure you couldn\u2019t lift it.<br /> <br /> <b>Crafting Supplies:</b> You\u2019re a pretty decent weaver, and supplies are cheap. You could buy a big bundle of bamboo and heat it and split it in your new apartments to weave whatever you need: baskets, chicken hutches, perhaps decorative bracelets\u2026it could be a safe indoor way to make yourself some more money. A big brace of bamboo will set you back three sixteenths\u2026and if you decide to buy twine and needles and a big steaming pot it\u2019ll cost you five sixteenths.<br /> <br /> <b>Occult Supplies:</b> You\u2019ve been lucky lately\u2026but bad luck comes after good! For five sixteenth-Dinars in scrip you could afford a decent lucky talisman from a spiritualist\u2019s stall, to ward off ill fortune and sickness.<br /> <br /> <b>Food:</b> Bags of dry rice. Bags of grain. Bags of dried beans. Butter. Salt. You have money now-spend it buying in bulk so you have food for the next few months. A single sixteenth-dinar bill will get you two ten-pound bags of rice, or an eight pound bag of grain or beans, or a pound of butter, or half a pound of salt (which has gone up in price lately).<br /> <br /> <b>Lockpicks. Cat\u2019s paws. Crowbars. Climbing equipment.</b> All of it would set you back about four sixteenths\u2026but you\u2019ve already proved to yourself that you\u2019re okay with picking people\u2019s pockets. If you\u2019re willing to sneak into their homes and pick their jewelry boxes, you could earn that money back fast.<br /> <br /> <b>Pickling Supplies:</b> You have a bunch of River Dragon bits...some of which might be useful. If you can get some glass jars and some brine or vinegar for pickling...well, if you can find the right books, you might be able to pull of some magic. Being able to talk to birds or being impervious to blades...that sounds pretty handy! And worst case, pickling the meat will preserve it for use as food. And you might be able to pickle other stuff like eggs or vegetables to make sure they keep. A couple of big clay jugs and brine will cost you three sixteenths...five if you want to spring for glass.<br /> <br /> <b>Interior Decor: </b>For four sixteenths, you could get a nice bedroll of your own, so you don't have to sleep on the hard floor or on Moth's bedroll. For one, you could get some cozy throw pillows, or a heavy blanket which will be handy once it gets cold in a few months.<br /> <br /> <b>Actually\u2026screw shopping.</b> You have a bunch of potentially very valuable River Dragon bits sitting in a chimney possibly going bad. You ought to head home as quickly as possible to secure them before flies and birds can get at them! If you\u2019re lucky and one of the pieces is alchemically useful\u2026well, you could have a lot more money to shop with.<br /> <br /> <b>Actually\u2026screw shopping.</b> You\u2019ve been getting by on no money for plenty of time now. You should safe your cash against a real emergency and instead see if you can track down Grinning Eel and see about that apprenticeship.<br /> <br /> <b>Actually\u2026something else!</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Resources You Have Available:</u></b><ul><li>Tattered Rags</li> <li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Steel spearhead (six-inch knife blade with a clumsy handle)</li> <li>2 Quarter-Dinars, 1 Eighth-Dinar</li> <li>1 Dinar in Guild Scrip (16 Bills, each one sixteenth Dinar)</li> <li>Personal Seal issued by the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants</li> <li>Ledger Book</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Account Balances with the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants</u></b><ul><li>Personal Account: 9 Dinars</li> <li>Time Deposit Account: 15 Dinars (Fixed Return of 9% after 9 Months)</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Resources Back at Your Nest:</u></b><ul><li>Fishhooks (2)</li> <li>A medium sized smoked fish</li> <li>Three River Dragon Fangs (one big one, four smaller ones)</li> <li>A four-by-four swatch of thick, scaly River Dragon hide</li> <li>A River Dragon Spleen? You think it\u2019s a spleen? Tied in a bundle</li> <li>A Spleenful of River Dragon Parts</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Resources at your Nightside Apartment:</u></b><ul><li>A Small Library</li> <li>Dishes (One Cupboard Full)</li> <li>1 Box Pressed Charcoal</li> <li>Small Iron Cooking Stove</li> <li>Several Dozen Empty Wine Bottles</li> <li>A potted plant (Deceased)</li> <li>Some hand-me-down clothes White Moth gave to you rather than throw away</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>You Have Gained:</u></b><br /> <b><u>Attributes: (FINALIZED).</u></b><br /> <b><u>Abilities: (28/28 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Specialties: (2/4 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <b><u>Merits: (4/7 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <b><u>Bonus Points: (11/21 Spent)-From now on, every update, we spend at least 1 BP.</u></b><ul><li>Thinking fast, talking fast, getting the hell out of a dangerous situation fast: Wits 3: 3BP</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 07-01-2017, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T22:09:51-07:00","id":1086071,"title":"","content":"I am really enjoying the adventure. I vote for pickling supplies (glass), then go back for your stuff, and then tell another young kid about your abandoned sleeping space. It is always good to do good and a warm sleeping space can save a kid's life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T22:16:40-07:00","id":1086073,"title":"","content":"Pickling Supplies and go back to get the rest of the stuff out of the chimney.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T06:05:00-07:00","id":1086157,"title":"","content":"3 sixteenths for clothes and a carrying bag, 2 sixteenths for clay pickling jars, and 1 sixteenth for a real knife. <br /> <br /> That will give us a nice, well-rounded inventory to work with. We can start working for Eel, warm and protected by work-clothes, armed against thieves, and able to preserve not only our river-dragon bits but also any fish we happen to pick up during off-hours on the job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T06:48:11-07:00","id":1086171,"title":"","content":"Get our stuff from the nest, mention the nest to some kid who's in the same state we were, then go to Aunt Dwi about getting the river dragon bits appraised. After that, a decent knife is an extremely useful tool, then go talk to Eel about that apprenticeship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T08:19:19-07:00","id":1086209,"title":"","content":"I'm going to buck the trend and suggest... food and livestock. We've never had a chicken before, but it seems like a great time to start!<br /> <br /> Pickling supplies are way too ambitious. We have no idea how to use them, and we're going to spend a lot of money on the potential that it'll make stuff last longer? We should just sell the bits and be done with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T15:02:04-07:00","id":1086347,"title":"","content":"Clothes, weapon, livestock. But seriously we gotta get the rest of that river dragon now that we have an idea of the value. If we also invest in a good luck charm then sell the river dragon bits it is a fun gamble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T15:22:39-07:00","id":1086356,"title":"","content":"Crafting Supplies and Pickling Supplies, and a stout walking stick!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T15:50:54-07:00","id":1086369,"title":"","content":"Clothes and a bag (3/16): nice duds from Aunt Dwi are fine, but we need some stout working clothes.<br /> A proper knife (1/16): we were able to talk our way past the Leopard Gang, but that may not always be possible.<br /> Food (2/16): let's lay in a stock of some basics.<br /> <br /> With food, shelter, clothing, and some financial security we can focus on making the most of our good fortune. Speaking of which...<br /> <br /> As soon as we're done with the shopping our very next priority needs to be recovering the rest of the stuff we have at the chimney. Pickling supplies are a waste; we don't know what we're doing and we can't read (so, books won't help!). Which means the River Dragon parts are only valuable as something we can turn into money. Let's do that right away, before they go bad or go missing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T13:52:36-07:00","id":1095225,"title":"","content":"<b>Buy Pickling Supplies: 4<br /> Get the Stuff From Your Nest: 4<br /> Pass Nest on to Another Urchin: 2<br /> Buy Clothes and Carrying Bag: 3<br /> Buy The Real Knife: 4<br /> Buy A Stout Walking Stick: 1<br /> Take the other Bits to Aunt Dwi: 1<br /> Go Talk to Eel about the Apprenticeship: 1<br /> Buy Food and Livestock: 3<br /> Buy a Good Luck Charm: 1<br /> Buy Crafting Supplies: 1</b><br /> <br /> \u201cPhantom Peppers, imported from Sijan! Fresh Phantom Peppers!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cStep right up, ladies and gentlemen, step right up! Only the finest in Varangian craftsmanship, clocks so small they\u2019ll fit in your pocket! The height of utility, the height of fashion, beloved by navigators and astrologers alike!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOy, get yer new shoes right here! We\u2019ll measure yer feet and cobble you while you wait! Sandals in five minutes, boots in fifteen, and either way a five-year guarantee!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cEels! Live Eels! Fresh and cranky, thick as your leg!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c-two Talents, only two? Why this Claw Strider is a purebred straight from the great plains of Zerebosh! She\u2019s broken in and well-trained, and just look at the red shine on those scales! Do I hear three Talents of silver? Ah, the lady with the enormous sword, is that a bid Madame? THREE, we have three Talents lords and ladies do I hear-\u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cPacks, bags, and purses! Finest leather, guaranteed water-proof!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDammit, seven Dirham, are you mad? What are we going to do with SEVEN DIRHAMS WORTH OF HONEY?!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTalismans, poultices, and unguents! Cure all ills, ward off ailments! Guaranteed effective or your money back!\u201d<br /> <br /> The Guild District in late afternoon is in full swing. Colorful stalls line every street. Wagons and carts and rickshaws crawl through the traffic, their drivers roaring abuse at the crowd to get out of their way. Hurried looking young men and women dash back and forth carrying ledgers, bidding on spices and tea and all manner of assorted oddities in bulk. Food vendors are few, having paid dearly for licenses to sell refreshments to the teeming throng, and they have hired attractive ushers to call to passersby and gently wave large fans to waft the scents of their fried wares out into the crowd. You spot a couple of pickpockets bumping and apologizing their way through the merchants-one you\u2019re impressed by and one you think you could teach a thing or two. The District is full of foreigners, too-tall silk-clad nobles from Calin with long thin swords bouncing on their hips, turban-clad traders from distant Khirigast and Chiarascuro yelling at each other in a mix of Guild Cant and Riverspeak and Firetongue, a huge Northerner with an axe the size of a small rickshaw riding an actual literal bear down the street, a dozen dour-faced Sijanese priests in black and violet robes haggling with a plump gentleman with blue hair and strings of cowries around his neck carrying a wooden coffin, and even a Dynast of the Scarlet Empire in red jade armor reclining in a palanquin carried by a dozen panting servants who dash back and forth to bid for various rare and dangerous animals brought from the Eastern Jungle.<br /> <br /> You smile. All around you there are young people gawping at the sights like idiot tourists, and as you watch one of the pickpockets you\u2019ve spotted bumps into one of them, who immediately starts apologizing and saying she\u2019s sorry she wasn\u2019t looking where she was going. You\u2019re a Nexus native, though: you\u2019re counting silver in your head and dodging crowds and holding your purse close and going exactly to the booth you planned on without getting distracted by odd people and interesting wares. Like so many of the locals, you take in this wondrous cavalcade of exotica with a studied expression of boredom and slight annoyance. <i>Talismans to help you find your way?</i> In your way, you avoid them. Steaming slices of fresh pie served with cream and shaved ice? Overpriced, you walk by without so much as a glance. Dazzling purses in crimson leather adorned with gold thread, just like the Empress herself is carrying? Surely the Scarlet Empress doesn\u2019t carry her own bags, and neither do I, sir, now please let me pass!<br /> <br /> First you find a bag-a nice sturdy leather one with a strap you can hold over your shoulder and another you can connect to a belt to spread out the weight. It\u2019s got some pockets and pouches and loops for holding things on the outside as well, and you\u2019re sure it\u2019ll keep the inside reasonably dry even on a rainy day. That\u2019s one of your six budgeted bills gone. You grab some serviceable working clothes as well, brown and green to match your new bag. That\u2019s three bills of scrip gone. Three to go...<br /> <br /> You decide on a real knife, and spend some time walking up and down stalls of steel looking for just the right one. Eventually you settle on a solid utilitarian piece, with serrations for sawing on the back of a heavy, sturdy blade suitable for a little prying or carving as well as stabbing. It comes with a nice leather sheath you can wear at your hip or on your forearm or shin, along with a small whetsone. That\u2019s another bill of scrip. You consider getting a stout staff\u2026but decide against it-with your new knife you can just carve a staff from a decently sized branch if you really want one later.<br /> <br /> Four bills gone. Two to go. You decide you ought to invest in making more money-some jars or pickling supplies to preserve food against hard times, and to preserve your River Dragon parts. If you can make sure they keep, you\u2019ll get a better price for them. You find a booth selling canning and pickling supplies, and spend some time haggling. For a full set of six clay jugs and a bottle of vinegar, the woman wants three bills of scrip\u2026but you\u2019re able to haggle her down to selling you four jugs and the vinegar for your two. You put three of the jugs in your new bag, putting the clothes between them to keep them from banging each other, and carry the other under your arm down the canal to hire a ride home, trying as hard as you can not to look at or be tempted by the other bargains on offer.<br /> <br /> When you reach the docks, it looks like Grinning Eel isn\u2019t around. Not too much a surprise, he usually works the Nighthammer canal to the south. You\u2019re able to hire a boat to take you back to Nightside. The Blackwall neighborhood is very close to the water, so it\u2019s only a short jaunt from the dock back to your new apartment. You can\u2019t help but get a little excited climbing the stairs and putting your key in the lock. It\u2019s your apartment! Yours!<br /> <br /> It\u2019s still nice and neat and clean, too! There\u2019s no sign of Moth, so you actually have the place to yourself! You stash your ledger and your money in a low cabinet behind the cleaning supplies. You\u2019re aware, having spend the whole morning trying to get her to help you tidy up, that Moth doesn\u2019t like bending over for things, and that she\u2019s never going to go looking in the cupboard with the cleaning supplies unless you make her\u2026so your finances should be safe, at least until you can get a lockbox or something. You also stash your spearhead and your Seal.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re tempted to stay and rest\u2026but no, you have a bunch of River Dragon bits back at your nest\u2026and also a whole fish, which sounds good for dinner, and a couple fish hooks, which could be handy for fishing in the canal down the block from your new apartment! You take a minute to change out of your tattered rags and into your new sturdy clothes-they have lots of pockets and pouches that\u2019ll be handy for cleaning out your nest. The clay jugs are clumsy to carry, you know from recent experience. You decide to leave two here and bring two with you in your bag\u2026and before you head out, you take a thick dress that Moth didn\u2019t want to throw away but said she\u2019d never actually wear and so gave to you and stuff it in. Hopefully using that as a lining will keep the stink off your nice new bag!<br /> <br /> Feeling more than a little fancy in your new clothes and your new bag with your new knife, you take care to avoid back alleys and known dangerous areas on your way back to your old nest. It takes a while-big the time you arrive, the sun is low on the western horizon and the buildings are casting long shadows on the street. You can see from down here that there\u2019s a wheeling flock of black raitons circling overhead, croaking and swooping and generally making a huge amount of noise. You hope they haven\u2019t eaten everything! Quickly, you climb the familiar handholds onto the roof amidst sounds or raucous cawing. There\u2019s your chimney, with twine tied around it. You can see your bundle of bits next to the chimney, river dragon meat and twine and a decently sized fish strewn along the roof tiles, and a desperately flapping raiton all tangled up in the twine. You don\u2019t have more than a moment to consider how it probably blinded itself in the smoke from the chimney trying to get at your stash and got itself all tangled in the twine, or to think about how lucky you are that it didn\u2019t all fall down the chimney, though.<br /> <br /> You freeze instinctively, halfway into climbing over the lip and onto the roof tiles, both hands and one knee up on the roof and one foot still hanging down below. Past the screeching, flapping raiton that\u2019s all tangled up in the offal that\u2019s supposed to be your windfall\u2026there are a pair of huge round eyes, gleaming gold in the shadows cast by the setting sun. No more than a stone\u2019s throw away, low and slow, creeping across the roof towards your prize and the screaming raiton, much bigger than you had pictured it being\u2026<br /> <br /> It\u2019s the raptor cat. The one from the rumors. It looks just like a housecat, but so much bigger, and you can see its claws flexing as it creeps along the roof. Its left side is a glimmering shadow, but its right side is lit by the sunset. Its scales glitter gold and red and green in the fading light. It moves so quietly that only the occasional rattle of a loose tile taking its weight as it pads forward makes it seem real rather than a dream.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s definitely not a dream, though, and as you slowly pull your other knee up onto the roof its head turns and its burning golden gaze meets yours. You wonder if it can hear your heart pounding. <div align=\"center\"><b><i>\u2026what are you going to do?</i></b></div> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Resources You Have Available:</u></b><ul><li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Knife (Up your sleeve in a forearm-sheath)</li> <li>Carrying Bag</li> <li>Two Heavy Clay Jugs</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Account Balances with the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants</u></b><ul><li>Personal Account: 9 Dinars</li> <li>Time Deposit Account: 15 Dinars (Fixed Return of 9% after 9 Months)</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Resources Back at Your Nest:</u></b><ul><li>Fishhooks (2)</li> <li>A medium sized smoked fish</li> <li>Three River Dragon Fangs (one big one, four smaller ones)</li> <li>A four-by-four swatch of thick, scaly River Dragon hide</li> <li>A River Dragon Spleen? You think it\u2019s a spleen? Tied in a bundle</li> <li>A Spleenful of River Dragon Parts</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Resources at your Nightside Apartment:</u></b><ul><li>Silver: 2 Quarter-Dinars, 1 Eighth-Dinar</li> <li>Guild Scrip: 9 Bills, each one sixteenth Dinar)</li> <li>Ledger Book, with blank Cheques</li> <li>Personal Seal issued by the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants</li> <li>Steel Spearhead (Six Inch Blade in need of a shaft)</li> <li>A Small Library</li> <li>Dishes (One Cupboard Full)</li> <li>1 Box Pressed Charcoal</li> <li>Small Iron Cooking Stove</li> <li>Several Dozen Empty Wine Bottles</li> <li>Two Heavy Clay Jugs</li> <li>One Large Glass Bottle of Vinegar</li> <li>A potted plant (Deceased)</li> <li>Tattered Rags, and Clothes White Moth gave to you rather than throw away</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>You Have Gained:</u></b><br /> <b><u>Attributes: (FINALIZED).</u></b><br /> <b><u>Abilities: (28/28 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Specialties: (2/4 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <b><u>Merits: (4/7 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <b><u>Bonus Points: (15/21 Spent)-From now on, every update, we spend at least 1 BP.</u></b><br /> Raised Craft (Urban Farming) to 1 -You apparently know how to pickle food to preserve it long-term, and you invested in food storage infrastructure before food production infrastructure!<br /> Raised Melee to 2-You're comfortable enough with a knife to know how to pick out a good one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 07-01-2017, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T16:14:42-07:00","id":1095274,"title":"","content":"Throw the raiton at it. Hopefully it will be distracted by the morsel. Grab whatever you can stuff in your bag in three seconds, then run away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T16:46:46-07:00","id":1095286,"title":"","content":"Oh shit. As much as I would like to, fighting this thing seems unlikely to go well, so I'm seconding semicasual's suggestion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T22:38:24-07:00","id":1095369,"title":"","content":"Yeah bail. We have money, education, and some income. No reason to go big on this risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T22:47:27-07:00","id":1095374,"title":"","content":"Toss the ration to the cat, grab what we can of the river dragon stuff, and scat!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T12:34:54-07:00","id":1095592,"title":"","content":"&quot;Here, Kitty Kitty. Want some fish?&quot; *Toss* *run*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T19:52:35-07:00","id":1096958,"title":"","content":"<b>Throw the trapped Raiton at the Raptor-Cat: 3<br /> Grab your stuff and run: 3<br /> Just Run: 1<br /> Toss the fish to the raptor cat: 1</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>Of course, the only option that didn\u2019t lead to Join Battle was \u201cImmediately back slowly and non-threateningly away and leave the predator to its prize,\u201d so\u2026</b></div> <br /> <br /> Your mind races.<br /> <br /> The raptor cat lets out a deep rumbling growl, warning you away from its delicious find.<br /> <br /> <i>Think, think!</i> The raptor cat is just a cat, it isn\u2019t bright, the amount of money sitting there on the roof is enough to set you up for literal years, the only way to run is backwards off a roof and then climb down the wall, and if the cat comes after you there\u2019s a risk you\u2019ll fall\u2026<br /> <br /> As the raptor cat snarls and crouches, you crouch yourself, preparing to lunge for the raiton so you can grab it and throw it at the cat, hopefully distracting it long enough for you to grab your loot and-<br /> <br /> -and-<br /> <br /> -and it leaps a split second before you do, covering nine yards in a great leap!<br /> <br /> Already prepared to dive for the raiton, you lunge forward and roll, drawing your knife and slashing blindly behind you. You manage to pass under the beast as it lands where you were just crouched, though your back stings with sudden stinging pain as its whirls and leaves four long claw marks right through your nice new shirt and down your back.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>(The Raptor Cat won Initiative, with 7 Initiative to your 6 and the Raiton\u2019s 5. It\u2019s just hit you with a Withering attack which, mercifully, only dealt 2 Withering Damage, raising the Raptor Cat to 10 Initiative and dropping you to 4.)</b></div> <br /> You are now crouched with a knife in one hand, a snarling raptor cat in front of you and behind it a long drop. There\u2019s a thrashing raiton slightly behind you and to your left, and just beyond it an eave that you don\u2019t think you can climb before the raptor cat gets you. There\u2019s about four yards of slick roof tiles to your right before a long drop to the cobblestones below. Behind you is about a twelve-yard run before the end of the building-there\u2019s another lower building that way you\u2019re not entirely sure you could jump to from this one-<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a horrible snarl from behind you and you spin your head-another Raptor Cat?!<br /> <br /> The raiton has stopped thrashing and trying to escape. Instead it has opened its toothy beak as wide as it can\u2026and it is making a deep rumbling growl identical to the one the Raptor Cat was just making a few moments ago before it tried to pounce on you. You look back at the real Raptor Cat, and it\u2019s looking around, confused, trying to locate another of its own kind. It\u2019s distracted, sniffing the air and hissing, not paying you its full attention as it looks around for feline competition.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>(The Raiton is\u2026apparently capable of a Distract Gambit? It\u2019s managed to give 4 of its Initiative to you! It has dropped its Initiative to 1 and raised yours to 8! It\u2019s your turn!)</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><br /> If you\u2019re going to do something, best do it now!</div> <br /> <br /> <b>We are now in Combat Time! Please be aware that a tied vote here will result in an attempted Flurry.</b><br /> <b>ROUND ONE:<br /> <i>Raptor Cat: 10 Iniative (Acted Already)</i><br /> Tavi: 8 Initiative (You! You're the Last Actor in Round 1)<br /> <i>Raiton: 1 Initiative (Acted Already)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b>Distances: You are currently within Close range of the Raptor Cat, and Short range of the Raiton. You are at Short range from the elevated eave on your left, Short range from the edge of the roof on your right, Short range from the edge of the roof ahead of you behind the raptor cat, and at Medium range from the edge of the roof behind you.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Environmental Factors: Slippery Footing! If you attempt a Combat Move action, you must either stunt in such a way as to avoid traveling across the damp tiles or treat the terrain as Difficult\u2026or you may make a Dex+Athletics roll to treat this as normal terrain. Failure on that roll on a slick and steeply sloped roof is...not recommended.</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Available Combat Resources:</u></b><ul><li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Knife (Currently Wielding in your Left Hand)</li> <li>Carrying Bag</li> <li>Two Heavy Clay Jugs (In the Bag)</li> <li>7 Health Levels</li> <li>4 Willpower</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Potentially Useful Scenery Scattered About the Roof?</u></b><ul><li>Fishhooks (2)</li> <li>A medium sized smoked fish</li> <li>A tangled-up Raiton</li> <li>Three River Dragon Fangs (one big one, four smaller ones-count as Knives)</li> <li>A four-by-four swatch of thick, scaly River Dragon hide</li> <li>A River Dragon Spleen? You think it\u2019s a spleen? Tied in a half-opened bundle. Tied to the Raiton.</li> <li>Assorted River Dragon Bits</li> <li>A Brick Chimney (and a column of thick black smoke above it)</li> <li>A loosely attached drain pipe</li> <li>A Swirling Flock of Croaking Raitons Overhead</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>You Have Gained:</u></b><br /> <b><u>Attributes: (FINALIZED).</u></b><br /> <b><u>Abilities: (28/28 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Specialties: (2/4 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <b><u>Merits: (4/7 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <b><u>Bonus Points: (17/21 Spent)-From now on, every update, we spend at least 1 BP.</u></b><ul><li>Dodge 0 to 1: As it turns out, a tumbling roll under a pouncing leopard does in fact teach the basics of Evasion!</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 05-25-2017, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T20:10:48-07:00","id":1096960,"title":"","content":"Can we yank off the drain-pipe and either 1) use it as great big beating stick, or 2) use it to break some of the tiles to throw at the raptor-cat?<br /> <br /> Fighting fair is for suckers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T20:14:11-07:00","id":1096962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1096960#post1096960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we yank off the drain-pipe and either 1) use it as great big beating stick, or 2) use it to break some of the tiles to throw at the raptor-cat?<br /> <br /> Fighting fair is for suckers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely! That pipe is on the eave to your left, so it'd be a Move and a Ready Weapon action to yank off the drain pipe, if that's what you wanna use your vote on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T05:42:39-07:00","id":1097087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1096962#post1096962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely! That pipe is on the eave to your left, so it'd be a Move and a Ready Weapon action to yank off the drain pipe, if that's what you wanna use your vote on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, what is the pipe made of? If it is lead or even ceramic, Tavi might need a Feat of Strenth to yank off/throw the thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T05:44:38-07:00","id":1097089,"title":"","content":"We've got a tiny advantage in initiative - I say we go for broke. <br /> <br /> On Turn 1, flail at the raptor cat with your knife (withering attack). We don't need to really hurt it, we just need to hold it at bay and get it to back up just a little. Use Willpower to enhance this attack.<br /> On Turn 2, use a Gambit to try to shove the raptor cat off the roof behind it. We only need to push it one range band. Again, use Willpower.<br /> <br /> <i>Variation 1:</i> Use the satchel as an improvised Smashing weapon instead of shoving on turn 2. Pray we don't break the jars inside. <br /> <i>Variation 2: </i>On turn 1, Go grab the drainpipe like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11892\" data-vbnamecard=\"11892\">Boston123</a> suggested. Use that as as Smashing weapon on Turn 2. I'm a little leerier of this plan, just because I don't like having to move two range bands on difficult terrain. I can't think of a way to do those moves without crossing the tiles, which means doing risky Dex+Ath checks. Also, our initiative won't be as high when we attempt the Smash, which could leave us at a disadvantage when the raptor cat counterattacks. <br /> <br /> BTW, are there pictures of raptor cats I can use for reference? I'm having trouble visualizing this creature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T06:33:24-07:00","id":1097100,"title":"","content":"Edit: Changing my vote. See post on the next page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9510,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","user":"BlueWinds","date":". 05-27-2017, 06:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T06:39:35-07:00","id":1097102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1097089#post1097089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, are there pictures of raptor cats I can use for reference? I'm having trouble visualizing this creature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Picture a large leopard or a small panther. Now give it dappled grey/brown/green snake scales instead of fur so it can blend in with the canopy of the Eastern jungles where it hunts, and a slightly bendier spine, and you have a pretty good picture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T06:47:28-07:00","id":1097104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1097102#post1097102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Picture a large leopard or a small panther. Now give it dappled grey/brown/green snake scales instead of fur so it can blend in with the canopy of the Eastern jungles where it hunts, and a slightly bendier spine, and you have a pretty good picture.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Holy shit, this thing is <u>far</u> bigger than I thought originally. I was thinking it was the the size of a large housecat or a lynx.<br /> <br /> <br /> It already attacked us, so the cat might be out of the bag (I'm so sorry), but have we tried staring it down yet?<br /> <br /> Animals like bears and dogs tend to view humans as potential rivals, so staring them down usually causes them to attack. Large cats, on the other hand, tend to view humans as potential <i>prey</i>, so staring them down usually makes them back off.<br /> <br /> Glaring the thing down, waving our hands wildly, screaming our head off, etc might scare the thing away, or make it decide we are too much trouble to be worthwhile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T08:37:32-07:00","id":1097136,"title":"","content":"Definitely flourish the knife at it, try to force it back or otherwise convince it that we're bad choice of potential meal. And do not break eye contact if at all possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T08:46:11-07:00","id":1097141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1097089#post1097089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've got a tiny advantage in initiative - I say we go for broke.<br /> <br /> On Turn 1, flail at the raptor cat with your knife (withering attack). We don't need to really hurt it, we just need to hold it at bay and get it to back up just a little. Use Willpower to enhance this attack.<br /> On Turn 2, use a Gambit to try to shove the raptor cat off the roof behind it. We only need to push it one range band. Again, use Willpower.<br /> <br /> <i>Variation 1:</i> Use the satchel as an improvised Smashing weapon instead of shoving on turn 2. Pray we don't break the jars inside.<br /> <i>Variation 2: </i>On turn 1, Go grab the drainpipe like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11892\" data-vbnamecard=\"11892\">Boston123</a> suggested. Use that as as Smashing weapon on Turn 2. I'm a little leerier of this plan, just because I don't like having to move two range bands on difficult terrain. I can't think of a way to do those moves without crossing the tiles, which means doing risky Dex+Ath checks. Also, our initiative won't be as high when we attempt the Smash, which could leave us at a disadvantage when the raptor cat counterattacks.<br /> <br /> BTW, are there pictures of raptor cats I can use for reference? I'm having trouble visualizing this creature.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I vote for this. No Flurries!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T15:59:37-07:00","id":1097342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1097089#post1097089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've got a tiny advantage in initiative - I say we go for broke.<br /> <br /> On Turn 1, flail at the raptor cat with your knife (withering attack). We don't need to really hurt it, we just need to hold it at bay and get it to back up just a little. Use Willpower to enhance this attack.<br /> On Turn 2, use a Gambit to try to shove the raptor cat off the roof behind it. We only need to push it one range band. Again, use Willpower.<br /> <br /> <i>Variation 1:</i> Use the satchel as an improvised Smashing weapon instead of shoving on turn 2. Pray we don't break the jars inside.<br /> <i>Variation 2: </i>On turn 1, Go grab the drainpipe like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11892\" data-vbnamecard=\"11892\">Boston123</a> suggested. Use that as as Smashing weapon on Turn 2. I'm a little leerier of this plan, just because I don't like having to move two range bands on difficult terrain. I can't think of a way to do those moves without crossing the tiles, which means doing risky Dex+Ath checks. Also, our initiative won't be as high when we attempt the Smash, which could leave us at a disadvantage when the raptor cat counterattacks.<br /> <br /> BTW, are there pictures of raptor cats I can use for reference? I'm having trouble visualizing this creature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vote for variation 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T20:16:45-07:00","id":1097400,"title":"","content":"I agree with wonderandawe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T21:56:46-07:00","id":1097418,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna vote against the grain and say we go all in on a Decisive attack right now. The Initiative we got from the Distract Gambit has to be used immediately or it's lost. That makes this our best chance to drive off the cat.<br /> <br /> Use the opportunity! Spend Willpower to slash the cat across the face, where it'll hurt the most. It will leave to lick its wounds and find easier food.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T00:58:45-07:00","id":1097451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1097418#post1097418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna vote against the grain and say we go all in on a Decisive attack right now. The Initiative we got from the Distract Gambit has to be used immediately or it's lost. That makes this our best chance to drive off the cat.<br /> <br /> Use the opportunity! Spend Willpower to slash the cat across the face, where it'll hurt the most. It will leave to lick its wounds and find easier food.</div> </div> </div> </div>This crazy...Let's do it.<br /> <br /> Seriously, we need to convince it to leave us be and we are only going to do that by being more dangerous than we are worth. Hopefully it won't get all territorial on us, cause then this will backfire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T03:26:58-07:00","id":1097474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1097451#post1097451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This crazy...Let's do it.<br /> <br /> Seriously, we need to convince it to leave us be and we are only going to do that by being more dangerous than we are worth. Hopefully it won't get all territorial on us, cause then this will backfire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it's immediately lost if not used? I didn't realize that, nor (I suspect) did others (pg. 200, if someone else wants to look it up like I did). Changing my vote. Now voting for:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1097418#post1097418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna vote against the grain and say we go all in on a Decisive attack right now. The Initiative we got from the Distract Gambit has to be used immediately or it's lost. That makes this our best chance to drive off the cat.<br /> <br /> Use the opportunity! Spend Willpower to slash the cat across the face, where it'll hurt the most. It will leave to lick its wounds and find easier food.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T05:28:50-07:00","id":1097494,"title":"","content":"I also did not realize that Distraction was temporary.<br /> <br /> In that case, I still think we should try to shove the cat, but on turn 1 instead of 2. If we succeed, we can injure it and also prevent it from immediately retaliating.<br /> <br /> (I guess a decisive attack pool of 8 is more than whatever our withering attack usually is?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T10:52:50-07:00","id":1097564,"title":"","content":"If the distract bonus is only temporary then let's go for a decisive shove now. Now that I think of it the cat should be at onslaught -1 because of the distract too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T09:56:36-07:00","id":1097804,"title":"","content":"Just noticed this, LOVE it so far! Even if the distract wasn't temporary, I'd say go for the decisive shove now.<br /> Although, iirk aren't all raitons, though small, still about the size of pterodactyls and supposed to be next level up in intelligence from ravens?<br /> Finally, is anyone else thinking of a CYOA website for creating Exalted characters?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T21:32:41-07:00","id":1099748,"title":"","content":"<b>Grab the Pipe: 1<br /> Wither, then Push: 1<br /> Strike Now (Decisive Knife): 3<br /> Strike Now(Push): 3<br /> Intimidate: 1</b><br /> <br /> You just have a moment while the Raptor Cat is distracted, and you seize it. With a wordless yell that you hope comes across as intimidating, you lunge toward the cat, slashing your knife towards its eyes. It twists back, snarling and swiping, but you press your advantage and keep making noise and thrusting at it aggressively. Startled and off guard, the cat tries to wriggle backwards away from you...and slips, losing its footing at the edge of the slippery roof! It yowls and scrabbles briefly at the eave\u2026before plummeting over the edge and out of sight.<br /> <br /> You wait a moment, crouched, knife forward, to make sure it's not going to come surging back up over the edge towards you...and when it doesn't you take a step forward and peer over the edge. It takes you a moment to spot the creature's dappled form on the darkening street below, limping away into a nearby alley. From the way it\u2019s walking, you think its back left leg was broken when it hit the cobblestones below.<br /> <br /> <b>(I called \u201cpush it off the roof\u201d a Gambit and eyeballed it as the same Difficulty as the Unhorse Gambit from the Core-they're both about causing your foe to suffer a fall that gives them a major tactical disadvantage. You hit only barely due to the cat\u2019s onslaught penalties, but rolled quite well on your Initiative, easily succeeding in the Difficulty 4 Gambit and spending your way down to 3 Initiative.<br /> <br /> The Raptor Cat, up first in Round 2, was now injured-poor thing took 6L in falling damage- and in a disadvantageous position. After being hurt, confused and unexpectedly attacked by what it thought from past experience with humans was going to be easy prey, it decided to flee and spent 10 Initiative to take a Withdraw Action. This Crashed the cat, giving you a bonus of 5 Initiative and getting you up to 8 Initiative at the top of Round 2.)</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The cuts on your back still sting, but you can\u2019t help beaming with a sense of victory.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>What\u2019s the very first thing you do now?</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> There\u2019s no time for basking in glory, don\u2019t let up! Pursue the Raptor Cat! It\u2019s already injured, and if you can finish the job\u2026well, you won\u2019t have to split this beast\u2019s body parts with a bunch of canal boatmen this time. You\u2019re pretty sure its hide alone would fetch a decent price! (Attempt to pursue the Raptor Cat. Continues combat.)<br /> <br /> Let the cat go. Even if you could get down the roof in time to chase it down, a desperate predator cornered in an alley could injure or kill you. It\u2019s not worth the risk. Instead, take a deep breath in, exhale slowly, and take a moment to offer your heartfelt thanks to the Dragons that you just survived a knife fight with a local legend that\u2019s been giving you occasional nightmares since you first heard rumors about it.<br /> <br /> Ignore the defeated cat, and immediately start gathering up your River Dragon pieces before the raitons eat them all! You're not here to risk your life fighting apex predators, you're here to get your money and take it home!<br /> <br /> Ignore the defeated cat, and go disentangle that raiton from the twine it\u2019s gotten itself tangled in. It may have been trying to steal your food\u2026but stealing food is something you\u2019ve been doing for years, and you\u2019re pretty sure that its distractingly accurate snarling raptor cat impression might have saved your life. Even if this whole situation is pretty much the raiton's fault, you at least owe it that much.<br /> <br /> The battle is won\u2026but while they don\u2019t seem major now while your heart is still pumping, you do have some claw marks down your back. Your immediate priority, painful as it\u2019s gonna be, is to use some of the vinegar you brought with you for pickling and disinfect your back before you get sick. You know wounds from alley cats are really prone to infection, you doubt Raptor Cats are much different.<br /> <br /> Something Else?<br /> <br /> <b><u>Combat Resources:</u></b><ul><li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Knife (Currently Wielding in your Left Hand)</li> <li>Carrying Bag</li> <li>Two Heavy Clay Jugs (In the Bag)</li> <li>7 Health Levels</li> <li>4 Willpower</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Potentially Useful Scenery Scattered About the Roof?</u></b><ul><li>Fishhooks (2)</li> <li>A medium sized smoked fish</li> <li>A tangled-up Raiton</li> <li>Three River Dragon Fangs (one big one, four smaller ones-count as Knives)</li> <li>A four-by-four swatch of thick, scaly River Dragon hide</li> <li>A River Dragon Spleen? You think it\u2019s a spleen? Tied in a bundle</li> <li>A Spleenful of River Dragon Parts</li> <li>A Brick Chimney</li> <li>A Swirling Flock of Croaking Raitons Overhead</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>You Have Gained:</u></b><br /> <b><u>Attributes: (FINALIZED).</u></b><br /> <b><u>Abilities: (28/28 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Specialties: (2/4 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <b><u>Merits: (4/7 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <b><u>Bonus Points: (21/21 Spent)-ALL BP is now spent.</u></b><br /> Survival 2 to 3: You just intimidated a Raptor Cat off a roof, with the help of a wild Raiton. It\u2019s clear that dealing with animals comes naturally to you.<br /> Melee 2 to 3: So far you\u2019ve used your knife for butchering and prying and climbing\u2026but now you\u2019ve actually used it for fighting. Fighting something with reflexes several times faster than your average human knife-fighter, though you don\u2019t know that. This will be a positive formative experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T23:57:50-07:00","id":1099766,"title":"","content":"Let the cat go; it's not a fight worth pursuing. Too much risk, too little reward. Give a quick thanks to the Dragons, then gather up our River Dragon pieces before the raitons eat them all! We're not here to risk our life fighting apex predators, we're here to get our money and take it home! Once we've gathered up our stuff, we should go disentangle that raiton from the twine it\u2019s gotten itself tangled in. Sure, it was trying to steal our food\u2026but stealing food is something we\u2019ve been doing for years, and its distractingly accurate snarling raptor cat impression might have saved our life. Besides, it's a just a bird, it's not malicious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T03:00:57-07:00","id":1099786,"title":"","content":"Priorities. Let it go and get our stuff. Once that's all safely packed up...yeah, let the raiton free. It might seem silly to be grateful to a bird, but that bird just saved our life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T08:25:40-07:00","id":1099829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1099786#post1099786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Priorities. Let it go and get our stuff. Once that's all safely packed up...yeah, let the raiton free. It might seem silly to be grateful to a bird, but that bird just saved our life.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Ten characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T11:33:30-07:00","id":1099867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1099786#post1099786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Priorities. Let it go and get our stuff. Once that's all safely packed up...yeah, let the raiton free. It might seem silly to be grateful to a bird, but that bird just saved our life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this course of action","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T14:38:37-07:00","id":1099919,"title":"","content":"All these things in order;<br /> 1- Thank the Dragons<br /> 2- Get our stuff<br /> 3- Free Raiton<br /> 4- Disinfect wounds<br /> 5- Go gather any blood from where the Raptor Cat landed to make a charm to ward off predators. (combine with blubber from the River Dragon's skin to make something that identifies you as a top tier predator)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T16:55:23-07:00","id":1099954,"title":"","content":"Priorities<br /> 1- Thank the Dragons<br /> 2- Get our stuff<br /> 3- Disinfect wounds; take no chances. How many kids have we seen who died slowly being poisoned by their own blood, their wounds twisted and colourful...not us, not ever.<br /> 4- Go gather any blood from where the Raptor Cat landed to make a charm to ward off predators. (combine with blubber from the River Dragon's skin to make something that identifies you as a top tier predator)<br /> [We need every advantage we can get and the raiton isn't going anywhere]<br /> 5- Free Raiton; it isn't holding a grudge but we got to take care of us first..<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T12:52:26-07:00","id":1100191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1099919#post1099919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All these things in order;<br /> 1- Thank the Dragons<br /> 2- Get our stuff<br /> 3- Free Raiton<br /> 4- Disinfect wounds<br /> 5- Go gather any blood from where the Raptor Cat landed to make a charm to ward off predators. (combine with blubber from the River Dragon's skin to make something that identifies you as a top tier predator)</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding this list","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T18:08:27-07:00","id":1100281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1099954#post1099954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Priorities<br /> 1- Thank the Dragons<br /> 2- Get our stuff<br /> 3- Disinfect wounds; take no chances. How many kids have we seen who died slowly being poisoned by their own blood, their wounds twisted and colourful...not us, not ever.<br /> 4- Go gather any blood from where the Raptor Cat landed to make a charm to ward off predators. (combine with blubber from the River Dragon's skin to make something that identifies you as a top tier predator)<br /> [We need every advantage we can get and the raiton isn't going anywhere]<br /> 5- Free Raiton; it isn't holding a grudge but we got to take care of us first..</div> </div> </div> </div>This is good for me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T05:08:11-07:00","id":1100406,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1624_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1624\" data-vbnamecard=\"1624\">FallenEco</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11567_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11567\" data-vbnamecard=\"11567\">Jairain</a> ; You do realize gathering up the blood and <i>then </i>freeing the raiton requires Tavi to climb down to street level, climb back up, then climb back down again, right? That sounds like a lot of extra work. That blood isn't going anywhere, and the Raiton is in Close range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T06:40:28-07:00","id":1100426,"title":"","content":"Gathering blood can wait. And I'd recommend we disinfect our wounds at the apartment, not here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T11:03:17-07:00","id":1100508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1099954#post1099954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Priorities<br /> 1- Thank the Dragons<br /> 2- Get our stuff<br /> 3- Disinfect wounds; take no chances. How many kids have we seen who died slowly being poisoned by their own blood, their wounds twisted and colourful...not us, not ever.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This list is full of living to see the next day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T15:29:29-07:00","id":1100620,"title":"","content":"I was saying disinfect after freeing the raiton just in case we get more scratches we'd need to disinfect. Scared animals don't always understand that you're trying to help. Also, yeah, climb down last.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T16:10:55-07:00","id":1100631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1100406#post1100406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> and <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> ; You do realize gathering up the blood and <i>then </i>freeing the raiton requires Tavi to climb down to street level, climb back up, then climb back down again, right? That sounds like a lot of extra work. That blood isn't going anywhere, and the Raiton is in Close range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Valid point, usually most benefit for least effort is the way to go. I acquiesce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T16:32:01-07:00","id":1100641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1100406#post1100406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1624_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1624\" data-vbnamecard=\"1624\">FallenEco</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11567_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11567\" data-vbnamecard=\"11567\">Jairain</a> ; You do realize gathering up the blood and <i>then </i>freeing the raiton requires Tavi to climb down to street level, climb back up, then climb back down again, right? That sounds like a lot of extra work. That blood isn't going anywhere, and the Raiton is in Close range.</div> </div> </div> </div>noted. gathering the blood is a lower priority than the raiton.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T17:44:53-07:00","id":1100658,"title":"","content":"Especially since cat-scratches are known for causing infections <i>really easily</i>. <br /> <br /> .... the fact that the raptor-cat is, well, a lizard, shouldn't change that very much. The bacteria is on the claws, not in the blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T08:18:10-07:00","id":1100850,"title":"","content":"Still better to disinfect at our apartment. Disinfecting might require removing our shirt. This is probably something we'd feel uncomfortable doing in a relatively public place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T06:25:13-07:00","id":1101195,"title":"","content":"We did it before. In this very spot only yesterday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T18:05:28-07:00","id":1101816,"title":"","content":"<b>Your List is Appreciated, But I Was Only Looking For Your Most <i>Immediate </i>Priority: Stuff Is Happening!<br /> Thank The Dragons: 6<br /> Get Your Stuff: 3</b><br /> <br /> Still panting from adrenaline, you stand tall on the roof in victory. Then, you bow your head in prayer.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, uh. Hey, Dragons\u2026there\u2019s no way I\u2019m this lucky,\u201d you say quietly. \u201cUm\u2026thanks. For looking out for me, I guess. It\u2019s\u2026not like much of anybody else really is.\u201d<br /> <br /> Praying out loud is a bit awkward, but it feels appropriate.<br /> <br /> After a few moments of staring at the setting sun and being really grateful not to be dead, you close your eyes and shake your head a little to clear your thoughts. You have things to do. You should grab your things-and, now that you think about it, you ought to untangle that raiton. You can\u2019t really stomach the idea of eating it-it did sort of help you, after all, and raiton is pretty greasy meat anyway\u2026and saving an innocent creature is the sort of thing Sextes Jylis would do, right?<br /> <br /> You turn and crouch to start gathering your things\u2026only to find yourself suddenly surrounded by black feathers and claws and beaks and harsh croaking. The flock of raitons overhead descends upon you, and upon the entire rooftop, with very little warning! Ignoring you, they are tearing into the bundle of river dragon parts, squabbling over them with each other! Twine tears, meat tears, and valuable bits of River Dragon are dragged and thrown all over the place! The tangled-up raiton has the misfortune to be tied to the big bundle at the center of it all, and is getting dragged all over the roof as its fellows fight each other to try and make off with it!<br /> <br /> Frustrated and enraged, you wade into the middle of the flock, yelling and kicking and waving your knife around. The horrible feathered reptiles screech angrily and flutter away when you get close, only to land again a few feet away and creep aggressively back toward morsels of River Dragon, watching you warily. The roof is slippery and it\u2019s getting dark and they seem to realize your mobility is much more limited than theirs. There\u2019s a big circle of them around you, and you\u2019ve grabbed the biggest bundle (and dangling from it, an angrily squawking feathered reptile who, up this close, you realize smells pretty strongly of smoked fish) for yourself, but you\u2019ve lost more than half your prize.<br /> <br /> Growing bold, one of the raitons darts in to try and snatch a bite from your bundle. You swat at with your knife, and it veers off and flaps away clumsily.<br /> <br /> The rest of them seem more wary now, and watch you curiously but stop trying to get closer. Maybe it\u2019s just your imagination, but\u2026their eyes seem oddly intelligent. Now that you think about it\u2026Nexus is full of people clambering about on the roofways, and they\u2019re not all as graceful as you. The local raitons probably know that people falling off roofs are a decent source of food\u2026most of these ones seem to be incapable of working cooperatively, they\u2019re just squabbling over scraps\u2026but there are a few dozen who are just sitting still and\u2026watching you. Are they smart enough to work together?<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>What now?</b></div> <br /> Flee: Stuff your bundle, and the attached raiton if cutting it away takes more than a few seconds, into your bag to prevent further flyby attacks. Then back away slowly, and climb down to street level. Don\u2019t risk your life gathering up what you\u2019ve already lost on a slippery roof in the dark fighting flying rats.<br /> <br /> Free the Raiton: Disentangling it from the twine and letting it go might let the others know you\u2019re not a threat, and you\u2019ve heard stories about people who take care of a raiton with a broken wing and have black-feathered friends bringing them coins and buttons and other shiny objects for months afterward. You could stand to make some new friends\u2026and you don\u2019t much relish the idea of trying to climb down with that thing struggling and wriggling right next to you.<br /> <br /> Go On The Offense: Put your stinky little bundle in your bag to protect it, then go gather up the bits scattered over the roof. Keep the knife in one hand, swing the heavy bag to keep the birds off with the other, and go after the ones that are sitting and watching you first to intimidate them out of any thoughts of cooperation. Get your stuff back!<br /> <br /> Make An Example: Hold up the tied-up raiton in front of them and snap its neck. You\u2019re pretty sure raitons are clever enough to understand the interspecies sign for \u201cFuck with me and you end up like this guy.\u201d<br /> <br /> Something Else: Do something else!<br /> <br /> <b><u>Combat Resources:</u></b><ul><li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Knife (Currently Wielding in your Left Hand)</li> <li>Carrying Bag</li> <li>Two Heavy Clay Jugs (In the Bag)</li> <li>7/7 Health Levels</li> <li>3/4 Willpower</li> <li>A River Dragon Spleen? You think it\u2019s a spleen? Tied in a bundle, but ripped up and leaking smaller pieces of meat.</li> <li>A Spleenful of River Dragon Parts</li> <li>A tangled-up Raiton</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Potentially Useful Scenery Scattered About the Roof?</u></b><ul><li>Fishhooks (2)</li> <li>A medium sized smoked fish-currently being eaten</li> <li>Three River Dragon Fangs (one big one, four smaller ones-count as Knives)</li> <li>A four-by-four swatch of thick, scaly River Dragon hide-currently being pecked at</li> <li>Assorted chunks of River Dragon organ meat-currently being eaten</li> <li>A Brick Chimney</li> <li>A Flock of Raitons</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Character Creation Status Update:</u></b><br /> <b><u>Attributes: (FINALIZED).</u></b><br /> <b><u>Abilities: (FINALIZED)</u></b>.<br /> <b><u>Bonus Points: (FINALIZED).</u></b><br /> <b><u>Specialties: (2/4 Allocated)</u></b><br /> <b><u>Merits: (4/7 Allocated)</u></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 06-08-2017, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T18:33:48-07:00","id":1101820,"title":"","content":"Free the Raiton. Let's be friends with at least one piece of local wildlife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T19:23:30-07:00","id":1101836,"title":"","content":"Try freeing the raiton. I figure it's either that or leave the river-dragon bits to be eaten while Tavi makes her escape - I don't relish trying to flee if the raitons decide to give chase and harry her as she climbs down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T19:42:00-07:00","id":1101838,"title":"","content":"Free it, sounds reasonable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T04:36:45-07:00","id":1101920,"title":"","content":"Go on the offense. We can free our new pat/familiar later, but we need our stuff so we can get out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T06:56:36-07:00","id":1101955,"title":"","content":"Free the Raiton. Cause they wouldn't tell stories if they were real right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T16:16:16-07:00","id":1102140,"title":"","content":"Free the Raiton, quickly. It helped you out, but it is also going to be in the way if it is still attached and you still have to fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T23:10:32-07:00","id":1102443,"title":"","content":"<b>Free Him! 5</b><br /> <b>Play Offense: 1</b><br /> <br /> As the dozens of raitons not tearing into your windfall stare at you, you raise their tangled compatriot and hold it out in front of you. It squawks and struggles, and tries to peck at your hand.<br /> \u201cStop it, you stupid little shit,\u201d you mutter, \u201cI\u2019m trying to help you.\u201d<br /> <br /> The raiton stops squawking, and cocks its head. It stops its thrashing. It\u2019s\u2026it\u2019s honestly a little creepy, you think. You know they\u2019re smart birds, but it\u2019s almost like it can actually understand you.<br /> <br /> You raise your knife. The quietly watching flock doesn\u2019t like that! Several of them spread their wings to look bigger, and hiss at you.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s okay,\u201d you tell them, trying to be as soothing as you can. \u201cLook. I\u2019m just cutting him loose.\u201d<br /> <br /> Your knife is new, and sharp. Your twine is old, and cheap. Cutting the raiton loose is easy, taking only a couple of quick cuts before the big black bird is free. It sits there for a moment, head cocked, watching you\u2026then hops out of your hand and flutters away into the sky, ignoring the food all the other raitons are squabbling over.<br /> <br /> The silent watchers watch it go, then look back at the meat scattered over the rooftop\u2026then back skyward. One by one, they take off to follow it. The raitons scavenging over the rest of the roof ignore them, continuing to croak and shriek at each other as they fight over your things\u2026but then the ones that have taken to the air circle back around and call to them, and they too leave the roof and take to the sky.<br /> <br /> The great black flock wings its way off southward, and you are left alone on the roof with your admittedly rather pecked-over prize.<br /> <br /> Quickly, not wanting to lose the daylight, you gather everything on the roof and toss it into your bag. Then you take out the small bottle of vinegar you brought with you and pour it over your back. You wince as the cold liquid hits the cuts on your back-you can\u2019t see how bad it is back there, but it stings something awful. You\u2019ll look at the wound again when you get back to your apartment.<br /> <br /> Slowly and carefully, you descend the drainpipe to street level. The world is dark gray and the sky overhead is a deep violet, with an evening star or two starting to poke their way through the omnipresent Nexus smog. You give a long and wary stare to the alley you last saw the Raptor Cat limping down\u2026but there\u2019s no sign of the beast, other than a scraping of fur and a little blood on the cobblestones where it hit the ground. After a moment of thought, you scrape this up with your knife as best you can and put it in one of your jars. Between River Dragon blubber and Raptor Cat fur, you might be able to come up with some sort of stinky ointment that\u2019ll scare away animals. You won\u2019t have much use for it, there aren\u2019t a lot of inhuman predators roaming the streets of Nexus\u2026but you might be able to sell it. There are lots of pack animals in town, and the power to spook them and cause wagons to go off course or overturn is something people might readily pay for\u2026<br /> <br /> Anyway, that\u2019s something for when you get home. <div align=\"center\">*****</div> <br /> It\u2019s a long walk home to your new apartment, and a stressful one-you know the area around Nighthammer pretty well, but as you\u2019re heading north through Nightside to your new neighborhood the territory gets less and less familiar. You don\u2019t know which alleys are safe shortcuts and which ones are meeting places for people you don\u2019t want to run into. You\u2019re not sure which areas of the night markets are \u201cprotected\u201d by street gangs who will want to charge you for passing through their territory. You\u2019re forced to stick to main thoroughfares and take slower paths than you normally would. It takes a little over an hour to get back to the Blackwall neighborhood. It\u2019s\u2026a lot less homey at night. There\u2019s garbage in streets and mean looking cats-and every time you hear a rustle in an alley and look down it to meet a pair of gleaming reflective cat-eyes, you find adrenaline surging through your body as your hands tighten on the handle of your knife. That Raptor Cat is still out there somewhere, licking its wounds.<br /> <br /> The figures lurking on stoops during the day are now laughing in alleyways, drinking and sometimes yelling at each other. The rooftop gardens aren\u2019t visible in the dark, and the only lights are from the windows of the apartment buildings-the streets are dark and menacing. Somewhere a block or so away you can hear loud sounds of merriment and cruel laughter-Blackwall is only a few minutes from the canal, and you remember there\u2019s a popular tavern there where some of the boatmen and dockworkers unwind.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re only accosted once or twice, but you must cut a pretty imposing figure, carrying a big knife and a heavy and- despite your best efforts- bloodstained bag, with torn clothes. Most people leave you alone, and the ones who don\u2019t are drunk enough it\u2019s easy to evade them.<br /> <br /> Finally, you arrive home. You dash up the creaky stairs, turn your key in the lock, and enter your apartment-and jump as White Moth shrieks in terror at the sight of you, throwing a piece of chicken on a stick at you.<br /> <br /> You close and lock the door as she calms down. You can\u2019t help smiling a little. Having people be afraid of you, having people want to get out of your way instead of seeing you as prey\u2026that feels good.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s just me, Moth,\u201d you sigh. \u201cYou can relax.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMerciful Ancestors, Tavi.\u201d She gasps. \u201cWhat happened to you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, you\u2019re wearing completely different clothes, and they\u2019re all ripped up, and you have cuts and scratches all over your face and hands, and you\u2019re carrying a giant knife, and you stink like dead fish, and\u2026is that bag dripping blood?\u201d<br /> <br /> You toss the bag onto your new counter.<br /> <br /> \u201cFuck.\u201d You mutter. \u201cThat was a brand new bag\u2026Moth, do you know any good ways to get bloodstains out?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLemon and table salt. Gods, what happened to your back?!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI, uh. I fought a bunch of raitons. And a Raptor Cat.\u201d<br /> <br /> White Moth looks at you like you\u2019ve sprouted wings and tentacles. \u201cYou\u2026fought a Raptor Cat.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah. There\u2019s been a rumor going around for a while that there\u2019s one loose in the city, living in the roofways. Some Merchant Prince\u2019s pet that got loose? Turns out it\u2019s true. Thing kind of came after me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Moth rolls off the bedroll where she had been eating, and starts digging through cupboards, and she comes out with\u2026bandages and several bottles of ointment? You can\u2019t help being surprised, she doesn\u2019t seem practical-minded enough to have medical supplies readily available.<br /> <br /> \u201cHere, Tavi. We\u2019re going to want to disinfect those right away or you\u2019re going to get sick. Raptor Cats are like those big lizards from the Southeast-they\u2019ll kill you right away if they can, but if they can\u2019t they\u2019ll just try to injure you. Their claws are <i>filthy</i>, so the wounds usually get infected\u2026and then they just follow you from a distance until you get too sick to fight.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI already put some vinegar on them,\u201d you say, \u201cBut yeah, it can\u2019t hurt\u2026so wait, how do you know so much about Raptor Cats?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI <i>read</i>,\u201d Moth says, rolling her eyes as she gently turns you around to get a better look at your back.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou, uh\u2026you say this thing is gonna be following me around now?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell\u2026you said you fought it. Did you give it a good scare?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI think so. Knocked it off a roof. I think it has a broken leg now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI guess we can hope that\u2019ll do the trick. But be on your guard. They\u2019re really good at tracking by scent, and they\u2019re ambush predators. They\u2019re\u2026<i>mostly </i>nocturnal, if I\u2019m remembering right.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s nocturnal?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey come out at night, and sleep through most of the day. I would avoid going out much at night for a few days, if I were you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026okay. OW!\u201d<br /> <br /> Moth pats your shoulder. \u201cSorry. This ointment will sting really badly, but it\u2019ll make sure you heal up really well. No dashing scars for you, young man.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cToo bad,\u201d you chuckle. \u201cBeing able to say \u2018I got this one fighting a giant panther-snake monster\u2019 is some nice bragging rights.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, I suppose a lot of girls <i>would </i>go for that\u2026though personally I prefer a boy who knows how to chant in the language of the Old Realm and can recite genealogies from memory.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026I have the <i>weirdest </i>roommate,\u201d you declare, wincing as she rubs the ointment into your cuts.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, <i>I\u2019m</i> not the one out fighting raptor cats and bringing home bags full of human hands.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat!? That\u2019s not full of human hands!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo? I just sort of assumed. What\u2019s in there then?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026none of your business!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs it a head?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not a head. It\u2019s just a fish and a bunch of meats I tried to smoke, and apparently I didn\u2019t do a very good job\u2026and managed to attract a Raptor Cat with the smell.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, they\u2019re all yours then. I hate fish. Here, take off your shirt.\u201d Moth tugs at your new outfit. \u201cI\u2019ll need to wrap this bandage up over your shoulder and around your chest.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou, uh\u2026you have to?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOtherwise it\u2019s going to fall off. I\u2019m going to want to get some around your waist as well, just to hold these dressings in place\u2026Don\u2019t worry, I won\u2019t tell anyone how scrawny you are.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>You\u2019re\u2026uncomfortable disrobing in front of people. The only ones who know you\u2019re a girl are Aunt Dwi and a couple of her people at the Flaming Peacock. Even Rat doesn\u2019t know, and he\u2019s the closest thing you have to a best friend. You don\u2019t know White Moth very well yet, and you\u2019re pretty sure that she\u2019s a bit\u2026well, disorganized and irresponsible and scatter-brained. You\u2019re not sure you want her knowing your secret. She seems like the sort of person who might tell people without even meaning to tell anyone.</b> <b>On the other hand, she does seem to know what she\u2019s doing with these bandages and disinfectants, and you don\u2019t much relish the thought of getting infected wounds. Especially if there\u2019s a Raptor Cat out there waiting for you to get weak before it shows up for Round Two.</b> <div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <b>What should you do?</b></div> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>Resources You Have Available:</u></b></div><ul><li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Twine ArmbandKnife (Up your sleeve in a nice leather forearm-sheath</li> <li>Carrying Bag</li> <li>Fishhooks (2)</li> <li>A medium sized smoked fish (Rather pecked over)</li> <li>Three River Dragon Fangs (one big one, four smaller ones)</li> <li>A four-by-four swatch of thick, scaly River Dragon hide</li> <li>A River Dragon Spleen? You think it\u2019s a spleen? Tied in a bundle</li> <li>A Spleenful of River Dragon Parts (Rather pecked over)</li> <li>Two Heavy Clay Jugs</li> </ul><br /> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>Account Balances with the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants</u></b></div><ul><li>Personal Account: 9 Dinars</li> <li>Time Deposit Account: 15 Dinars (Fixed Return of 9% after 9 Months)</li> </ul><br /> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>Resources at your Nightside Apartment:</u></b></div><ul><li>Silver: 2 Quarter-Dinars, 1 Eighth-Dinar</li> <li>Guild Scrip: 9 Bills, each one sixteenth Dinar)</li> <li>Ledger Book, with blank Cheques</li> <li>Personal Seal issued by the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants</li> <li>Steel Spearhead (Six Inch Blade in need of a shaft)</li> <li>A Small Library</li> <li>Dishes (One Cupboard Full)</li> <li>1 Box Pressed Charcoal</li> <li>Small Iron Cooking Stove</li> <li>Several Dozen Empty Wine Bottles</li> <li>Two More Heavy Clay Jugs</li> <li>One Large Glass Bottle of Vinegar</li> <li>A potted plant (Deceased)</li> <li>Tattered Rags, and Clothes White Moth gave to you rather than throw away</li> </ul><br /> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>You Have Gained:</u></b></div> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>Attributes: (FINALIZED).</u></b><br /> <b><u>Abilities: (28/28 Allocated)</u></b></div> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>Merits: (7/7 Allocated)</u></b></div> <div align=\"left\">Gained Familiar 3: Chupong, the Daimyo of Raitons</div> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>Bonus Points: (21/21 Allocated)<br /> Specialties: (2/4 Allocated)</u></b><br /> If you've read this far down-I'm looking for votes on how to spend our two remaining Specialties! We currently have a Bureacracy Specialty in Haggling and a Larceny Specialty in Nexus Street Gangs. Suggestions welcome!</div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 06-17-2017, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T23:44:44-07:00","id":1102446,"title":"","content":"Specialty suggestion: Survival - Dealing with Animals. We've done this a lot now (river dragon, cat, raitons, our new familiar), so seems appropriate.<br /> <br /> Tell her that you'd rather tie the bandages yourself. Covered in blood as you are you need to clean up anyway, so might as well put the bandages on yourself after you've washed up. It's a flimsy excuse, but you weren't expecting to be put on the spot right now, so it'll have to do. Just be insistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T06:01:12-07:00","id":1102485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1102446#post1102446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specialty suggestion: Survival - Dealing with Animals. We've done this a lot now (river dragon, cat, raitons, our new familiar), so seems appropriate.<br /> <br /> Tell her that you'd rather tie the bandages yourself. Covered in blood as you are you need to clean up anyway, so might as well put the bandages on yourself after you've washed up. It's a flimsy excuse, but you weren't expecting to be put on the spot right now, so it'll have to do. Just be insistent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea. I'd also recommend either an Athletics specialty in climbing or go ahead and get the specialty in Alchemy we're developing. I don't know if you're going to put the Alchemy in craft, occult, or lore. I'd probably lean toward craft since we're learning more by doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T17:00:06-07:00","id":1102653,"title":"","content":"Tie the bandages yourself, specialty in survival dealing w animals and in melee knife combat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T22:00:28-07:00","id":1102706,"title":"","content":"I'll go against the grain and vote to let Moth do it. Having her learn our secret isn't great, but she's our roommate now. It's going to be hard to keep up the pretense for long anyway.<br /> <br /> Also...Moth knows more about medicine than we do and is willing to treat us for free. This is likely not the last time we'll need patching up. She's turning out to be more useful than she seemed at first, so let's not blow her off. Money and shelter go a long way, but we'll need friends too if we're going to get ahead in this city. Might as well start at home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T03:28:50-07:00","id":1102751,"title":"","content":"Let Moth do it. Like Ferryman said, this won't be the last time we have an awkward moment, and Moth is clever enough to get suspicious. Also, I don't know how Tavi is supposed to bandage her own back. If she asks why, just tell her, in so many words, &quot;The only thing worse than being a boy alone on the streets is being a girl alone on the streets.&quot;<br /> <br /> Craft Specialty : Kitbashing from junk. We've done that a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 06-12-2017, 07:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T05:48:15-07:00","id":1102780,"title":"","content":"Agreed. With decent food we're going to be developing a woman's form in the near future, and hiding our actual sex from Moth isn't going to be possible. Better to bring her in now, and if questioned, semicasual put it well. Also, I like the kitbash speciality idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T10:03:46-07:00","id":1102842,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, I'm swayed. I change my vote to honesty with moth with a strongly worded conversation about trust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T07:09:20-07:00","id":1103117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1102751#post1102751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let Moth do it. Like Ferryman said, this won't be the last time we have an awkward moment, and Moth is clever enough to get suspicious. Also, I don't know how Tavi is supposed to bandage her own back. If she asks why, just tell her, in so many words, &amp;quot;The only thing worse than being a boy alone on the streets is being a girl alone on the streets.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Craft Specialty : Kitbashing from junk. We've done that a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with all this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T19:58:59-07:00","id":1104956,"title":"","content":"<b>Survival-Dealing with Animals 2<br /> Athletics-Climbing 2<br /> Craft-Alchemy 1<br /> Craft-Kitbashing with Junk 2<br /> Melee-Knife Fights 1<br /> <br /> Looks like a three-way tie between Survival (Animal Handling), Athletics (Climbing), and Craft (With A Box of Scraps!). Please vote on your favorite of those three, our top two will be selected.<br /> <br /> Do the Bandages Yourself 1<br /> Let Moth In On Your Secret: 5</b><br /> <br /> \u201cFine,\u201d you tell Moth. \u201cHere, I\u2019ll take my shirt off so you can do the bandages. But\u2026listen. Don\u2019t tell anybody.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t tell anybody about wha-oh.\u201d She nods as you take off your shirt. \u201cYou, um. You\u2019re a girl?<br /> \u201d<br /> \u201cI\u2026yeah. But nobody knows that, Moth. I want to keep it that way?\u201d<br /> <br /> She seems confused. \u201cHow come?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe only thing worse than being a boy alone on the streets is being a girl alone on the streets.\u201d You shake your head. \u201cIt\u2019s dangerous.\u201d<br /> <br /> Moth nods. \u201cI think I get it\u2026but how long do you plan to keep up the act? I mean, you are really very masculine-no offense? But surely you can\u2019t pretend forever?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell\u2026I don\u2019t know. I mean, I hear if you don\u2019t eat well it can delay puberty, so\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s only in cases of extreme malnutrition, Tavi.\u201d Moth frowns. \u201cI mean\u2026you\u2019re way too skinny\u2026have you been <i>deliberately starving </i>yourself?!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat? No!\u201d You find yourself actually chuckling. \u201cNo, I eat everything I can, whenever I can!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen the gods blessed you with a much better metabolism than mine,\u201d she sighs.<br /> <br /> \u201cMetabowhat?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMetabolism. It\u2019s, um\u2026it\u2019s the speed at which your body burns food. People like me with slow metabolisms don\u2019t have to eat much and we still put on fat.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m pretty sure I\u2019m not skinny because of a\u2026metabolism. Pretty sure I\u2019m skinny because I usually don\u2019t have money for food.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. Oh! I\u2019m so sorry!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026for what?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI didn\u2019t mean to be insensitive\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou don\u2019t need to be sorry, Moth. It\u2019s not your fault. Now bandage me up? It\u2019s a bit chilly.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh! Right!\u201d<br /> <br /> She winds the bandages snug but not tight enough to be really constricting, and then she starts a small fire in the stove as you put ointment on the raiton-claw scratches on your face and arms. It stings.<br /> <br /> \u201cTavi\u2026\u201d Moth asks quietly. \u201cWhat do you do?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou mean, like, for a job?\u201d You finish up with the ointment and put it away, and walk across the room to grab another outfit to put on.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m\u2026well, I\u2019m hoping I\u2019m an apprentice canal boatman? We\u2019ll see, it depends on if my teacher was serious about teaching me or not. He agreed to it last night, but I haven\u2019t actually talked to him since, and it was kind of a weird night.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI see. I know the feeling. My teacher sometimes makes me feel more like a servant than an apprentice. Always running around town fetching ingredients and stirring cauldrons and drawing eyes on pieces of obsidian with white chalk\u2026there\u2019s a lot less one on one instruction time than I\u2019d like. But you learn by doing, you know?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI guess.\u201d You button up your new short, and toss the torn one on the counter. You grab one of your fishhooks and bend it against the stove, flattening the curve with your knife and curling the end into an eye.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019re you doing?\u201d Moth, who is now on her bedroll munching the rest of her fried chicken strips. She gestures at you with one of the long wooden skewers.<br /> <br /> \u201cMaking this fishhook into a needle. I\u2019m going to sew up that torn shirt.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know how to sew?\u201d She seems impressed. \u201cI\u2019d have just thrown it out.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah. I just bought that shirt. I\u2019m going to damn well get some use out of it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d offer you one of my needles, but they\u2019re not much good for sewing. No eyes\u2026I guess they\u2019re pins, really?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat are they for?\u201d You get your twine and sit cross-legged next to her on the bedroll.<br /> <br /> \u201cAcupuncture. They\u2019re good for clearing my mind if I want to meditate.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s the thing where you stick pins in yourself?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI mostly stick them in my feet. It helps me think.\u201d<br /> <br /> You shake your head as you sew. \u201cI have the weirdest roommate.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, yeah\u2026listen, Tavi. You said part of me staying here was I had to teach you to read, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI did.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright. Well, I have some reading I\u2019d like to do myself\u2026but the Master of Nine Black Chains had some homework for me. He needs me to inscribe a bunch of prayer strips for him. When you\u2019re done sewing, if you want to help me out, I can show you how to write some words. We have to write them over and over again, so you\u2019ll learn them pretty quickly.\u201d<br /> <br /> You nod. \u201cOkay. Sure. Which words?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey\u2019re kind of a long prayer strip. When we\u2019re done, they\u2019ll say, \u2018In the name of the Dual Monarchy, in the name of Setesh, in the name of Saturn who brings to each their appointed Ending, I do bind thee, O Spirit of the Departed, and seal thee within this, thy prison, until these words fade and their power is broken. By the power of the Lords of the Dead, Be It So!\u2019\u2026we\u2019re going to have to use some fancy ink I bought. It\u2019s made from the aqueous humors of dead jailers.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026what\u2019s an Aqueous Humor?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s the liquid from inside their eyeballs.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGross.\u201d You squinch up your face. \u201cWhat\u2019s your teacher\u2026doing? With these prayer strips?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey\u2019re for binding angry ghosts so they can\u2019t hurt anyone. You trap the ghost in a clay pot or a statue, and wrap prayer strips all around it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHm. Okay, I can help you with that.\u201d <div align=\"center\">***<br /> </div> You finish your sewing, and put your River Dragon bits in big clay jars with vinegar to preserve them. You eat some dinner-leftover smoked fish, heated with a bit of butter and rice on an actual stove! Then you help White Moth with her homework. Your first few prayer strips are kind of ugly-it takes you a while to get a hang of the lettering-but after a several dozen repetitions you feel like you\u2019re starting to get the hang of it. This word is \u201cseal\u201d and this word is \u201cpower,\u201d and this word is \u201cSetesh.\u201d Moth tells you it\u2019s important to do the prayer strips in Riverspeak, because the ghosts probably only spoke Riverspeak, but that for other types of spirits usually prayer strips should be done in the language of the Old Realm, which has its own alphabet. She tells you it\u2019s much harder to write in, even she has trouble with it sometimes.<br /> <br /> After a long night of reading and writing practice, you finally sleep. White Moth, now that she knows you\u2019re not a boy, is apparently fine with letting you share her bedroll. It\u2019s soft and warm and you drift off quickly. <div align=\"center\">***<br /> </div> In your dreams, you are running through unfamiliar alleyways in the long black shadows of a full moon. The walls are papered with long strips, with your face draw in them in ink, like prayer strips or the Wanted posters that the Guild hangs up offering bounties on criminals who have cheated them. Something is chasing you through the alleyways, something big, with burning golden eyes and long claws that glint in the moonlight and drip hissing poison onto the cobblestones. It is huge, a great shadow that blots out the thin strips of sky past the hanging clotheslines overhead, but it is slow-it has a limp, and it drags one leg behind it with a heavy shuffling scraping sound. You keep running, afraid to look back at it for some reason\u2026until you run into a dead end. The clicking of claws on stones gets closer. Click. Click. Click. In terror, you turn to look into its horrible burning eyes\u2026CLICK. CLICK. CLICK.<br /> <br /> You start awake.<br /> <br /> CLICK.<br /> <br /> Your heart is pounding, and Moth is snoring gently next to you on the bedroll.<br /> <br /> CLICK.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s coming from the window.<br /> <br /> You stand up. There\u2019s a black shape beyond the bamboo shutters of your window.<br /> <br /> CLICK<br /> .<br /> It\u2019s a raiton, tapping its beak against your shutters.<br /> <br /> CLICK.<br /> <br /> You go to open the window, and the bird flitters away. On the sill, next to the dead potted plant, you find...a gleaming mother-of-pearl button, a small fish head, and a shiny strand of gleaming red ribbon.<br /> <br /> \u2026it appears you have made a new friend!<br /> <br /> You yawn, and stretch. The sun is just rising, and lighting the Nexus smog in brilliant pinks and lavenders and oranges.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a brand new day. You have a place to stay, and you have money, and you have something to eat for breakfast! Your hand hurts a bit, cramped from all that writing, and your back hurts when you move from where the Raptor Cat got you, and the cool wet morning air stings a bit on all the little cuts on your face and hands\u2026but you find yourself nevertheless in a really good mood this morning. <div align=\"center\"><b>What should you do today?</b></div> <br /> <b><u>Resources You Have Available:</u></b><ul><li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Twine Armband</li> <li>Knife (Forearm Sheath)</li> <li>Carrying Bag</li> <li>Fishhooks (1)</li> <li>Sewing Needle (1)</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Account Balances with the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants</u></b><ul><li>Personal Account: 9 Dinars</li> <li>Time Deposit Account: 15 Dinars (Fixed Return of 9% after 9 Months)</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Resources Here at your Nightside Apartment:</u></b><ul><li>Silver: 2 Quarter-Dinars, 1 Eighth-Dinar</li> <li>Guild Scrip: 9 Bills, each one sixteenth Dinar)</li> <li>Ledger Book, with blank Cheques</li> <li>Personal Seal issued by the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants</li> <li>Four Heavy Clay Jugs Full of Pickling River Dragon Bits</li> <li>Three River Dragon Fangs (one big one, four smaller ones)</li> <li>A four-by-four swatch of thick, scaly River Dragon hide</li> <li>Steel Spearhead (Six Inch Blade in need of a shaft)</li> <li>A Small Library</li> <li>Dishes (One Cupboard Full)</li> <li>1 Box Pressed Charcoal</li> <li>Small Iron Cooking Stove</li> <li>Several Dozen Empty Wine Bottles</li> <li>One Large Glass Bottle of Vinegar</li> <li>A potted plant (Deceased)</li> <li>One nice set of Clerk/Merchant clothes</li> <li>Tattered Rags, and Clothes White Moth gave to you rather than throw away <div align=\"left\"><b><u>You Have Gained:</u></b></div> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>Attributes: (FINALIZED).</u></b><br /> <b><u>Abilities: (FINALIZED)</u></b></div> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>Merits: (FINALIZED)</u></b></div> <b><u>Bonus Points: (FINALIZED)<br /> Specialties: (2/4 Allocated-VOTE FOR THE REMAINING 2!)</u></b></li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T20:19:34-07:00","id":1104961,"title":"","content":"I vote for Climbing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T22:02:41-07:00","id":1104981,"title":"","content":"My first pick is still Craft (With a Box of Scraps!). For my second, I vote for Survival - Dealing with Animals. Between the raptor cat, the raiton, and the river dragon, it seems Tavi has spent almost as much time dealing with Nexus' fauna as she has with its people.<br /> <br /> As for what to do today - probably should track down Eel and see if he was serious about that apprenticeship. If we let that sit for too long, Eel will think <i>Tavi </i>isn't serious, and that career path will be closed off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T07:09:23-07:00","id":1105062,"title":"","content":"Survival (Animal Handling), Athletics (Climbing) are my votes.<br /> I second tracking down Eel for the apprenticeship, though throw in a prayer to the Elemental Dragons before we go. If there's time we'll sell the River Dragon bits that evening before reading/writing lessons.<br /> This is of course assuming everything goes according to plan. I'm guessing it won't. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T16:37:56-07:00","id":1105219,"title":"","content":"I vote survival. I say sell the bits and bobs then hit the canals. Merchants are active for a shorter period of time than the boatmen. Though much has happened since we thought of being a boatman. Perhaps we have started upon the path of a merchant with an animal focus. Either in parts or whole. As an aside I love our super awesome familiar! Can we give him a nickname like Flappers McFlighty?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T07:16:35-07:00","id":1105676,"title":"","content":"Caught up with this Quest too! This thread has been a really fun surprise! Thanks for writing Guru!<br /> The craft, survival and climb suggested specialties all sound really good, but I'm going to have to go with melee (knives) as my strongest suggestion, for too reasons.<br /> #1. Tavi has been using that little knife <i>a lot</i>, and not just in combat (or at least the spearhead). If it keeps being useful (like to cut a net loose quickly, or whatever), the specialty might help somehow.<br /> #2. Failing a craft and survival check can be really bad. But in combat, insufficient knife combat can be fatal. It just feels like there's too many street thugs and angry raptor cats out there for us to avoid combat forever, and the last fight was really close.<br /> My final vote is melee (knives) and craft (alchemy) (or occult: alchemy, whichever alchemy is located under).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3752-mushroom-king","name":"Mushroom King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3752_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T14:19:15-07:00","id":1110353,"title":"","content":"<b>Climbing 1<br /> Box of Scraps 1<br /> Animal Handling 2<br /> <br /> Not a ton of votes for narrowing things down. Animal Handling has a solid win, so that gets added to the sheet. As Climbing and Box of Scraps are tied with only a vote apiece, I\u2019ll leave the other specialty slot open, for now. We can pick our final Specialty later.<br /> <br /> Track Down Grinning Eel 2<br /> Sell River Dragon Bits First 1</b><br /> <br /> You scrub your teeth with your finger and a twig from the potted plant on the windowsill, spit down at the cobblestones, and gather some water from the dripping of the eaves over the window. It\u2019s a bit gritty-it\u2019s apparent that Gleaming Smile hasn\u2019t invested in roof repairs in some time, and you\u2019re getting a bit of clay dust. You leave your spare clay jugs out on the sill to collect more rainwater-it\u2019s the Season of Water, it\u2019s likely to rain again today or tonight-and filter the water through one of your rags to get rid of the detritus. While White Moth continues to snore, you poke at the dim coals in the stove and heat up a small pot of water, and make use of your new chamber pot while it slowly comes to a boil.<br /> <br /> Watching White Moth sleep, you briefly consider going back to bed yourself. It was so warm, and soft\u2026but even though the sun\u2019s not quite up all the way, you\u2019re feeling oddly energized. You\u2019ve been blessed with a lot of good fortune over the past couple of days\u2026and part of you is afraid that the other shoe is going to drop suddenly and it\u2019s all going to get yanked out from under you. You shake your head as you prepare breakfast, and when it\u2019s ready you bow your head over it and offer a silent but sincere prayer of thanks to the Dragons for offering you the chance at a better life. You tell them, and you tell yourself, that you intend to seize it.<br /> <br /> Breakfast is a bowl of White Moth\u2019s rice, with just a splash of vinegar for flavor.<br /> <br /> By a warm stove on a cold wet foggy morning. Under your own roof. It tastes\u2026 heavenly.<br /> <br /> After briefly considering buying some tea or herbs or spices to mix up your diet, you decide to save your money. Instead, you really ought to go find Grinning Eel and take him up on that apprenticeship. You\u2019ve been given a windfall, but regular work is the way to keep making money. If you can only keep making money, you can keep putting a little bit into your savings with the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants and hopefully build up enough money for\u2026something. Buying Grinning Eel\u2019s boat? Buying multiple boats and leasing them to boatmen? Raising chickens and selling pickled eggs?<br /> <br /> \u2026something.<br /> <br /> You finish your breakfast.<br /> <br /> Knowing Eel, he\u2019s probably been up for an hour or two already, and he\u2019s currently ferrying the morning-shift folks down to the Nighthammer foundries. They usually arrive a half hour or so after sunrise. From there he\u2019ll probably pick the graveyard-shift workers up and ferry them back up the canal. That doesn\u2019t give you too much time.<br /> <br /> You throw on your new outfit. You did good work last night, the stitches in the back are only visible with close examination, and White Moth\u2019s suggestions on removing bloodstains did wonders-there\u2019s a little discoloration, but not so much you\u2019d notice it without looking hard. You take a moment to look at yourself in the little mirror Moth has in her makeup kit (you already know where she keeps everything and which of her possessions are valuable\u2026it\u2019s not that you necessarily plan on robbing her and selling all her stuff, but it\u2019s a reflex born of long habit). Your face is still covered in little scratches, and your hair is a big frizzy black mess. You grin. You\u2019re not sure you could pull off \u201ccute kid\u201d if you wanted to, but you\u2019ve definitely got \u201croguish young street tough desperate enough to do something stupid\u201d covered. You suspect if you showed up looking as mean as you do right now, Rat\u2019s new friends might let you join the Sluice Gang. You can see why Moth was so scared of you last night.<br /> <br /> If all goes well, Grinning Eel is going to put you to work today, so you pack light. You grab your knife, tuck your remaining fish hook into your pocket along with your roll of twine so you\u2019re equipped to go fishing again if there\u2019s time for it\u2026or so that Eel can fish while you steer, if it gets to that point. You can\u2019t live on rice forever! You also grab your bag, so you have something to carry fish in. You sort of wish you hadn\u2019t bought such a nice bag-it\u2019s waterproof, but you keep filling the interior with stinking meat and fish, which sort of ruins the point. It still smells faintly of smoke and fish from last night\u2026but it\u2019s sturdy and reasonably light, and more importantly it\u2019s the only bag you\u2019ve got, so you bring it. Hopefully the smell will wash out\u2026<br /> You head out, and lock the door behind you. Moth is still snoring gently.<br /> <br /> The Blackwall neighborhood is quiet around sunrise. There are a few drunks asleep on stoops, and a few house swallows fluttering about below the clotheslines hung overhead catching bugs as the early morning sun starts to burn off the morning fog. As you head south towards the foundry districts of Nighthammer, the street markets are just getting going-vendors are putting up their stalls, laborers are trundling up and down the streets on their way to their various places of work, carts are being loaded\u2026the city of Nexus is waking up. Not that Nexus sleeps\u2026but there\u2019s a sense of early-morning calm coming from the knowledge that most of the thieves and ruffians and knife-wielding \u201cNeighborhood Watches\u201d are still sleeping off a long night.<br /> <br /> Your trip down to Nighthammer is largely uneventful. You rush through shortcuts and back alleys you\u2019d avoid later in the day, you clamber up swaying bamboo ladders and dash along the roof ways you\u2019d avoid in the rain or after dark, and once or twice you gingerly step over sleeping men you\u2019d give a wide berth if it weren\u2019t for all the empty bottles around their snoring forms. Several times, you spot raitons perched on clotheslines or rooftops. They're not exactly uncommon around here, but you get the distinct impression they're watching you-mostly because when you stop and watch them back they always look away and stare intently at something else for a while before flying away. Can a bird look sheepish?<br /> <br /> Finally, after about forty minutes of urban navigation, you reach the Nighthammer docks. The sun is peeking over the rooftops now, and the streets are bustling as always with the eternal scurrying of wagons and carts and merchants merchants on their way to and from the barges moored in the Nighthammer Pool. You follow the canal until you reach the forge-district where Eel and the other boatmen usually drop off the morning shift workers. It looks like you\u2019ve made it just in time-dozens of canal boats are in the process of unloading their packs of passengers. You shield your eyes from the morning sun with one hand, looking for Eel\u2019s distinctive hat-broad-brimmed and black, with white koi painted on it\u2026<br /> <br /> But you don\u2019t see it.<br /> <br /> As the workers are clambering up the docks, you weave your way through the crowd.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey,\u201d you call out to one of the boatmen. \u201cHave you seen Grinning Eel?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot this morning,\u201d he calls back.<br /> <br /> \u201cOld bastard probably skipped the early morning shift,\u201d another of the boatmen chuckles. \u201cToo busy counting his coin from yesterday!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLucky codger,\u201d the first one sighs. \u201cWish I\u2019d been out the other night.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t.\u201d Another, older boatman chimes in. \u201cRed Dog and Singing Fish got <i>eaten </i>the other night, and a lot of other folk got <i>boiled alive</i>. It was a <i>nightmare</i>.\u201d<br /> <br /> The younger boatman looks a little sheepish. \u201cYeah\u2026Emissary doesn\u2019t mess around, I guess\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy you lookin\u2019 for Eel, young man?\u201d The old boatman eyes you suspiciously.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe was thinking about taking me on as an apprentice,\u201d you shrug. No reason to lie. \u201cSays if I\u2019m any good maybe he can retire and lease me his boat.\u201d<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a general nodding of heads.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, Eel\u2019s been complaining a lot about his joints lately\u2026if you\u2019re looking for him, I\u2019d try the Drowned Feather. He usually drinks there when he\u2019s in a good mood\u2026and his mood yesterday was good enough I\u2019ll wager he\u2019s sleeping it off there this morning.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks,\u201d you nod your head. \u201cI\u2019ll go see if I can find him.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood luck, kid.\u201d<br /> <br /> You make your way back through the oncoming rush of foundry workers on their way to the docks, tired and groaning and chattering about how much they\u2019re looking forward to getting home and going to bed after a long night of pumping bellows and pouring molten iron.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\">***<br /> <br /> </div> The Drowned Feather isn\u2019t too far, it\u2019s right on the canal, but it takes you a while to get there anyway-the place obviously caters mostly to boatmen, and while it\u2019s easy to access from the canal the streetside entrance proves a little difficult to find. You inquire with the proprietor, a middle-aged woman cleaning up after last night\u2019s festivities, and she tells you that Grinning Eel is in fact sleeping off a raucous night in one of the guest rooms upstairs.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe was up until well after midnight, throwing Guild scrip around and buying drinks for everybody and dancing like an idiot. Apparently he sold a River Dragon\u2019s heart to an alchemist and walked away a small mountain of coin. Pretty sure he\u2019s got a couple of girls with him, too,\u201d she glowers. \u201cI swear, a man his age\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI see.\u201d It sounds like Eel hasn\u2019t been as\u2026frugal with his windfall as you\u2019ve tried to be with yours. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>\u201cYou want me to go wake him up?\u201d</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>What Do We Do With A Drunken Sailor:</b> You want to be a boatman. It\u2019s steady work, the pay is good, there\u2019s a canal right by your new apartment\u2026but you can\u2019t start a career as a canal boatman without a teacher, and Eel is <i>gonna be</i> that teacher. Splitting headache or not. You're going to wake him up, and he's going to teach you a lucrative new career, whether he wants to or not! You're pretty sure standing in a rocking boat in the canal surrounded by the smell of dead fish and Nexus sewage is the perfect hangover cure anyway.<br /> <br /> <b>Let Sleeping Eels Lie:</b> Leave a message with the owner of the Drowned Feather asking her to let Eel know you stopped by and asking him to get in touch so you can get him to mentor you when he\u2019s in full possession of his faculties. This frees your morning up to do something else! (If you vote for this option, please suggest what else you wanna do this morning.)<br /> <br /> <b>The Tide Waits For No Man:</b> Your few memories of your father includes lots of stuff about tying knots and currents and tides and canal gossip and lore. You watched Eel the other night poling his boat through heavy traffic in the pouring rain and, to be sure, you wouldn\u2019t want to try that on your first time\u2026but the river is in your blood (you do have Sail 1), and today\u2019s weather is clear and lovely. You can see Eel\u2019s boat moored at the dock right there. You could take her for a spin, maybe take a fare or two, learn a bit and make a bit of money\u2026if you move quickly, you\u2019d probably be back before the old man even wakes up!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Resources You Have Available:</u></b><ul><li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Knife (Up your sleeve in a nice leather forearm-sheath)</li> <li>A fish hook</li> <li>Your Bag</li> <li>Your Apartment Key</li> </ul><br /> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>You Have Gained:</u></b></div> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>Attributes: (FINALIZED).</u></b><br /> <b><u>Abilities: (FINALIZED)</u></b></div> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>Merits: (FINALIZED)</u></b></div> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>Bonus Points: (FINALIZED)<br /> Specialties: (3/4 Allocated)</u></b></div><ul><li>Survival (Animal Handling)</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T17:02:40-07:00","id":1110411,"title":"","content":"Waking him or taking his boat will probably get him honked off, which is a lousy way to start an apprenticeship, sao let's leave a message for him, then go back to get and sell our river dragon parts, and finally check back with Eel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T18:19:20-07:00","id":1110427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1110411#post1110411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Waking him or taking his boat will probably get him honked off, which is a lousy way to start an apprenticeship, sao let's leave a message for him, then go back to get and sell our river dragon parts, and finally check back with Eel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly what I was going to suggest","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T06:50:46-07:00","id":1110529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1110411#post1110411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Waking him or taking his boat will probably get him honked off, which is a lousy way to start an apprenticeship, sao let's leave a message for him, then go back to get and sell our river dragon parts, and finally check back with Eel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. And if he's not out of bed before noon, anything goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T07:08:35-07:00","id":1110533,"title":"","content":"Yeah, let's not get too cocky, do what we can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T20:13:21-07:00","id":1110738,"title":"","content":"I agree, I think that it would be a good idea to let him sleep and spend a half day trying to sell off the river dragon parts. If nothing else, we can get some spending money and perhaps a good second knife for when we really get into trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T21:54:13-07:00","id":1113104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1110738#post1110738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, I think that it would be a good idea to let him sleep and spend a half day trying to sell off the river dragon parts. If nothing else, we can get some spending money and perhaps a good second knife for when we really get into trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. Let's try not to get too far ahead of ourselves either. What he said to us before might not be considered binding... especially if he doesn't remember anything. That said, we want to keep an eye on him, in case he wakes up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T13:21:12-07:00","id":1116530,"title":"","content":"<b>Let Sleeping Eels Lie: Unanimous!</b><br /> <br /> You ask the innkeeper to let Grinning Eel know you stopped by. You briefly consider just stealing his boat and learning by doing\u2026but no. The other boatmen would probably come after you, they look after their own, and besides there\u2019s no need to antagonize a man who has offered to help you\u2026and now that you think about it, while the rains are a little late this year, it is still Resplendent Water: the rivers haven\u2019t flooded yet, but the water is high and fast this season. Maybe practicing on your own isn\u2019t the best idea anyway.<br /> <br /> You decide instead to head to the markets and see if you can find a buyer for your River Dragon parts. Might as well spend your morning trying to make some more money! This area of town doesn\u2019t have too many alchemists, it\u2019s mostly merchants focused on trading with the docks, so you head for the Nexus district. It doesn\u2019t take too much asking around to figure out where Blue Root, Aunt Dwi\u2019s alchemist, does business. His shop is in a slower neighborhood near the bustling Tailor District. Most of the folks you ask for directions seem to assume you\u2019re delivering an order for one of the Guild artisans in that district-apparently Blue Root does a lot of work manufacturing unusual dyes for the various textile companies in the Tailor District. You suspect Aunt Dwi probably made his acquaintance while shopping for clothes-it\u2019s just like her to run into someone by chance and then get her hooks into him in search of a discount on herbs and medicines...<br /> <br /> Blue Root\u2019s shop is clean and professional, with honest-to-the-gods glass windows and a Guild seal posted prominently on his sign. You\u2019re not sure exactly what the rest of the sign says (you\u2019re guessing it says he\u2019s an alchemist), but everyone in Nexus knows the difference between a Guildsman and a free merchant. The Guildsman will charge you more\u2026but he\u2019ll still be around tomorrow if your wares are defective, and he\u2019ll usually have some sort of return policy because he\u2019ll pass the cost of the defective merchandise on to his supplier. Free merchants aren\u2019t usually able to offer that sort of protection.<br /> <br /> As you enter, the opening of the door pulls a cord and rings a small bell. It\u2019s a clever contraption, and you find yourself thinking about setting something similar up around your apartment building so you\u2019ll know if anyone\u2019s around. Just to be safe. There\u2019s only a wooden door and a lock between you and everyone else in the Blackwall neighborhood, after all\u2026<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a desk, and the woman behind it has turned from organizing a vast array of bottles and jars to look you up and down. All the walls of this shop appear to be covered with little square shelves with small labels on them and little glass jars full of powder or herbs, or small clay jugs, or occasionally packets of parchment. There are dozens of powerful smells mingling in the air-you can make out several dried herbs and something like vinegar or brine\u2026but there are many more you don\u2019t know. It reminds you a bit of the New Friends Curry stall that sometimes operates on the west side of the Nighthammer market and will refuse to serve you until someone sits next to you to order, even before sunset.<br /> <br /> \u201cCan I help you?\u201d The woman behind the desk raises an eyebrow, interrupting your thoughts. She is strangely pale, with black hair tied tightly in a bun, and she\u2019s wearing a leather apron and gloves. The left side of her face has\u2026writing on it, on the forehead above her left eye and down onto her cheek. Some kind of swirly foreign lettering in deep blue ink, it\u2019s definitely not Riverspeak.<br /> <br /> \u201cI hope so.\u201d You smile. \u201cI have some supplies to sell, and I\u2019m looking for a buyer.\u201d<br /> <br /> She seems dubious. \u201cOh. You're selling for yourself? I assumed you were a runner for one of the tailors. Blue Root doesn\u2019t normally purchase at the shop, he goes out to the Guild market for ingredients\u2026what are you looking to sell?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re Blue Root\u2019s apprentice?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m the guy who got Dwi the River Dragon eye and the teeth.\u201d<br /> <br /> She leans over the counter, suddenly interested. \u201cI see. And the supplies you\u2019re looking to sell..?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI went to Aunt Dwi because she knows some alchemists, and I figured she\u2019d get me a fair price. But I didn\u2019t give her everything-I kept some of it to sell on my own once she found me an alchemist, so I wouldn\u2019t have to split my profits with Dwi.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI see\u2026what\u2019s your name?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m Tavi. And you are?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGolden Smoke. Tavi, what parts of the River Dragon do you have?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSeveral parts.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026do you have the liver?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not sure-it was dark when we butchered the thing, and I\u2019m not really an expert on River Dragon anatomy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt would be about\u2026this big?\u201d She holds her arms out. \u201cDarker in coloration than the other organs, sort of oval shaped and flat? Very tough and rubbery?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026yeah, I\u2019ve got something like that. I thought it was a spleen, it looked a bit like the pig spleens kids blow up and make balls out of\u2026I cut it open and stuffed a bunch of other bits inside it, then tied it up with twine. Been using it as a bundle to keep the rest fresh.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI see.\u201d Smoke takes a deep breath, composing herself. You can tell she\u2019s trying not to get excited\u2026or trying not to let you know she\u2019s excited. \u201cIf it <i>is </i>the liver, and if it is still <i>fresh </i>enough that it\u2019s <i>usable</i>...we would be willing to buy it from you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve also got three more teeth, two small ones and a big one. I have a section of scales and hide about\u2026about this big, roughly rectangular. And I have assorted smaller sections of meat stuffed inside the liver.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can buy the teeth as well, we\u2019ll grind them to powder for strength draughts, but I can\u2019t offer you very much for them, the market is a little saturated right now. The hide\u2026honestly there\u2019s not a lot I can do with River Dragon scales, you\u2019d be better off taking it to the Tailor District and finding a good tanner who knows how to work with crocodile hide. I\u2019m happy to buy assorted bits of River Dragon flesh, and for the liver I can offer decent money, but I\u2019ll have to actually see what sort of shape it\u2019s in.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s\u2026it\u2019s a little smoked. I kept it in a chimney to keep birds and bugs from getting to it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHm. That shouldn\u2019t hurt it, not if the inside is still good\u2026what kind of smoke?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat were you burning under it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. No, I hung it over a smokestack at the foundry. Cheaper than burning a bunch of stuff myself.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI see\u2026one of the foundries over in Nighthammer?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWas it the big blast foundry powered by a waterwheel?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, I\u2019m pretty sure they use oxen turning a crank.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHm. Probably some phosphorus and sulfur\u2026maybe some lime\u2026no spiritual contaminants or anything that would interfere with the process, probably\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe process?\u201d This is sounding like money. \u201cI\u2019ve heard you can use the bile from the liver to make a potion to make yourself invulnerable.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot quite...invulnerable. Just\u2026it hardens your flesh, so it\u2019s like River Dragon hide. Swords and arrows will slide off you, but your inner organs are still soft and things like hammers can still break your bones. There are a number of undesirable side effects, but it\u2019s something a Guild Merchant might like for his bodyguards or gladiators.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSounds expensive.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is. For the liver in perfect condition, fresh out of the beast, we\u2019d probably get enough bile to make a couple batches...we'd be willing to offer\u2026say, two and a half Dirham.\u201d<br /> <br /> &quot;I...see.&quot; You do some quick mental calculations. That\u2019s a thousand Dinar! You\u2019re now the one taking a deep breath to try and appear calm. It\u2019s difficult not to tremble.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat's fresh, though, Tavi. It\u2019s been a couple of days now, and I expect it\u2019s been considerably dried out by the smoking, and possibly contaminated\u2026we\u2019d offer much less, if we bought it at all.\u201d<br /> <br /> You scowl. \u201cIf I put it in a jar with some vinegar to keep it from going rancid, would that count as contamination?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shakes her head and sighs. \u201cYes, that\u2019ll make it more expensive to purify, and I expect it\u2019ll reduce the potency\u2026but it could be worse. If it\u2019s soaked in vinegar, say\u2026one Dirham.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOne and a half.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry. It\u2019s one Dirham, and if you wait to sell it the price is just going to keep going down as it gets more pickled and less fresh.\u201d<br /> <br /> You grit your teeth, trying not to burst out giggling. A Dirham is four hundred Dinar! That is still a <i>laughably vast</i> amount of money! That\u2019s enough money to pay rent every month for\u2026well, for practically the rest of your life!<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you have it with you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t. I left it back home for safekeeping.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHm. It\u2019s quite valuable. If you\u2019d like, I\u2019d be willing to come pick it up personally. I will need to get my Master to approve the expense, and hire a couple of guards to escort me, and that may take some time anyway. Would it be alright if I come by this afternoon to pick it up and deliver you a Cheque?\u201d<br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>Okay, hold on. Deep breath. Slow down. How are you going to play this?</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Show Me The Money:</b> You\u2019re not handing your goods over for a slip of paper, Guild-backed or no. That Cheque might bounce! And more importantly, Guild-backed currency is easier to track, and that\u2019s enough money that the Council of Entities is going to start getting interested in your taxes. Best to avoid a paper trail, for you and for the alchemist. You want your money in silver. Sixteen pounds of hard silver, half up front and half upon delivery of the liver.<br /> <br /> <b>Have Your People Contact My People:</b> That\u2019s way more than enough money to kill someone over. Waaay more! You are not just <i>telling </i>her where you live or where you\u2019re keeping the goods. It would be way cheaper to hire ten guys to kill you and rob your place and bring the liver back without knowing what it is than to actually pay you a whole Dirham. You need security. Go to the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants, talk to Fifteen-Fingers Liu, and have them set up the deal as a middleman. They\u2019ll probably take a hefty cut, but this way it'll be a deal between Guild companies-you can get it in writing and make use of the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants' security.<br /> <br /> <b>I Am <i>Altering </i>The Deal:</b> If she\u2019s willing to pay a Dirham for it\u2026that means Blue Root will be able to sell the resulting potions at a significant markup. Probably for at least three or four Dirham. The right move here isn\u2019t to sell it-it\u2019s to use theft or the threat of violence to get the recipe (and maybe even the other alchemical ingredients-you ARE in a fully stocked alchemist's shop!), and then go make that potion yourself. Then you can sell it for more money than you\u2019ve ever even thought about! Or maybe drink it yourself, and never worry about guys with knives in alleys again<b>!<br /> <br /> Sure, We're All Friends Here:</b> This isn't just some random stranger. This apprentice\u2019s Master is a regular client of Aunt Dwi, and she\u2019s probably bringing in regular business in herbs and medicines\u2026not to mention something of an intimate relationship with Blue Root and now with his apprentice Golden Smoke. She trusts them enough to do business, and Aunt Dwi is a good judge of character. You can probably trust these people, and if you offend them you may lose your chance at four hundred Dinar...and you've already dropped Dwi's name, so they might get offended at her and cost you an ally if things go badly. Don\u2019t get greedy, don\u2019t get paranoid-agree to the deal, go home and get the liver out of that vinegar to keep its value from going down further, and be ready to take the Cheque when the apprentice arrives.<br /> <br /> <b>That's Interesting-But I Have A Better Idea:</b> Something Else?<br /> <br /> <b><u>Resources You Have Available:</u></b><ul><li>Your Apartment Key</li> <li>Rough twine (1 roll)</li> <li>Your Lucky Pebble</li> <li>Knife (Up your sleeve in a nice leather forearm-sheath)</li> <li>A fish hook</li> <li>Your Bag</li> </ul><br /> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>You Have Gained:</u></b></div> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>Attributes: (FINALIZED).</u></b><br /> <b><u>Abilities: (FINALIZED)</u></b></div> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>Merits: (FINALIZED)</u></b></div> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>Bonus Points: (FINALIZED)<br /> Specialties: (3/4 Allocated)</u></b></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 07-15-2017, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T14:07:35-07:00","id":1116549,"title":"","content":"<b>Have Your People Contact My People</b>. Let's... let's not get ourselves killed here. This is so much damned money that getting greedy and not paying middle men is how people end up dead dead dead. Middle men exist for a reason. 400 dinars minus a large cut... is still so much money we're trying not to faint over the thought. And trying to figure out how not to disappear over the reality, one more tragic death that no one in Nexus will even notice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T19:06:32-07:00","id":1116634,"title":"","content":"Aren't we getting ahead of ourselves? We don't even know for sure if what we have is a liver! <br /> <br /> Lets just go home, get the parts, and bring them back (why didn't we do that to begin with?) posthaste. Smoke can appraise the goods and trade for cash or cheque or whatever she has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T04:05:23-07:00","id":1116789,"title":"","content":"Ask her to call the Master (the expense requires permission anyway) and offer to go get the stuff in the meantime for a proper evaluation and the final transaction. It should spare the shop the expense and wastes the least time. Pretty sure we can get our stuff and get back here without getting into too much trouble. We might well look like a courier or other delivery person...which should keep us from being jumped immediately, after all they can't be sure whom they are robbing and there is always someone you don't want to mess with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T07:13:34-07:00","id":1116832,"title":"","content":"Agreed. Bring the stuff to the shop for examination and appraisal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T09:50:50-07:00","id":1116871,"title":"","content":"Bring it to the shop, agreed. Let's stay calm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T17:53:45-07:00","id":1117023,"title":"","content":"<b>Have Your People Contact My People:</b> And let's take advantage of the situation to learn some more economics while we're at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T22:51:39-07:00","id":1117616,"title":"","content":"My answer depends on current situation. If there is no one around snooping on our conversation bring it to the shop, but dont tell her you're going to. Just say you'll contact her soon. If there are other people who might be able to over hear then we should go through a middle man","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8897-joshopotamus","name":"joshopotamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T18:29:27-07:00","id":1118018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>joshopotamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1117616#post1117616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My answer depends on current situation. If there is no one around snooping on our conversation bring it to the shop, but dont tell her you're going to. Just say you'll contact her soon. If there are other people who might be able to over hear then we should go through a middle man</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. Seconded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T20:47:43-07:00","id":1126573,"title":"","content":"<b>Have Your People Contact Mine: 4</b><br /> <b>Bring the Liver to Smoke at her Shop: 3</b><br /> <br /> <b>This is Nexus. There\u2019s always someone living upstairs or next door who might have heard you through thin walls. Aside from nosy or sharp-eared neighbors, the Guild has spies, the Council has spies, various criminal syndicates have spies\u2026it\u2019s usually dangerous to assume you\u2019re not being eavesdropped on at any given point in time. Well, nobody eavesdrops on random street rats like you, but on wealthy alchemists? The odds are good. </b><br /> <br /> \u201cBringing a couple of guards into my neighborhood might be a bad idea,\u201d you smirk. \u201cIt\u2019d just attract the wrong sort of attention.\u201d You flash Golden Smoke your best dangerous-rogue sort of smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cI see.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cListen. We don\u2019t want to get ahead of ourselves here, this might not even actually be the liver. I\u2019d like you to look it over, appraise it, and then make an offer.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nods. \u201cThat makes sense\u2026would you be able to bring it here?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNormally yes, but given how valuable you tell me it is, I\u2019d rather ensure safe storage if you decide not to buy or if I decide not to accept your offer. I\u2019ll have someone contact you later today to arrange a meeting and an appraisal.\u201d<br /> <br /> Smoke seems dubious. \u201cI\u2019m not sure I\u2019m comfortable meeting in an unknown location on your say-so.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe meeting will be under the roof of a legitimate Guild merchant I do some business with from time to time. If I\u2019m making such a highly specialized trade I\u2019m going to want their expert advice anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026very well. I will look forward to your messenger, and in the meantime I\u2019ll discuss the matter with Blue Root.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you. Say\u2026you\u2019re an alchemist. Do you know anything about Raptor Cats?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTheir scales make excellent purses.\u201d She shrugs. \u201cI\u2019ve heard you can use their musk as the main ingredient in an aphrodisiac? But there are plenty of aphrodisiacs out there that don\u2019t call for dangerous voyages into the eastern jungles. Why do you ask?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRan into one yesterday, and a friend says since it scratched me it\u2019ll probably be waiting for me to get sick from the wound and stalking me for a while. I was thinking it might be profitable to trap it, if its corpse would be as valuable as the River Dragon.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou ran into a Raptor Cat? In Nexus?\u201d She\u2019s raising an eyebrow in disbelief.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d heard rumors of it and hadn\u2019t given them much thought myself,\u201d you nod. \u201cBut it\u2019s real, alright. The story I hear says some Merchant Prince had it captured for a pet and it got loose.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell\u2026I\u2019ll look into it, but honestly I wouldn\u2019t know what to do with most of a Raptor Cat. You don\u2019t see many of them. River Dragons wash up dead sometimes, or get tangled up in fishing nets and drown themselves and then float up to the surface. And sometimes the Dragonblooded go hunting for them. It\u2019s rare, but it\u2019s happened often enough for people to figure out how to make use of them. Raptor Cats\u2026don\u2019t get brought back to civilization very often. It\u2019s probably worth more alive than dead.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHm. I guess that Merchant Prince from the rumor might pay to get it back\u2026something to think about!\u201d You shrug. \u201cThank you for your help, Golden Smoke. I\u2019ll look forward to seeing you again later today.\u201d<br /> <br /> You head out, the little bell ringing again behind you.<br /> <br /> You calmly walk past the shuttered windows of Blue Root\u2019s alchemical shop.<br /> <br /> You calmly walk around the corner and duck into an alley.<br /> <br /> You do a little dance involving lots of skipping and silently but enthusiastically pumping your arms. Four. Hundred. Dinar! <div align=\"center\"> <hr /></div> <br /> <br /> It\u2019s still early, and the trip back to the Blackwall neighborhood is reasonably quick and uneventful. You check several times along the way to make sure you\u2019re not being followed from the alchemist\u2019s shop. You take a couple of odd and inconvenient routes and spend a few minutes hiding in odd spots to lose pursuit, just in case. You\u2019re pretty good at that-pretending to be a boy out on the street does get you less unwelcome attention than people knowing your gender\u2026but it doesn\u2019t prevent that sort of thing entirely, and so you\u2019ve gotten quite familiar with losing creepy but determined tails.<br /> <br /> This time, you don\u2019t think you\u2019re being followed. Not by people, anyway. But everywhere you go, you notice there\u2019s at least one and sometimes three or four raitons perched nearby, looking as studiously nonchalant as it\u2019s possible for a bird to look. When you duck into alleys or hide, you can hear them croaking and cawing to one another, and the flapping of wings as they take flight. When you come back out of your nooks and hiding spots, you find them circling high overhead, and they usually slowly come down and land on clotheslines or rooftops nearby to continue watching you after a few minutes.<br /> <br /> When you get home, White Moth is awake. She\u2019s brewing some tea and reading a book. The cover is black and the title is in some sort of silver embossed ribbon. You recognize some of the words from last night: the big words on the front of the book say \u201cThe Spirits of the Departed,\u201d and then under that there\u2019s some smaller words you don\u2019t know, and then \u201cDead.\u201d Then at the bottom there\u2019s another couple of words you don\u2019t understand. So\u2026probably a book about ghosts?<br /> <br /> \u201cGood morning!\u201d Moth says to you as you come in the door. \u201cHave you already had breakfast?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAte some rice.\u201d You nod. \u201cWith a little vinegar.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUgh. Rice again? I need to get some vegetables or something\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou have\u2026money?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026no.\u201d She sighs. \u201cNo vegetables. Maybe I should research dead criminals and see if I can find a pirate or something whose ghost I can summon to ask where he hid his silver\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can\u2026do that?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, yeah. I\u2019ve got the summoning part down pretty well, but I\u2019m only allowed to do it when the Master of Nine Black Chains is around. I\u2019m, uh, not so great with warding or binding yet.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s that mean?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt means I could probably call up a pirate ghost, but he might cut my throat and drink my blood and then ride around town drinking and fighting using my dead body, though.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat sounds\u2026less like a good plan then.\u201d You\u2019re finding yourself regretting being all intimidating with White Moth. She doesn\u2019t seem to know it, but she\u2019s legitimately frightening. People shouldn\u2019t talk about evil spirits possessing corpses so casually! It\u2019s bad luck!<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah\u2026thanks for your help with the prayer strips last night. I\u2019m gonna bring them over to the Master this afternoon. He says just after noon is the best time to research in dangerous places, the sun keeps most of the really bad stuff hiding until after dark. If you want I could introduce you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks. But I have someone I have to meet.\u201d You take what you hope is a liver and not some other less valuable organ out of its clay jar, pat it dry with one of your rags, wrap it in another rag, and put it in your carrying bag.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, gross.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Princess of the Umbral Infinitudes is grossed out by a random organ?\u201d You tease. \u201cI\u2019d assume you\u2019re used to a little blood and guts.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIck.\u201d She wrinkles her nose. \u201cTavi, I have literally cut open dead guys, and I\u2019m telling you most of them smelled better than that thing, and looked more appetizing. You\u2019re not gonna....eat that, are you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNope. Gonna sell it. Good luck with your prayer strips!\u201d You head for the door. \u201cI hope you catch plenty of ghosts!\u201d <div align=\"center\"> <hr /></div> <br /> <br /> Your prize in hand, you make your way to the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants! It\u2019s almost noon by the time you arrive, and Yinhang Square is bustling with Guildsmen hurrying this way and that in search of profit. You give the grizzled mercenary guarding the door a nod, and to your surprise he grins and nods back as you approach.<br /> <br /> \u201cTavi, right?\u201d He says.<br /> <br /> \u201cUm. Yes.\u201d You smile. Smiling is a good thing to do when you\u2019re unsure of social context.<br /> <br /> \u201cI appear to have you at a disadvantage, Tavi! I\u2019m Toad in Spring. I try to remember our clients.\u201d He grins right back at you. \u201cYou run out already, kid? Coming back to withdraw your money?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026no?\u201d You shake your head, slightly confused. \u201cI\u2019m actually looking for help setting up a business deal I hope is going to make me some more money.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell shit!\u201d he laughs. \u201cLooks like I owe Liu a bit of silver!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow so?\u201d You\u2019re not liking the turn this conversation is taking.<br /> <br /> \u201cKid like you? I bet him you\u2019d be back the very next day to try and pull most of your money out to spend it on one thing or another. He bet me not only would you not do that, you\u2019d be back within the week to put more money in. Said something about you reminding him of a young Merchant Prince he once knew.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHm. How much do you make if I go in there and pull all my money out? It might be worth doing, if I split your winnings with you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHa!\u201d The mercenary pats your back and almost knocks you over. \u201cOld Liu\u2019s a good judge of character alright! A nice thought, kid, but no. That\u2019d be cheating, and that that would take all the fun out of gambling.\u201d<br /> <br /> He waves you in. You\u2019re not sure you understand the\u2026allure\u2026 of gambling.<br /> <br /> You wait for a middle-aged woman and what you quickly surmise are her two burly teenage sons to drop off a small sack of silver (you gather from their conversation that she runs a small stall in the market nearby, though you\u2019re unable to make out what she sells) and make her way out. She doesn\u2019t pay you much mind, but her sons give you wary looks and puff themselves up a bit. Your new clothes make you look more professional, but you still apparently look like trouble.<br /> <br /> You explain your intent to the clerk at the front desk, who asks you to wait a few minutes while he ducks into the back office, and then Fifteen-Fingers Liu comes out to meet you. He\u2019s wearing a completely different set of fancy silk robes from yesterday-these ones are deep green, and have little dancing grasshoppers embroidered on them in yellow and gold, playing tiny instruments. Just as yesterday, you find yourself taking a comfortable seat in Liu\u2019s office, admiring his tapestries of armored frogs at war.<br /> <br /> \u201cFeng tells me you are looking for our help to broker a sale, young man.\u201d Liu strokes his long white beard, an expression of slightly satisfied amusement on his face. \u201cWould I be wrong to guess that you\u2019re selling more, what was it\u2026alchemical supplies?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019d be right.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was under the impression that you sold your previous goods using Dwi as your broker. Why is it that you are coming to us?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI knew Dwi knows several alchemists she\u2019s worked with in the past. I wanted to see who she trusted enough to work with. She\u2019s a pretty good judge of character.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe recommended you come to us to open your accounts, so I suppose I can\u2019t argue.\u201d Liu smiles. \u201cAnd once you knew which alchemists she preferred to work with, you decided to cut out the middleman?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI figured I\u2019d make more if I sold directly to the alchemist, yes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen why come to us?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMy goods are, um. Worth more than I thought. I\u2019d prefer to make the exchange here, with Guild backing and your security nearby. And I\u2019d prefer to put the money into my accounts right away rather than having to walk across Nexus with that much silver on me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Silently, Fifteen-Fingers Liu stands up, walks to the open door of his office, closes it, and returns to his seat. Sitting down again, he steeples his fingers under his chin and leans forward until his long beard is almost brushing the polished surface of his desk.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow much silver are we talking about, Tavi?\u201d<br /> <br /> You gulp. Liu is pretty old, but this is a bank-he has mercenary guards pretty close by. You consider the possibility that maybe your banker will just kill you and take the goods\u2026but no. Dwi is, after all, a really good judge of character.<br /> <br /> You put the bag on his desk. Liu gingerly opens it, sees the wrapped wrags, wrinkles his nose at the smell, and looks at you quizzically.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat is-I hope-a River Dragon liver. My alchemist buyer says fresh out of the Dragon it\u2019d be worth two and a half Dirham. She says that if it\u2019s a couple days old and a bit pickled, which this is\u2026she\u2019s willing to offer a single Dirham.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liu whistles. \u201cThat\u2019s a hefty sum for lizard guts.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is. She\u2019s going to want to appraise it to make sure it\u2019s actually the liver and that it\u2019s in good enough shape for the potions she wants to make-potions that make your skin as hard as River Dragon scales. Apparently Merchant Princes might want them for their guards or gladiators.\u201d<br /> <br /> The old man nods. \u201cMakes sense\u2026and the only person who has offered you an appraisal of the value of this liver is\u2026the woman you\u2019re selling it to?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you-\u2026oh.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHeh. I suspect she might lowballing you, my boy. Pick a number that seems really big to shake \u2018em up, cut that number down a bit to a still hefty number to make it seem realistic because nobody trusts their own good luck, and they won\u2019t even think about how that first number you pulled out of the air maybe ought to have been even bigger to start with. It\u2019s an old trick when you\u2019re in a specialized industry dealing with somebody unfamiliar with the trade. Did she tell you that you ought to sell right away because it\u2019s going down in value fast?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026she did.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell\u2026I\u2019m not an alchemist. Maybe she was being perfectly honest with you! But if I were you, I\u2019d want an appraisal by a separate alchemist unrelated to the deal. This is just an old man\u2019s hunch, but\u2026well, there\u2019s a lot more than a couple of Dirham riding on gladiatorial matches sometimes. We might be able to sell this thing for a lot more if you get a couple different alchemists bidding on it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2026makes sense.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s a hitch, though.\u201d Liu frowns. \u201cWhen we broker a deal like this, we just take a flat five percent cut of the sale, so you can\u2019t lose any money on the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants\u2026but I don\u2019t know a River Dragon Liver from a cow liver. Alchemists don\u2019t appraise things for free. So if we hire an appraiser and our appraiser says your goods are worthless, you\u2019re out his fee and you don\u2019t have a sale to make it up. And if you skip the appraiser and trust your buyer\u2026well, there\u2019s a chance she tells you your goods are almost worthless and buys \u2018em for a pittance and screws us over.\u201d<br /> <br /> Now you\u2019re frowning.<br /> <br /> \u201cLiu\u2026how much would an alchemist normally charge for an appraisal?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLast time I had to have my usual man appraise something, he charged four Dinar.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOuch\u2026I want that money for rent\u2026but even if it\u2019s not as valuable as I\u2019m hoping for, if it\u2019s River Dragon bits I\u2019ll probably make the money back.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026I hope so. Even if it\u2019s not worth a Dirham, it\u2019s probably worth something. I\u2019ll send Feng to call over my alchemist friend., then.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t mention it. Say, Tavi\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t often encounter young men your age blessed with your head for business. You said yesterday you\u2019re looking to work as a canal boatman? I hope I\u2019m not offending you saying this, but I think that\u2019d be a terrible waste.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026are you\u2026offering me a job, sir?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m trying to get you to ask me for a job, kid.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI see.\u201d You keep your expression as serious as you can\u2026as you steeple your fingers and lean across the desk, mimicking Liu\u2019s demeanor when you mentioned large amounts of silver. \u201cTell you what, Liu. You say you normally take a five percent cut of my sale? How about you take one percent instead, and in exchange I work as an apprentice for you for a while, see if I\u2019m suited for the work.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHrm. Assuming three percent of two and a half Dirham\u2026\u201d Liu\u2019s fingers nimbly clack scarlet beads along the rails of his abacus.<br /> <br /> \u201cThirty Dinar,\u201d you say, a split second before he does.<br /> <br /> He raises an eyebrow. \u201cFor one of my clerks, that\u2019s about eight months\u2019 pay.\u201d<br /> <br /> You do some more math in your head. That\u2019s\u2026significantly more than a boatman would make.<br /> <br /> \u201cThen, assuming we make the sale, in exchange for you only taking a two percent cut, what if I work for you for three months for free? After that we can decide based on my work whether you keep me on and start paying me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSeven months free.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFour.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTavi, you\u2019re a smart kid, but you\u2019re a still just a kid. I couldn\u2019t pay you that much more than a trained clerk, it wouldn\u2019t be fair to-\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLiu, you\u2019re talking as though we sell this thing for price I\u2019ve been quoted for an unblemished fresh liver. If we\u2019re talking only one Dirham, which might be a lowball but might be an honest and fair price, three percent is only, um\u2026twelve Dinars. So you\u2019d be saving\u2026two Dinars, I think? Besides, none of your trained clerks remind you of a certain young Merchant Prince you once knew.\u201d<br /> <br /> You wink.<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026who said that?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cToad in Spring. Your guard at the door.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liu chuckles. \u201cTavi, you haggle like my grandmother, and that\u2019s a compliment. Tell you what-how about we make the deal, I charge you five percent as normal, and then afterwards...we talk about the possibility of my hiring you for a position that would be paid right away.\u201d<br /> <br /> You nod. \u201cThat sounds pretty reasonable.\u201d <div align=\"center\"> <hr /></div> <br /> <br /> It takes a couple hours for Red Clover, Liu\u2019s alchemical appraiser of choice, to arrive and complete his appraisal. It\u2019s good news! You do, in fact, have a River Dragon liver! Well\u2026part of one. Clover informs you that what you have is the front quarter or so of the liver, the rest must have been cut away and gone to someone else during the chaotic butchering process. He advises you that the way you stuffed other organs inside and tied it shut probably helped preserve the organ, as did the smoking and the pickling. After poking about a bit with a long wooden spoon, he declares that the organ probably has enough quality bile to produce one skin hardening draught, perhaps two if you\u2019re lucky. He declares to you and Liu that while one of those potions would probably sell for somewhere between two and five Dirham, the process to make them is expensive and requires lots of other unusual ingredients in addition to River Dragon bile. For what you have, he tells you a fair price would be around half a Dirham.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s two hundred Dinar.<br /> <br /> Red Clover actually offers to buy it from you on the spot for one hundred and ninety six Dinar, just taking his appraisal fee off the cost of the goods, and you almost spit and shake his hand on the spot, but Fifteen Fingers Liu puts his hand on your shoulder and shakes his head, and you instead tell Clover that you have another buyer, and you\u2019d like to hear her offer before you accept his.<br /> <br /> Clover smiles ruefully. \u201cFair enough. I can stick around.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants arrange a runner with a message, and about forty minutes after that Golden Smoke shows up, looking serious. The two of you sit across a gleaming table, you with Fifteen Fingers Liu standing slightly behind you on your right and Red Clover leaning on the wall nearby.<br /> <br /> Smoke greets you perfunctorily and examines the goods.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis\u2026is in pretty bad shape, and it\u2019s far from the whole liver, Tavi.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s what our Red Clover, our appraiser tells me,\u201d you sigh. \u201cI was hoping it would be in nearly ideal shape and I\u2019d be able to sell it to you for most of the two and a half Dirham you said you\u2019d offer for perfect condition. In the condition it\u2019s in\u2026he said he\u2019d only be willing to offer me two thirds of a Dirham for it.\u201d<br /> <br /> In the corner, Red Clover\u2026manages to turn the noise he\u2019s making into a plausible sneeze.<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026I see.\u201d Golden Smoke sighs. \u201cI wasn\u2019t expecting an auction, young man. I\u2019ll offer you three quarters of a Dirham. That\u2019s as high as I\u2019m going. Red Clover?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cToo thin a margin for me, lass.\u201d Clover gives her a rueful grin. \u201cThat\u2019s the advantage of dealing in bulk like Master Blue Root, eh?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI suppose so.\u201d Smoke nods, and gets out a gleaming black leather account book embossed with silver lettering. \u201cTo whom should I make out the Cheque?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can make it out to Tavi,\u201d Fifteen Fingers Liu declares, eyeing her ledger the way you\u2019ve seen Rat sometimes eye a clumsy foreigner with a fat purse. \u201cYou\u2019re with the Silver Falcon Consortium?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s right. Master Blue Root\u2019s sister-in-law works as one of their auditing clerks.\u201d Smoke shrugs. \u201cHe says he gets the family rates.\u201d She pulls her necklace out of her shirtfront to reveal the small seal dangling on it, inks the seal, and stamps the cheque with the image of a tree depicted with branching roots and starts hanging in its branches.<br /> <br /> \u201cI see. I won\u2019t try to seduce him away from them, then.\u201d Liu winks, and accepts her Cheque. \u201cI\u2019ll just deposit this into your account, young Master Tavi.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you, Liu.\u201d You can\u2019t help smiling, but you try to keep it a cool collected sort of smile. You\u2019ve just made three hundred Dinar. Well, two-eighty-one with the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants\u2019 cut and the appraisal fee for Red Clover, but still!<br /> <br /> Some brief additional haggling and a small bidding battle between Golden Smoke and Red Clover sees you selling your remaining River Dragon fangs and pickled bits for an additional twelve Dinar. The alchemists gather the supplies and take their leave\u2026and you are left behind in a rather fancy meeting room with Fifteen-Fingers Liu.<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026I think Red Clover likes you, Tavi,\u201d Liu chuckles.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s nice. Also, YES!\u201d You jump to your feet and laugh in delight. \u201cI didn\u2019t think she was gonna buy that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was bold.\u201d Liu smirks, pulling out a long pipe and lighting it. \u201cBut with an offer already made there was no reason not to risk being bold. So, if my calculations are correct, after our five percent charge, you just made two hundred fifty two Dinars, young man. \u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHm? Five percent of three hundred and twelve is a little under sixteen Dinars, Liu.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTrue. But for the sale of alchemical ingredients, there\u2019s a ten percent tax to pay to the Council of Entities as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> You scowl. \u201c\u2026oh.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIndeed.\u201d Liu shrugs. \u201cCost of doing business.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026I guess I wouldn\u2019t be making any money at all if it weren\u2019t for the Emissary.\u201d You shrug, then break into a grin again. \u201cIt\u2019s still a good day!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIndeed. Tavi, have you had formal training in arithmetic?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s just that you seem to have an excellent head for numbers. Most of my clerks would be breaking out the abacus for calculations you seem to be doing quite quickly in your head.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI mean\u2026my mother taught me a bit about money.\u201d You shrug. \u201cAnd Aunt Dwi is always talking about percentages, she takes a share of the profits each of her girls makes. So I guess I know how to figure those.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHm.\u201d Fifteen Fingers Liu inhales slowly, and then lets curling wisps of smoke from his pipe roll out to twirl around his magnificent moustache. \u201cI recommend that we deposit the proceeds from this deal into your interest bearing time-sealed account. It\u2019s fixed at nine percent interest for the next nine months, so that will let you make back our fee and some of the cost of the tax.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat leaves me with\u2026five Dinars I can access, right? You took the four for the appraisal out of my other account before the deal?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s right.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLet\u2019s put fifteen Dinars into my Cheque account. That way I have the money if I need it. You can put the rest into the time sealed account.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liu nods.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll do that. Now, Tavi, about the other matter we discussed\u2026I think you have what it takes to be a Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchant. I\u2019m willing to offer you a position as an apprentice clerk. You\u2019d be expected to show up here looking clean and presentable just before dawn every morning and work until sunset. You\u2019d be paid two Dinar each month. It\u2019s not easy work. Our apprentice clerks are expected to do basic accounting and sales work, but they also handle a lot of the unpleasant tasks-most notably debt collection, which can sometimes be a bit dangerous. It involves going along with our mercenaries and tracking down people who owe us money and don\u2019t wish us well to force them to pay up or get dragged off to forced labor. But if you\u2019re as talented as I think you\u2019re going to be, there will be chances to rise within the ranks. What do you say?\u201d <div align=\"center\"><b>This is a life-changing decision. What <i>do </i>you say?</b></div> <br /> <b>Accept the Offer: This is a chance to join the Guild, albeit at the bottom rung of the ladder. Joining the Guild is a way to get rich and powerful. The Guild pretty much runs Nexus\u2026but you\u2019ll be a part-time bank clerk, part-time legbreaker. Remember back when we were picking what life path to go down and we opted to go get an apartment and put off that decision? This is one of those paths. It leads to a life of disciplined and vaguely-legitimized theft and regular violence against down-on-their luck people a lot like yourself as you were last week. Tavi's great at Bureaucracy but can't actually read or write, which complicates office work and accounting, so she's gonna end up spending a lot of time with Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants' hired Guild Mercenaries doing investigation, tracking, and roughing up of debtors if you go down this road.<br /> <br /> Decline the Offer: You just made a ton of money. More money than you can really hold in your brain right now. Enough to pay the rent every month for years and years! You don\u2019t need to risk your life for two Dinar a month. You don\u2019t have to jump at the first offer you get, you can afford to find a more appealing profession, or maybe go into business on your own. There are lots of other paths to take!<br /> <br /> Haggle: You don\u2019t want to accept the offer as-is\u2026but perhaps you can talk Liu into offering you a better deal. If you pick this option, you should tell me what you\u2019re asking him for to get you to accept the position, and if it wins I\u2019ll be rolling to see if you can persuade Fifteen Fingers Liu. If you succeed I'll count your vote as an Accept vote but modify the deal to include your specifications. If you fail I'll count it as a Decline vote.</b><br /> <hr /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">INVENTORY:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Asset</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">NOTES:</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">On Your Person:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Apartment Key</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Rough twine (1 roll)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Your Lucky Pebble</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Knife</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Up Sleeve In Nice Leather Forearm Sheath</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Fish Hook</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Your Bag</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Silver: 2 Quarter-Dinars, 1 Eighth-Dinar</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Guild Scrip: 9 One-Sixteenth Dinar Bills</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">One nice set of Clerk/Merchant clothes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Bank Accounts:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Personal Account: 20 Dinars</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Time Deposit Account: 252 Dinars (Fixed Return of 9% after 9 Months)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Nightside Apartment:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Ledger Book, with blank Cheques</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Personal Seal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">For your Cheques with the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Four Heavy Clay Jugs</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">A four-by-four swatch River Dragon hide</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Steel Spearhead</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">(Six Inch Blade in need of a shaft)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">A Small Library</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Property of White Moth</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Dishes (One Cupboard Full)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Property of White Moth</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">1 Box Pressed Charcoal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Small Iron Cooking Stove</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Several Dozen Empty Wine Bottles</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Ten Pound Bag of Rice</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Property of White Moth</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">One Large Glass Bottle of Vinegar</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">A potted plant (Deceased)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Tattered Rags and Hand-Me-Downs</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Clothes White Moth gave to you rather than throw away</td> </tr> </table></div> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>You Have Gained:</u></b></div> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>Attributes: (FINALIZED).</u></b><br /> <b><u>Abilities: (FINALIZED)</u></b></div> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>Merits: (FINALIZED)</u></b></div> <div align=\"left\"><b><u>Bonus Points: (FINALIZED)<br /> Specialties: (3/4 Allocated)</u></b></div> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 08-08-2017, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T00:14:06-07:00","id":1126606,"title":"","content":"Let's wait a bit, maybe learn to read, make a less brutal decision. What was it than fifteen-finger Liu was just saying about accepting the first offer that comes your way?<br /> <br /> <b>Decline the Offer. </b>We've spent a lot of our life so far running from gangs and avoiding people seeking to take advantage of us. The Guild is a far, far nicer gang than we've had the option to join so far, but... debt-collection is not a pretty business. Let's not get comfortable in a job doing exactly the sort of thing that killed our father.<br /> <br /> (Meta - I'm pulling for 'Caravan Master' or 'Commodities Broker' rather than 'Banker', since we're clearly destined to be a merchant of some type or other. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9510,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","user":"BlueWinds","date":". 08-09-2017, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T05:11:13-07:00","id":1126661,"title":"","content":"<b>Decline. </b><br /> <br /> On the surface, Liu's offer looks great. But if I've got a decent read on Tavi, she'd probably get a distaste for the job pretty quickly once it got down to dirty work. <i>More importantly, we have enough money to take time and shop around now. </i><br /> <br /> Two days ago, becoming a priest looked great mostly because it meant not starving to death. This morning, becoming a boatman looked good because it meant sustainable income. Right now, we've got enough capital to start our own small business, and no <i>particular </i>reason to get involved in this one. Choice is an incredible luxury - let's not be too quick to toss it aside. <br /> <br /> (Meta - maybe we can become an occultist after all! Or some kind of artisan. Ooh! We should ask Ms. Umbral Infinitudes if there's any money in talismongering!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T09:31:16-07:00","id":1126740,"title":"","content":"<b>Decline...politely.</b><br /> <br /> Liu has been more than fair to us, considering that until just recently we were a street urchin and still pretty much look like one. Even though it's part of his job, he still went out of his way to help us when he didn't have to. That makes him a valuable contact, at least, if not exactly a friend.<br /> <br /> But...the job he's offering sounds like something Tavi really wouldn't enjoy in the long run. Collections? No thanks. Let's decline, and then maybe get serious about broadening our education with White Moth. There have got to be some better opportunities out there for a kid with a head for numbers who can also read and write and who knows what else, and we have the luxury of looking for them now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T16:54:50-07:00","id":1126890,"title":"","content":"I agree with ferryman. This guy is cool but we don't want to be a debt collector. Joining the guild isn't out of the question but not like this . Let's learn to read and use our ability to buy food for the foreseeable future to get some more education. Also let's trap a cat! And learn to speak bird!<br /> <br /> I'm so happy this quest is still running, it's a favorite of mine!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T18:15:23-07:00","id":1126908,"title":"","content":"Decline. While Liu is a stand up guy, the rest of the Guild is a bunch of rat bastards. Anyway, you are a clever girl, but it is not like you could hide your sex for long if you are working from dusk till dawn. With over 250 Dinars, you are also modestly wealthy by your standards. Anyway, you will be making over 2 Dinars a month from interest slone, so why bother working for a living for the same amount?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 08-09-2017, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T20:09:13-07:00","id":1127459,"title":"","content":"Decline very politely. We've got money, and we want to learn to read and write, and maybe we'll pick up a few things from White Moth in the process. We have to learn to read by reading from something, after all.<br /> <br /> OOC: Learning to read can take, depending on aptitude, application, and most of all, the script in use, anywhere from an afternoon to several months. I, personally, once put about 15 minutes into learning to read hangul and made enough progress to be able to sound out a few simple words. For those of you not familiar with it, hangul is the writing system of Korea, and the Korean emperor who created it said that &quot;a wise man can learn it in a morning, a dullard in a week.&quot; The scripts of Creation were designed by Solar Exalted in the First Age, so with the exception of Old Realm, I doubt they'd be harder to learn than Canadian Aboriginal syllabics, a script almost as quickly learned as hangul, and for the same reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T20:58:47-07:00","id":1127471,"title":"","content":"screw these other guys. Tavi hasn't had a job in her life and while you can't take the first offer you get, we'd be declining the boat man job for this and this would be a nice fall back in case our other ventures fall apart in the future. I'd accept. Sure its not exciting but i hope we can convert that into a training montage, gain contacts and learn the biz before hopefully using our new found knowledge to springboard into cool new adventures. <br /> <br /> <b>ACCEPT ALL THE WAY</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8897-joshopotamus","name":"joshopotamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T23:11:46-07:00","id":1127500,"title":"","content":"<b>Beg off an answer for a time, ask to think it over</b>.<br /> This is somewhere between Decline politely and Haggle. It is a big decision and it is unfair to expect an immediate answer, especially when you don't know all your options. Liu is likely to be sympathetic to the idea that we want to seriously consider it and it's a softer sell than a hard no. Given as how we, as a majority, don't want to accept the job as is, asking for time should give us a chance for personal growth that can give us a better bargaining position.<br /> <br /> If pushed for an immediate answer, we should sorrowfully decline as we cannot be certain we can handle some over the lesser known tasks at the moment. But time to think it over and potentially haggle? That keeps the door a possibility rather than tie us to a path right away. An absolute decline, no matter how polite could have negative consequences. Especially if we take a 'lesser' offer, like the boatman.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem is debt collecting from unfortunates. That is a Hard No for what I envision of Tavi. Getting people to honour their obligations is one thing, throwing families out on the street is another. Violence is not really an issue, at least when the other guy starts it and theft...well we were a beggar-thief not a week ago. To be honest, I don't think Tavi wants to go back to that life and condemning someone else to it would be crossing the line. Taking from rich merchant cartels and others who won't miss it in order to survive is one thing, taking from those who need it; we might as well have joined a gang.<br /> <br /> We really need to learn how to read and write.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T12:06:56-07:00","id":1127730,"title":"","content":"I'm voting for accepting as well. We have to start at the bottom after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T14:35:21-07:00","id":1127785,"title":"","content":"I'm in favor of accepting for a few reasons. First, You're doubling your income which will keep us from dipping too much into our savings. That way we can keep it for a rainy day. Secondly, training in reading, writing, and business will probably go better if you have reason to use it daily. Yes, you'll probably be working in collections a lot, but, as Eel showed earlier, not everyone uses their money wisely and they don't think about the consequences. It'll suck being one of the ones dealing out those consequences, but its better than being one of those getting the consequences. (Meta: This can also lead to more adventures as you investigate missing debtors and uncover conspiracies and such) These can lead to a variety of jobs and gives great training. Later, we can start our own business with more ability.<br /> <br /> That said: Ask for a day or two to consider. This isn't an unreasonable request, and I think we can manage it. Its a good bargaining position to work from and you might be able to get him to at least provide you with a few &quot;uniforms&quot; to wear on the bank's dinar. (As an &quot;operations expense&quot;) Maybe after, haggle for &quot;hazard pay&quot; each time you do collections. Not much, just a few coppers each time. In the meantime, go capture yourself a Raptorcat; Dead or Alive, hang out(covertly) around some Alchemy stores and see what you can learn about what's valuable and what isn't (also see if you can't figure out some stuff to help you heal, fight, etc.), maybe make the birds more your friends, and learn more reading and writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T21:28:37-07:00","id":1137594,"title":"","content":"<b>Decline: 4<br /> Accept: 3<br /> Ask for Time To Think: 2</b><br /> <br /> \u201cThat is a generous offer, Liu\u2026but I hope you won\u2019t be offended if I decline, at least for now.\u201d You give him an earnest smile. \u201cToday I just made what would be, um\u2026nine years\u2019 pay, I think? At the job you just offered me. Dragons know it was mostly luck, but I want to take some time and think about what I do next. This is the first time in a long time I\u2019ve had the opportunity to relax for a few days and come up with a plan.\u201d<br /> <br /> Fifteen Fingers Liu grins. \u201cI was hoping you\u2019d haggle me up, but I understand. Listen. As of today, your balances with us qualify you for free advice and financial consultations. Once you come up with that plan, I\u2019d love to go over it with you and see what we can do to help you get started.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks, Liu.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo need to thank me. It was a pleasure doing business with you, Tavi. Most of my time these days is spent on persuading Guild Merchants to invest with us, or wining and dining prospective clients. It\u2019s been years since I was in on brokering an exciting little deal like this one. You remind me a bit of myself at your age, though my big break was art pieces rather than alchemical ingredients. Take the time you need, but know that the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants have your back...and if you change your mind, well\u2026I can usually find an opening.\u201d<br /> <br /> You give him a bow. \u201cThank you, sir.\u201d <div align=\"center\">******</div> <br /> By the time all the paperwork is done, it\u2019s late afternoon. You buy a big sack of dried fish, a bigger stack of dried mushrooms, and several dozen boiled eggs at the market on the way home, along with some cheap spices and a ginger root to plant in that empty flowerpot on your windowsill. No more plain rice for you! You also buy a couple sticks of incense.<br /> <br /> You are in a great mood as you putter about your apartment. You put the dried foods away in your cupboards, you tidy up the dishes that Moth left sitting out from her breakfast, and you light an incense stick from the banked coals in your little iron stove so you can properly offer a heartfelt prayer of gratitude to the Dragons for blessing you with such astounding good fortune. The incense smells really nice, like the sweet spices down at the markets, and you sit for a time cross-legged and smiling, enjoying the smell and feeling incredibly lucky and incredibly rich. You hope the incense will help a bit with the smells of the apartment-between your pickling vinegar, the River Dragon bits, the fish-and-sewage smells of the nearby canal wafting in the open window, and Moth\u2019s sweaty bedroll, this place is less pleasant to at least one sense than sleeping on a rooftop under a smokestack.<br /> <br /> After a time, you rise from your meditation and go to your windowsill to plant your ginger root in your flower pot. Thoughts of growing and selling ginger, or perhaps selling pickled ginger, flit through your head. You\u2019re so used to the hustle, to having nothing and trying to turn every advantage, every possession into a way to survive\u2026hm. There are more little presents on the windowsill. There\u2019s a fat wooden bead painted red and yellow, the back half of a decently sized lizard, and a shiny blue piece of silk with some sort of writing on it. As you plant your ginger, you spot a raiton watching you from the eaves of the building next door.<br /> <br /> \u2026you consider briefly, and take the gifts. Then you break off a piece of dried fish and leave it on the windowsill for your new friends. You smile at the lizard. Just a few days ago, you would have fought for that scrap of food. You decide to debone it and cook it up with rice. You can just tell Moth that it\u2019s fish.<br /> <br /> As the sun slowly sets and the pot of water on your little stove slowly heats up, you lie back on Moth\u2019s bedroll and look at the ceiling. You\u2019re safe. You\u2019re dry. You\u2019re warm. You\u2019re well-fed. You have a home. You\u2019re rich now, sort of\u2026 you don\u2019t need to struggle to make it through to tomorrow, or worry about dying on the street next winter. The Dragons have blessed you with the luxury of thinking past the present. You can think about next year, and the year after that.<br /> <br /> You can\u2019t shake the feeling that your good fortune isn\u2019t just dumb luck. The Dragons gave you the chance for a reason. With the money you now have in the bank, you can start a new life. You could probably do whatever you wanted\u2026or at least, you have the resources to try.<br /> <br /> As the water starts to steam, you find your mind is already boiling. Should you start a business? Should you invest in somebody else\u2019s? Should you find a job? Should you try and find an apprenticeship and learn a skilled trade? Should you buy a stake and try to join a merchant caravan? Should you train raitons to do tricks? Should you hunt down the Raptor Cat? Should you join the drug trade? Should you still learn to be a canal boatman? What makes you happy in life, other than food and shelter? What do you want to care about now that you\u2019re like Moth and you have the luxury of caring about things not immediately relevant to survival? Who do you want to be?<br /> <br /> You boil rice and grill your lizard with a pinch of the seasonings you bought. You eat alone; White Moth is apparently coming back late tonight. You hope she hasn\u2019t gotten eaten by a ghost.<br /> You have the evening to yourself to think, and your mind turns inward. After several hours of quiet contemplation, you come to a decision: <div align=\"center\">*****</div> <br /> <br /> You already have what you\u2019ve always wanted-you\u2019re less worried about getting more and more worried about losing what you have. This is Nexus-guys like the Leopard Gang might show up and try to take it from you, once they realize you\u2019re loaded now. You have resources, and you have brains\u2026but you need some muscle. And, frankly, you\u2019re sick of being all on your own. You need friends. You need to either get in with a dangerous crew that\u2019ll have your back\u2026or start your own. <b>(Gain final Specialty in Presence: Organized Crime. You decide to work towards becoming a crime lord.)</b><br /> <br /> You need muscle\u2026but a dangerous crew is as likely to turn on you and steal everything you have as they are to give you the time to prove yourself and earn their loyalty. If the Raptor Cat taught you anything, it\u2019s that you can\u2019t rely on others-at the end of the day, you need to get strong enough to protect yourself. You should start hanging around the mercenary companies\u2019 training and display grounds so you can watch them and learn their moves. You want to get personally deadly enough that nobody will dare mess with you. <b> (Spend your last Specialty on Melee: Ruthless Lethality. You decide to work towards becoming a deadly warrior or assassin.)</b><br /> <br /> You\u2019re enjoying spending time with Moth learning to read\u2026and more than that, you now know the kind of money that alchemists are carrying around. If you want to get richer, it\u2019s clear to you that the way to do that is to become a scholar-learn to read books, learn how to do alchemy or magic yourself. You won\u2019t have to worry about Raptor Cats or street toughs if you can bind spirits to your will or drink a potion to make your skin hard as River Dragon scales, after all. You\u2019ll learn all you can from Moth, and then move on to other sources of knowledge. <b>(Spend your last Specialty on Occult: Sacrificial Magic. You decide to work towards becoming an occultist or savant.)</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s clear you have a head for business. Your next move should be to study up a bit on economic matters and then start a business enterprise. Maybe you should start that rooftop chicken farm and sell pickled eggs and pickled ginger, or maybe you should take a few lessons with Grinning Eel before buying a few boats and starting a ferry company. Or you could hire some of the street kids you know and help them out by forming a messenger service\u2026whatever you do, though, first you\u2019ll need to study up on Nexus taxation policies and Guild licensing requirements. <b>(Spent your last Specialty on Bureaucracy: Business Management. You decide to work towards becoming a successful Nexus merchant.)</b><br /> <br /> Nexus is full of cutthroats and sellswords and pickpockets and scheming businessmen. You\u2019re always seeing rubes showing up in Nexus for the first time getting taken for everything they have. Your city is a dangerous city\u2026but if you could get out of Nexus, you\u2019d be surrounded by those rubes all the time. If you take your business sense on the road with a Guild Caravan, you\u2019d be dealing with a lot less competition, and you\u2019d get to see the world. You have enough money to buy a cart and a small stake, an even hire a couple employees to travel with you. You\u2019d need to do some research to figure out what business to get into and what caravan to join and what routes would be most profitable\u2026 <b>(Spend your last Specialty on Sail: Navigation. You decide to work towards being able to see the world as a cutthroat caravan merchant.)</b><br /> <br /> Getting out of town is a great idea, but merchant caravans travel slow and often run into bandits or worse. River travel is faster, and that means your investments would turn around and become profits faster. You ought to buy some goods to sell up and downriver and maybe even look at prices to see if it would be worth buying your own ship. You\u2019d need to do some research and you\u2019d probably want to spend some time learning how to sail from Grinning Eel first, but it\u2019s a solid long term career option. <b>(Spend your last Specialty on Sail: River Travel. You decide to work towards becoming a speculator in the commodities business and maybe even a riverboat captain.)</b><br /> <br /> You asked about becoming an Immaculate Monk, were turned away and told to ask yourself what Sextes Jylis would do\u2026and then that very night a dragon appeared and died and left you with a fortune. It\u2019s clear that this was a gift from the Dragons, and possibly a test as well-the right thing to do here is keep what you need and use the rest of your windfall to help others. Perhaps start that rooftop farm and give out free eggs to other urchin kids, or hire somebody to teach them to read? Maybe find a way to get a roof over their heads? The Dragons gave you this gift so that, like Sextes Jylis, you could use it to raise others up along with you. You can start by asking that monk, Banked Coals, for her advice <b>(Spend your last Specialty on Presence: Inspirational Speeches. You decide to work towards making Nexus a better place for the poor. If you want to eventually pursue Martial Arts rather than Melee, this is your chance.)</b><br /> <br /> You appear to have made a connection with a flock of raitons. That\u2019s a chance that you ought to take advantage of. Like you, they\u2019re clever opportunistic scavengers and survivors\u2026and animals, unlike human allies, are usually predictable and trustworthy. You should keep leaving food out for them, and if you can get them to trust you enough to come close. You should study up on how to train birds-if you could get them to bring you coins or jewelry instead of shiny ribbons or beads, that could come in handy\u2026and if you could get them to do tricks, well, that could make you some real money over in the Players\u2019 District. Also\u2026well, having a flock of weirdly intelligent raitons obeying you could give you the sort of imposing and possibly-supernatural cachet that would help convince businessmen or crime lords to take a twelve year old seriously. <b>(Take a second Survival Specialty, in Falconry. You decide to become the master of Nexus' skies. This is your chance to train pets to do tricks\u2026and teach your still-mysterious raiton Familiar how to unlock his hidden abilities and combat gambits other than Distract!)</b><br /> <br /> The real power in Nexus isn\u2019t money, and it isn\u2019t swords. It\u2019s the Emissary, and the Council of Entities. Their spies are everywhere, their laws are inviolable, and their servants enjoy power and privilege. What you learned today is that you need to get lucky AND be smart AND work hard to get ahead\u2026but the Council just needs to sit back and collect the taxes when you do! That\u2019s an excellent racket, and you want in on it. You\u2019ll need to do some research on the Council and how to get into Nexus government as a clerk\u2026but if Liu\u2019s instincts about you are right, you think you could rise through the ranks pretty quickly. <b>(Take your last Specialty in Socialize: City Politics. You decide to work towards getting onto the Council of Entities someday.)</b><br /> <br /> Something Else! You settle on a different plan for your immediate future! <b>(Take your last Specialty in something else! You decide to work towards...a thing?)</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T08:24:01-07:00","id":1137682,"title":"","content":"My first instinct is to go with either the <b>Occult: Sacrificial Magic</b> or the <b>second Survival Specialty, in Falconry</b>. But I don't think the rest of the chat will agree.<br /> If either of the previous two get another vote then put me down for that. (Occult if both get a vote)<br /> Otherwise, I'll vote for <b>Sail:River Travel</b>. We can take advantage of our apprenticeship with Eel and develop our business acumen as well. Also, getting out of Nexus = Good Idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T09:30:07-07:00","id":1137713,"title":"","content":"We're likely best off either learning more about the occult, or starting a business of our own. Foreign trading takes a very long time to get established in, almost as long as we've been alive. So I think Business Management or Sacrificial Magic would be our best options. But human sacrifice is right out! Killing animals? We've done that; rats and pigeons are edible and disgustingly abundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T09:48:49-07:00","id":1137723,"title":"","content":"<b>Sail: River Travel</b>. It's what our father did, and it's something we're familiar with. The past wasn't a pleasant place, but it's what we know, and there's some security in familiarity. So much is changing so quickly, let's hang on to some part of the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T10:13:18-07:00","id":1137735,"title":"","content":"<b>Something Else:</b><br /> <br /> You've always felt comfortable <i>making </i>things. Simple sewing, repurposing old junk, and shaping whatever you find into what you need to get by is natural to you. You could definitely make a living from that. But then again, in the past few days you've had a glimpse of the world of magic, and it's amazing. Making a river boil, binding ghosts with words on paper, turning organ parts into potions that make skin like scales, communing with animals like the raitons... These things fascinate you, and you want to learn more. Maybe there's a way to put them together - your intuitive understanding of craftsmanship, and your growing knowledge of occult arts. You can start by learning to read, pumping Princess Infinitudes for information, and maybe getting her to introduce you to her master. With a teacher and the ability to study from books, who knows what wondrous things you could learn to devise?<br /> <br /> <b>(Spend your last Specialty on Craft: Charms and Talismans. You decide to work towards becoming an urban shaman, or magewright.)</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>(My second choice would be </i><b>Occult: Sacrificial Magic</b><i>, but I think this slight change of course would be more interesting. I am also okay with </i><b>Presence: Inspirational Speeches.</b><i>)</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":".  Following BlueWinds lead 09-05-2017, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T10:25:26-07:00","id":1137745,"title":"","content":"I'd like to note that 'everyone gives their first choice', when there are so many options, isn't likely to actually reflect what people actually want - thus all the conditionals, second choices, etc. that people feel the need to give.<br /> <br /> If you give everyone any number of votes, you'll get a more accurate sense for what people while still keeping things simple. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=orybDrUj4vA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=orybDrUj4vA\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=orybDrUj4vA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=orybDrUj4vA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T10:42:52-07:00","id":1137756,"title":"","content":"<b>Falconry.</b> I love the idea of doing something that's a little bit offbeat and unusual. Even in Nexus, where the exotic is commonplace, this would be unique. And how <i>cool </i>would it be to become Nexus' Master of Raitons! There's a lot of sky above this city - let's own it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T14:25:33-07:00","id":1137825,"title":"","content":"My first choice would be occult, second bureaucracy, third presence (inspirational speeches)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T15:16:53-07:00","id":1137844,"title":"","content":"something else...The real power in Nexus is the Council of Entities and if we want to make a real difference, joining the council is the way to do it. Going the straight up politician route seems like a boring way to go about it though. Lets work our way up to becoming Nexus's Spymaster and Master of Secrets. We should make the most of the one advantage we have over any potential competition by training a flock of loyal raiton spies and take a <b>second survival specialty in Falconry</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1203-caladon","name":"Caladon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T21:26:15-07:00","id":1137915,"title":"","content":"I started checking this forum again, got caught up on this, and then thought it was dead... and now it's not, yay!<br /> <br /> In order of preference, I'd say... Falconry is my first choice, followed by Navigation, Sacrificial Magic, Inspirational Speeches, City Politics, River Travel, Ruthless Lethality, Organized Crime, Business Management last. However, I'd like to offer a suggestion; whatever we do, is it out of the question to still work on making the city better for the poor, with that skill? A master of raitons seems like she could do a lot for people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T17:13:27-07:00","id":1138457,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm, I'd say beurocracy or city politics. Let's become a city player! Although I do love me some falconry...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T17:56:46-07:00","id":1139590,"title":"","content":"I think a Falconry specialty would be raiton the money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13575-jumble","name":"jumble","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T19:19:52-07:00","id":1139607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jumble</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1139590#post1139590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a Falconry specialty would be raiton the money.</div> </div> </div> </div>...hey...I see what you did there. \ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T20:01:47-07:00","id":1139614,"title":"","content":"semicasual's idea of Craft: Charms and Talismans or Occult: Sacrificial Magic please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T20:30:53-07:00","id":1142019,"title":"","content":"<b>Sacrificial Magic 6<br /> River Travel 3<br /> Business Management 3<br /> Craft: Charms and Talismans 2<br /> Presence: Inspirational Speeches 3<br /> City Politics 1<br /> Navigation: 1<br /> Ruthless Lethality: 1<br /> Organized Crime: 2<br /> Falconry 6+ 5 Vote Terrible Pun Bonus to Break The Tie=11<br /> <br /> For the record, I\u2019m definitely using the \u201cjust add up all the votes and don\u2019t worry about preference\u201d method. If you tell me your first, second, and third choice\u2026I just count that as one vote for each, like in the linked video. I\u2019m lazy, you guys. Also, in the event of a tie, I\u2019m totally just going with whoever makes the best pun. Raiton the money indeed!</b><br /> <br /> You consider a number of grandiose ambitions-sailing away, or joining a caravan, or becoming a crime lord, or becoming a sorcerer\u2026but the more you think about it, the more you start to think these dreams aren\u2019t realistic. Nobody\u2019s going to take a kid your age seriously, and the more people you have to get close with the more you\u2019ll have to worry about people figuring out your gender, which you\u2019d still rather keep a secret\u2026<br /> <br /> Animals, though\u2026raptor cats and raitons don\u2019t care whether you\u2019re male or female. They don\u2019t care whether you\u2019re an adult or a kid. They can\u2019t lie to you or cheat you or steal from you the way people can. As friends and minions go\u2026well, they\u2019re a lot more trustworthy than a human criminal organization would be! You have a slight and unusual advantage, and you decide that since you have some time to spare, you\u2019re going to see how far it can get you.<br /> <br /> Your decision made, you tidy up your dishes, lighting one of Moth\u2019s many candles for light as the evening deepens. You\u2019re determined to keep the apartment clean, if only to provide Moth with a good role model. Once you\u2019re done cleaning up after dinner, you decide to start preparing for the future-and as is your old habit, food is at the forefront of your mind. You take a few minutes to peel your eggs. You put four of them aside for breakfast tomorrow, and then stack the rest of them in your clay jug and fill it with vinegar and a couple dried peppers. You put the jar on the stovetop until the vinegar starts to boil, then apply some dripping wax from the candle to the hot clay rim before putting the top on tight so that wax seeps up around the edge of the lid. Hopefully that seal will hold as it cools, and the eggs will pickle and be good for a few months.<br /> <br /> After about an hour of fruitlessly trying to read one of Moth\u2019s books by candlelight, picking out and copying the words you recognize and giving yourself a headache trying to fill in the words in between, you disrobe and take a look at your bandages. Moth did good work. You poke them gingerly-the scratches from the Raptor Cat are still sore, but you don\u2019t feel any swelling or any sign of infection. You probably ought to remove the bandages and clean the wounds again\u2026but you\u2019re not sure you could re-apply the dressings without assistance from Moth, and she still hasn\u2019t gotten home yet. Concluding that they\u2019ll probably be okay at leat until tomorrow, you leave them on, blow out the candle, and crawl into the bedroll. <div align=\"center\">***</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>You dream of soaring high over Nexus by night. You have great black wings, and the feel of the wind streaming over your feathers is rapturous. You turn northward, winging your way out beyond the city walls. Rice paddies and herds of goats slumbering on terraced hills pass below you, the moon glinting on puddles and night-dew when it slips briefly out from behind the clouds. You glance up at the handful of stars visible through that gap, reorient yourself North, and continue flying\u2026but as you go the wind begins to pick up and you see distant thunderheads flickering on the Northern horizon. Not willing to chance a storm, you turn back home towards Nexus, but the wind is no longer with you, and heavy rain begins to fall, drenching your feathers and weighing you down\u2026and then something huge moves through the flickering clouds overhead, a great slithering dragon-shape surrounding by howling winds\u2026and then it ROARS, with a voice like thunder, and-</i><br /> <br /> You jolt awake, heart pounding, to the sound of pots and pans clattering, instinctively reaching your hand towards the knife you usually keep tied to your arm but which you decided to sleep without. For a moment your terror deepens as you realize you\u2019re unarmed\u2026but then as you awaken further, you orient yourself-you\u2019re in your apartment, and the dark figure moving pots around is White Moth. You\u2019re safe.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey,\u201d Moth says softly. \u201cSorry to wake you up. I didn\u2019t mean to drop that.\u201d<br /> <br /> It\u2019s raining outside. You can hear the dull rumble of rain on the roof, and you see that Moth has closed the shutters in the window.<br /> <br /> You groan. \u201cIt\u2019s alright\u2026gods, you\u2019re back late.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah.\u201d She shrugs. \u201cIt\u2019s, uh\u2026it\u2019s been a very educational evening.\u201d Something in Moth\u2019s voice seems a little shaken. She puts a pot of water on the stove, stirs up the low coals and adds some more charcoal, and slumps against the wall, exhausted. Her normally wild and tangled hair is wet and flat over her face and shoulders.<br /> <br /> \u201cLong day?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah. Not as long as it\u2019ll be for the Master of Nine Black Chains, though. I finished my part so he let me go home, but he won\u2019t be able to stop working until at least sunrise tomorrow\u2026and probably he\u2019ll keep going until about half an hour before sunset.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s he doing? Catching ghosts?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah.\u201d Moth nods. \u201cI caught a couple myself. Like I said. Very educational.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2026um. You didn\u2019t bring them home with you, did you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHa! No. The Master needed them for guides.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhere\u2019s he going?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSomeplace I\u2019m not ready to follow him. Not yet.\u201d She sighs. \u201cI know he\u2019s from Sijan, but the dead around here aren\u2019t always as cooperative. I really hope he\u2019s okay.\u201d<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a flicker of lightning from the window, and for a moment the room is stark white except for Moth, who is silhouetted in black except for white bandages on her left hand and arm, and the red of blood on both hands.<br /> <br /> Then it\u2019s dark again.<br /> <br /> \u201cI hope he\u2019s okay too,\u201d you declare softly. \u201cMoth, are <i>you </i>alright?\u201d<br /> <br /> She fumbles with the bag of rice a little, opening it and scooping out some to pour into the pot of water on the stove. Then she sits down on the bedroll next to you. You can smell her sweat and a cloying acrid scent like herbs\u2026and also an old earthy rotting sort of smell, and blood.<br /> <br /> The thunder follows several long seconds after the flash, a long low rumble that rattles the dishes in the cupboard.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026I\u2019ll be fine, Tavi.\u201d She sighs. \u201cJust\u2026it\u2019s been a hard day. If the Master hadn\u2019t been there I think I probably would have died. I\u2019ve never\u2026I\u2019ve always seen ghosts and stuff, ever since I was little, but they\u2019ve always been\u2026wispy. This is the first time they\u2019ve been able to touch me.\u201d<br /> <br /> She holds up her bandaged arm. \u201cThe Master says I should consider studying some sort of athletics or martial arts or dance or something. I was too slow today.\u201d<br /> \u201c\u2026a ghost did that to you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah. I mean, I cut my hand for an offering to bring it close, but it, uh, wanted more than I offered I guess.\u201d She shrugs. \u201cNext time I do this sorta thing I\u2019ll weave together some warding prayer strips to make armor, I think. I had a knife coated with salt, but I was too slow to do anything with it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026is that why you\u2019re so good with bandages?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCutting yourself for ghosts?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. No, I don\u2019t usually do that. The Master does it all the time, though. His blood is apparently delicious. So I\u2019ve gotten pretty good at bandaging him up. He heals pretty quick, usually.\u201d<br /> You shake your head. \u201cThis all sounds pretty dangerous, Moth.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, yeah. That\u2019s why most people don\u2019t do it. But if you pull it off, you can do something most people can\u2019t, and that\u2019s power.\u201d Moth shrugs again. \u201cI decided a long time ago that I was going to take the little gift the gods gave me and use it to become as powerful as I could. When I die, I don\u2019t want to be some sad little ghost whining about all the things she should have done with her life, I want to be rich and powerful in a fancy mausoleum with lots of servants and I want people to remember me after I\u2019m gone.\u201d<br /> <br /> You prop yourself up on your elbow. \u201cMoth, you\u2026 want\u2026 to be a ghost?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, not anytime soon! But we all have to die sometime, right? So I\u2019m gonna plan for it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut\u2026you\u2026shouldn\u2019t you think about moving on to your next life instead?\u201d<br /> <br /> Moth gives you a strange look. Or maybe her face just looks strange because it\u2019s dark.<br /> <br /> \u201cTavi, the Dragons don\u2019t usually look too fondly on necromancers.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026I guess not.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cListen, you go back to sleep. Will it bother you if I light a candle and read a bit while I eat?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll be fine.\u201d<br /> <br /> You snuggle into the bedroll, and hear the flare of a match, and the darkness of your closed eyes goes deep red with candlelight. You worry about Moth and the fate of her soul for a little bit, and then drift off to sleep to the sound of pages turning.<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t have any more dreams. <div align=\"center\">***</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> You awaken early again the next morning. Rain is still pounding dully against the roof, and Moth has curled up around you on the bedroll, snoring gently. She must have washed and changed before bed; the bandage on her left hand is clean and white instead of dripping red like it was last night. Her arm is wrapped around you, so you have a pretty good vantage point.<br /> You enjoy just relaxing and being warm for a little while, but you grow bored after a few minutes. It\u2019s clear you\u2019re not falling back asleep\u2026and you have to pee. You gingerly wriggle out from under Moth\u2019s arm and get up, making your way over to the chamber pot. Once you\u2019ve finished your business you empty it out the window and rinse it out with rainwater-might as well take advantage of the pouring rain while you have it.<br /> <br /> Your little ginger root seems to be enjoying the wet weather, it\u2019s pushed out a small leaf overnight. The raitons don\u2019t appear to have left any gifts on your windowsill this morning; you expect they\u2019re all sheltering someplace against the rain.<br /> <br /> As you\u2019re about to close the shutters to stop the damp getting in, your expectations are proved wrong: a big black raiton laboriously flaps its way through the gloom, alighting on your windowsill. You notice it\u2019s carrying a shiny button in its beak. It places the button on the windowsill, nudges it once towards you, then rustles its feathers, preening, as you stare at it.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood morning,\u201d you murmur softly. Then, an idea occurring to you, you back slowly away and grab one of the boiled eggs you were saving for breakfast. You return to the window and slowly hold the egg out to the raiton.<br /> <br /> It looks at your hand\u2026then at your face. After several seconds, it snaps forward suddenly, and it takes all your self-composure not to flinch away from the flash of little needle-sharp teeth as it digs into the egg. You hold your hand flat, the way you\u2019ve heard one is supposed to feed horses or goats without getting bitten, but that doesn\u2019t work very well for sharp beaks and you get poked a couple of times, though nothing that breaks the skin.<br /> <br /> The raiton eats about half the egg before just picking up the rest and swallowing it whole, its head tilted back and bobbing up and down comically. Then it\u2019s staring at you again, considering. It croaks, looks up, and flutters away above the window. Then it flutters back down, perching on the windowsill and cocking its head to peer at you quizzically. It repeats this pantomime several times, flying up and returning, as though it expects you to come out the window and follow it skyward.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry, friend,\u201d you whisper. \u201cI can\u2019t fly.\u201d<br /> <br /> Not seeming to understand you, it again flutters out and up into the rain, cawing, and you can\u2019t help the impression that the bird thinks you\u2019re not particularly bright.<br /> <br /> \u201cShush, you\u2019ll wake Moth,\u201d you mutter. \u201cFine. I\u2019ll follow you. Just be quiet!\u201d<br /> <br /> You close the shutters, put on your shoes, throw on a baggy old shirt you don\u2019t mind getting wet, and grab your key. You and Moth are on the third floor, which is the topmost floor of your building. Some of the buildings in nicer parts of Nexus are old First Age structures with dozens of stories, but out here in the Blackwater District it\u2019s mostly big squat square tenement buildings.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a short walk down the hall to the stairs, and then a short walk up to the rooftop. Gleaming Smile\u2019s rooftop is wide and gently sloped so the water runs away from the center of the building and out towards either side. The tiles are rough clay, and many of them are cracked. It\u2019s not very steep, it\u2019s almost flat. Even if it wasn\u2019t easy to walk on, there\u2019s a short railing around the eaves on all sides. A big round iron grill rusts under an awning next to the door going downstairs and inside, and there\u2019s a long wooden table set out and tall poles with ropes strung between them for hanging paper lanterns. You expect that during the summer months, the tenants probably come up here to cook and spend time with each other\u2026and to have somebody to eat with after dark.<br /> Right now, it\u2019s bleak and gray and blurry in the unrelenting rain. Somewhere in the East, you\u2019re pretty sure the Sun is rising behind the clouds, because the gray is lighter than it was from your window downstairs. The awning is pouring a small waterfall out onto the roof, and tiny rivers run between the clay tiles, forming puddles and pools before draining off the eaves. There are no paper lanterns hanging on the rope between the poles this morning.<br /> <br /> There are, however, five puffy and unhappy looking raitons, dripping wet and obviously in a foul mood, because one of them hisses at you as you step out onto the roof. The others follow suit, glaring at you and extending their wings to look larger and more threatening. The one from your window downstairs flaps up over the lip of the roof and circles overhead, cawing several times. You recognize it by the yellow bits of yolk dusting its beak and the feathers of its head. The others watch it, then gradually they seem to calm, though they still eye you warily.<br /> <br /> The raiton above circles several times, then lands next to you, looks up at you expectantly, and hops away towards the others. Passing under its perched companions, it hops under the table and out of sight\u2026and you hear a hacking gurgle. Slowly following the bird (instantly regretting it as soon as you come out from under the awning into the cold rain), you lower your body and turn your head sideways.<br /> <br /> It is vomiting up the boiled egg you gave it! You feel briefly insulted! Raitons eat corpses and eyeballs and garbage! More than that, it\u2019s throwing away FOOD!<br /> <br /> Your anger fades quickly, though, as you notice another shape under the table. A wet feathered clump, it trembles and extends a beak to peck at the pile of egg the other raiton has deposited. Where the other raitons are constantly preening, this one appears scruffy, and you notice several places where feathers are missing and you can see dull gray and black scales underneath. You suspect it\u2019s injured.<br /> <br /> The raiton that delivered the egg hops out from under the table and looks up at you again quizzically as its bedraggled fellow slowly consumes the egg.<br /> <br /> You turn your back on it and go back inside, shutting the door behind you.<br /> <br /> Two minutes later, you return with another boiled egg and a fistful of dried fish. Again, most of the raitons hiss and puff up at your approach, but this time they shut up when the sick one under the table croaks quietly. They watch you silently as you crawl under the table and deposit another boiled egg and some dried fish in front of it. The injured bird doesn\u2019t even bother acting afraid of you, it just starts eating. This close, you realize that it smells strange-not quite like urine, but like some of the chemicals they sometimes cart in over at the foundry. And on closer examination, its feathers aren\u2019t just missing in places-the feathers around those places are singed, as though the feathers were burned away. It also still has a bit of twine around its left foot. This is the raiton that found your bundle hanging in the smokestack and got all tangled up in your twine trying to get it out. The one you saved from the Raptor Cat, the one that saved you from the Raptor cat with its distracting Raptor Cat impression.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat happened to you, huh?\u201d You wonder aloud.<br /> <br /> You hear scuffling and cawing, and as you crawl out from under the table, you find the rest of the raitons (except for the one with yolk on its beak) have fallen from their perches and are croaking and flopping on their backs. Several of them are hopping with wings outstretched at an odd angle, pretending to have broken wings. One is huddled in a feathery ball, making a piteous gargling sound.<br /> <br /> They have figured out that you give free food to sick raitons. You can\u2019t help but burst out laughing, rolling onto your back on the cold wet roof as the rain streams down your face. You\u2019ve done the same routine to get pity handouts, especially during the colder months. You remember Rat even got you a set of crutches from someplace. Seeing such foreboding creatures, symbolic of the finality of death and ill omens, flapping about in the hopes of a free meal\u2026you don\u2019t stop chuckling for a while.<br /> <br /> You hand out pieces of dried fish to the rest of the raitons, and they instantly stop playacting and wolf it down as fast as they can. The quicker ones even have the nerve to sidle up to the slower ones and try to snatch food from them. Nobody is going after the big pile you gave the injured raiton under the table, though.<br /> <br /> You remember Moth\u2019s talk last night, and you resolve not to waste the opportunity the Gods have given you. You hold some dried fish in your clenched fist, and hold it out. A couple of the raitons peck at it, smelling the food but not sure how to get at it. One of them nips at you, and you bap it on the beak, sending it croaking and cawing and scurrying away. The others also move back\u2026but quickly return.<br /> <br /> Eventually, by trial and error, one of them figures out what you want, hopping up onto your wrist. You open your fist slightly and let it get a few bites of fish, before shaking your arm to send it flapping away. Then you hold out your fist again.<br /> <br /> They learn quickly. Soon, the idea that landing on an outstretched fist results in a treat has spread to the lot of them, and they start squabbling with each other to perch on your arm when you hold it out. The squabbling escalates into a chaotic aerial battle full of squawks and warbles and wet flapping wings, before a low, quiet hiss cuts the whole thing short.<br /> The sick raiton has finished its meal and emerged from under the table, and it\u2019s hissing at the rest of them. Looking positively sheepish, they flutter away from you and from each other to alight once more on the rope around the rooftop picnic area, desperately attempting to regain a sense of dignity.<br /> <br /> You kneel next to the sick raiton and hold out your fist. It looks at the fist, then cocks its head sideways to look at you with one eye. Another raiton croaks, and the sick one squawks back, and there\u2019s a raucous chorus of harsh cries as they all express their opinions on whatever is being discussed\u2026and then the sick one hops up onto your outstretched fist. You unclench your fist to allow it to eat some dried fish, then stand up. The bird stays steady on your hand.<br /> <br /> Abruptly all the rest of the raitons take to the air, cawing and croaking and circling overhead before winging away through the rain to the south. The one on your hand calls after them, and extends its wings a bit\u2026but doesn\u2019t fly after them. It turns to look at you again, and then pecks your hand once, hard.<br /> <br /> You bap it on the beak with your free hand, and it hisses.<br /> <br /> You bap it on the beak again, and it shuts up. <div align=\"center\">***</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cWha\u2026what\u2019s that smell?\u201d Moth asks, stirring in her bedroll and yawning. It\u2019s a couple hours before noon. It\u2019s still drizzling gently outside. \u201cUgh, it\u2019s like something died\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry about that.\u201d You gesture to the scruffy raiton perched on the wooden chair next to the stove. \u201cHe does smell a bit rank.\u201d<br /> <br /> Moth rubs her eyes. \u201cTavi\u2026why\u2026why is there a raiton?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe\u2019s hurt. I\u2019m taking care of him. Going to see if I can maybe teach him a few tricks.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026can one of those tricks be baths? It\u2019s like\u2026wet feathers and piss and\u2026ozone?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s ozone?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s air that\u2019s heavily charged with Essence. You sometimes smell it near a Dragon Line coming down from the North, or where lightning has struck.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLightning, huh? That\u2019d explain the singe marks? Did you get struck by lightning, little guy?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf it got struck by lightning, it\u2019d be cooked.\u201d Moth blearily pushes off her blanket and sits up. \u201cLook, um. I\u2019m fine with a pet raiton, he looks really neat and it kind of works with my Princess of Shadows thing\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI thought it was Umbral Infinitudes?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShush. But if he\u2019s gonna crap in the apartment and smell bad, I have concerns.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou. Have concerns about how the apartment smells.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cListen, it\u2019s fine if they\u2019re MY smells, Tavi. I don\u2019t notice those. And you don\u2019t really smell, but that bird-\u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright, I\u2019ll keep him clean.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s his name?\u201d Moth picks her nose, looks at the resulting bit of snot on her finger impassively, then reaches out to wipe it on the underside of the chair.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe doesn\u2019t have one?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHm. You should let <i>me </i>pick a name for him!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh gods.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe can be\u2026The Ill Omened Harbinger! Ooh, no, we should call him Midnight Lightning, since he\u2019s black and he smells like lightning\u2026oh, wait, wait. How do you say Midnight Lightning in Skytongue...what\u2019s midnight\u2026lightning\u2019s Kaummulak-\u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cUsi!\u201d croaks the raiton. \u201cKaummulak Omajualuk. Nimak.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026Tavi? Why does your raiton speak Skytongue?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s Skytongue?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s a language they speak way up North. I only know a few words, I don\u2019t even know how their sentence structure works\u2026\u201d Moth puts her hand on her chest. \u201cAtik\u2026White Moth.\u201d<br /> <br /> Moth extends her hand to the raiton, and it cocks its head, then speaks, very slowly, in a low croaking voice. \u201cAtik\u2026Chupong. Nakuk AngajukKak.\u201d<br /> <br /> Moth's eyes widen in excitement. \u201cI think his name is Chupong Nakuk Angajukkak?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cChupong,\u201d the raiton corrects her. \u201cAtik. Chupong.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUm. Moth? Do you happen to have a book that says what words mean in Skytongue?\u201d You appear to have brought home a talking raiton.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, it\u2019s\u2026just a minute.\u201d Moth starts rummaging around her disorganized piles of books. \u201cDo you suppose he used to be somebody\u2019s pet, and learned words? Raitons can be very clever.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPitsik? Ak Pitsik.\u201d The raiton, seeming to be enjoying the attention, flaps its wings and pecks at your hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think Pitsik means he wants more fish,\u201d you sigh and grab some from the bag. You hold it out, fist clenched. \u201cPitsik?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPitsik!\u201d The raiton bobs its head and pecks at your hand. You don\u2019t open it.<br /> <br /> \u201cChupong.\u201d You say its name and the bird goes still and quiet. \u201cCome.\u201d You hold out your fist again, and the raiton hops onto your wrist. Now that it's done the trick you give it some fish. \u201cCome. Pitsik.\u201d<br /> <br /> The raiton scarfs down the dried fish. \u201cCome. Pitsik,\u201d it agrees, and continues to sit on your wrist as it preens its feathers.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat was so cool!\u201d Moth declares. \u201cYou got him on your hand!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah. Any luck with that book?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBook? Oh! Yes, one second\u2026\u201d She goes back to rummaging, then finds the book she\u2019s looking for and flips it open. \u201cHere it is! A Guildsman\u2019s Guide to Gethamane, complete with Riverspeak to Skytongue Dictionary\u2026hm\u2026Pitsik means dried fish.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s Chupong mean?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026it\u2019s not in here. And it\u2019s weird, Chupong doesn\u2019t sound like Skytongue\u2026but what was it? Nakuk Anchorjack?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNakuk AngajukKak!\u201d The raiton croaks at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cNakuk\u2026.nakuk\u2026okay, that means strong, or\u2026faultless? Says it\u2019s used to describe goods of high quality. And Anga, anga\u2026.oh, here it is. It means war-leader or chieftain or daimyo. There\u2019s a note saying he\u2019s the guy you want to barter with.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo he\u2019s\u2026Chupong the Flawless Daimyo?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI mean, I can\u2019t really speak Skytongue, and this book\u2019s intended less as a grammatical guide and more as a guide to not getting cheated by whoever you hire as a translator\u2026but maybe Perfected Daimyo Chupong would sound better in Riverspeak?\u201d<br /> <br /> The raiton is looking back and forth between the two of you intently as you keep saying its name. You hold it out in front of your face. \u201cUh, Moth? How do you say \u2018name,\u2019 again?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAtik.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, then. Atik\u2026Tavi. Tavi Nakuk AnjajukKak.\u201d<br /> <br /> The raven hops off your hand and back onto the chair, its body shaking slightly at it croaks repeatedly. Laughter sounds the same in any language.<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026did you just try to convince it that you were Perfected Daimyo Tavi?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was worth a shot.\u201d You scowl. \u201cDidn\u2019t want to get outranked by a damn raiton.\u201d Moth snorts and bursts out laughing, and this sends the raiton into further levels of hilarity. It warbles in amusement. Eventually, once they both get tired of it and shut up, you sigh. \u201cLook, we should see if we can find out more\u2026how do you say, \u2018what\u2019 in Skytongue?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUh\u2026.Suna?\u201d<br /> <br /> You gently touch the bird\u2019s scorched feathers. \u201cSuna?\u201d<br /> <br /> Chupong\u2026you\u2019re starting to think of him by his name, now\u2026looks up at you. \u201cNimak. Kaummulak Omajualuk.\u201d<br /> <br /> Moth runs her finger down the pages, searching\u2026 \u201cNimak\u2026that\u2019s, um\u2026Hurt? Injury? And Kaummulak is lightning, I know that one\u2026Omaj, Omaj\u2026Omajualuk! Oh.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOmajualuk is\u2026monster.\u201d<br /> <br /> You close your eyes and take a deep breath. Moth keeps talking.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo\u2026he got hurt by a\u2026lightning monster? But-\u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cMoth, how do you say Snake? Big flying lightning snake?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLet\u2019s see\u2026Kullugiak?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cKullugiak! Kaummulak Kullugiak Omajualuk!\u201d The raiton is excited again.<br /> <br /> You sit down.<br /> <br /> You had a dream last night about flying north, and a thunderstorm, and at the end before you woke up there was a huge thing slithering through the clouds overhead\u2026this is too weird. <div align=\"center\">***</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> You spend the rest of the morning with Chupong and White Moth, going through her Riverspeak to Skytongue dictionary. The raiton learns quickly once you repeat words to it. Pitsik is Fish. AnjajukKak is Daimyo. Omajualuk is Monster.<br /> <br /> It becomes slowly and haltingly clear that Chupong is grateful to you for fighting the cat-monster and saving him, and that the other raitons you met today are Chupong\u2019s\u2026the translation is a little unclear, but whatever Guildsman wrote the book about travelling in the North said to think of them as deeply loyal bodyguards. Chupong is the son of\u2026the best analog you can get is \u201cGrand Sky King,\u201d and he has come south to\u2026conquer and prove himself in battle, if Moth\u2019s translation is right. Those are tasks which you\u2019re not really sure how a raiton would go about accomplishing. Chupong had hoped to slay the\u2026lightning monster\u2026in the storm, but was defeated without ever even getting close to it.<br /> <br /> Moth has no idea why you dreamed about what Chupong was doing last night, and Chupong either doesn\u2019t know or doesn\u2019t understand the translation-the Guild Dictionary is very specific on fractions and percentages, but there\u2019s not much room devoted to dreams or descriptive language, and anyway you and Moth have no idea how grammar works in Skytongue-which becomes crystal clear after the raiton starts using full sentences, then switches back to short one-word bursts in apparent disappointment at your lack of fluency.<br /> <br /> White Moth\u2019s theory is that the raiton is part spirit, perhaps the mortal offspring of a raiton god and a normal raiton, and she\u2019s equally fascinated by your dreaming about Chupong\u2019s adventures and jealous of the fact that you found him first. The bird, for his part, seems to like you-he feels comfortable resting on your wrist, or on your shoulder while you sit by the stove, though now that he\u2019s figured out the word for fish he won\u2019t shut up about it.<br /> <br /> You find Moth\u2019s dictionary just as fascinating as the magic raiton, and honestly a lot less unnerving. If only there was a Riverspeak to Pictures dictionary\u2026you ask, but Moth says she doesn\u2019t know of any books like that.<br /> <br /> The morning turns into the afternoon, and Moth leaves you to go check on the Master of Nine Black Chains. You stay, and keep teaching the Raiton words.<br /> <br /> \u201cRice.\u201d<br /> \u201cEgg.\u201d<br /> \u201cNo.\u201d<br /> \u201cChair.\u201d<br /> \u201cFire.\u201d<br /> \u201cCoin.\u201d<br /> \u201cNO!\u201d<br /> \u201cHair.\u201d<br /> \u201cCome.\u201d<br /> \u201cSit.\u201d<br /> \u201cStay.\u201d<br /> <br /> You\u2019re pretty sure you learn a few curse words in Skytongue when you take the egg away from him, but over the course of the day the two of you develop an understanding, and eventually the bird even lets you scrub him with some warm water and a brush to clean his feathers. He helps, preening and preening even after you\u2019re finished. <div align=\"center\">***</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> The day turns into night. Moth comes back, reporting that her Master is tired and a little anemic but otherwise unharmed, and is now resting safely. The three of you spend your evening with the dictionary, you writing out words for things in the apartment and saying them out loud for the raiton, and the raiton repeating them. Eventually he starts bringing you the things-chopsticks, books, the corner of the blanket.<br /> <br /> The next day your learning continues. You take Chupong up on the roof now that it\u2019s no longer raining, and he hops around under the cloudy sky, not yet ready to take wing. Moth comes up with you, and you continue your lessons. You teach Chupong to bring you coins, and reward him with bits of boiled egg. Chupong teaches you to get a firm grasp on the coins first-once he gets the egg he\u2019ll hop away without letting go of the quarter-dinar bit of silver if you let him. He has trouble figuring out that you don\u2019t want him defecating in the apartment, and he refuses to go out the window the way you were trying to teach him\u2026but after observing you do so, he starts using the chamber pot.<br /> <br /> A day turns into a week. Chupong\u2019s injuries are starting to heal, and his feathers are starting to come back in, though he looks scruffy. He\u2019s getting basic two word combinations down: \u201cTavi NO!\u201d and \u201cFish me!\u201d are his favorites, though he\u2019s also fond of abruptly screeching \u201cDEATH FIRE!\u201d without any warning. Moth has found you a picture book meant to teach rich children to read. It has lots of words in Riverspeak, along with pictures. You and the raiton both study it with deep interest. You copy the letters onto parchment. The raiton tries to copy you and draw them with his beak, but he\u2019s clumsy. Moth is both amused and impressed by how quickly both of you are learning. The Master of Nine Black Chains recovers from his exertions (a trip to the Underworld, Moth tells you), and Moth goes back to the University of Nexus every day to assist him. Apparently things are going well at the University; the Master was able to gather the ingredients in the Underworld he needed and selling a couple of angry ghost in clay jugs to unscrupulous Guildsmen will pay for the rest of them. Moth says the Master is getting ready for a big ritual on the night of the New Moon.<br /> <br /> A week turns into a month. Resplendent Water ends, and Descending Water begins. You talk to Gleaming Smile, and pay him the two months\u2019 back rent Moth owes him-you\u2019d rather he not send the Iron League after your reading teacher. He agrees to let you rent the roof, and set up a little garden (as well as a couple of wood-and-wicker structures to grow beans on with little bars in them for the raitons to perch). You\u2019ll just add it onto what Moth owes you when she gets her stipend from her mother at the start of Ascending Earth next month. Chupong has healed enough that he can fly again. The rest of the raitons, his \u201cbodyguards,\u201d are learning a lot of the same tricks that he is. You start getting bits of silver dropped on your windowsill in the mornings instead of buttons and ribbons and dead lizard bits. The others aren\u2019t as clever as Chupong, but they fly out over the city and then croak and caw at their Daimyo and then he croaks back to you: \u201cCat Monster. East,\u201d or \u201cRed wagon, South.\u201d You\u2019re well on your way to using them as spies, even if the communication is still pretty imprecise. You\u2019ve noticed there are several flocks of raitons in the city, and yours are a little bit bigger than the average bird-the others make way for them in the sky, and the big Northern birds tend to get first pickings of any decent scavenging due to their superior size and strength. Chupong has told you their names: Gerel and Tsetseg, always squabbling with one another. Erdene, who flies oddly due to one bad eye. Rishi, the only one who refuses fish and prefers eggs. Tara, chubby and extremely aggressive, prone to biting your fingers and requiring a much firmer hand than the others when it comes to beak-bopping. Prem, Chupong\u2019s mate, the one who led you to him when he was injured. After a month working with them, it\u2019s clear they\u2019re all a bunch of thieving scoundrels who can\u2019t be trusted for a minute\u2026but they seem to listen to Chupong, and Chupong likes you.<br /> <br /> You like him too. Sometimes, when you dream, you see the world through his eyes. Under Moth\u2019s guidance, you\u2019ve been meditating, trying to do the same trick when you\u2019re awake. It\u2019s even worked a couple of times. Moth seems very excited by all this, and refers to Chupong as your \u201cfamiliar.\u201d Chupong seems unfazed, and describes your relationship with some Skytongue word that\u2019s not in White Moth\u2019s book that sounds a lot like gargling rocks. Your wounds have healed, and so have your Raiton\u2019s.<br /> <br /> You have a flock of vaguely obedient spies who are\u2026.reasonably reliable, but a bit bad at reporting what they\u2019ve seen. They\u2019ve all mastered the \u201ccome,\u201d command, though, so you can pull the trick where you raise both arms and seven raitons land on you at once, or rise up to circle menacingly overhead. Between that and teaching Chupong to say, \u201cKneel, mortal,\u201d you\u2019re pretty sure you\u2019re capable of intimidating most street thugs you run across, though you\u2019re not eager to test it in action.<br /> <br /> Paying rent and stocking up on groceries has reminded you, though, that you\u2019re still losing money every month-albeit less now that the raitons are bringing you spare change they find. As Moth put it, the gods have given you a gift. Now it\u2019s time to turn that gift into power!<br /> <br /> <b>What should you do:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Start Your Own Gang:</b> Go see if you can round up Rat and maybe some of his friends from the Sluice Gang and use your new feathered friends to look imposing enough to get put in charge.<br /> <br /> <b>Join A Gang: </b>You\u2019re not dangerous, not yet, not really. But you can be useful. You should use your raitons to gather some intel about how valuable goods are getting moved and see if you can get into a real gang like the Leopard Gang by offering that intel (and the promise of more) to their leadership. Membership would give you protection from other ruffians as well as a cut of the earnings\u2026and with your brain, those earnings would grow.<br /> <br /> <b>Find a Crew:</b> Nexus is nice\u2026but where having a bunch of raitons spying for you would really shine is out on the water. There are boats up and down the river laden with all manner of valuables, and river pirates would love to have somebody on board with talking birds who could scout out cargo ships to see if they were worth going after\u2026and cargo ships might pay good money to have somebody on board who could scout upriver for pirates.<br /> <br /> <b>Serve the Master:</b> White Moth\u2019s teacher, the Master of Nine Black Chains, is obviously a skilled occultist. You\u2019re feeling in a bit over your head here-Chupong is obviously magic, which is usually dangerous. You\u2019re concerned that if the bird is part god like Moth says, feeding it fish might count as prayer outside of an Immaculate feast day\u2026and more importantly, if you\u2019re getting dragged into the world of gods and spirits you want to be prepared. Anybody who can survive overnight in the Underworld is worth learning from\u2026but Moth has made it clear that if you want to learn from the Master, you\u2019ll need to work for the Master, and he obviously has some kind of major plan in the works that may be dangerous for a relative amateur to join partway through.<br /> <br /> <b>Renegotiate with Fifteen Fingers Liu:</b> Now that you\u2019ve got flying scouts, you can probably set up a better arrangement with the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants. Perhaps they could use your help tracking down debtors without your having to risk actually going out and meeting those debtors in person, for example. You\u2019re pretty sure the birds (or at least Chupong) can recognize and follow different people based on a good picture. And the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants have a trading house and offices in other cities, they might like to have fast-winged messengers to carry news and more up to date pricing information to their caravans than their competition is able to manage.<br /> <br /> <b>Enter the Service of the Midnight Queen:</b> The Council of Entities has spies all over Nexus. They have eyes and ears everywhere\u2026but as far as you know, those spies don\u2019t include the city\u2019s raitons. You should try and get assigned duties working for the Council\u2019s intelligence network. The pay would be decent and perhaps more importantly\u2026if you\u2019re on the Council\u2019s business, people are going to be a lot more reluctant to mess with you.<br /> <br /> <b>Start a Business:</b> Three words-Aerial Dumpling Deliveries! Or maybe you should start that pickling business you\u2019ve been mulling over, you could deliver pickles by air!<br /> <br /> <b>Start Smuggling:</b> Three words-Aerial Drug Deliveries! Everything\u2019s legal in Nexus, but there are folks who would pay you good money to smuggle illegal drugs to other places like Lookshy or Thorns or Calin. And Aunt Dwi can probably hook you up with those folks.<br /> <br /> <b>Go Hunting:</b> With raitons acting as your hunting dogs, you\u2019ve been keeping tabs on that Raptor Cat. You know what areas of the city it\u2019s been prowling, and you\u2019re pretty sure you could set a trap and drive the cat into it. The creature would be very profitable to sell\u2026or if you could chain it up and train the thing, it might be helpful in ways raitons aren\u2019t.<br /> <br /> <b>Plan a Heist: </b>Your raitons are clever, and Chupong is able to identify people or objects from pictures. You should pick something small and valuable and see if you can get into the jewel-thief game.<br /> <br /> <b>Start a Cult</b>: Why lead a street gang when you can be worshipped as a god? You have a bunch of raitons doing your bidding, and one of them might even actually be a god. Or maybe you should claim to be the high priest of a god? If he's actually a divine being like Moth thinks he is, Chupong might get more out of the prayers than you would. The Dragons wouldn\u2019t approve, but you remember how lavishly appointed their temple was. People would just give you free money in the form of donations if they worship at your temple, especially if you were able to pull off a miracle or three. You have enough money to buy a small lot in the Temple District and set up a nice looking shrine to draw people in, but that would drain a lot of your resources.<br /> <br /> <b>Something Else?</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 09-19-2017, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T00:16:34-07:00","id":1142059,"title":"","content":"As much as starting a business or renegotiating with Fifteen Fingers Liu is probably the smartest short-term option and most in line with our existing skill set, I am <i>not</i> voting for those - my vote is going towards <b>Serve the Master</b>. There's a lot to learn, and the arcane arts (even the ones that aren't so bright and pretty) can bring in quite a bit of money along with giving us our own chance of having something resembling personal strength. Additionally, while the job itself is clearly pretty dangerous, we've got good evidence that it won't be <i>quite</i> as risky as a regular Necromancer's apprenticeship - the Master is explicitly on record taking some damage to maintain Moth's safety, and Moth has both the start of a personal connection with us (only likely to grow stronger) and, more importantly, a vested interest in helping to protect us from the Master doing anything to mess us up <i>too badly</i>, since we're the only reason she has a place to live.<br /> <br /> Edit: On the other hand, we don't want to run out of rent money. Hm. Don't suppose <b>Liu might consider part-time employment concurrent with our studies</b>. That might be a bit too modern of an idea, but getting a future Occultist or even possibly full-fledged Necromancer with some personal loyalty on his side might be a great bet for Liu. We won't have much time for sleep or fun - but we aren't used to those things in abundance anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12682-remedy","user":"Remedy","date":". 09-20-2017, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12682-remedy","name":"Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T07:05:11-07:00","id":1142127,"title":"","content":"<b>First choice: Go Hunting. </b> We're on a path to becoming the beastmaster of Nexus. That is awesome. <br /> <br /> <b>Second choice: Serve the Master. </b>Finding a real expert to teach could be invaluable, especially if we focus more on the &quot;magic&quot; end of things instead of the &quot;animal&quot; end of things. <br /> <br /> None of these others really interest me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T11:02:53-07:00","id":1142223,"title":"","content":"<b>\u200bEnter the service of the Midnight Queen.</b> We can fill a unique niche there, get paid regularly, and we'd have at least some protection. Moth's studies are just way too creepy, not to mention heretical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T13:43:53-07:00","id":1142288,"title":"","content":"Go Hunting. We can get revenge on the little beastie, and more importantly, we can still go after the other options afterwards, better equipped with our new portfolio of beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T17:07:59-07:00","id":1142345,"title":"","content":"First, thanks again guru for continuing the quest. I really look forward to it! Second, oh man oh man let's get us a pretty new kitty and name him admiral scaley bottoms! Or sell it for parts. Whatever the situation calls for. Then let's totally sign on with this Midnight Queen lady! We not only have our winged friends but also our connections with Aunt Dwee and the prostitutes as well as with the river boatman, both prime buddies for an information gathered. Let's be a spymaster with beasty friends!<br /> <br /> For pun points I wanted to combine &quot;cats got your tongue&quot; with some kind of double entendres about tongues, spies, and prostitution but I ran out of intellect about half way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T18:37:52-07:00","id":1142370,"title":"","content":"Despite raitons being a scavenger, I'm not really feeling Tavi as a necromancer. I think we should either stick to our roots as a <b>thief and plan a heist,</b> or <b>go hunting</b> and work on becoming the Beastmaster of Nexus. Or <b>both! </b>Both is good! After all, what makes a better cat burglar, than a burglar with a giant cat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1419,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","user":"WarDragon","date":". 09-20-2017, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T08:06:30-07:00","id":1142519,"title":"","content":"<b>Go Hunting. </b>Beastmaster of Nexus sounds awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T06:34:40-07:00","id":1142883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1142127#post1142127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>First choice: Go Hunting. </b> We're on a path to becoming the beastmaster of Nexus. That is awesome.<br /> <br /> <b>Second choice: Serve the Master. </b>Finding a real expert to teach could be invaluable, especially if we focus more on the &quot;magic&quot; end of things instead of the &quot;animal&quot; end of things.<br /> <br /> None of these others really interest me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the same way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T21:47:30-07:00","id":1143670,"title":"","content":"My opinions (in order for a reason <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <b>Go Hunting</b>: One flock of raitons is cool; more is better! Let's take over the skies! (And any critter that seems to good to pass up, like say... a raptor cat)<br /> <b>Enter the Service of the Midnight Queen</b>: Information is power, and we'll be getting a lot of information<br /> <b>Something Else</b>: Spying on everyone in Nexus will surely turn up something we can use - seize any opportunity that comes our way, whether business or blackmail.<br /> <br /> A life of crime is too likely to end with a knife in the back, and playing with ghosts all day sounds like an even worse deal; besides, we OWN Moth","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/649-nightwinder","name":"Nightwinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T22:14:03-07:00","id":1150073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1142127#post1142127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>First choice: Go Hunting. </b> We're on a path to becoming the beastmaster of Nexus. That is awesome.<br /> <br /> <b>Second choice: Serve the Master. </b>Finding a real expert to teach could be invaluable, especially if we focus more on the &quot;magic&quot; end of things instead of the &quot;animal&quot; end of things.<br /> <br /> None of these others really interest me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ditto. Pretty sure anything involving Gangs is too risky and we aren't quite ready to be self-employed just yet. Really need to be offically literate beforehand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T13:37:57-07:00","id":1152599,"title":"","content":"<b>Serve the Master: 3<br /> Go Hunting: 7<br /> Work for Liu: 1<br /> Join the Midnight Queen: 3<br /> Plan a Heist: 1<br /> Gather Intel: 1</b><br /> <br /> After a month of training animals, you\u2019re feeling pretty good about your bird training skills. With the help of Chupong and his odd little flock, you feel like you\u2019ve learned a lot about training raitons. You\u2019ve even started training a few local Nexus birds, though it\u2019s slower going-they\u2019re not as bright at Chupong or his big Northern breed, but they\u2019re also not as prone to being rebellious. They\u2019ve figured out there\u2019s free food on your roof, and their numbers are growing a little at a time, day by day. You picked a good season to take over Nexus\u2019 skies-the constant rains are rough on raitons and they\u2019re happy to do tricks for food and lean-to on your roof to huddle under. The rains are rough on people too-the streets of the Blackwall neighborhood are flooded again, and canal-boats ply their way door to door through the streets. Even with you expert knowledge of the local rooftop-ways, transportation during the flood season is another of numerous unexpected expenses that are starting to nibble away at your budget. You find yourself thinking frequently that it\u2019s expensive being poor-the rich folks, on the other hand, have nice big houses well above the flood lines and never have to pay just to go out the front door.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a dreary afternoon in the first week of Descending Water when you decide to go after the Raptor Cat. Mostly, it\u2019s because you want the money-if you can capture it, some Merchant Prince would probably pay handsomely for the thing, or failing that one of the consortiums running gladiatorial fights might want an exotic monster to pit their contestants against\u2026or you might try to train it. You\u2019re a bit wary about that-you\u2019ve been reading up (or at least, making Moth read you the books aloud) on animal training, and everything you\u2019ve learned says that cats are difficult to break in and wildcats doubly so\u2026but having a well-trained pet Raptor Cat is the sort of thing that could have some major advantages.<br /> Preparations take you some time. Chupong tells you that \u201cCat Monster,\u201d as he calls the thing, \u201cHunt South Net Ladders. Hunt dogs, hunt cats. Hunt humans. Sunset.\u201d Your magic raiton\u2019s Riverspeak is rapidly improving now that he has you to talk to regularly.<br /> <br /> \u201cToday we hunt the Cat Monster,\u201d you tell him.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood. Kill monster. Strong,\u201d he agrees. \u201cGerel hunter. Erdene hunter. Wait!\u201d<br /> <br /> He flies out your window (which these days you keep open pretty much all the time) and up towards the roof, where you hear raucous cawing. You start making a mental list of stuff you\u2019re going to need. You don\u2019t much relish the idea of going after that thing again with just a knife. Your wound from last time you tried that healed a couple weeks ago, but Moth thinks you\u2019re going to have scars on your back forever.<br /> <br /> Bait, first off. You know it\u2019s attracted to prey that\u2019s weak or injured-when you first met it Chupong being caught in the twine and making a ton of noise and all the raitons circling like they would over a soon-to-die animal probably lured it in. And you know from Moth that the way it hunts is often by injuring its prey and then stalking it until it\u2019s weak from infection\u2026buying some cheap animal like a small pig or a goat and injuring it and getting the raitons to circle overhead might do it\u2026the question is what to do once you get it where you want it.<br /> <br /> Chupong flutters back in the window, followed by Gerel and one-eyed Erdene, two of his subordinate raitons. They perch on the back of your chair, Gerel giving Erdene a bit of space. Chupong lands on your shoulder.<br /> <br /> \u201cErdene hunt monster,\u201d he croaks loudly and directly into your ear.<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026what?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cErdene hunt.\u201d Chupong cocks his head quizzically at you. \u201cFish me.\u201d<br /> <br /> You absentmindedly give him a piece of dried fish, which Chupong gobbles down greedily.<br /> <br /> \u201cChupong\u2026Erdene is a raiton. What monsters can she hunt?\u2019<br /> <br /> \u201cStrong!\u201d Chupong warbles. \u201cErdene strong!\u201d<br /> <br /> The raitons chatter and squawk at each other briefly before settling down again.<br /> <br /> \u201cFish. Erdene fish monster. Hunt.\u201d Chupong goes back to pecking at his fish.<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026Erdene wants to use fish as bait?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBait? Nagiak pittusigak sinsik, pijagiakittuk,\u201d Chupong says something in Skytongue and you groan in frustration as you hunt through the dictionary for the meaning. Chupong copies your voice exactly, groaning in frustration at having to wait for you to go through the book again. Nagiak is \u2018attract,\u201d but you\u2019re not sure on the rest\u2026wait, there it is. Sinsik is\u2026falling asleep?<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026Chupong\u2026tell Erdene she is a genius!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGenius? What is?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cErdene smart. Clever raiton!\u201d You give her some fish directly, and she gobbles it. Gerel, perched next to her, eyes the fish but doesn\u2019t go after it.<br /> <br /> Capturing a sleeping Raptor Cat sounds a lot easier. If you just drug the bait, and then let it eat its fill, all you\u2019ll have to do is show up and put a collar on the thing! And conveniently\u2026you know just who to talk to in order to get a bunch of poppy juice.<br /> <br /> The question is\u2026are you going to tell Aunt Dwi what it\u2019s for? She\u2019s going to want to get in on selling the Raptor Cat, and while you did go shopping with her (she got you a really nice outfit, per your agreement) a couple weeks ago, you still haven\u2019t told her about selling the River Dragon liver or how much money you have beyond what you made selling the eye and the teeth through her. You haven\u2019t told anybody-news spreads fast in a brothel, and you don\u2019t want to become a target if somebody at the Peacock mentions your good luck to a client.<br /> <br /> But you\u2019re going to need a bunch of decently pure drugs-you really don\u2019t want to skimp on the Raptor Cat\u2019s dosage and try chaining up and carting off a less than fully sedated beast-and that means telling her how you plan to pay for all that opium.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <b>-Just Tell Her The Truth: She\u2019s gonna be offended you lied, at least by omission, and cut her out of a deal to the tune of a couple hundred dinars, true\u2026but the alchemist you sold it to goes to her brothel, she might find out eventually anyway, might as well have it be from you while you\u2019re offering to cut her in on a new deal.<br /> <br /> -Tell Her Part of the Truth: Tell her you\u2019re investing most of the money you made from the deal she was in on in this scheme, and that you hope to sell the raptor cat to make a bunch more money. Dwi appreciates an entrepreneurial spirit\u2026and if things go well, you can just pretend you have money because of selling the Raptor Cat, not because you cut her out of a deal.<br /> <br /> -Skip Dwi, go to her Supplier: Dwi deals the drugs, but you can probably spy on the Peacock a bit and figure out who she buys from. It\u2019ll be cheaper to cut out the middleman again, they\u2019ll probably ask fewer questions about what it\u2019s for as long as you can pay for the goods-actually, they\u2019ll probably just assume you\u2019re gonna try to sell it or get high off it-and that means you don\u2019t have to let anybody know you\u2019re hunting Raptor Cat.<br /> <br /> -Skip drugging the cat. The people you\u2019d have to deal with to pull it off are dangerous, and them starting to pay attention to you might be more dangerous than even a fully-lucid reptilian leopard beast. You can instead just bait a snare trap or build a portable cage to lure it into and shut the door. You\u2019re crafty, and supplies for that would be cheaper than the drugs.<br /> <br /> -Something Else?</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T17:23:54-07:00","id":1152646,"title":"","content":"<b>Something Else - go ask Golden Smoke / Blue Root.</b><br /> <br /> Why involve Dwi at all? Poppy juice isn't just a narcotic - it's a common medicinal painkiller. Any alchemist or druggist should have some or know where to buy some. So, why don't we go to an alchemist we already (kind of) know?<br /> <br /> What's more, we already told Golden Smoke about the Raptor Cat last time we visited. If she's learned anything about them since then, now is a convenient time to ask. <i>And </i>she may be able to give us an informed opinion about how much of the drug we'll need to make the cat sleep soundly without killing it. A street dealer probably would not be so helpful. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T19:05:31-07:00","id":1152671,"title":"","content":"I like going to the alchemist. It makes sense she would know about this stuff and deepen our little business relationship. We can pay a small bit extra for the opioid in exchange for the info. That being said I like keeping a good relationship with aunt Dwi, she took care of us when no one else would in her own way. This is a toughy. Ok I vote tell aunt dwi partial truth. We don't owe her a full explanation but she's practically family and has her fingers on the pulse of the city. We should use her as a resource and compensate her accordingly but this is still our venture and our risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T23:11:07-07:00","id":1152721,"title":"","content":"Agreed, go talk to Golden Smoke. Aunt Dwi,'s not going to be offended by our buying the opium elsewhere. But she's our best option for selling the cat, so tell her some of the truth. We don't want her mad at us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T03:27:33-07:00","id":1152741,"title":"","content":"I also vote for the Golden Smoke option. It'll cost a bit more out of pocket since we aren't involving anybody else in a cut of the deal, but if we pull it off, it leaves us in a much better position, even for bargaining with Aunt Dwi (if we wanted to do that). She'd probably appreciate us being resourceful enough to pull it off on our own anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12682-remedy","name":"Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T04:25:41-07:00","id":1152755,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing, lets ignore all the routes that end up with us as Raptor Cat dinner.<br /> <br /> Okay, we capture the apex predator of the rooftops, we can either:<br /> <br /> 1. Train it ourself<br /> 2. Sell it to Dwi<br /> 3. Both 1 and 2<br /> <br /> In all 3 of these outcomes, its better if <i>Dwi doesn't know. </i>For 2 and 3, it ends up as a nice surprise, a bonus in-fact, for her. Much better than telling her, trying, failing and then having to run back to her with our tail between our legs.<br /> <br /> If we train it ourself and keep it, then we <b><i>really </i></b>should not tell her anything, she might get nosy, or half of Nexus might find out that you have a killer pet, thats the kind of attention our protagonist can't afford right now.<br /> <br /> So I vote, get the drugs from Golden Smoke, yes, but don't tell Dwi until we are 100% sure that we want her to know how capable we are. And if we want to keep our kind Aunt in the dark about our new friend, also all to the good. We shouldn't trust her <i>too</i> much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 10-25-2017, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T12:42:20-07:00","id":1152878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1152755#post1152755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing, lets ignore all the routes that end up with us as Raptor Cat dinner.<br /> <br /> Okay, we capture the apex predator of the rooftops, we can either:<br /> <br /> 1. Train it ourself<br /> 2. Sell it to Dwi<br /> 3. Both 1 and 2<br /> <br /> In all 3 of these outcomes, its better if <i>Dwi doesn't know. </i>For 2 and 3, it ends up as a nice surprise, a bonus in-fact, for her. Much better than telling her, trying, failing and then having to run back to her with our tail between our legs.<br /> <br /> If we train it ourself and keep it, then we <b><i>really </i></b>should not tell her anything, she might get nosy, or half of Nexus might find out that you have a killer pet, thats the kind of attention our protagonist can't afford right now.<br /> <br /> So I vote, get the drugs from Golden Smoke, yes, but don't tell Dwi until we are 100% sure that we want her to know how capable we are. And if we want to keep our kind Aunt in the dark about our new friend, also all to the good. We shouldn't trust her <i>too</i> much.</div> </div> </div> </div>What he said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T16:32:20-07:00","id":1152978,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'll amend my vote to clarify I don't want to involve Aunt Dwi at all if it can be helped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12682-remedy","name":"Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T19:39:51-07:00","id":1153366,"title":"","content":"No strong opinion here, just glad to see it still going! Keep at it, Guru!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T22:42:54-07:00","id":1153398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1152721#post1152721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed, go talk to Golden Smoke. Aunt Dwi,'s not going to be offended by our buying the opium elsewhere. But she's our best option for selling the cat, so tell her some of the truth. We don't want her mad at us.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn'r have to be opium, just something that will make the damn Cat tired/sleepy.<br /> <br /> I also think we need a sturdy cage to put the darn animal in after it's knocked out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T19:21:44-07:00","id":1154275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1152646#post1152646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Something Else - go ask Golden Smoke / Blue Root.</b><br /> <br /> Why involve Dwi at all? Poppy juice isn't just a narcotic - it's a common medicinal painkiller. Any alchemist or druggist should have some or know where to buy some. So, why don't we go to an alchemist we already (kind of) know?<br /> <br /> What's more, we already told Golden Smoke about the Raptor Cat last time we visited. If she's learned anything about them since then, now is a convenient time to ask. <i>And </i>she may be able to give us an informed opinion about how much of the drug we'll need to make the cat sleep soundly without killing it. A street dealer probably would not be so helpful.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. The cage idea is a good one, too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T20:50:15-07:00","id":1232990,"title":"","content":"<b>Ask Golden Smoke/Blue Root: The Obvious Winner</b><br /> <br /> You consider bringing Aunt Dwi in on your scheme\u2026but decide against it. You can\u2019t help feeling a little bit guilty, Dwi took care of you when nobody else cared if you lived or died\u2026but you know she tends to take over things she gets involved with, and there\u2019s a good possibility she might get really worried by the prospect of you talking to magic birds and hunting dangerous wild animals. After some thought, you decide to get in touch with Golden Smoke. Blue Root obviously has money, and she said she\u2019d look into the Raptor Cat thing. Maybe she can give you more ideas about what to do with it once you\u2019ve caught it.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a long walk over to Blue Root\u2019s alchemical shop near the Tailor\u2019s district most of the year...but during the late Season of Water with the streets flooded, you have to take roofways and catwalks and scaffolds well out of your way to avoid having to hire a canal boat, and so it\u2019s an even longer trip. By the time you arrive (clambering down a gutter in the alley behind the shop), it\u2019s mid-afternoon.<br /> <br /> You peep through the windows instinctively, and see that the shop isn\u2019t empty: two unreasonably large men are looming inside. One of them is idly looking over the shelves full of herbs and ingredients in bottles while the other is leaning an elbow on the counter and sitting with his head in his hand chatting with Golden Smoke. Even bent over as he is, he\u2019s as tall as she is. You immediately notice the strangers have shaved heads and are carrying machetes at their waists, and that the one eyeing up the shelves has a black tattoo of a meditating monkey on his shoulder. These guys are with the Obsidian Monkey Gang. They\u2019re way outside their home turf over on the east side of town between Firewander and Sentinel\u2019s Hill\u2026<br /> <br /> The guy looking over the supplies glances out the window and your eyes meet briefly. Slowly, deliberately, he grins, and then winks.<br /> <br /> You make yourself scarce, wait until after the two strangers leave with a paper bag, and descend once again from the rooftops to visit the now-empty shop. The Obsidian Monkey Gang is bad news. They\u2019re rather famously brutal, even as Nexus gangs go. You\u2019ve heard that killing a blood relative just to join is a condition of membership.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019re cl-\u2026oh, hello, Tavi,\u201d Golden Smoke says as you come in the front door. \u201cI\u2019m just closing up shop for the day. What can I help you with?\u201d You\u2019d expect someone who was just chatting with the Obsidian Monkeys to be shaken up, but she\u2019s actually grinning a little. The strange blue writing tattooed on the side of her face is interrupted by a dimple.<br /> <br /> \u201cHi, Smoke.\u201d You nod and close the door behind you. \u201cI\u2019m going Raptor Cat hunting and I was hoping I could buy something from you to put on meat. I figure it\u2019s safest to drug the bastard to sleep AND give it a full belly before I try anything.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHm. You saw it before. Would you say it\u2019s about the size of a tiger?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve never seen a tiger.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright. Bigger or smaller than a horse?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSmaller. Bigger than a goat or a pig, though.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI have just the thing. It\u2019s a bit stronger than poppy juice, so it won\u2019t take a lot of it. Blue Root has a couple of clients who, um. Insist that they are actually farmers who need to put bulls to sleep for purposes of artificial insemination? Pretty sure they\u2019re slavers, though\u2026anyway, a little bit goes a long way, and you can mix it with food. Should be okay for a Raptor Cat, I guess\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you.\u201d You watch as she rummages about and comes back with a small glass phial full of something that flows slowly, like syrup or molasses, as she turns it in front of a candle.<br /> \u201cThis should do the trick. That\u2019ll be\u2026twenty two Dinar.\u201d<br /> <br /> You frown. \u201cWhat do you say fifteen Dinar and I agree to sell the Raptor Cat musk to you instead of Red Clover?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026sure, why not.\u201d She shrugs. \u201cYou\u2019ve been good luck for me so far, and it\u2019s not like it\u2019s my money.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDid you have a chance to look into uses for Raptor Cats other than the musk?\u201d You get out your cheques and write one out for her, stamping it with your personal seal.<br /> <br /> \u201cI checked into it a little. Apparently you can use their eyes to make a potion that lets you see spirits for three days and three nights, which is a really good duration, but there\u2019s cheaper ways to pull that off. And their spit is one of several ingredients you can use in a glue to trap someone\u2019s shadow, but I\u2019d also need sap from the Linowan forest, and it\u2019s expensive getting ingredients shipped in from that far East\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSpeaking of exotic eastern stuff\u2026what\u2019re the Obsidian Monkeys doing all the way over here? They\u2019re not looking to expand their territory, are they?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo. Couple of buyers, that\u2019s all. Gladiators aren\u2019t the only ones who want skins like River Dragon scales.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI see.\u201d You shrug. \u201cWell, I hope they enjoy their bile.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI doubt they will. Nasty side effects. But their coin is good.\u201d Smoke smirks as she bags your phial of sleep drugs. \u201cListen, if you\u2019re serious about this Raptor Cat thing\u2026it\u2019s probably worth more to just sell the whole animal, but the best way to monetize it for alchemy would be to lock it up someplace, feed it, and keep harvesting the musk for aphrodisiacs. There\u2019s cheaper aphrodisiacs, but there\u2019s always a market for weird exotic stuff. People think it\u2019s stronger because we charge more for it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHm.\u201d You heft your bag. \u201cI\u2019ll keep that in mind.\u201d <div align=\"center\">*****<br /> </div> It\u2019s a simple matter to buy a bunch of organ meat at one of the many butcher shops on the way to Nighthammer. You build a sturdy cage on the roof with hefty wooden bars reinforced with woven wire. You buy some sturdy ropes, and a leather collar, and a muzzle. Between that and the drugs, you\u2019ve burned through all your ready money-the rest is locked up in a Time Deposit account with the Chrysanthemum Abacus Merchants for another eight months. You\u2019d worry about being penniless again if you fail to capture the Raptor Cat\u2026but Chupong and his raiton bodyguards have gotten pretty good about bringing you small shiny objects, and a lot of those small shiny objects are coins.<br /> <br /> But it does mean that you\u2019re a bit light on cash for actual transportation of the Raptor Cat itself\u2026and so you pay a visit to Grinning Eel. You find him a couple days later in the afternoon down by the Nighthammer Docks, sitting in his boat just offshore with a fishing line.<br /> <br /> \u201cEel!\u201d You shout to him.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, kid! Been a while.\u201d He nods, tipping his conical hat in your direction and releasing a small cloud of smoke out the back. Looks like he\u2019s been burning some of his newfound coin in his hashish pipe. Slowly, Eel poles his boat back over to the dock. \u201cWhat have you been up to?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSelling monster parts. Making money.\u201d You shrug. \u201cLearning to read.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cReading eh?\u201d Eel snorts, squinting at you. \u201cCan\u2019t say as I ever had much use for it\u2026new knife. Looks like nice work. You made off good with all that lizard meat, huh.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI hear you did pretty well on that River Dragon heart yourself, old man.\u201d You smile. \u201cListen. I need a favor.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI just need a late-night ride. I\u2019m not sure where from yet, but I\u2019ll need to get back to Blackwall as quick as you can go.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHrm. You paying?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026There\u2019s money in this, but I get it after. I can pay you then.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGods, you sound just like your old man, kid\u2026but you\u2019ve been good luck so far. I\u2019m in.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks, Eel.\u201d You give him a little bow. Old folks love getting bowed at. \u201cI promise you won\u2019t regret this.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey. How am I going to know where to pick you up if you don\u2019t know yet yourself?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026do you have one of the red paper lanterns the canal men all use for the Fire Festival?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLight it. This is gonna sound a little crazy, but, um. I\u2019m going to send a bird to find you. He\u2019ll tell you where to pick me up.\u201d<br /> <br /> Grinning Eel leans back, raising the brim of his hat with one hand so he can look you in the eye, concerned. \u201cYou got a fever, kid?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTrust me, old man.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026you promised I wasn\u2019t gonna regret this. I <i>already </i>regret this. But it sounds like you\u2019re stickin\u2019 your nose in trouble, and I\u2019m not gonna let my prospective apprentice get in hot water by himself. I\u2019ll pick you up.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAs fast as you can.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAs fast as I can.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGreat. It\u2019s really very important that we hurry because therewillbeahugedruggedcatmonsterintheboatwithusan difitwakesupbeforewegetithomeitmightkillusbothOkay ThanksForYourHelpBye!\u201d<br /> <br /> You dash up the dock and you\u2019re around the corner by the time his explosive, \u201cWHAT?!\u201d reaches you.<br /> <div align=\"center\">******<br /> </div> That evening after some consultation with your birds, you\u2019re walking in the rain. It\u2019s drizzling lightly, and Gerel and Tetseg have been taking turns spying on the Raptor Cat and reporting back to Chupong, who reports back to you in croaking human speech.<br /> <br /> \u201cMonster cat. Hiding under roof bucket. Wet, angry.\u201d Chupong informs you. The roof bucket, you\u2019re fairly certain, is a large wooden rain-collector on a rooftop near the Blackhand Company. They pipe the water in for\u2026something in the foundry, you\u2019re not entirely sure, you\u2019ve never worked in the foundry.<br /> <br /> You have ropes and muzzle and a bag you wove yourself (that\u2019s not your nice bag!) full of organ meats you\u2019ve dosed with the sleeping poison. Soon, you have set up the organ meat in an alley near the Blackhand Company building with the rain collector. You chose this alley because it runs right up to a ledge overlooking the canal-you should be able to drag the raptor cat down onto a boat with minimal difficulty. Once the bait is in place, you head up on the roof to keep an eye out from across the street. You can see Tetseg flying big circles around the rain collector, and you imagine you see something moving in the shadows under it\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cReady?\u201d Chupong squawks in a stage-whisper, landing on your shoulder. He smells like wet bird and bad fish.<br /> <br /> \u201cReady.\u201d You turn to Chupong. \u201cTell your raitons to circle over the meat, but don\u2019t eat it! It is poison. Bait for cat-monster.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen, go find red light on water. Tell man with circle hat\u2026Alley Ledge by Blackhand Foundry. Alley Ledge by Blackhand Foundry Bring man here.\u201d<br /> <br /> Chupong cocks his head at you. \u201cCircle\u2026hat?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCircle hat man in boat. Alley Ledge. Blackhand Foundry.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHat man.\u201d<br /> <br /> The raiton flies off. You\u2026really hope he understood you.<br /> <br /> Soon, the raitons are circling over the alley and squawking up a storm. You briefly worry they\u2019ll draw actual human attention\u2026but the sun is setting and it\u2019s raining, and all the folk on the street are hurrying home from a long day in the foundry. Soon, as the shadows lengthen and the streets clear, you see a pair of gleaming golden circles peering out from under the huge wooden rain collector across the street.<br /> <br /> The Raptor Cat watches the raitons for a while and then emerges into the drizzling dusk. It looks\u2026a lot less intimidating from across the street. It has scales instead of fur, but it still manages to look exactly as grumpy as any other cat caught out in the rain. You notice that even several weeks later, it\u2019s still limping on its back left leg. It also seems skinnier than when last you met. Perhaps the injury from when it fell off the roof has interfered with hunting. You feel a pang of sympathy-you know what it\u2019s like to be a starving street animal. But hopefully this will make it more eager to take your bait.<br /> <br /> Slowly, your sympathy fades. It turns out sitting patiently watching wild animals is infuriating. Do Raptor Cats always move this slowly? It feels like ten minutes before the damn thing makes its way down to the street, carefully analyzing each hop down to the next ledge or awning. Finally, it slides into the alley and out of sight.<br /> <br /> You wait patiently. The alley only has two exits-the canal and the street, and the street exit is visible from here. Or\u2026well, you suppose it\u2019s possible the cat could climb a trash bin to the bamboo fire escape scaffoldings and make it up to the roof where you are.<br /> <br /> You get out your knife, just in case.<br /> <br /> \u2026after a few minutes of standing in the rain, you creep to the edge of the roof and look down. The Raptor Cat is down there, and it\u2019s definitely eating the meat you left out.<br /> It looks up at you, and the dull shine of its eyes meeting yours in the dark sends a wave of cold up your spine. This was all\u2026a terrible idea. What if it doesn\u2019t eat all the bait? What if the drug takes too long to take effect? What if the rain has washed the drug away and it doesn\u2019t take effect at all? What if Eel doesn\u2019t show up? What if-<br /> <br /> The Raptor Cat hisses at you, and you back away from the edge of the roof. Below, you can hear gulping and slurping as it continues to devour your bait. Then, after several minutes\u2026the gulping and slurping stops, and there\u2019s a gentle slap.<br /> <br /> You peek over the edge of the roof again. The cat has slumped into the puddle against the wall by the big trash bin, and is breathing slowly. The drugs seem to be taking effect. You wait a few minutes to be sure\u2026then climb down to the alley. Slowly, cautiously, you approach the prone feline. Its eyes are open but unfocused, and its tongue is hanging out of its mouth.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>\u2026what now?</b></div> <br /> <b>-Wait a few minutes to make sure the drugs have taken effect before doing anything-you don\u2019t know how long these drugs will take to fully kick in! The last thing you need is to wake it up and get mauled. Once you\u2019re sure it\u2019s really out, truss it up in ropes and the muzzle and start dragging it towards the canal so Eel can pick you up.<br /> <br /> -Don\u2019t waste any time-you don\u2019t know how long these drugs will keep the cat sedated! Get in there right away and truss it up and drag it over to the canal immediately. It\u2019s a long ride to the Blackwall Neighborhood, even in a hurry, so you should use any extra time before Eel gets here to make sure it\u2019s tied up really well in case it wakes up in the boat.<br /> <br /> -There\u2019s a broom right here on the other side of the trash bin. Gingerly poke it with the broom to make sure it\u2019s actually out cold, THEN move fast.<br /> <br /> -You\u2026actually feel bad for this thing. Sure, it\u2019s a monster that tried to eat you, and probably has eaten lots of street kids like you\u2026but it\u2019s far from its home and it\u2019s injured. And you know what it\u2019s like to desperately scarf down food you found in a back alley and wind up slumped against a dumpster feeling sick. You decide to Malfeas with the money. You walk away, and let it go.<br /> <br /> -Okay, this plan where you get in a boat with a drugged-out man eating predator is actually insane, now that you\u2019re looking at said man-eating predator up close. Take advantage of the cat\u2019s weakened state to get in and slit its throat as quick as you can, taking care not to damage the hide too much. It might not be worth as much in parts as it is alive, but it\u2019ll be a hell of a lot easier to convince Eel to help you move a dead Raptor Cat than a sleeping one.<br /> <br /> -You\u2019ve been reading up on training animals, and while cats are famously hard to train, you\u2019ve learned a bit about how to soothe them and make them feel comfortable. Instead of getting in its space, you squat across the alley from the Raptor Cat and extend one arm. If it doesn\u2019t respond, you\u2019ll slowly creep closer and see if you can splint its leg before you tie it up and drag it. The last thing you want to do is make its injury even worse.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T22:20:18-07:00","id":1232998,"title":"","content":"<b>-You\u2019ve been reading up on training animals, and while cats are famously hard to train, you\u2019ve learned a bit about how to soothe them and make them feel comfortable. Instead of getting in its space, you squat across the alley from the Raptor Cat and extend one arm. If it doesn\u2019t respond, you\u2019ll slowly creep closer and see if you can splint its leg before you tie it up and drag it. The last thing you want to do is make its injury even worse.</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T02:14:18-07:00","id":1233016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1232998#post1232998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>-You\u2019ve been reading up on training animals, and while cats are famously hard to train, you\u2019ve learned a bit about how to soothe them and make them feel comfortable. Instead of getting in its space, you squat across the alley from the Raptor Cat and extend one arm. If it doesn\u2019t respond, you\u2019ll slowly creep closer and see if you can splint its leg before you tie it up and drag it. The last thing you want to do is make its injury even worse.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>So much this. Keep the monster calm and look after it. I'm a tad leery of the drug we gave it now (if the cat has a bad reaction, it might mess with the musk) but taking care of it's wounds can only help us.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T03:37:57-07:00","id":1233026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1233016#post1233016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So much this. Keep the monster calm and look after it. I'm a tad leery of the drug we gave it now (if the cat has a bad reaction, it might mess with the musk) but taking care of it's wounds can only help us.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can harvest the musk, why not keep the apex predator around? After all, our protagonist is becoming a regular Mother of monsters and oddities.<br /> <br /> Good to see you back, by the way, Guru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 07-07-2018, 07:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T07:11:20-07:00","id":1233045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1233026#post1233026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can harvest the musk, why not keep the apex predator around? After all, our protagonist is becoming a regular Mother of monsters and oddities.<br /> Good to see you back, by the way, Guru.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to keep it around, I was more worried that we may have 'broken' the poor creature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T22:18:40-07:00","id":1233142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1232998#post1232998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>-You\u2019ve been reading up on training animals, and while cats are famously hard to train, you\u2019ve learned a bit about how to soothe them and make them feel comfortable. Instead of getting in its space, you squat across the alley from the Raptor Cat and extend one arm. If it doesn\u2019t respond, you\u2019ll slowly creep closer and see if you can splint its leg before you tie it up and drag it. The last thing you want to do is make its injury even worse.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Thiiiiiiiiis.<br /> Also I'm so happy this quest isn't dead. Go Guru.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T08:58:08-07:00","id":1233208,"title":"","content":"<b>You\u2019ve been reading up on training animals, and while cats are famously hard to train, you\u2019ve learned a bit about how to soothe them and make them feel comfortable. Instead of getting in its space, you squat across the alley from the Raptor Cat and extend one arm. If it doesn\u2019t respond, you\u2019ll slowly creep closer and see if you can splint its leg before you tie it up and drag it. The last thing you want to do is make its injury even worse.</b><br /> <br /> If we wind up selling it, we'll want it as healthy as possible. And if we wind up keeping it as a pet (as opposed to a musk-generator), we'd better start building a good relationship with it. <br /> <br /> And while we're here, might as well figure out if it's male or female. The whole &quot;musk-generator&quot; thing becomes moot if it's female.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T15:10:03-07:00","id":1233284,"title":"","content":"Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeee! You're back, you're back! So glad to see it, Guru!<br /> <br /> I agree with everyone else; splint the leg, then transport. Keep our options open. Also, note that pet and musk generator aren't mutually exclusive!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T17:09:04-07:00","id":1233312,"title":"","content":"So glad you\u2019re back!!!!!!!!<br /> <br /> Oh man you guys are thinking great. Let\u2019s name him Daimyo Mittens! My vote is splint and transport. That being said his claws are more dangerous than his teeth so we could fashion some cute little booties for him. That may be a future goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T01:35:25-07:00","id":1233364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1232998#post1232998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>-You\u2019ve been reading up on training animals, and while cats are famously hard to train, you\u2019ve learned a bit about how to soothe them and make them feel comfortable. Instead of getting in its space, you squat across the alley from the Raptor Cat and extend one arm. If it doesn\u2019t respond, you\u2019ll slowly creep closer and see if you can splint its leg before you tie it up and drag it. The last thing you want to do is make its injury even worse.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thiiiiiiiiiiis (also super glad this is still going as I just read through the whole thing)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T18:35:56-07:00","id":1251255,"title":"","content":"<b>Again, we have a clear winner. Veterinary care it is.</b><br /> <br /> Gingerly, you creep across the alley towards the raptor cat. Its eyes are still wide open, and its pupils huge and glinting yellow in the gloom\u2026but its tongue is hanging out, it\u2019s lying on its side, and is breathing is slow\u2026<br /> <br /> You briefly debate which limb you\u2019re least attached to before poking it with your left foot. No reaction. Gingerly, you poke it again, this time moving its wounded leg slightly. The huge cat twitches, and you leap back-but no other reaction.<br /> <br /> Good.<br /> <br /> First things first. You tie the leather muzzle you wove onto the cat\u2019s head. It\u2019s completely limp, and its head is much heavier than you expected it to be. The scales feel hard and smooth\u2026and warm. The dull thudding of its heartbeat, slower than yours, is audible this close. You can feel it in your fingers as you you get the muzzle on. This cat is big. You\u2019re thinking you might actually need Eel\u2019s help to drag it down the alley and into the boat\u2026<br /> <br /> You\u2019ve set a broken bone before, once-when Rat fell off a roof and broke his arm, he told you how to do it and then held a rag in his mouth. Your patient here is bigger, but frankly a lot more cooperative-setting the leg is relatively simple, the hard part is the cat\u2019s limbs are slippery from the rain so it takes a bit of effort to get the right grip. There\u2019s an old wooden pallet leaning on the dumpster in the alley. You pry it apart, and use a couple of planks along with some of your rope to splint the cat\u2019s injured leg, which should keep the bones where you put them. You\u2019ve seen it\u2019s trying to keep its weight off the leg, so hopefully between that and the splint it\u2019ll help it heal up.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s at about this time that you hear the splash of a pole over the sound of rain, and a familiar croaking voice crying, \u201cHat man! Blackhand Alley! Come!\u201d<br /> <br /> You head down to the end of the alley, where it becomes a ledge overhanging the canal.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, Eel,\u201d you call as the boat gets closer. \u201cGood timing!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cKid, you have got a lot of nerve,\u201d Eel barks, \u201cBut this damned scavenger of yours is even worse. Bastard keeps trying to steal my hat!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cChupong. Come.\u201d The raiton soars to land on your shoulder and turns to look at Eel reproachfully.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot gonna lie to you, kiddo. That is really creepy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood,\u201d you chuckle. \u201cLess chance I get mugged. Listen, I\u2019ve got a big unconscious raptor cat drugged asleep up this alley.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026you don\u2019t say.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve built a cage for it at my place in the Blackwall neighborhood. But it\u2019s a bit heavy for me to move by myself. You mind tying up here and helping me get it in the boat?\u201d<br /> <br /> Eel looks at you, and his rain-lashed face experiences a dramatic conflict between horror and pride. It settles eventually on a compromise, and gets very concerned. \u201cA\u2026raptor cat, you say.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBig cat. Will kill us both if it wakes up.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026then why are we letting it wake up, kid?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBecause it needs to be alive to make musk, and the alchemist I sold the dragon bits to said that musk is an ingredient we can sell to make a super expensive aphrodisiac, and I don\u2019t wanna kill the goose that lays the jade eggs, Eel.\u201d You sigh, exasperated. \u201cNow come on up here and help?\u201d<br /> <br /> Eel grumbles and ties up and clambers out of the boat. Chupong, always dramatic, chooses this moment to launch into a frightening high-pitched laughter, and Eel startles so bad he almost ends up in the canal.<br /> <br /> \u201cStop that,\u201d you grunt, bopping the raiton on the beak. He nips your hand, but he does shut up.<br /> <br /> \u201cGods,\u201d Eel mutters. \u201cDamned thing sounds just like you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWait, really? He\u2019s copying me? Is that what my laugh sounds like?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, yeah.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026oh.\u201d You shrug. \u201cI didn\u2019t realize my voice was so\u2026high pitched.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cEh, don\u2019t worry about it. Your dad had a real deep bass, we could hear him all the way up and down the canal when he was singin\u2019 while he worked. Made him real popular with the ladies. I expect once your balls drop, you\u2019ll probably inherit some of the magic. You\u2019ve got his eyes, after all.\u201d Eel shrugs. \u201cAnd hey, if you don\u2019t, there\u2019s other ways to impress girls. Like catching raptor cats, I guess\u2026oh shit. That is a, uh, big cat there kid.\u201d<br /> <br /> You smile. \u201cYeah. That\u2019s why I need your help.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot sure it\u2019s gonna fit in the boat with both of us.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019ll make it work. Hell, I\u2019ll hang on the side and swim next to you if I need to. Let\u2019s move fast, I don\u2019t know how long those drugs\u2019ll keep it under.\u201d<br /> <br /> Between the two of you, you drag the cat down to the end of the alley and drop it down onto the boat. The sound of the rain covers the splash, and the cat twitches again in the bottom of the boat before going still.<br /> <br /> Carefully, you and Eel climb into the boat. He stands at the front with his pole, and you squat at the back over the slumbering predator, doing your best not to put any of your weight on the actual cat. Eel unties the boat, and poles you out into the canal. \u201cKid?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGet out your knife and have it right by that thing\u2019s throat. If it looks like it\u2019s about to wake up, cut it right away. Got it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026got it.\u201d You get out the knife, and lean in real close.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo. This cage you built. How far from the canal is it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s right by the canal. It\u2019s the same building as my apartment, up on the roof.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026on the roof.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026okay, yeah. Hadn\u2019t considered that.\u201d You groan. \u201cIt\u2019s only\u2026three flights of stairs?\u201d<br /> <br /> Eel stares off into the evening rain, expressionless.<br /> <br /> \u201cI mean, if we get a couple of poles and rig up a stretcher, we could-\u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cKid. Are you, in fact, insane? Are you possessed or some shit?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026no.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBecause you\u2019re sitting here with a talking raiton on your shoulder like it\u2019s the most natural thing in the world, and a sleeping snake-leopard-thing, and you\u2019re telling me you are taking this thing home without a plan to actually get it into a cage? What in the name of the gods is going on with you?!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cJust\u2026grabbing an opportunity to make a quick Dinar where I can, Eel.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, but\u2026this?\u201d Eel gestures at Chupong. Chupong squawks at him.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, he gives me coins. More than most people I usually run into have usually felt like doing, Eel.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026okay. Alright. That's fair. I\u2019ve got a spare pole strapped to the side of the boat in case I lose my grip. You have a sheet where we\u2019re going to make up a stretcher?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026alright. Let\u2019s\u2026let\u2019s do this, then, kid. But I want fifty percent.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTen.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTwenty.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI still gotta get my landlord on board with a man-eating monster on the roof. I expect he\u2019ll want a piece too. Fifteen.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026Fine.\u201d Eel spits in his hand, you do the same, and the two of you shake on it. <div align=\"center\"><br /> *****</div> The two of you arrive at the Blackwall dock by your new home as quickly as Eel can pole you there. The water is high from the frequent rains, and it\u2019s actually starting to seep out into the streets of your new neighborhood, which is convenient today-your destination is even closer to the canal than usual. You were hoping the street would be completely empty because of the pouring rain, and your prayers have mostly been answered-there are two or three people out on the street, but they\u2019re not paying any attention to you, they\u2019re setting up small walls of sandbags around their doorways. You dash upstairs get into your room, and grab the blankets off of Moth\u2019s bedroll, shaking several books off as you go.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, what are you-\u201c Moth, who is currently sitting at the stove stirring something in a pot, starts as you storm into the place.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo time! Sleeping cat!\u201d You dash back out again with the blanket.<br /> <br /> \u201c-Hey! That\u2019s mine!\u201d<br /> <br /> At the bottom of the stairs, you find Eel has already dragged the cat to your building. He\u2019s got two poles, and you quickly roll them up on the ends of the blanket and tie some rope. You hope it\u2019ll hold, you wish you\u2019d thought to sew a proper stretcher earlier\u2026The two of you manhandle the raptor cat onto the sheet, and you groan with the weight as you and Eel pick the beast up.<br /> <br /> \u201cGet the poles on your shoulders, kid.\u201d Eel grunts. \u201cHold \u2018em in place, and lift with your legs. Keep your back straight.\u201d<br /> <br /> Slowly, you stump your way up the stairs. As you pass the second floor, Moth is coming out onto the landing, waving a wooden spoon.\u201cTavi, what are you doing with my blanket?\u201d.<br /> <br /> \u201cBusy, Moth!\u201d you grunt.<br /> <br /> \u201cIs that\u2026is that the raptor cat that mauled you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWait, it mauled you?\u201d Eel barks.<br /> <br /> \u201cShut up,\u201d you grumble. \u201cMoth, this thing is heavy, and might wake up soon, and you\u2019re in the way. Either help me or MOVE.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. Sorry.\u201d Unexpectedly, she steps in next to you and grabs a pole, helping with some of the weight.<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026thanks. Could you get the door on the roof for us?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay.\u201d She dashes up the last flight of stairs ahead of you.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, uh\u2026who is <i>she</i>?\u201d Eel asks, and even though you can\u2019t turn around and he\u2019s below you and behind you, you can hear the leer in his voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cMy roommate.\u201d Eel can't see your face, but you hope he can hear your scowl.<br /> <br /> \u201cBit old for you, isn\u2019t she?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not like that.\u201d You groan, stumping up stair after stair.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo she\u2019s single, then?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cEel, even if you <i>weren\u2019t</i> a hideous lecherous and thoroughly unlovable bastard, you\u2019re old enough to be her grandfather.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHa ha! Who knows, kiddo.\u201d Eel bounces the pallet slightly. \u201cI might be!\u201d<br /> <br /> It is at this point that the raptor cat makes a noise, and you both shut up and get up the stairs far quicker than you thought possible.<br /> <br /> Moth dashes out onto the roof ahead of the two of you, and under your instruction opens the door of the big wooden cage you built on the roof. You and Eel put down the raptor cat inside its cage, get out, and shut the door, which you latch. And then tie closed with rope, just to be safe.<br /> <br /> You\u2019ve captured a raptor cat!<br /> <br /> The three of you stand in the rain for a little bit, peering in through the spaces between the thick wood bars. The cat, for its part, continues to sleep peacefully.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, uh. Now what?\u201d Eel asks. <div align=\"center\"><b>Now what indeed?</b><br /> <br /> </div> <b>Invite Eel In For Dinner:</b> He\u2019s been a big help today, everybody is cold and wet, and Moth was making something hot on the stove. He already knows what building you live in, and you figure at this point you can probably trust him with knowing which room. If the two of you are going to be musk-harvesting business partners, it makes sense to spend some time getting a bit closer with him.<br /> <br /> <b>Have Eel For Dinner: </b>Fifteen percent?! And now this old bastard knows where you live? This guy sure looks like cat food to me...<br /> <br /> <b>Call It A Night:</b> You\u2019re physically exhausted. Tell Eel you\u2019re going to bed, encourage him to go home and do the same, and tomorrow morning he can come by and the two of you will figure out what to do with the raptor cat. How to extract its musk, or go about finding a good buyer, or whatever.<br /> <br /> <b>Get It Off My Roof:</b> Ask Eel to start discreetly looking for posh nobles or Dynasts or merchant princes who might like a pet raptor cat for their menagerie. The logistics of a caged raptor cat are rapidly increasing in complexity in your head now that you have one up here.<br /> <br /> <b>And I\u2019ll Have Fries With That:</b> Ask Eel to go buy up a bunch of cheap meat so you have something to feed this thing in the morning.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lion\u2019s Den: </b>Let Moth and Eel go back to their regular evenings, you\u2019ll stay up here all night in the rain keeping a vigil over the cat to make sure it doesn\u2019t hurt itself-or worse, break out of its cage-when it wakes up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T22:23:06-07:00","id":1251277,"title":"","content":"How about a combination of things:<br /> <br /> 1. Send Eel out to get fixings for a celebratory meal, with enough meat for like 6 people (the good stuff of course) all on your dime. Wine and the lot of it..<br /> <br /> 2. While he\u2019s gone, if it\u2019s still raining, pay Moth back for her blanket that she is never going to use again and set it up as a water proof-ish awning (you have poles and whatnot there). Also see if you can convince her to get the stock boiling for your celebratory punch up.<br /> <br /> 3. While your erstwhile allies are busy, think very hard about your plans for the immediate future so you have something to tell Eel when he gets back.<br /> <br /> 4. Party on the roof!<br /> <br /> 5. See Eel off and keep an eye on the cat until it wakes, feed it (with the extra meat) take care of it. Y\u2019know get that imprinting started. You\u2019re going to have it get very, used to you before you can collect anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T09:05:17-07:00","id":1251401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1251277#post1251277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a combination of things:<br /> <br /> 1. Send Eel out to get fixings for a celebratory meal, with enough meat for like 6 people (the good stuff of course) all on your dime. Wine and the lot of it..<br /> <br /> 2. While he\u2019s gone, if it\u2019s still raining, pay Moth back for her blanket that she is never going to use again and set it up as a water proof-ish awning (you have poles and whatnot there). Also see if you can convince her to get the stock boiling for your celebratory punch up.<br /> <br /> 3. While your erstwhile allies are busy, think very hard about your plans for the immediate future so you have something to tell Eel when he gets back.<br /> <br /> 4. Party on the roof!<br /> <br /> 5. See Eel off and keep an eye on the cat until it wakes, feed it (with the extra meat) take care of it. Y\u2019know get that imprinting started. You\u2019re going to have it get very, used to you before you can collect anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T16:09:14-07:00","id":1251515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1251277#post1251277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a combination of things:<br /> <br /> 1. Send Eel out to get fixings for a celebratory meal, with enough meat for like 6 people (the good stuff of course) all on your dime. Wine and the lot of it..<br /> <br /> 2. While he\u2019s gone, if it\u2019s still raining, pay Moth back for her blanket that she is never going to use again and set it up as a water proof-ish awning (you have poles and whatnot there). Also see if you can convince her to get the stock boiling for your celebratory punch up.<br /> <br /> 3. While your erstwhile allies are busy, think very hard about your plans for the immediate future so you have something to tell Eel when he gets back.<br /> <br /> 4. Party on the roof!<br /> <br /> 5. See Eel off and keep an eye on the cat until it wakes, feed it (with the extra meat) take care of it. Y\u2019know get that imprinting started. You\u2019re going to have it get very, used to you before you can collect anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Third.<span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"> 10char</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T18:36:08-07:00","id":1251532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1251277#post1251277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a combination of things:<br /> <br /> 1. Send Eel out to get fixings for a celebratory meal, with enough meat for like 6 people (the good stuff of course) all on your dime. Wine and the lot of it..<br /> <br /> 2. While he\u2019s gone, if it\u2019s still raining, pay Moth back for her blanket that she is never going to use again and set it up as a water proof-ish awning (you have poles and whatnot there). Also see if you can convince her to get the stock boiling for your celebratory punch up.<br /> <br /> 3. While your erstwhile allies are busy, think very hard about your plans for the immediate future so you have something to tell Eel when he gets back.<br /> <br /> 4. Party on the roof!<br /> <br /> 5. See Eel off and keep an eye on the cat until it wakes, feed it (with the extra meat) take care of it. Y\u2019know get that imprinting started. You\u2019re going to have it get very, used to you before you can collect anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're Back! YAY!<br /> Welcome back!<br /> Also, I fourth this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T20:02:14-07:00","id":1251546,"title":"","content":"Because my advice doesn\u2019t seem, by popular consensus, to be terrible, could I maybe make a long term suggestion (maybe something she discusses with Eel over dinner?)<br /> <br /> Poling a boat through Nexus seems more and more like a poor use of our protagonist\u2019s valuable time. How about you try to corner the market on boat rental? Do it like a Creation Style Ride Share, make deals with the workshops that repair them and then rent them out for a share of the profits. Our heroine already knows how the business is run and the risks involved, just take it one level up. (It also appears that boats are a significant investment for the subset of people that pole them, maybe this makes it more attractive?)<br /> <br /> And passenger boat polers hear a lot of interesting things and transport a lot of interesting cargo. Maybe put a bounty on valuable info while you are at it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 09-05-2018, 02:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T05:35:25-07:00","id":1251631,"title":"","content":"Got tto be honest, not sure if Eel can be trusted to return if we give him money...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T11:28:34-07:00","id":1251723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1251546#post1251546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because my advice doesn\u2019t seem, by popular consensus, to be terrible, could I maybe make a long term suggestion (maybe something she discusses with Eel over dinner?)<br /> <br /> Poling a boat through Nexus seems more and more like a poor use of our protagonist\u2019s valuable time. How about you try to corner the market on boat rental? Do it like a Creation Style Ride Share, make deals with the workshops that repair them and then rent them out for a share of the profits. Our heroine already knows how the business is run and the risks involved, just take it one level up. (It also appears that boats are a significant investment for the subset of people that pole them, maybe this makes it more attractive?)<br /> <br /> And passenger boat polers hear a lot of interesting things and transport a lot of interesting cargo. Maybe put a bounty on valuable info while you are at it?</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think this is feasible for the forseeable future. We'd have to outcompete all of the independent boat-taxis, and we have no means of doing that.<br /> <br /> More importantly, becoming a taxi magnate sounds really boring. This is Exalted! We live in a world of magic and wonder, and your highest ambition is to become a successful small business owner? What legends will they tell of our deeds then? (Answer: None, probably.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1251631#post1251631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got tto be honest, not sure if Eel can be trusted to return if we give him money...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's not like it's a *lot* of money. Eel hasn't demonstrated much financial restraint in the past, but I doubt he'd run out on Tavi over the equivalent of a week's groceries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T19:21:55-07:00","id":1251812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1251723#post1251723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't think this is feasible for the forseeable future. We'd have to outcompete all of the independent boat-taxis, and we have no means of doing that.<br /> <br /> More importantly, becoming a taxi magnate sounds really boring. This is Exalted! We live in a world of magic and wonder, and your highest ambition is to become a successful small business owner? What legends will they tell of our deeds then? (Answer: None, probably.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, I think you are right here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, it's not like it's a *lot* of money. Eel hasn't demonstrated much financial restraint in the past, but I doubt he'd run out on Tavi over the equivalent of a week's groceries. </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m rather hoping his cupidity for future profits outweigh his current greed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T19:39:03-07:00","id":1251816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1251277#post1251277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a combination of things:<br /> <br /> 1. Send Eel out to get fixings for a celebratory meal, with enough meat for like 6 people (the good stuff of course) all on your dime. Wine and the lot of it..<br /> <br /> 2. While he\u2019s gone, if it\u2019s still raining, pay Moth back for her blanket that she is never going to use again and set it up as a water proof-ish awning (you have poles and whatnot there). Also see if you can convince her to get the stock boiling for your celebratory punch up.<br /> <br /> 3. While your erstwhile allies are busy, think very hard about your plans for the immediate future so you have something to tell Eel when he gets back.<br /> <br /> 4. Party on the roof!<br /> <br /> 5. See Eel off and keep an eye on the cat until it wakes, feed it (with the extra meat) take care of it. Y\u2019know get that imprinting started. You\u2019re going to have it get very, used to you before you can collect anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I jump on the band wagon. I\u2019m so happy to read more of this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T20:41:34-08:00","id":1283419,"title":"","content":"\u201cNow what?\u201d You look up at Eel and put your hands on your hips\u2026and break into a huge grin. \u201cNow we <i>celebrate</i>, you old bastard! Eel, if I give you some cash to go buy us a nice dinner and something to drink, can I trust you to actually come <i>back </i>with a nice dinner and something to drink?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cKid\u2026I know you. I get that you\u2019re just trying to be sorta friendly and snarky,\u201d Eel frowns. \u201cBut, well, it\u2019s raining, and your hair is covering your eyes, and I dunno if you\u2019ve noticed but there\u2019s a bunch of ravens circlin\u2019 over your head. You\u2019re comin\u2019 across real threatening-like.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026really?\u201d You turn to Moth.<br /> <br /> She nods. \u201cI mean\u2026the Master is much more imposing, but\u2026yes. I think it\u2019s as much the storm as anything, but you\u2019re definitely coming across like some sort of evil mastermind from a play.\u201d<br /> <br /> You grin wider. \u201cGreat! But seriously, Eel. We just pulled off our second stupid dangerous thing this season! And this one\u2019s <i>also </i>going to make us some coin! We ought to celebrate!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026Fine. I\u2019ll go grab a bite. But only because I don\u2019t much like the look of the canal in this weather. I\u2019m spending the night at your place.\u201d<br /> <br /> You look at Moth again.<br /> <br /> She looks Eel up and down, makes a slightly sour face\u2026but shrugs. \u201c\u2026I guess it\u2019s okay by me. If you\u2019re bringing something to drink.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGreat! Moth, I don\u2019t think you\u2019re going to get the smell off that blanket, and I don\u2019t wanna just leave the cat in the rain. Is it okay if I get you a new blanket and use yours as a tarp to give it a bit of shelter?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI guess. You don\u2019t want it catching a cold after all that work catching it, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight. If you want to head downstairs and keep the stove going, I\u2019ll stay up here and set up the tarp and, uh\u2026reinforce the cage. A bit. Just in case.\u201d<br /> <br /> Moth and Eel both look at the cat sleeping in the wooden bars and nod silently before departing. It seemed real sturdy when you first put it together. Those hefty wooden bars and expertly woven wire connection points seem\u2026a bit more ephemeral now, with a huge slumbering cat inside them. You heft the sturdy ropes you and Eel used in your stretcher and do a little bit of weaving and knotwork to reinforce the places that look weak.<br /> <br /> Then you sit in the rain for a while and watch the cat sleep. It yawns and stretches, and you observe the splint you made for its leg. Your work looks to be holding. That\u2019s good\u2026or not? It briefly occurs to you that a raptor cat without legs is probably easier to collect musk from, but...the thought saddens you a little. Even if it\u2019s a man-eating monster, as you sit here in the rain watching it sleep, the Raptor Cat seems\u2026beautiful. <div align=\"center\">*****</div> <br /> You lose track of time for a little while, and the raitons land on your head and shoulders, making little squawks and jostling each other for the best seating atop you, but mostly staying still and silent and respecting the mood. You feel better than you have felt in quite a while. Your plan came together. All that scheming and bartering and training the raitons\u2026it paid off. There\u2019s a deep and calm sense of satisfaction in that. The River Dragon felt like a stroke of luck, a gift from the Dragons, but this\u2026this is a victory you made happen. Feeling like you have control of your life is\u2026new. You decide you really like it.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been at least half an hour before your reverie is interrupted by shouting from the street below. You walk over to the edge of the roof and look down at the street, its uneven surface sparkling black with several inches of rain. Eel is down there, carrying a big sack over his shoulder and two bottles of something in one hand. The other hand has a single bottle, which you surmise is open, because Eel is walking a little less stiffly and singing a bit more loudly than usual. You gently put your palm to your forehead-the old man is just asking for a mugging-but can\u2019t help smiling at the boatman\u2019s good mood.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou still up there, you little brat?\u201d He calls up to you.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah. Come in and get something to eat before you catch your death out there, old man!\u201d You call back down. A warm dry evening with\u2026friends\u2026and hot food on a rainy night, celebrating a victory\u2026that sounds just lovely, and you chuckle as you call down to Eel.<br /> <br /> So you\u2019re watching as a six-foot high wall of black water sweeps down the street toward the canal, baskets and street stalls and a throng of desperately paddling rats bouncing in its wake. You have time to yell Eel\u2019s name, and he has time to turn and see it coming and throw down the groceries and start towards the door of your apartment building\u2026and then the flood bowls him over like a child trying to move against the foot traffic in the Guild District at lunch hour.<br /> <br /> <b>You only have moments, and time seems to slow to a crawl as you decide what you are going to do with them. What\u2019s your play?</b><br /> <br /> Jump off the second story roof-<i>no wait, that\u2019s stupid, slide down the drainpipe</i>-to the street so you can rescue Eel-he\u2019s a clever old bastard, but he\u2019s old. He doesn\u2019t have the strength to swim against a flood. You\u2019re young and lucky, so you do\u2026probably. If you hurry and the fall doesn\u2019t kill you, it\u2019s the fastest way down there. Time is of the essence here. If you don\u2019t reach him right away, the current will drag him right down the street.<br /> <br /> Grab the blanket off the top of the Raptor Cat\u2019s cage and use it as a makeshift parachute. If you\u2019re lucky and the Raitons grab on and help provide a little lift, you think you can make it half a block out to the canal to where Eel\u2019s boat is still tied, if wildly rocking in the flood. It\u2019ll be rougher sailing than you\u2019ve practiced, but you feel a lot better about saving your friend in a boat than you do swimming in the floodwaters\u2026though if you\u2019re wrong, you\u2019ll land in the floodwaters with a heavy blanket wrapping around you, which would certainly make drowning a lot easier.<br /> <br /> Run down the three flights of stairs to the ground floor. It\u2019s probably already starting to flood down there, so you\u2019ll be fighting the flow of people moving upstairs from the floor-level apartments\u2026but if you can get past them and brute-force the door open against the weight of the water, and if Eel\u2019s been able to fight the current and grab hold of your front steps you might be able to help him inside.<br /> <br /> Tell Chupong to follow Eel in the flood and keep making noise so you can track him. You don\u2019t like the idea of heading down into those floodwaters, but you can cannibalize some rope from the Raptor Cat\u2019s cage, hope the thing stays asleep for a while yet, and try and follow him along the roofways above and throw down a rope for Eel to catch, and hopefully pull the old man to safety.<br /> <br /> Stand on the rooftop and watch as the flood drags the old man down the street. It\u2019s a shame to lose him, and you feel terrible for not doing something\u2026but...fifteen percent\u2026no. You shake your head. You\u2019re going to feel shitty for years that you thought about the money for a minute. But\u2026 if you try to save him you\u2019re only going to get dragged under and drown yourself. You need to save your strength for things you can actually accomplish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T21:58:17-08:00","id":1283434,"title":"","content":"I feel somewhat guilty in that it was my own greedy suggestion that precipitated this turn of events.<br /> <br /> Knowing which, I suggest doubling down on the stupid awesome, grabbing that blanket and jumping off the roof, hoping that some pattern spiders are paying a lot of attention!<br /> <br /> (Oh and heaps of thumbs up for continuing to do this! Made my day! *I\u2019m not trying to get our protagonist killed, honest!*)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 01-29-2019, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T05:35:01-08:00","id":1283490,"title":"","content":"&quot;Tell Chupong to follow Eel in the flood and keep making noise so you can track him. You don\u2019t like the idea of heading down into those floodwaters, but you can cannibalize some rope from the Raptor Cat\u2019s cage, hope the thing stays asleep for a while yet, and try and follow him along the roofways above and throw down a rope for Eel to catch, and hopefully pull the old man to safety.&quot;<br /> <br /> Seems like the most sensible option.<br /> Also THE GURU LIVES *STOMP STOMP*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T05:26:00-08:00","id":1283687,"title":"","content":"Start by cannibalizing rope from the cage. If Eel has washed away by the time you've got enough to throw down, proceed to follow him over the roofs with Chupong guiding the way. <br /> <br /> If he hasn't, secure the rope to a chimney or something up here, throw it down to him so he has something to hold onto, and *then* take the stairs down to the door. <br /> <br /> And if we survive this, we should look into finding another apartment in a part of town that's above the water line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T07:33:14-08:00","id":1283717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1283490#post1283490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Tell Chupong to follow Eel in the flood and keep making noise so you can track him. You don\u2019t like the idea of heading down into those floodwaters, but you can cannibalize some rope from the Raptor Cat\u2019s cage, hope the thing stays asleep for a while yet, and try and follow him along the roofways above and throw down a rope for Eel to catch, and hopefully pull the old man to safety.&quot;<br /> <br /> Seems like the most sensible option.<br /> Also THE GURU LIVES *STOMP STOMP*</div> </div> </div> </div>I SECOND BOTH THE SANITY AND THE CELEBRATION.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T20:53:02-08:00","id":1283846,"title":"","content":"Sorry but I say let him go. We aren\u2019t Exalted or even god blooded. We are little more than a child. A clever, lucky, and gifted child but not a hero, at least not yet. Discretion is the better part of valor. We can honor his memory and make generous offerings for him to ease his stay in the underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T23:11:11-08:00","id":1284670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jairain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/955241-urchin-quest?p=1283846#post1283846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry but I say let him go. We aren\u2019t Exalted or even god blooded. We are little more than a child. A clever, lucky, and gifted child but not a hero, at least not yet. Discretion is the better part of valor. We can honor his memory and make generous offerings for him to ease his stay in the underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And with an attitude like that, we never will be! I'm not saying you have to do something incredibly stupid and valorous to exalt, but it helps! However, there's no need to be totally boneheaded. I also vote for the grab rope and use Chupong to scout option. This might result in an escaped raptor cat, but it's drowsy and has a broken leg so I doubt it'll go far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T22:57:57-08:00","id":1286977,"title":"","content":"I favour the rope-andr-aiton plan. We're a kid, we can't fight a flood and win. But we can toss Eel a rope and anchor it to something so he can use it to swing himself out of the main current. I know this is possible, I've seen similar things done with boats in heavy currents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T23:17:39-08:00","id":1286984,"title":"","content":"Rope+raiton plan, please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T00:50:13-08:00","id":1286989,"title":"","content":"In light of the sanity everyone is displaying I would like to change my plan to rope + ration as well.<br /> <br /> May I suggest if it is narratively possible, save some of that meat? Not for ourselves, mind, but by doing what we are doing we might be coming back to an awake, hungry man-eating predator?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}